hadiths[2809]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection I will come to the gate of Paradise and ask for it to be opened. The keeper of Paradise will ask, 'Who are you?' I will reply, 'I am Muhammad.' He will say, 'It is for you that I was commanded not to open it for anyone before you.'"""
"2","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among what people have received from the words of the earlier prophets is this: when you have no modesty left, then do whatever you wish."""
"3","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The last to be driven (to the place of gathering) will be two shepherds from the tribe of Muzaynah. Calling out to their sheep, they will head for Madinah, but they will find it completely deserted, until, when they reach Thaniyyat al-Wada', they will fall on their faces."""
"4","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The last person to enter Paradise will be a man who walks on the Sirat in such a way that at times he walks on, at times he falls on his face, and at times the Fire scorches him. When he has crossed it (the Sirat), he will turn and look at it (the Fire) and say: 'Blessed is the One who has saved me from you. Allah Almighty has certainly given me a blessing that He has not given to anyone among the first and the last.' Then a tree will be brought before him, and he will say: 'O my Lord! Bring me close to this tree so that I may rest in its shade and drink of its water.' Allah Almighty will say: 'O son of Adam! If I give you this, will you not then ask Me for something else?' He will say: 'No, O my Lord!' and he will make a firm pledge to Allah that he will not ask for anything besides it. His Lord will excuse him (that is, overlook his impatience), because he will see something over which he cannot remain patient. So Allah will bring him close to that tree, and he will rest in its shade and drink of its water. Then another tree, more beautiful than the first, will be shown to him. He will say: 'O my Lord! Bring me close to this one so that I may drink of its water and rest in its shade; I will not ask You for anything besides it.' He will say: 'O son of Adam! Did you not pledge to Me that you would not ask Me for anything else? Perhaps if I bring you close to it, you will ask Me for something else?' So he will pledge to Him not to ask for anything besides it, and his Lord will excuse him, because he sees something over which he cannot remain patient. So He will bring him close to it, and he will rest in its shade and drink of its water. Then a tree will be shown to him at the gate of Paradise, more beautiful than the first two. He will say: 'O my Lord! Bring me close to this one so that I may rest in its shade and drink of its water; I will not ask You for anything besides it.' He will say: 'O son of Adam! Did you not pledge to Me that you would not ask Me for anything else?' He will say: 'Yes, O my Lord, but bring me close to this one; I will not ask You for anything besides it.' His Lord will excuse him, because he sees something over which he cannot remain patient, and He will bring him close to it. When He brings him close to it, he will hear the voices of the people of Paradise and will say: 'O my Lord! Admit me into it.' He will say: 'O son of Adam! What will put an end to your asking of Me? Would it please you if I gave you the world and the like of it along with it?' He will say: 'O my Lord! Are You mocking me, while You are the Lord of the worlds?' He will say: 'I am not mocking you, but I have power over whatever I will.'"""
"5","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who consumes usury (riba), the one who feeds it (that is, pays it), the one who writes it down and its two witnesses, when they know that; the woman who tattoos (the body) for beautification and the woman who has herself tattooed; the one who withholds zakah; and the one who reverts to being a Bedouin after the Hijrah (that is, cuts himself off from the religion and the community and returns to ignorance): all of these are declared accursed on the Day of Resurrection by the blessed tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) (that is, they have been cursed)."""
"6","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I eat as a slave eats. By the One in whose Hand is my soul! If the world weighed as much as the wing of a mosquito in the sight of Allah, He would not give a disbeliever a single sip (of water) from it."""
"7","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I eat as a slave eats, and I sit as a slave sits."""
"8","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I eat as a slave eats, and I sit as a slave sits, for in reality I am only a servant and slave (of Allah)."""
"9","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is it poverty and need that you fear? By the One in whose Hand is my soul! The world (and its wealth) will be poured upon you in such abundance that if the heart of any of you deviates from the truth, it will deviate only because of it (love of the world). And by Allah! I have certainly left you upon a bright and clear path whose night and day are exactly alike (in brightness)."""
"10","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I command you to do four things and forbid you from four things. I command you to believe in Allah alone. Do you know what believing in Allah alone is? It is bearing witness that there is no true god except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, establishing the prayer, paying zakah, fasting in Ramadan, and that you give a fifth of the spoils of war (in the way of Allah). And I forbid you from using the dubba', the naqir, the hantam and the muzaffat (names of particular vessels used for making wine). Memorise these things well and inform those you have left behind about them."""
"11","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I command you to do four things and forbid you from four things. Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, pay zakah, fast in Ramadan and give a fifth of the spoils of war (in the way of Allah). And I forbid you from four things, namely using the dubba', the hantam, the muzaffat and the naqir (particular vessels used for making wine)."""
"12","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I command you to do three things and forbid you from three things. I command you to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, to hold fast all together to the rope of Allah and not be divided, and to listen to and obey the one whom Allah has put in charge of your affairs (that is, the ruler). And I forbid you from 'it was said and he said' (idle argument or spreading rumours), from asking much (begging without need or asking needless questions), and from wasting wealth."""
"13","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Consult women regarding their own (marriage) affairs, for a previously married woman (a widow or divorcee) expresses herself by speaking, while the permission of a virgin is her silence."""
"14","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Consult an orphan girl regarding her own (marriage) affair, and her permission is her remaining silent."""
"15","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Love for the Ansar is a sign of faith, and hatred of the Ansar is a sign of hypocrisy."""
"16","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The signs of a hypocrite are three: when he speaks he lies, when he makes a promise he breaks it, and when something is entrusted to him he betrays the trust."""
"17","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Come to your tilth (that is, your wife) however you wish; feed her when you yourself eat, clothe her when you yourself are clothed, do not speak ill of her face, and do not beat her."""
"18","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat olive oil as a condiment and anoint yourselves with it, for it comes from a blessed tree."""
"19","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eat from this tree as a condiment, meaning the olive; and whoever is offered perfume, let him make sure to use some of it."""
"20","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are invited, accept the invitation (that is, attend it)."""
"21","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allow women to pray in the mosque at night."""
"22","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allow women to go to the mosques at night."""
"23","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has refused to grant the killer of a believer the ability to repent."""
"24","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Bakr! Allah Almighty and the believers will never accept that there be disagreement over you (over your becoming caliph)."""
"25","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I take your pledge of allegiance on condition that you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the obligatory prayer, pay zakah, act sincerely towards every Muslim, and completely disavow polytheism (shirk)."""
"26","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I take your pledge of allegiance on condition that you will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit adultery, will not kill your children, will not bring a slander that you have invented yourselves, and will not disobey me in anything good. So whoever among you fulfils this pledge, his reward rests with Allah; and whoever commits any of these (sins) and is punished for it in this world, that punishment will be an expiation and a purification for him; and whoever's sin Allah conceals (that is, he is not punished in this world), his matter rests with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: if He wills He will punish him, and if He wills He will forgive him."""
"27","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(In charity and spending) begin with those whose support is your responsibility."""
"28","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Begin with yourself and give charity (that is, spend) on yourself. Then if anything remains, on your family; if anything remains after them, on your close relatives; and if anything still remains after spending on your relatives, then spend like this and like this, to the right and to the left (on other people in need)."""
"29","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Delay the Zuhr prayer until it is cooler (when the intensity of the heat has lessened)."""
"30","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Delay the Zuhr prayer until it is cooler (when the intensity of the heat has lessened), for the intensity of the heat comes from the breath (and raging) of Hell."""
"31","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ammar! Rejoice, you will be martyred by a rebellious group."""
"32","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rejoice, for Allah Almighty says: 'This (fever) is My fire which I set upon My believing servant in this world, so that it may be his portion of protection from the Fire (of Hell) on the Day of Resurrection.'"""
"33","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rejoice! Among the blessings of Allah upon you is that at this hour no one among people other than you is praying."""
"34","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rejoice! One end of this Qur'an is in the Hand of Allah and the other end is in your hands, so hold fast to it; you will certainly never be destroyed or go astray after it."""
"35","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Receive glad tidings, and give glad tidings to those you have left behind, that whoever bears witness sincerely from the heart that there is no true god except Allah will enter Paradise."""
"36","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Rejoice! This is your Lord, who has opened one of the gates of the heaven and is boasting about you to the angels, saying: 'Look at My servants! They have performed one obligation and are now waiting for another.'"""
"37","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umm al-Ala'! Rejoice, for the illness of a Muslim removes his sins just as fire in a furnace removes the rust of iron."""
"38","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aishah! Rejoice, Allah Almighty has revealed your innocence."""
"39","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most detested of men in the sight of Allah is the one who is fiercely quarrelsome."""
"40","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most detested of people in the sight of Allah are three: one who commits deviation and wrongdoing in the Haram (of Makkah), one who seeks the ways of the Jahiliyyah in Islam, and one who pursues a person to kill him in order to shed his blood unjustly."""
"41","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek me among your weak, for you are provided for and helped only by virtue of your weak."""
"42","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The human body has 360 joints, and every day charity is due for each one of them. So a good word that a person speaks is charity; a man helping his brother with something is charity; a drink of water that he gives someone is charity; and removing something harmful from the road is charity."""
"43","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of a people's sister (their nephew) is counted as one of them."""
"44","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The traveller is the first to drink, meaning from Zamzam."""
"45","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The two sons of al-As are believers: Hisham and Amr."""
"46","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(When drinking water) move the cup away from your mouth and then take a breath."""
"47","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These two sons of mine, Hasan and Husayn, are the leaders of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than both of them."""
"48","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever two matters were put before the son of Sumayyah (Ammar bin Yasir), he always chose the more correct and rightly guided of the two."""
"49","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O my sons! Do not stone Jamrat al-Aqabah until the sun has risen."""
"50","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, Zubayr is in Paradise, Abdur-Rahman bin Awf is in Paradise, Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas is in Paradise, Sa'id bin Zayd is in Paradise, and Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah is in Paradise."""
"51","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Bakr and Umar, apart from the Prophets and the Messengers, are the leaders of all the middle-aged people of Paradise, from the first to the last."""
"52","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Sufyan bin al-Harith is the best of my family."""
"53","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Yemen have come to you; they are the softest and most tender of heart. Faith is Yemeni and wisdom too is Yemeni. Pride and arrogance are among the camel owners, while tranquillity and dignity are among the shepherds of sheep (that is, the people of the flocks)."""
"54","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Yemen have come to you; they are very soft-hearted and tender. Understanding of the religion (fiqh) is Yemeni and wisdom too is Yemeni."""
"55","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The month of Ramadan has come to you, a blessed month. Allah has made its fasting obligatory upon you. In it the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the rebellious devils are shackled and confined. In it there is a night that is better than a thousand months; whoever is deprived of the good of that night has truly been deprived (of all good)."""
"56","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One came to me from my Lord (an angel), and he gave me the choice: either half of my Ummah would be admitted into Paradise, or I would be given the right of intercession. So I chose intercession, and this intercession will be for everyone who dies in a state of not having associated anything with Allah."""
"57","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One came to me from my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic (an angel), and said: Whoever of your Ummah sends blessings (salah) upon you once, Allah Almighty will, in return, record for him ten good deeds, erase from him ten sins, raise him ten degrees, and he will be answered with the like of it (in mercy and blessing)."""
"58","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tonight one came to me from my Lord and said: Pray in this blessed valley, that is, the valley of al-Aqiq, and say: I intend Umrah combined with Hajj."""
"59","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tonight my Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, came to me in the most beautiful form and said: O Muhammad! Do you know what the angels near to Allah (the Exalted Assembly) are disputing about? I said: No. So Allah Almighty placed His hand between my shoulders until I felt its coolness in my chest, and I came to know whatever is in the heavens and the earth. Then Allah Almighty said: O Muhammad! Do you know what the angels near to Allah are disputing about? I said: Yes, about the expiations (deeds that wipe out sins) and the degrees (deeds that raise one in rank). The expiations are: remaining in the mosques after the prayers, walking on foot to the congregational prayers, and performing ablution thoroughly despite hardship (cold or discomfort). Allah Almighty said: You have spoken the truth, O Muhammad! Whoever does these things will live in goodness and die in goodness, and he will be as free of his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him. And Allah Almighty said: O Muhammad! When you have prayed, then make this supplication: O Allah! I ask You for the doing of good deeds, the abandoning of evil deeds, and love for the poor, and that You forgive me, have mercy on me and accept my repentance; and when You intend a trial for Your servants, then take me to Yourself without being put to trial. And the degrees (deeds that raise one in rank) are: spreading the greeting of peace, feeding people, and praying at night while people are asleep."""
"60","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me with fever and plague. I kept the fever in Madinah and sent the plague to Syria (al-Sham). So the plague is martyrdom and mercy for my Ummah, while for the disbelievers it is a punishment."""
"61","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and informed me that my Ummah will kill this son of mine, that is, al-Husayn, and he brought me some of its soil, which was red."""
"62","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and commanded me to command my Companions and those with me to raise their voices when calling out the Talbiyah (that is, Labbayk)."""
"63","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and gave me the glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are both the leaders of the youth of Paradise."""
"64","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and gave me the glad tidings that whoever of your Ummah dies without having associated anything with Allah will enter Paradise. I asked: Even if he committed adultery and even if he stole? He replied: Even if he committed adultery and even if he stole."""
"65","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: Allah commands you to teach your Ummah to recite the Qur'an in one harf (mode of recitation). I said: I ask Allah for His pardon and forgiveness; my Ummah is not able to do that. Then he came to me a second time and said: Allah commands you to teach your Ummah to recite the Qur'an in two ahruf. I said: I ask Allah for His pardon and forgiveness; my Ummah is not able to do that. Then he came to me a third time and said: Allah commands you to teach your Ummah to recite the Qur'an in three ahruf. I said: I ask Allah for His pardon and forgiveness; my Ummah is not able to do that. Then he came to me a fourth time and said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, commands you to teach your Ummah to recite the Qur'an in seven ahruf (modes of recitation); whichever harf of them they recite in, they will have recited correctly."""
"66","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: Give your Ummah the glad tidings that whoever dies without having associated anything with Allah will enter Paradise. I asked: O Jibril! Even if he stole and even if he committed adultery? He said: Yes. I asked (again): Even if he stole and even if he committed adultery? He said: Yes. I asked (a third time): Even if he stole and even if he committed adultery? He said: Yes, and even if he drank wine."""
"67","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said to me: Allah commands you to command your Companions to raise their voices in the Talbiyah, for it is one of the rites of Hajj."""
"68","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: I came to you last night, but nothing prevented me from entering the house you were in except that there were statues at its door, inside the house there was a curtain bearing images, and inside the house there was a dog. So give the order concerning the head of the statue in the house that it be cut off so that it becomes like the shape of a tree; give the order concerning the curtain that it be cut up and made into two cushions to be trodden upon (put to use); and give the order concerning the dog that it be put out of the house."""
"69","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: O Messenger of Allah! Here is Khadijah coming to you; she has a vessel containing curry, food or something to drink. When she comes to you, convey to her the greeting of peace from her Lord and from me, and give her the glad tidings of a house of pearls in Paradise, in which there will be neither noise nor fatigue."""
"70","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and asked: O Muhammad! Are you ill? I replied: Yes. He said: In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah over you, from everything that harms you, from the evil of every soul and from the eye of every envier. In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah over you, and may Allah grant you cure."""
"71","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad! Are you not pleased that your Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, says: Whoever of your Ummah sends blessings upon you once, I will send down ten mercies upon him in return, and whoever of your Ummah sends the greeting of peace upon you once, I will send peace upon him ten times? So I said: Certainly, O my Lord!"""
"72","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad! Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has cursed wine, and He has cursed the one who presses it, the one who has it pressed, the one who drinks it, the one who carries it, the one to whom it is carried, the one who sells it, the one who buys it, the one who serves it, and the one for whom it is poured."""
"73","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad! Live as long as you wish, for you must eventually die; love whomever you wish, for you must part from him; do whatever deeds you wish, for you will be recompensed for them. And know that the honour of the believer lies in standing (in prayer) at night, and his dignity lies in being independent of people."""
"74","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad! Say. I asked: What shall I say? He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which no righteous or wicked person can transgress, from the evil of everything He has created and brought into being, from the evil of what descends from the sky, from the evil of what ascends into it, from the evil of what He has created and spread in the earth, from the evil of what comes out of it, from the evil of the trials of the night and the day, and from the evil of every visitor that comes by night, except a visitor that comes with good, O Most Merciful!"""
"75","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad! Whoever lives to see one of his parents, then dies and enters Hell (for not having served them), Allah has distanced him from His mercy. Say: Amin. So I said: Amin. He said: O Muhammad! Whoever lives to see the month of Ramadan, then dies without being forgiven and so enters Hell, Allah has distanced him from His mercy. Say: Amin. So I said: Amin. He said: And whoever you are mentioned in front of and he does not send blessings upon you, then dies and enters Hell, Allah has distanced him from His mercy. Say: Amin. So I said: Amin."""
"76","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the earliest days of revelation Jibril came to me and taught me the method of ablution and prayer. When he had finished the ablution, he took a handful of water and sprinkled it on his private part."""
"77","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril came to me from Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, and said: O Muhammad! Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: I have made five prayers obligatory upon your Ummah. Whoever comes having performed them with due observance of their complete ablution, their appointed times, their bowing and their prostrations, has a covenant with Me that I will admit him into Paradise because of them. And whoever meets Me having fallen short in any of that has no covenant with Me: if I will, I shall punish him, and if I will, I shall have mercy on him."""
"78","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril and Mika'il came to me. Jibril sat on my right and Mika'il on my left. Jibril said: O Muhammad! Recite the Qur'an in one harf (mode of recitation). Mika'il said: Ask him for more. So I said: Increase it for me. Then Jibril said: Recite it in three ahruf. Mika'il again said: Ask him for more. I said: Increase it further for me. So it went on until it reached seven ahruf, and Jibril said: Recite it in seven ahruf; each of them is healing and sufficient."""
"79","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An angel came to me and greeted me with peace. He had descended from the sky and had never descended before that. He gave me the glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise, and that Fatimah is the leader of the women of Paradise."""
"80","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Would you like your heart to become soft and your need to be fulfilled? Be merciful to the orphan, pass your hand over his head and feed him from your own food; your heart will become soft and you will attain your need."""
"81","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Would you like to strive hard (and exert yourselves) in supplication? Then say: O Allah! Help us to thank You, to remember You and to worship You in the best manner."""
"82","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep sheep and goats, for there is blessing in them."""
"83","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep sheep and goats, for when they return in the evening they bring good (and blessing), and when they go out to graze in the morning they go with good."""
"84","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know where this sun goes? It keeps moving until it reaches its resting place beneath the Throne and falls down in prostration. It remains in that state until it is told: Rise and return to where you came from. So it returns and rises from its place of rising (the east). Then it moves on until, reaching that same resting place of its beneath the Throne, it falls down in prostration and remains in that state until it is commanded: Rise and return to where you came from. So it returns and rises from its place of rising. Then it keeps moving, and people find nothing strange about it, until it reaches that same resting place of its beneath the Throne, and it will be told: Rise, and today rise from your place of setting (the west). So it will rise from the west. Do you know when that will be? It will be when {No soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or had not earned some good through its faith}. [Surah al-An'am: 158]"""
"85","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know what 'adh (tale-bearing and slander) is? It is carrying people's words to one another in order to create mischief (and discord) among them."""
"86","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know what backbiting (ghibah) is? It is your mentioning your brother in a way he dislikes. If what you say is in him, you have backbitten him, and if it is not in him, you have slandered him."""
"87","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know who the bankrupt one is? The bankrupt one of my Ummah is the person who will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds such as prayer, fasting and zakah, but he will come having abused someone in the world, falsely accused someone, consumed someone's wealth, shed someone's blood and beaten someone. So this (wronged) person will be given some of his good deeds, and that (other wronged) person will be given some of his good deeds as well. Then, if his good deeds run out before the rights owed by him are settled, their (the wronged people's) sins will be taken and cast upon him (the wrongdoer), and then he will be thrown into the Fire."""
"88","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know what these two books are? Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said about the book in his right hand: This is a book from the Lord of the Worlds containing the names of the people of Paradise, and the names of their fathers and forefathers and their tribes; then a total has been drawn up at the end of them (that is, their number has been completed), so nothing will ever be added to them or taken away from them. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said about the book in his left hand: This is a book from the Lord of the Worlds containing the names of the people of Hell, and the names of their fathers and forefathers and their tribes; then at the end of them too the number has been completed, so there will never be any increase or decrease in them either. Keep to the right course and be moderate, for the one destined for Paradise will have his life sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise, whatever deeds he may have done (in his life), and the one destined for Hell will have his life sealed with the deeds of the people of Hell, whatever deeds he may have done. Your Lord has finished deciding about His servants: {A group will be in Paradise and a group in the Blazing Fire (Hell)}. [Surah al-Shura: 7]"""
"89","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Are you pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise? Are you pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise? Are you pleased to be half of the people of Paradise? Only a Muslim (submissive) soul will enter Paradise, and you, compared with the polytheists, are merely like a white hair on the hide of a black bull, or a black hair on the hide of a red bull."""
"90","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave the Abyssinians alone as long as they leave you alone (that is, do not be the first to fight them), for no one will take out the treasure of the Ka'bah except a man with two thin shins from Abyssinia."""
"91","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave me alone regarding what I have left for you (that is, do not probe into it); but when I tell you something, then take it from me firmly, for those before you were destroyed only because of their excessive questioning of their Prophets and their disagreeing with them."""
"92","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Mu'adh! Do you want to put people to trial (hardship)? When you lead people in prayer, recite surahs such as {By the sun and its brightness} [Surah al-Shams], {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} [Surah al-A'la], {By the night when it covers} [Surah al-Layl] and {Read in the name of your Lord} [Surah al-'Alaq]."""
"93","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you want to make it die many deaths? Why did you not sharpen your knife before laying it down on the ground?!"""
"94","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you think that I will be the last of you to die? Listen! I am among the first of you to die, and you will follow me in different groups, killing one another."""
"95","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you hear what I hear? I hear the creaking of the sky, and it is right for it to creak, for there is not a space of a hand-span in it except that an angel is there in prostration or standing."""
"96","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know? The first group of my Ummah to enter Paradise will be the poor Muhajirun. They will come to the gate of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection and ask for it to be opened, and the keepers of Paradise will ask them: Have you been brought to account? They will reply: For what should we be brought to account? We kept our swords on our shoulders in the path of Allah until we died in that state. So the gate will be opened for them, and they will be resting in Paradise forty years before the other people enter it."""
"97","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fear Allah wherever you are, follow an evil deed with a good deed and it will wipe it out, and treat people with good character."""
"98","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fear Allah and never regard any good deed as insignificant, even if it is pouring water from your bucket into the vessel of one who asks for water, or meeting your brother with a cheerful (smiling) face. And beware of letting your izar (lower garment) hang below the ankles, for letting the izar hang down is a sign of arrogance, and Allah does not love arrogance. And if a person abuses you and taunts you with a fault that is not in you, do not taunt him with a fault that is in him; leave him, its evil consequence will be upon him and its reward will be for you. And never abuse anyone."""
"99","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu al-Walid! Fear Allah, lest you come on the Day of Resurrection carrying on your back a groaning camel, or a lowing cow, or a bleating goat."""
"100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid what has been made unlawful, and you will be the most devout worshipper among people. Be content with what Allah has allotted to you, and you will be the richest (most self-sufficient) of people. Treat your neighbour well, and you will be a complete believer. Love for people what you love for yourself, and you will be a true Muslim. And do not laugh much, for excessive laughter deadens the heart."""
"101","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of oppression, for indeed oppression will be (deep) darkness on the Day of Resurrection."""
"102","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of oppression, for indeed oppression will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection; and beware of stinginess and greed, for indeed it was this greed that destroyed those before you and drove them to shed one another's blood and to make lawful what had been made unlawful for them."""
"103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fear Allah, for the most treacherous of you in our sight is the one who himself seeks a post (or office)."""
"104","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fear Allah regarding these speechless animals: ride them while they are healthy and fit for riding, and eat them (slaughter them) while they are healthy (and well-fed)."""
"105","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep fearing Allah regarding the prayer and regarding those whom you own (that is, male and female slaves)."""
"106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep fearing Allah regarding those whom you own (that is, your slaves and those under your authority)."""
"107","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fear Allah and act with justice and fairness among your children."""
"108","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep fearing Allah and maintain the ties of kinship (treat your relatives well)."""
"109","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fear Allah, pray your five (obligatory) prayers, fast your month (of Ramadan), pay the zakah on your wealth willingly, and obey your rulers; (by the blessing of these deeds) you will enter the Paradise of your Lord."""
"110","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of two deeds that bring down curses: one is the person who relieves himself on the people's path, and the other the one who does so in the place where they take shade."""
"111","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep away from one afflicted with leprosy just as one keeps away from a lion."""
"112","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of three deeds that bring down curses: relieving oneself at watering places, in the middle of the road, and in a shaded place."""
"113","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of three deeds that bring down curses: that any one of you should sit to relieve himself in a shade where people rest, or on a public road, or in standing water."""
"114","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Protect yourselves from the Fire of Hell, even if it be with (giving in charity) a piece of a date."""
"115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Protect yourselves from the Fire of Hell, even if it be with (giving in charity) a piece of a date; and if you do not find even that, then save yourself from the Fire with a good word (spoken gently)."""
"116","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of the house (that is, the public bath) that is called the hammam; whoever enters it should cover his private parts ('awrah)."""
"117","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for it is carried up upon the clouds, and Allah Almighty says: 'By My Might and My Majesty, I shall surely help you, even if it be after some time.'"""
"118","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for indeed it rises to the sky as though it were a spark."""
"119","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, even if he is a disbeliever, for indeed there is no veil (or barrier) before it (the supplication)."""
"120","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of these altars, that is, the mihrabs (for the craving for leadership and prominence is ruinous to a person's religion)."""
"121","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform the bowing (ruku') and prostration fully (with humility and devotion). By the One in whose Hand is my soul, when you bow and when you prostrate, I see you even from behind my back."""
"122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Complete the front row first, then the one after it; and if there is any shortfall, let it be in the very last row."""
"123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Complete the rows, for indeed I see you even from behind my back."""
"124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform ablution (wudu) completely; woe to the heels (left dry), from the Fire (that is, ruin)."""
"125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A servant from among the servants of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to whom Allah had given wealth, will be brought before Him. Allah will ask him: 'What did you do in the world?' He will say: 'O my Lord, I did no (special) deed, except that You gave me wealth, so I used to trade with people, and it was my habit to be lenient with the well-off and to grant respite to those in hardship.' Allah Almighty will say: 'I am more entitled to that than you. (O angels,) pardon My servant.'"""
"126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Approaching women in their back passages (that is, the anus) is unlawful."""
"127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Buraq was brought to me, and it was a tall white animal, larger than a donkey and smaller than a mule, which would place its hoof as far as its sight reached. I mounted it until I reached Bayt al-Maqdis, where I tied it to the ring to which the prophets used to tie (their mounts). Then I entered the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs in it. Then, when I came out, Jibril brought me a vessel of wine and a vessel of milk. I chose the milk, and Jibril said: 'You have chosen the fitrah (natural disposition).' Then we were taken up to the heaven. Jibril asked for the gate to be opened, and it was asked: 'Who are you?' He said: 'I am Jibril.' It was asked: 'Who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' It was asked: 'Has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes, he has been sent for.' So the gate was opened for us, and there I met Adam (peace be upon him); he welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then we were taken up to the second heaven. Jibril asked for the gate to be opened, and it was asked: 'Who are you?' He said: 'I am Jibril.' It was asked: 'Who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' It was asked: 'Has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes, he has been sent for.' So the gate was opened for us, and there I met the two maternal cousins, Isa bin Maryam and Yahya bin Zakariyya (peace be upon them both); they both welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then we were taken up to the third heaven. Jibril asked for the gate to be opened, and it was asked: 'Who are you?' He said: 'I am Jibril.' It was asked: 'Who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' It was asked: 'Has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes, he has been sent for.' So the gate was opened for us, and there I met Yusuf (peace be upon him), who had been given half of (the world's) beauty; he welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then we were taken up to the fourth heaven. Jibril asked for the gate to be opened, and it was asked: 'Who is this?' He said: 'I am Jibril.' It was asked: 'Who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' It was asked: 'Has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes, he has been sent for.' So the gate was opened for us, and there I met Idris (peace be upon him); he welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Allah Almighty has said: {And We raised him to a high station.} [Surah Maryam: 57] Then we were taken up to the fifth heaven. Jibril asked for the gate to be opened, and it was asked: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Jibril.' It was asked: 'Who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' It was asked: 'Has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes, he has been sent for.' So the gate was opened for us, and there I met Harun (peace be upon him); he welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then we were taken up to the sixth heaven. Jibril asked for the gate to be opened, and it was asked: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Jibril.' It was asked: 'Who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' It was asked: 'Has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes, he has been sent for.' So the gate was opened for us, and I met Musa (peace be upon him); he welcomed me and prayed for good for me. Then we were taken up to the seventh heaven. Jibril asked for the gate to be opened, and it was asked: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Jibril.' It was asked: 'Who is with you?' He said: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' It was asked: 'Has he been sent for?' He said: 'Yes, he has been sent for.' So the gate was opened for us, and I met Ibrahim (peace be upon him), who was sitting with his back reclining against al-Bayt al-Ma'mur, which seventy thousand angels enter every day and never return to it again. Then I was taken to Sidrat al-Muntaha (the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary), and its leaves were like the ears of elephants and its fruits were the size of large earthenware jars. When, by the command of Allah, there covered it what covered it, it changed, so that none of Allah's creation is able to describe its beauty. Then Allah revealed to me what He revealed, and He made fifty prayers obligatory upon me in every day and night. Then I descended to Musa (peace be upon him), and he asked: 'What has your Lord made obligatory upon your Ummah?' I said: 'Fifty prayers.' He said: 'Go back to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction, for your Ummah will not be able to bear that; I have tested the Children of Israel and have experience of them.' So I went back to my Lord and said: 'O my Lord, lighten it for my Ummah,' and He reduced five prayers for me. Then I came back to Musa (peace be upon him) and said: 'Five prayers have been reduced for me.' He said: 'Your Ummah will not be able to bear even that, so go back to your Lord and ask Him for a reduction.' So I kept going back and forth between my Lord and Musa (peace be upon him) until Allah Almighty said: 'O Muhammad, they are five prayers in every day and night, each prayer counting as ten, so that makes fifty prayers. Whoever intends a good deed but is unable to do it, one good deed is recorded for him, and if he does it, ten good deeds are recorded for him; and whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, nothing is recorded, and if he does it, one evil deed is recorded.' Then I descended until I reached Musa (peace be upon him) and informed him, and he said: 'Go back to your Lord again and ask Him for a reduction.' I said: 'I have gone back to my Lord so many times that I now feel shy before Him.'"""
"128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Buraq was brought to me, and it was a tall white animal which would place its hoof as far as its sight reached. Jibril and I did not leave its back until I reached Bayt al-Maqdis; then the gates of the heaven were opened for me, and I saw Paradise and Hell."""
"129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night of the Mi'raj I passed by a people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire; every time they were cut, they became whole again as before. I asked: 'O Jibril, who are these people?' He said: 'These are the preachers (orators) of your Ummah who used to say what they themselves did not do, and who used to recite the Book of Allah but did not act upon it.'"""
"130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night of the Mi'raj (angels) came to me and took me to the water of Zamzam; then my chest was opened, then it was washed with the water of Zamzam, and then it was put back in its place and closed."""
"131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Uhud! Be firm (that is, be still), for upon you at this moment are a Prophet, a Siddiq, and two martyrs."""
"132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Hira! Be still, for upon you is a Prophet, or a Siddiq, or a martyr."""
"133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The heaviest prayers upon the hypocrites are the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer; and if they knew how much reward lies in these two (prayers), they would certainly come to them, even if they had to come crawling on their knees. And indeed I resolved to order that the prayer be established, then to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then to take with me some men carrying bundles of firewood, go to those people who do not attend the prayer, and burn their houses down upon them with fire."""
"134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(On the Day of Resurrection) the heaviest thing in the Scale (Mizan) will be good character."""
"135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The heaviest thing in the scale of the believer will be good character. Indeed, Allah Almighty intensely dislikes the one who is shameless, foul-mouthed and given to obscene speech."""
"136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two people whose prayer does not rise above their heads (that is, it is not accepted): a slave who has run away from his masters until he returns, and a woman who has disobeyed her husband until she desists (from that conduct)."""
"137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two sins whose punishment Allah Almighty hastens in this very world: transgression and oppression, and disobedience to parents."""
"138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two traits among people which amount to disbelief in them: attacking someone's lineage and wailing (lamenting) over the dead."""
"139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two things that the son of Adam dislikes: he dislikes death, although death is better for him than trial (fitnah); and he dislikes having little wealth, although having little wealth makes the reckoning easier."""
"140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two things admit one into Paradise: whoever guards what is between his two jaws (that is, the tongue) and what is between his two legs (that is, the private parts) has entered Paradise."""
"141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""During the time of Jahiliyyah, eleven women gathered together and made a pact among themselves that they would speak truthfully and would not conceal anything about the state of their husbands. The first said: 'My husband is like the meat of a lean camel placed on the top of a mountain; the path is not easy so that it may be climbed, nor is the meat fat so that it may be carried off (with ease).' The second said: 'I cannot describe my husband's condition, for I fear that if I mention him, I will disclose all his faults, open and hidden.' The third said: 'My husband is very tall; if I speak, he will divorce me, and if I remain silent, he will keep me hanging.' The fourth said: 'My husband, when he eats, gathers up everything; when he drinks, he empties the vessel; and when he sleeps, he wraps himself up alone in a cloth and does not put his hand in to know my distress.' The fifth said: 'My husband is foolish and feeble-minded; every illness in the world is found in him; he will split your head, or break your bone, or do both.' The sixth said: 'My husband is like the night of Tihamah, neither excessively hot nor cold; there is neither fear of him nor weariness with him.' The seventh said: 'My husband, when he comes into the house, is like a cheetah, and when he goes out, he is like a lion, and he does not even ask about what he has left in the house.' The eighth said: 'My husband's touch is soft like a rabbit's, and his fragrance is like that of zarnab (a fragrant plant); I prevail over him, and he prevails over people.' The ninth said: 'My husband is a man of lofty pillars, of a long sword-belt (brave), of abundant ashes (generous), and his house is right next to the place of assembly.' The tenth said: 'My husband's name is Malik, and what is Malik? Malik is far better than anything I could describe. He has few camels out at pasture and many kneeling at home; when those camels hear the sound of the lutes, they become certain that the time of their ruin (that is, of being slaughtered for guests) has come.' The eleventh said: 'My husband's name is Abu Zar', and what is Abu Zar'? He loaded my ears with jewellery and filled my arms with fat (that is, he fed me until I grew plump); he gave me so much joy that I myself began to take pride in myself. He found me among the owners of a few goats living in a ravine, then he brought me among people who had the neighing of horses, the groaning of camels, threshing and clean grain. Whatever I said to him, I was not rebuked; when I slept, I slept late into the morning; and when I drank, I drank until fully quenched. The mother of Abu Zar' (my mother-in-law), what of her? Her large vessels were full and her house was very spacious. The son of Abu Zar', what of him? His sleeping place was as slender as the sheath of a drawn sword, and the foreleg of a four-month-old kid would satisfy him. The daughter of Abu Zar', what of her? She was obedient to her father and dutiful to her mother, she filled out her clothes, and she was a cause of rage for her co-wife. The slave girl of Abu Zar', what of her? She did not spread our talk among people, she did not waste our provisions, and she did not fill our house with rubbish. One day Abu Zar' went out while the milk was being churned, and he passed by a woman who had two children, like young cheetahs, playing with two pomegranates beneath her waist; so he divorced me and married that woman. After him I married a very noble and brave man who rode a swift horse and held a spear in his hand; he would bring many fine animals to me in the evening and give me a pair of every kind of animal, and he would say: 'Eat, O Umm Zar', and feed your family as well.' Yet if I were to gather together all the things he gave me, they would not fill even the smallest of Abu Zar''s vessels.' (On hearing this) the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyidah Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her): 'O Aishah, I am to you just as Abu Zar' was to Umm Zar', except that Abu Zar' divorced, and I will not divorce.'"""
"142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gather together over your food and mention the name of Allah; blessing will be placed in it for you."""
"143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid anger."""
"144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid the seven destructive sins: associating partners with Allah, practising magic, killing a soul whom Allah has made sacred except by right, consuming usury (riba), consuming the wealth of an orphan, turning one's back and fleeing on the day of battle, and slandering chaste, unaware believing women."""
"145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid the seven major sins: associating partners with Allah, killing unjustly, fleeing from the battlefield, consuming the wealth of an orphan, consuming usury (riba), slandering a chaste woman, and reverting to desert life after the Hijrah (that is, being cut off from the religion and the community and returning to ignorance)."""
"146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid the major sins, stay on the right course (adopt moderation), and accept the glad tidings."""
"147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid every intoxicant."""
"148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid whatever intoxicates."""
"149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Avoid these filthy deeds (indecencies and sins) which Allah Almighty has forbidden. Whoever falls into any of them should keep it concealed with the concealment of Allah and repent to Allah, for whoever exposes his sin before us, we will carry out upon him the punishment according to the Book of Allah."""
"150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave some interval between your adhan and your iqamah, so that the one making ablution may attend to his need at ease and the one eating may finish his food calmly."""
"151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make Witr the last of your prayers at night."""
"152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Place a barrier of the lawful between yourselves and the unlawful. Whoever does that has safeguarded his honour and his religion. And whoever grazes in it (doubtful matters), his example is that of a shepherd who grazes his animals around a protected pasture; they are about to stray into it. Indeed every king has a protected pasture, and indeed Allah's protected pasture on earth is the things He has made unlawful."""
"153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Place a screen between yourselves and the Fire, even if it be with half a date (given in charity)."""
"154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform some of your prayers (the Sunnah and voluntary prayers) in your homes, and do not make them graveyards."""
"155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sit down, for you have harmed people and you have come late."" (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to a man who was stepping over people's necks on Friday.)"
"156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Turab! Sit down."" (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him).)"
"157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be moderate in seeking this world, for everyone is facilitated towards what has been written for him of it."""
"158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Accept the invitation of one who invites you, do not return a gift, and do not strike the Muslims."""
"159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are invited to this invitation (a wedding feast and the like), accept it."""
"160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved religion to Allah Almighty is the Hanifiyyah (the religion of pure devotion to Allah), in which there is gentleness and ease."""
"161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah and Abdur-Rahman."""
"162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah, Abdur-Rahman and Harith."""
"163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved of deeds to Allah is that which is done continually, even if it is little."""
"164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved deed to Allah is performing the prayer at its proper time, then kindness to parents, and then jihad in the path of Allah."""
"165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved deed to Allah is that death comes to you while your tongue is moist with the remembrance of Allah."""
"166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved deeds to Allah are belief in Allah, then maintaining ties of kinship, then enjoining good and forbidding evil. And the most hated deeds to Allah are associating partners with Allah and then severing ties of kinship (breaking family relations)."""
"167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved places in the lands to Allah are their mosques, and the most hated places in the lands to Allah are their markets."""
"168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best jihad in the sight of Allah is a word of truth spoken before a tyrannical ruler."""
"169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved speech to me is the most truthful."""
"170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved fasting to Allah is the fasting of Dawud (peace be upon him); he would fast one day and leave off fasting one day. And the most beloved prayer to Allah is the prayer of Dawud (peace be upon him); he would sleep half the night, stand in prayer for a third of it, and then sleep for a sixth of it."""
"171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved food to Allah is that upon which there are many hands (of those eating)."""
"172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved of servants to Allah Almighty is the one who is most beneficial to His dependents (that is, His creation)."""
"173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved speech to Allah Almighty is four phrases: Subhan Allah (Glory be to Allah), wal-hamdu lillah (and praise be to Allah), wa la ilaha illallah (and there is no god but Allah) and wallahu akbar (and Allah is the Greatest). It will not harm you with which of them you begin your remembrance."""
"174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved speech to Allah Almighty is that the servant says: Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi (Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him)."""
"175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved speech to Allah Almighty is that which Allah Almighty has chosen for His angels: Subhana Rabbi wa bihamdihi, Subhana Rabbi wa bihamdihi, Subhana Rabbi wa bihamdihi (Glory be to my Lord and praise be to Him)."""
"176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved of people to Allah Almighty is the one who is most beneficial to people, and the most beloved deed to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is the joy that you bring into the heart of a Muslim, or that you remove a hardship from him, or pay off a debt for him, or drive away his hunger. And that I walk with my Muslim brother to fulfil some need of his is more beloved to me than that I observe i'tikaf in this mosque for a month. Whoever restrains his anger, Allah will conceal his faults; and whoever swallows his rage when, had he wished to carry it out, he could have done so, Allah will fill his heart with contentment on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever walks with his Muslim brother to fulfil his need until he secures it for him, Allah Almighty will make his feet firm on the Day when feet will slip. And indeed bad character spoils deeds just as vinegar spoils honey."""
"177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved of people to me is Aishah, and among men, her father (Abu Bakr)."""
"178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Love your friend in moderation, for perhaps he may become your enemy one day; and hate your enemy in moderation, for perhaps he may become your friend one day."""
"179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most beloved of Allah's servants to Him are those who are best in character."""
"180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Love for people what you love for yourself."""
"181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Endow its source (the land or tree) and give its fruit in charity in the path of Allah."""
"182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your children in (from going out at the time of Maghrib) until the first darkness of Isha passes, for it is a time in which the devils spread out."""
"183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adam and Musa (peace be upon them both) argued with one another, and Adam (peace be upon him) prevailed over Musa (peace be upon him) (with his argument)."""
"184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Adam and Musa (peace be upon them both) argued with one another. Musa (peace be upon him) said: 'You are Adam, whom Allah Almighty created with His Hand, breathed into you of His spirit, made His angels prostrate to you and settled you in His Paradise; then, because of your sin, you caused people to be expelled from Paradise and brought them into hardship!' Adam (peace be upon him) replied: 'O Musa! You are the one whom Allah Almighty chose for His messages and His speech, and upon whom He sent down the Torah. Do you blame me for a matter which Allah Almighty had written in my decree even before He created me?!' Thus Adam (peace be upon him) prevailed over Musa (peace be upon him)."""
"185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise and the Fire disputed with one another. Paradise said: 'The weak and the poor will enter me.' And the Fire said: 'The tyrants and the arrogant will enter me.' So Allah Almighty said to the Fire: 'You are My punishment; through you I will take retribution from whomever I will.' And He said to Paradise: 'You are My mercy; through you I will show mercy to whomever I will.' And each of you two shall have its fill."""
"186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Throw dust in the faces of those who praise others to their faces."""
"187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Throw dust into the mouths of those who praise others to their faces."""
"188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform Hajj and Umrah on behalf of your father."""
"189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make it one, make it one."" (That is, point with one finger.)"
"190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make it one, O Sa'd!"" (That is, point with one finger.)"
"191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it."""
"192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of this world, for it is green and sweet (alluring)."""
"193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The worst name in the sight of Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection will be that of a man who is called Malik al-Amlak (King of kings)."""
"194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of people in recitation is the one who, when he recites the Qur'an, you feel that he fears Allah."""
"195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Establish the rows properly and straight in the prayer."""
"196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be good to the doers of good among the Ansar, and pardon the wrongdoers among them."""
"197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gather together, for I will recite to you a third of the Qur'an."" Then he recited {Say: He is Allah, the One} [Surah al-Ikhlas: 1] and said: ""Listen! Indeed it is equal to a third of the Qur'an."""
"198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep count of the crescent of Sha'ban for the sake of Ramadan (its fasting)."""
"199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep count of the crescent of Sha'ban for the sake of Ramadan, and do not join (fasts) to Ramadan by fasting a day or two before it, unless that day coincides with a fast which one of you customarily observes. Fast upon sighting it (the crescent) and break the fast (celebrate Eid) upon sighting it. If it is obscured from you by clouds, then complete the count of thirty days, for the count is not hidden from you."""
"200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Attend the Friday prayer and sit close to the imam, for a man keeps on staying back until he is placed behind in Paradise, even if he enters it."""
"201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Attend the Friday prayer and sit close to the imam, for a man keeps staying behind from the Friday prayer until he is even kept behind from Paradise, even though he is one of its people."""
"202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dig the graves, make them deep and spacious, and bury two and three people in a single grave, and place in front (in the niche) the one who knows more of the Qur'an."""
"203","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guard your private parts except from your wife or your slave woman."" It was asked (of him): ""What if people are mixed together with one another?"" He said: ""If you are able to ensure that no one sees them, then let no one see them."" Then it was asked: ""What if one of us is alone in private?"" He said: ""Allah Almighty is more deserving than people that one should feel shy before Him."""
"204","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guard your tongue."""
"205","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guard your tongue. O Mu'adh, may your mother lose you! Is there anything that throws people on their faces other than their tongues?"""
"206","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remember my instruction regarding my Companions, then regarding those who come after them, then regarding those who come after them. Then (after that) lying will become widespread, until a man will give testimony though his testimony was not sought, and will swear an oath though he was not asked to swear."""
"207","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trim the moustaches closely and let the beards grow."""
"208","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Either keep both feet bare or wear shoes on both. When you put on your shoes, begin with the right foot, and when you take them off, begin with the left foot."""
"209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gold and silk have been made lawful for the women of my Ummah and forbidden to its men."""
"210","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Two kinds of dead animals and two kinds of blood have been made lawful for us. As for the two dead animals, they are fish and locusts, and as for the two bloods, they are the liver and the spleen."""
"211","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Swear by Allah, fulfil your oaths and speak the truth, for Allah loves that oaths be sworn by Him."""
"212","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Either shave it (the hair of the head) completely or leave it completely."""
"213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Sometimes the revelation comes to me like the continuous ringing of a bell, and this is the hardest on me; then, when this state leaves me, I have already retained all that he (the angel) said. And sometimes the angel takes the form of a man before me and speaks to me, and I retain what he says."""
"214","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I fear three things for my Ummah after me: the injustice of the rulers, belief in (the influence of) the stars, and denial of divine decree."""
"215","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I fear two traits for my Ummah after me: denial of divine decree and belief in the stars."""
"216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I fear six things for you: the rule of the foolish, bloodshed, the buying and selling of judgement (the office of judge), severing the ties of kinship, a young generation who will take the Qur'an as musical instruments, and a multitude of police (oppressive officials)."""
"217","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of a deed which, if you adopt it, you will catch up with those who went before you and outstrip those who come after you, except someone who does the like of it? After every prayer, say Subhan Allah (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times, Allahu Akbar (Allah is the Greatest) thirty-three times, and Alhamdu lillah (All praise is for Allah) thirty-four times."""
"218","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) informed me that cupping (hijamah) is the most beneficial of all the things with which people treat themselves."""
"219","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) informed me that Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him) will be martyred on the bank of the Euphrates."""
"220","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell me of a tree that resembles the Muslim man: its leaves do not fall, and neither this nor that, and it gives its fruit in every season? It is the date palm."""
"221","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ibrahim (peace be upon him) circumcised himself at the age of eighty with an adze (or at a place called al-Qadum)."""
"222","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Choose four of them (your wives) and part with all the rest."""
"223","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Zayd took the banner and was martyred, then Ja'far took it and was martyred, then Abdullah bin Rawahah took it and he too was martyred. Then Khalid took it on his own without being appointed, and Allah granted victory at his hands. And it would not please me that they were with us"" - or he said - ""and it would not please them that they were with us."""
"224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, took a covenant from me just as He took their covenant from all the prophets, and Isa ibn Maryam gave glad tidings of me, and my mother saw in her dream that a lamp came out from between her legs by which the palaces of Syria were lit up."""
"225","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We have taken your good omen from your own mouth (from your own words)."""
"226","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Speaking (debating and arguing) about divine decree has been deferred to the worst people of my Ummah at the end of time."""
"227","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umar, step back from me! I was given a choice, so I chose. It has been said to me: 'Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them; even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them.' [Surah at-Tawbah: 80] If I knew that he would be forgiven if I asked forgiveness more than seventy times, I would ask forgiveness even more than that."""
"228","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep the loads at the back, for the hands are tied and the feet are fettered."""
"229","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go out and announce among the people: whoever testifies to La ilaha illallah (there is no true god except Allah), Paradise has become obligatory for him."""
"230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Expel the effeminate men (men who adopt the manner and appearance of women) from your houses."""
"231","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula, and honour the delegations with gifts and rewards in the same way that I used to honour them."""
"232","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula."""
"233","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Expel the Jews of the Hijaz and the people of Najran from the Arabian Peninsula, and know that the worst of people are those who took the graves of their prophets as places of prostration."""
"234","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go out to him, for he does not know the proper way of asking permission. Tell him to say it like this: As-salamu alaykum (peace be upon you), may I come in?"""
"235","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go out and cut the fruit of your date palms; perhaps you will give some of it in charity or do some other good deed."""
"236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(When circumcising women,) cut a little and do not cut from the root (do not overdo it), for this brings more radiance to the face and is more pleasing to the husband."""
"237","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most humiliating and disgraceful name in the sight of Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection will be that of a man who called himself Malik al-Amlak (King of Kings), whereas there is no true king except Allah."""
"238","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your servants are your brothers; Allah Almighty has made them your property and placed them under your authority. So whoever has his brother under his authority, let him feed him from what he himself eats, clothe him from what he himself wears, and not burden them with work beyond their strength; and if he does burden them with more than their strength, then let him help them (in that work)."""
"239","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What I fear most for my Ummah is every hypocrite who is highly skilled with his tongue (smooth-talking)."""
"240","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Return the trust to the one who entrusted it to you, considering you trustworthy, and do not betray the one who has betrayed you."""
"241","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On behalf of every free person and slave, young and old, pay (as Sadaqat al-Fitr) one sa' of wheat between two people (that is, half a sa' per person), or one sa' of dates, or one sa' of barley."""
"242","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the occasion of Eid al-Fitr, pay one sa' of food grain (as Sadaqat al-Fitr)."""
"243","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty admitted into Paradise a man who was gentle and generous when buying, when selling, when judging and when asking for his due."""
"244","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Call upon your Lord who, if some harm touches you and you call upon Him, will remove it from you; and if you lose your way in a desolate, barren land and you call upon Him, will return you to your destination; and if a year of drought befalls you and you call upon Him, will cause grain and vegetation to grow for you."""
"245","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Supplicate to Allah Almighty while being fully certain of a response, and know that Allah Almighty does not answer a supplication that comes from a heedless and careless heart."""
"246","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Invite people (to the religion), give glad tidings and do not drive them away; make things easy for them and do not make things difficult."""
"247","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Call your father Abu Bakr and your brother so that I may write a document, for I fear that someone may wish (for it) and someone may say: 'I am more entitled (to the caliphate),' whereas Allah Almighty and the believers refuse to accept anyone other than Abu Bakr."""
"248","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hand her (the girl) over to her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt holds the position of a mother."""
"249","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Bury the martyrs in the very places where they were martyred."""
"250","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Bring the orphan close to you, treat him with kindness, pass your hand over his head and feed him from your food, for this will surely soften your heart and be a means of fulfilling your need."""
"251","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O my son, come closer, mention the name of Allah (say Bismillah), eat with your right hand and eat from what is in front of you."""
"252","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The person with the lightest punishment among the people of Hell will be the one who is made to wear two sandals of fire, from whose heat his brain will boil."""
"253","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform Hajj and Umrah one after the other, for they both remove poverty and sins just as the furnace removes the rust and dross of iron."""
"254","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty grants you wealth, then the effect of Allah's blessing and His favour and generosity should be visible on you."""
"255","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty grants you wealth, its effect should be visible on you, for Allah Almighty loves that the good effect of the blessing He has given be seen on His servant, and He dislikes wretchedness and deliberately making oneself appear wretched."""
"256","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty grants you some wealth which you did not ask for and which your heart did not covet, then accept it, for it is only provision that Allah Almighty has sent your way."""
"257","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you buy food grain, do not sell it on until you have taken full possession of it."""
"258","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty afflicts a Muslim servant with an illness in his body, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says (to the angels): 'Keep recording for him the good deeds (he used to do while healthy).' Then, if Allah cures him, He washes him clean of sins and purifies him, and if He takes his soul, He forgives him and has mercy on him."""
"259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you send a messenger to me, send someone who has a handsome face and a good name."""
"260","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a slave runs away (from his master), none of his prayers is accepted."""
"261","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you comes to the prayer and the imam is in whatever position, he should do just as the imam is doing."""
"262","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you goes to relieve himself, he should neither face the qiblah nor turn his back towards it; rather, he should face east or west."""
"263","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you comes to his wife (has intercourse) and then intends to do so again, he should perform ablution."""
"264","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the servant of any of you brings him his food, having already borne the toil of cooking it and the discomfort of its smoke, he should seat him with himself; and if he cannot seat him with himself, he should at least give him a morsel or two of it."""
"265","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you comes to a herd of livestock, if their owner is present there, he should ask his permission; if he gives him permission, he may milk and drink. And if no one is present there, he should call out three times; then if anyone answers, he should ask his permission, and if no one answers, he may milk and drink, but he should not carry any away with him."""
"266","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man comes to a people and they say 'welcome' to him, there will be a welcome for him too on the Day of Resurrection, when he meets his Lord. And if a man comes to a people and they say words of rebuke and rejection to him, then on the Day of Resurrection there will be rejection and rebuke for him too."""
"267","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a beggar comes to you, be sure to put something in his hand, even if it is only a burnt hoof."""
"268","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the zakah collector comes to you, (let it be that) he returns from you in a state of being pleased with you."""
"269","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the honoured man of a people comes to you, show him honour and respect."""
"270","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When someone whose character and religious commitment satisfy you comes to you (asking for a marriage proposal), marry (your daughters) to him. If you do not do so, there will be great tribulation in the land and widespread corruption."""
"271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the garment is wide, wrap it around your shoulders and then pray; and if it is too narrow for that, tie it around your waist and pray without an upper wrap."""
"272","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you come to the prayer, come with dignity and tranquillity; then pray whatever (of the prayer with the imam) you catch, and make up (afterwards) whatever you have missed."""
"273","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you come to your wife (for intercourse), act with wisdom (and refinement)."""
"274","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you pass by a camel herder, call out three times: 'O camel herder!' If he answers you (then ask his permission); otherwise, milk and drink, but do not spoil (it). And when you come to an orchard, call out three times: 'O owner of the orchard!' If he answers you (then well and good); otherwise, eat, but do not cause any damage."""
"275","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you come to the prayer, you must keep to calmness and tranquillity, and do not come running. Then pray whatever rak'ahs you catch, and complete whatever you have missed."""
"276","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you come to your bed, perform ablution as you do for prayer, then lie down on your right side, then say this supplication: 'Allahumma aslamtu wajhi ilayka, wa fawwadtu amri ilayka, wa alja'tu zahri ilayka, raghbatan wa rahbatan ilayka, la malja'a wa la manja minka illa ilayka, amantu bi-kitabika alladhi anzalta wa bi-nabiyyika alladhi arsalta' (O Allah, I have submitted my face to You, entrusted my affair to You and placed my back under Your protection, out of hope for Your mercy and fear of Your punishment. There is no place of refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You revealed and in Your Prophet whom You sent). Then if you die that very night, you will die upon the natural religion (Islam). And make these words the last thing you say."""
"277","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When your neighbours praise you, saying that you are a doer of good, then you truly are a doer of good; and when your neighbours say of you that you are a wrongdoer, then you certainly are a wrongdoer."""
"278","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you perfume the deceased with incense, do so three times."""
"279","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you loves his (Muslim) brother, he should tell him that he loves him."""
"280","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you loves one of his brothers for the sake of Allah, he should tell him, for it is something that better preserves mutual affection and more firmly strengthens love."""
"281","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you loves his friend, he should go to his house and tell him that he loves him for the sake of Allah."""
"282","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty loves a servant, He protects him from the world (its trials and evils) just as one of you protects his sick person from (harmful) water."""
"283","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty loves a servant, He calls Jibril (peace be upon him): 'Allah loves so-and-so, so you love him too.' So Jibril also comes to love him. Then Jibril calls out among the inhabitants of the heaven: 'Allah Almighty loves so-and-so, so you love him too.' So the inhabitants of the heaven also come to love him, and then acceptance is placed for him among the people of the earth."""
"284","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty loves a servant, He calls Jibril (peace be upon him) and says: 'I have loved so-and-so, so you love him too.' So he calls out in the heaven, and then love for him is sent down on the earth. This is the meaning of the saying of Allah Almighty: 'Indeed, those who believe and do righteous deeds, the Most Merciful will appoint for them affection (in hearts).' [Surah Maryam: 96] And when Allah Almighty hates a servant, He calls Jibril and says: 'I hate so-and-so.' So he calls out in the heaven, and then hatred and aversion for him are sent down on the earth."""
"285","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty loves a people, He puts them to trial."""
"286","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the ablution of any of you breaks during his prayer, he should hold his nose and then leave (the prayer to perform ablution)."""
"287","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you makes his Islam excellent, then every good deed he does is recorded for him multiplied from ten times its like up to seven hundred times, and every bad deed he does is recorded for him only as its equal, until he meets Allah."""
"288","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the seller and the buyer fall into disagreement, the seller's word will be accepted, and the buyer will have the option (to uphold or cancel the sale)."""
"289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the buyer and the seller fall into disagreement and neither of them has any witness, the decision will be what the owner of the goods says, or else the two of them abandon the sale."""
"290","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the buyer and the seller fall into disagreement, there is no witness between them, and the item sold is still present in its original state, then the word will be what the seller said, or else the two of them abandon the transaction (sale)."""
"291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you disagree about (the width of) a road, fix it at seven cubits."""
"292","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you go to your bed at night, recite 'Say: O disbelievers' [Surah al-Kafirun: 1], then go to sleep upon completing it, for it is a declaration of freedom from shirk."""
"293","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you puts his feet into his leather socks while they are in a state of purity, he may wipe over them; for the traveller the period is three days, and for the resident one day (and night)."""
"294","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you catches one prostration (that is, one rak'ah) of the Asr prayer before the sun sets, he should complete his prayer; and if he catches one prostration of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, he should complete his prayer."""
"295","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a slave fulfils the right of Allah and the right of his masters, he will have a double reward."""
"296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Ibn Umm Maktum gives the adhan, eat and drink; and when Bilal gives the adhan, do not eat or drink."""
"297","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the muezzin has given the adhan, no one should leave (the mosque) until he has prayed."""
"298","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you give the adhan for Maghrib, give it quickly, right with (the setting of) the sun."""
"299","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you wishes to go to relieve himself and the prayer has been started, he should first go to relieve himself."""
"300","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you wishes to marry off his daughter, he should seek her permission."""
"301","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you wishes to fulfil his need with his wife, let him come to her, even if she is at the oven (baking bread)."""
"302","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for a ruler, He appoints for him a truthful minister: if the ruler forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him. And when Allah intends otherwise for him, He appoints for him an evil minister: if he forgets, he does not remind him, and if he remembers, he does not help him."""
"303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for the people of a household, He brings gentleness and kindness into them."""
"304","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for a servant, He puts him to work."" (The Companions) asked: ""What does He put him to work at?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He opens for him the door to a righteous deed before his death, until the people around him become pleased with him."""
"305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When (Allah Almighty) intends good for a servant, He puts him to work."" (The Companions) asked: ""How does He put him to work?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He grants him the ability to do a righteous deed before death, and then takes his soul in that (state of doing good)."""
"306","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for a servant, He purifies him before he dies."" The Companions said: ""What is meant by the purification of the servant?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is a righteous deed which Allah inspires in him (grants him the ability to do), until He takes his soul in that very state."""
"307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for a servant, He makes him sweet like honey."" (The Companions) asked: ""What does his being made sweet like honey mean?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He opens for him the door to a righteous deed before his death, then takes his soul in that state."""
"308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends good for His servant, He hastens his punishment for him in this world; and when He intends evil for His servant, He withholds the punishment of his sin from him until He repays him for it in full on the Day of Resurrection."""
"309","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends punishment for a people, the punishment engulfs everyone who is among them; then (on the Day of Resurrection) they will be raised according to their own deeds."""
"310","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends to create something, nothing can prevent Him."""
"311","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends to take the soul of a servant in a (particular) land, He creates some need for him there."""
"312","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you want to spit, do not spit to your right, but spit to your left if that space is empty; and if that space is not empty, then spit under your foot."""
"313","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you release your trained hunting dogs and mention the name of Allah (upon releasing them), then eat what they catch and hold for you, even if they kill it, except if the dog eats some of it, for I fear that it caught it only for itself. And if other dogs join your dogs, then do not eat, for you do not know which dog killed it. And if you shoot an arrow at game and find it after a day or two with no mark on it except that of your arrow, then eat it; and if it falls into water, then do not eat it."""
"314","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you release your trained dog and it kills (the game), then eat it; and if it eats some of it, then do not eat, for it has then caught it for itself. And if you find another dog with it, then do not eat, for you pronounced (the name of Allah) over your own dog and not over any other dog."""
"315","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you release your trained hunting dog and remember Allah and mention His name, then eat what your trained dog catches and holds for you, even if it kills it. And if you release your dog that is not trained and you find (the game) alive and slaughter it, then eat it. And eat what your arrow brings you, even if it kills it, provided that you have mentioned the name of Allah (when shooting)."""
"316","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you release your hunting dog, mention the name of Allah. If it catches and holds (the game) for you and you find it alive, then slaughter it; and if you find that it has killed it and not eaten any of it, then eat it. And if you find another dog with your dog and it has killed the game, then do not eat, for you do not know which of them killed it. And when you shoot your arrow, mention the name of Allah; then if (the game) is lost to you for a day and you find no mark on it except that of your arrow, eat it if you wish. And if you find it drowned in water, then do not eat, for you do not know whether the water killed it or your arrow."""
"317","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you commit an evil deed, then follow it with a good deed."""
"318","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you asks permission three times and is not given permission, let him go back."""
"319","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the wife of one of you asks his permission to go to the mosque, let him not prevent her."""
"320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When permission is sought from a man while he is praying, his granting of permission is to say Subhan Allah, and when permission is sought from a woman while she is praying, her granting of permission is to clap."""
"321","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you cleans himself with stones (after relieving himself), let him use an odd number (i.e. one, three, five) of stones."""
"322","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you purifies himself (after relieving himself), let him not purify himself with his right hand; rather, he should clean himself with his left hand."""
"323","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman puts on perfume and then passes by people so that they may smell her fragrance, she is (in a sense) an adulteress."""
"324","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you face the qiblah, say the takbir, then recite Surah al-Fatihah (Umm al-Qur'an), then recite whatever you wish. Then when you bow, place your palms on your knees, stretch your back out straight and perform your bowing with composure. Then when you raise your head, stand your back fully upright until all the bones return to their joints. Then when you prostrate, perform your prostration with composure. Then when you sit, sit on your left thigh. Then do the same in every rak'ah and every prostration."""
"325","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you persists in his oath (and does not break it, even though breaking it would be better), this act of his is a greater cause of sin in the sight of Allah than the expiation he has been commanded to give."""
"326","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you lies flat on his back, let him not place one foot on the other."""
"327","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you draw water into your nose, blow it out; and when you clean yourself with stones, use an odd number."""
"328","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a newborn child cries (i.e. is born alive), he becomes an heir."""
"329","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you wakes from sleep, let him say: Al-hamdu lillahil-ladhi radda 'alayya ruhi wa 'afani fi jasadi wa adhina li bi-dhikrih (All praise is for Allah, who returned my soul to me, granted me well-being in my body and permitted me to remember Him)."""
"330","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you wakes from his sleep and performs ablution (wudu), let him blow out his nose three times, for Satan spends the night in the upper part of his nose (the upper part of the nostrils)."""
"331","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it."""
"332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it three times, for none of you knows where his hand spent the night."""
"333","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man wakes up at night and also wakes his wife, and they both pray two rak'ahs, they are recorded among the men and women who remember Allah abundantly."""
"334","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you wake up (from sleep), pray."""
"335","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man accepts Islam, he has the greatest right to his land and his wealth."""
"336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant accepts Islam and his Islam becomes excellent, Allah Almighty records for him every good deed he did before (in the state of disbelief), and every sin he committed before is erased from him. Then after that, the recompense (for good and bad deeds) is such that a good deed is rewarded with ten like it up to seven hundred times, and an evil deed is recompensed only with its equal, unless Allah Almighty overlooks it."""
"337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant accepts Islam and his Islam becomes excellent, Allah Almighty erases from him every sin he committed before, and after that the recompense is such that a good deed is rewarded with ten like it up to seven hundred times, and an evil deed is recompensed with its equal, unless Allah Almighty overlooks it."""
"338","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man points a weapon at his (Muslim) brother, they are both on the brink of Hell; then if he kills him, they both fall into it (Hell) together."""
"339","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the heat becomes intense, delay the prayer until it is cooler (i.e. pray it later), for the intensity of the heat is from the vapour of Hell."""
"340","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the heat becomes intense, delay the Zuhr prayer until it is cooler (pray it later), for the intensity of the heat is from the vapour of Hell."""
"341","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you buys a slave girl, let him say: Allahumma inni as'aluka khayraha wa khayra ma jabaltaha 'alayhi, wa a'udhu bika min sharriha wa sharri ma jabaltaha 'alayhi (O Allah, I ask You for her good and the good of the disposition upon which You have created her, and I seek refuge in You from her evil and the evil of the disposition upon which You have created her), and he should pray for blessing. And when one of you buys a camel, let him take hold of the top of its hump, pray for blessing and say similar words."""
"342","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you buy something, do not sell it on until you have taken possession of it."""
"343","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim servant falls ill, Allah Almighty says to the angels who record deeds: 'Keep writing for him the best of the deeds he used to do when he was in good health, until I cure him (of this illness).'"""
"344","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the believer falls ill, (that illness) purifies him of sins just as the furnace removes the rust of iron and purifies it."""
"345","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the eyes of a person in the state of ihram become sore, let him apply a poultice of aloe (a herb called sabir) to them."""
"346","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you feel any pain, place your hand where you feel the pain, then say: Bismillah, a'udhu bi-'izzatillahi wa qudratihi min sharri ma ajidu min waja'i hadha (In the name of Allah, I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of the affliction I feel and of this pain of mine). Then lift your hand, and then repeat it an odd number of times (three, five or seven times)."""
"347","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a calamity befalls one of you, let him remember the calamity of (losing) me, for it is among the greatest of calamities (for the Ummah)."""
"348","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When grief or hardship and distress befalls one of you, let him say: Allahu Allahu rabbi la ushriku bihi shay'a (Allah, Allah is my Lord; I do not associate anything with Him)."""
"349","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a mukatab (a slave who has made a contract to pay a price for his freedom) becomes liable to a hadd (prescribed punishment) or receives an inheritance, he shall be given inheritance in proportion to the extent he has been freed, and the hadd shall be applied to him in proportion to the part of him that has been freed."""
"350","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the blood of menstruation gets on the garment of any of you women, she should scrape it off (with her fingers), then pour water over it, and then pray in that same garment."""
"351","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the son of Adam wakes up in the morning, all the limbs of his body humble themselves before the tongue and say: 'Fear Allah concerning us, for our existence is bound up with you. If you stay straight, we will stay straight, and if you become crooked, we will become crooked.'"""
"352","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you wakes up in the morning, he should say: 'Asbahna wa asbaha al-mulku lillahi rabbi al-'alamin. Allahumma inni as'aluka khayra hadha al-yawm, fathahu wa nasrahu wa nurahu wa barakatahu wa hudahu, wa a'udhu bika min sharri ma fihi wa sharri ma qablahu wa sharri ma ba'dahu' (We have entered the morning, and the dominion of Allah, the Lord of all the worlds, has entered the morning. O Allah, I ask You for the good of this day: its victory, its help, its light, its blessing and its guidance; and I seek refuge in You from the evil that is in it, the evil that is before it and the evil that is after it). Then when he reaches the evening, he should say similar words."""
"353","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you wakes up in the morning, he should say: 'Allahumma bika asbahna wa bika amsayna wa bika nahya wa bika namutu wa ilayka al-masir' (O Allah, by Your enabling we have reached the morning and by Your enabling we have reached the evening; by Your command we live and by Your command we die, and to You is the return). And when he reaches the evening, he should say: 'Allahumma bika amsayna wa bika asbahna wa bika nahya wa bika namutu wa ilayka al-nushur' (O Allah, by Your enabling we have reached the evening and by Your enabling we have reached the morning; by Your command we live and by Your command we die, and to You is the resurrection)."""
"354","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you wake up in the morning, say: 'Allahumma bika asbahna wa bika amsayna wa bika nahya wa bika namutu wa ilayka al-masir' (O Allah, by Your enabling we have reached the morning and by Your enabling we have reached the evening; by Your command we live and by Your command we die, and to You is the return)."""
"355","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two Muslim men are walking together and a tree, a stone or a clod of earth comes between them (and they separate and then meet again), then one of them should greet the other with salam, and they should exchange greetings of salam with each other."""
"356","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you has been away from home for a long time, he should not come to his family unexpectedly at night."""
"357","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man gives another man safety and security, and then kills him after having reassured him, a banner of treachery will be raised for him (the killer) on the Day of Resurrection."""
"358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty grants any of you good and plenty, he should begin (his spending) with himself and his household."""
"359","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are given something without having asked for it, eat from it and give (the remainder) in charity."""
"360","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you acquires a woman (as a wife), a servant or a riding animal, he should take hold of her forelock, pray for blessing, and say: 'Allahumma inni as'aluka min khayriha wa khayri ma jubilat 'alayhi, wa a'udhu bika min sharriha wa sharri ma jubilat 'alayhi' (O Allah, I ask You for her good and the good of the nature upon which she has been created, and I seek refuge in You from her evil and the evil of the nature upon which she has been created). And if it is a camel, he should take hold of the top of its hump."""
"361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you extends his hand to his private part (and touches it), he should perform ablution."""
"362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you extends his hand to his private part, with no covering or cloth between his hand and it, then ablution has certainly become obligatory upon him."""
"363","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you breaks his fast, let him break it with a date, for it is pure blessing. If he cannot find a date, let him break it with water, for water is a means of purification."""
"364","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the night approaches from this side (the east), the day departs from this side (the west), and the sun has set, then it is time for the fasting person to break his fast."""
"365","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When time draws near (that is, when the Hour is near), the dream of a Muslim man will hardly ever be false, and the truest in dreams among you will be the one who is most truthful in speech."""
"366","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the believer is made to sit up in his grave and (the angels) come to him, he bears witness that there is no true god except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. That is the meaning of the saying of Allah Almighty: 'Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word.' [Surah Ibrahim: 27]"""
"367","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is started, perform the circuit (tawaf of the Ka'bah) riding on your camel behind the people."""
"368","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is started, say the takbir (Allahu Akbar), then recite whatever is easy for you of the Qur'an, then bow until you are at rest in bowing, then rise until you are standing straight, then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration, then rise until you are at rest sitting, then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration, and then do this throughout your whole prayer."""
"369","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is started, do not come to it running, but come to it walking, and upon you is dignity and calmness. Whatever (of the prayer with the imam) you catch, pray it, and whatever you miss, complete it (afterwards)."""
"370","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is called (iqamah), do not stand up until you see me (coming out of my room)."""
"371","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the (obligatory) prayer is started, there is no prayer (to be offered) except the obligatory prayer."""
"372","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is started and one of you is fasting, he should begin with the evening meal (iftar) before the Maghrib prayer, and do not hurry away from your evening meal."""
"373","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is started and a man needs to relieve himself, he should first go to relieve himself."""
"374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is started and the evening meal is served, first eat the evening meal."""
"375","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you applies kohl, he should apply it an odd number of times, and when he cleans himself with stones (after relieving himself), he should use an odd number."""
"376","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When they (the enemy) come close to you, shoot arrows at them, and save some of your arrows (for the final moment)."""
"377","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man declares his (Muslim) brother a disbeliever, then one of the two will certainly return with it (disbelief)."""
"378","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is eating food and his morsel falls, he should remove whatever dirt has got on it and then eat it, and not leave it for Satan."""
"379","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats food, he should not wipe his hand with a napkin until he has licked it himself or had it licked (by someone else)."""
"380","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats food, he should mention the name of Allah. If he forgets to mention the name of Allah at the beginning, he should say: 'Bismillahi 'ala awwalihi wa akhirihi' (In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end)."""
"381","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats food, he should say: 'Allahumma barik lana fihi wa abdilna khayran minhu' (O Allah, bless it for us and grant us in exchange something better than it). And when he drinks milk, he should say: 'Allahumma barik lana fihi wa zidna minhu' (O Allah, bless it for us and give us more of it), for nothing other than milk can fulfil the need for both food and drink."""
"382","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats food, he should lick his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies."""
"383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats, he should eat with his right hand, and when he drinks, he should drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."""
"384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats, he should eat with his right hand, drink with his right hand, take with his right hand and give with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand, drinks with his left hand, takes with his left hand and gives with his left hand."""
"385","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the two circumcised parts meet, the ritual bath (ghusl) becomes obligatory."""
"386","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the two circumcised parts meet and the glans (the head of the male organ) disappears, the ritual bath (ghusl) becomes obligatory, whether or not there is ejaculation."""
"387","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two Muslims face each other with their swords and one of them kills the other, then both the killer and the one killed will be in Hell. It was asked: 'O Messenger of Allah, this outcome is fitting for the killer, but what is the fault of the one killed?' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'He too was eager to kill his companion.'"""
"388","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two Muslims meet and one of them raises a weapon against his brother, they are both on the brink of Hell. Then if one of them kills the other, they both enter it."""
"389","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty puts into a man's heart the intention to propose marriage to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her."""
"390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When pre-seminal fluid (madhi) comes out of any of you and he has not touched (a woman), he should wash his private part and his two testicles, then perform ablution and pray."""
"391","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you leads the people in prayer, he should keep it light (short), for among them (those following) are the young and the old, the weak, the sick and those with needs. And when he prays by himself, he may lengthen it as much as he wishes."""
"392","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man leads the people in prayer, he should not stand in a place higher than their (the followers') place."""
"393","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you lead the people in prayer, recite (in the prayer) 'By the sun and its brightness' [Surah al-Shams: 1], 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' [Surah al-A'la: 1] and 'By the night when it covers' [Surah al-Layl: 1]."""
"394","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you lead a people in prayer, keep the prayer light (short) for them."""
"395","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the imam says Amin, you too say Amin, for whoever's Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels, his past sins are forgiven."""
"396","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the reciter (the imam) says Amin, you too say Amin, for the angels also say Amin. So whoever's Amin coincides with the Amin of the angels, his past sins are forgiven."""
"397","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When half of the month of Sha'ban has passed, do not fast until Ramadan comes."""
"398","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you puts on his shoes, he should begin with the right foot, and when he takes them off, he should begin with the left foot, so that the right foot is the first to be shod and the last to be unshod."""
"399","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you arrives at a gathering, if room is made for him, he should sit down; otherwise he should look for the most spacious place he can see and sit there."""
"400","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you arrives at a gathering, let him give the greeting of peace (salam). Then, if he wishes to sit there, let him sit. Then, when he gets up to leave, let him give the greeting (again), for the first greeting is not more deserving (or more important) than the second."""
"401","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty sends down a punishment upon a people, that punishment engulfs all those who are present among them; then (on the Day of Resurrection) they will be raised up each according to his own deeds."""
"402","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man spends on his family with the intention of earning reward, it is counted as charity for him."""
"403","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman spends from her husband's house without his instruction (that is, some ordinary charity in line with the usual custom), she too has half of his (the husband's) reward."""
"404","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman spends from her husband's house without causing ruin (that is, with moderation), she has a reward for what she spent, her husband has a reward for what he earned, and the storekeeper (the one in charge) has the like of that as well; and none of them diminishes anything from the reward of the other."""
"405","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in one sandal until he has mended his strap; and let him not walk in one leather sock (khuff), nor eat with his left hand, nor sit with his knees drawn up wrapped in a single garment (ihtiba'), nor wrap himself in the manner of as-samma' (a garment wrapped so that there is no opening for the hands to come out)."""
"406","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the strap of the sandal of one of you breaks, let him not walk in the other (single sandal) until he has mended it."""
"407","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you goes to his bed, let him dust it off with the inner edge of his lower garment (izar), for he does not know what may have come onto it (the bed) after he left it. Then let him lie on his right side and recite this supplication: Bismika rabbi wada'tu janbi wa bika arfa'uhu, in amsakta nafsi farhamha, wa in arsaltaha fahfazha bima tahfazu bihi 'ibadaka as-salihin (O my Lord, in Your name I have laid down my side, and by Your name I shall raise it up. If You take my soul, then have mercy on it, and if You release it, then protect it as You protect Your righteous servants)."""
"408","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman spends the night having deserted her husband's bed (in anger), the angels keep cursing her until morning."""
"409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sells a goat or a milch she-camel, let him not (with the aim of deceiving) keep the milk held back in its udders."""
"410","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you urinates, let him not touch his private part with his right hand; when he goes to the toilet, let him not clean himself (istinja') with his right hand; and when he drinks (something), let him not breathe into the vessel."""
"411","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you buy and sell, say: 'There must be no deception (with me).'"""
"412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the edge of the sun begins to rise, delay the prayer until it has fully appeared; and when the edge of the sun begins to set, delay the prayer until it has fully set."""
"413","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you send a man to me (as an envoy), send one with a handsome face and a good name."""
"414","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man of my Ummah reaches the age of sixty years, Allah Almighty has left him no excuse in the matter of his lifespan."""
"415","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty lets a servant reach the age of sixty years, He has left him no excuse and has given him ample respite in his lifespan."""
"416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When water reaches the quantity of two qullahs (a specific measure), it does not take on the effect of impurity."""
"417","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When water reaches the quantity of two qullahs, nothing can make it impure."""
"418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When your children reach seven years of age, separate their beds; and when they reach ten years of age, beat them over (not performing) the prayer."""
"419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Banu Abi al-As reach thirty men in number, they will take the servants of Allah as their slaves, the wealth of Allah as their personal estate (circulating only among the rich), and the Book of Allah as a means of deception and fraud."""
"420","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you reach Hayya 'ala al-falah (in the Fajr call to prayer), then (after it) say: As-salatu khayrun min an-nawm (Prayer is better than sleep)."""
"421","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the pledge of allegiance is given to two caliphs (at the same time), kill the latter (the second) of the two."""
"422","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two men engage in a sale with each other, each of them has the option (to cancel the deal) as long as they have not separated and are together, or one of them gives the other the option. If one gives the other the option and they conclude the sale on that basis, the sale becomes binding. And if they separate after having concluded the sale and neither of them has abandoned the sale, the sale also becomes binding."""
"423","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you deal in 'inah transactions (a form of usury), take hold of the tails of cattle (that is, become absorbed in tending livestock), become content with farming, and abandon jihad, Allah Almighty will impose upon you a humiliation which He will not remove until you return (fully) to your religion."""
"424","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you follow a funeral procession, do not sit until it has been placed (on the ground)."""
"425","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you yawns, let him hold it back as much as he can, for when one of you says 'Ha' (making a sound while yawning), Satan laughs at him."""
"426","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters (into the mouth) with the yawn."""
"427","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you yawns during the prayer, let him suppress it as much as he can, for Satan enters (through the open mouth)."""
"428","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you marries, let this supplication be said to him: Barakallahu laka wa baraka 'alayka (May Allah bless you and send down blessing upon you)."""
"429","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man marries a virgin while he already has a previously married woman (as wife), he should stay with her (the virgin) for seven days; and when he marries a previously married woman while he has a virgin (as wife), he should stay with her for three days."""
"430","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant marries, he has completed half of his religion, so let him fear Allah (adopt taqwa) regarding the remaining half."""
"431","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you name (yourselves) after my name, do not take my kunyah as your kunyah."""
"432","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you recites the tashahhud (in the prayer), let him seek refuge from four things: from the punishment of Hell, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the False Messiah (al-Masih ad-Dajjal); then after that let him supplicate for himself with whatever he wishes."""
"433","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two Muslims shake hands with each other, they are forgiven before their hands separate."""
"434","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man purifies himself and then goes to the mosque with the intention of praying, his recorder (angel) writes for him ten good deeds for every step he takes towards the mosque. The one who sits waiting for the prayer is like one engaged in devout worship, and he is counted among those praying from the time he leaves his house until he returns to it."""
"435","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two men come to you for judgement, do not judge in favour of the first until you have also heard what the other has to say; (by doing so) you will know well how to judge."""
"436","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty speaks through revelation, the angels of the lowest heaven hear a clanging like a chain being dragged over a smooth rock, and they fall unconscious. They remain in that state until Jibril (peace be upon him) comes to them. Then, when Jibril reaches them, the terror is removed from their hearts and they ask: 'O Jibril, what has your Lord said?' He answers: 'He has spoken the truth.' Then all those angels also call out: 'He has spoken the truth, He has spoken the truth.'"""
"437","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you wishes (to receive something from Allah), let him wish for much, for he is asking only of his Lord."""
"438","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you spits (or expels phlegm) (in the mosque or in prayer), let him by no means spit in front of his face, nor to his right side; rather, let him spit to his left side or under his left foot."""
"439","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in the mosque and spits out phlegm, let him conceal his phlegm (that is, bury it in the earth), so that it does not get on the skin or the clothing of a believer and cause him harm."""
"440","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you performs ablution and does it very well, then goes out for the prayer, he does not lift his right foot except that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, writes a good deed for him, and he does not put down his left foot except that Allah Almighty wipes away one of his sins. So let any of you live near (the mosque) or come from far away, as he wishes. Then, if he comes to the mosque and prays in congregation, he is forgiven. If he comes to the mosque when the people have prayed part of the prayer and part of it remains, let him pray the remaining part with them and complete (afterwards) what he missed. And if he comes to the mosque when the people have already prayed, and he completes his prayer on his own, he will still receive the same (reward of the congregation)."""
"441","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you performs ablution and does it very well, then goes out to the mosque, and nothing but the intention of prayer brings him out (of his house), his left foot keeps wiping away a sin from him and his right foot keeps writing a good deed for him until he enters the mosque. And if people knew how much reward there is in the Isha and Fajr prayers, they would surely come to them, even if they had to come crawling on their knees."""
"442","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you performs ablution and does it very well, then goes out intending the mosque, let him not interlace the fingers of his hands (tashbik), for he is (even while walking to the mosque) in a state of prayer."""
"443","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you performs ablution, let him put water into his nose and then blow it out to clean it; and when he uses stones (for istinja'), let him use an odd number."""
"444","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you performs ablution, let him put water into his nose and then blow it out; and when he blows his nose, let him do so an odd number of times (once, three times and so on)."""
"445","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you performs ablution in his house and then comes to the mosque, he remains in a state of prayer until he returns, so let him not do like this."" And he (peace and blessings be upon him) interlaced his fingers (tashbik) to demonstrate."
"446","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has performed ablution for the prayer, let him not interlace his fingers (that is, let him not do tashbik)."""
"447","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you performs ablution and puts on his leather socks (khuffs), let him pray in them and wipe over them; then, if he wishes, he need not take them off, except in the state of major ritual impurity (janabah, when ghusl becomes obligatory)."""
"448","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim man performs ablution, his sins leave from his hearing, his sight, his hands and his feet; then, if he sits down, he sits in a state in which he has been forgiven."""
"449","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a believing servant performs ablution and rinses his mouth, the sins leave from his mouth. Then, when he blows out his nose, the sins leave from his nose. Then, when he washes his face, the sins leave from his face, until they leave even from beneath his eyelashes. Then, when he washes his hands, the sins leave from his hands, until they leave even from beneath the fingernails of his hands. Then, when he wipes his head, the sins leave from his head, until they leave even from his ears. Then, when he washes his feet, the sins leave from his feet, until they leave even from beneath the toenails of his feet. Then his walking to the mosque and his prayer become additional reward (nafilah) for him."""
"450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim or believing servant performs ablution and washes his face, every sin he looked at with his eyes comes out from his face with the water, or with the last drop of the water. Then when he washes his hands, every sin his hands committed comes out from his hands with the water, or with the last drop of the water. Then when he washes his feet, every sin towards which his feet walked comes out with the water, or with the last drop of the water, until he emerges completely pure of sins."""
"451","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you perform ablution, blow out your nose, and when you clean yourself after relieving yourself (with stones and the like), use an odd number (of stones)."""
"452","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you perform ablution, pass your fingers between the fingers of your hands and the toes of your feet."""
"453","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you perform ablution, pass your fingers between your fingers."""
"454","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you perform ablution, begin with your right side."""
"455","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you dies and he has something (of financial means), let him be shrouded in a striped Yemeni cloth (hibarah)."""
"456","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the iqamah is called for the prayer, do not come to it running, but come to it in a state of dignity and tranquillity. Pray whatever (of the prayer) you catch, and complete (afterwards) whatever you have missed, for when one of you sets out intending the prayer, he is already in a state of prayer."""
"457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you comes to the Friday prayer, he must never make anyone get up from his place and then sit there himself."""
"458","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you comes to the Friday prayer, he should take a ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"459","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you comes to the prayer, let him walk calmly and gently; let him pray whatever part he catches and complete (afterwards) whatever has passed him."""
"460","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you comes to the mosque, let him pray two rak'ahs (tahiyyat al-masjid) before he sits down; then after that he may sit if he wishes, or go about his business."""
"461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you comes to the mosque, let him look (at his sandals); if he sees any dirt or impurity on his sandals, let him wipe it off and pray in them."""
"462","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you comes to a gathering and room is made for him, let him sit there, for it is an honour with which Allah Almighty and his Muslim brother have honoured him. And if room is not made for him, let him look for the most spacious place and sit there."""
"463","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you comes and his brother makes room for him, it is indeed an honour with which Allah Almighty has honoured him."""
"464","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you comes (to the mosque) on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon, let him pray two rak'ahs (tahiyyat al-masjid) and keep them brief."""
"465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If someone comes asking for the price of a dog, fill his palm with dust (that is, give him nothing at all)."""
"466","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man comes to visit a sick person, let him say this supplication: 'Allahumma-shfi 'abdaka fulanan yanka'u laka 'aduwwan aw yamshi laka ila as-salah' (O Allah, heal Your servant so-and-so, so that he may inflict harm on an enemy of Yours for Your sake, or walk to the prayer for Your pleasure)."""
"467","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you come (to the mosque), pray with the people (in congregation), even if you have already prayed (alone)."""
"468","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you come to the prayer while we are in prostration, then prostrate too, but do not count it as anything (i.e. as a rak'ah); and whoever catches the rak'ah has caught the prayer."""
"469","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the servant of one of you brings him his food, let him seat him with him, or give him some of it to eat, for he is the one who endured its heat and smoke (in preparing the food)."""
"470","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the month of Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are bound in chains."""
"471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the month of Ramadan comes, the gates of mercy are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are bound in chains."""
"472","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the month of Ramadan comes, fast thirty days, unless you see the (Shawwal) crescent moon before that."""
"473","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When something of this wealth comes to you while you were neither hoping for it nor asking for it, take it; and whatever does not come to you, do not let your soul chase after it (do not covet it)."""
"474","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man has intercourse with his wife and then becomes slack (before ejaculation), let him wash what has touched him from the woman, and then perform ablution."""
"475","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the circumcised part passes beyond the circumcised part (that is, when the private parts of the man and the woman meet), the ritual bath (ghusl) becomes obligatory."""
"476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you place in front of you (while praying) something like the back post of a camel saddle (as a sutrah), whoever passes in front of you will not harm you (with any sin)."""
"477","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sits to relieve himself, let him neither face the qiblah nor turn his back towards it."""
"478","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two disputing parties sit before you (with their case) and you have heard from one of them, do not judge for either of them until you have heard from the other just as you heard from the first, for when you do that, the judgement will become perfectly clear to you."""
"479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man sits between a woman's four limbs (her arms and legs) and then exerts himself with her (in intercourse), the ritual bath (ghusl) becomes obligatory upon him, even if there is no ejaculation."""
"480","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man sits between a woman's four limbs and the circumcised part touches the circumcised part (the private parts meet), then the ritual bath (ghusl) certainly becomes obligatory."""
"481","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you perfume the deceased with incense, do so an odd number of times."""
"482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty gathers the first and the last on the Day (of Resurrection) about which there is no doubt, a caller will call out: Whoever did a deed for Allah but associated someone else with Him in it, let him seek the reward for his deed from that (partner), for Allah Almighty is, of all partners, the most free of need of partnership."""
"483","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty gathers the first and the last on the Day of Resurrection, a banner will be raised for every betrayer (deceiver), and it will be said: This is the sign of the treachery and betrayal of so-and-so, son of so-and-so."""
"484","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When something troubles your heart (that is, raises doubt), leave it."""
"485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a child who has not reached puberty performs Hajj, it counts for him as a (voluntary) Hajj until he comes of age (reaches puberty); when he reaches puberty, another (obligatory) Hajj is due from him. And when a Bedouin performs Hajj, it is a Hajj for him; then when he migrates, another Hajj is due from him."""
"486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man says something and then looks around (to see that no one is listening), it is a trust (with the one who heard it)."""
"487","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is faced with an important matter which he fears he will miss, let him pray in this way, that is, let him combine two prayers (together)."""
"488","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has performed his (obligatory) prayer in the mosque, let him also set aside a portion of his (voluntary and sunnah) prayer for his home, for Allah Almighty will bring about good in his home through the blessing of his prayer."""
"489","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the scholars come before their Lord on the Day of Resurrection, Mu'adh bin Jabal will be ahead of them (all) by the distance of a stone's throw."""
"490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the time of death approaches the believer, the angels of mercy come to him with a white silk cloth and say: O soul, come out, pleased (with Allah) and with Allah pleased with you, to rest and fragrance and to a Lord who is not angry with you at all. So it comes out like the finest scent of musk, until the angels pass it from hand to hand among themselves, and they bring it to the gate of heaven, and the angels there say: How pure is this fragrance that has come to you from the earth! Then those angels take it to the souls of the other believers, and they rejoice at its arrival more than any of you rejoices when an absent loved one returns to him. Then they (the souls already there) ask it: What did so-and-so do? How is so-and-so? And the angels say: Leave him for now, for he was in the grief and hardships of the world. Then when the arriving soul says to them: So-and-so (who had died in the world), did he not come to you? they reply: He was taken to his abode, Hawiyah (Hell). And when the time of death approaches the disbeliever, the angels of punishment come to him with a sackcloth (a coarse cloth) and say: Come out, displeased (with Allah) and with wrath sent down upon you, to the punishment of Allah. So it comes out like the most foul stench of a carcass, until the angels bring it to the gate of the earth, and the guards say: What a foul stench this is! Until they take it to the souls of the disbelievers."""
"491","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are present with a dying person, say good things (supplicate for good), for the angels say Amin to whatever you say."""
"492","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you go to your dying ones, close their eyes, for the eyes follow the (departing) soul; and say good things, for the angels say Amin to whatever the people of the household say."""
"493","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a ruler (or judge) exerts himself in reasoning (ijtihad) when judging and reaches the correct conclusion, he has a double reward; and if he exerts himself in reasoning when judging and errs, he has one reward (for his ijtihad)."""
"494","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you judge, act with justice and fairness; and when you take a life (in retribution, slaughter and the like), do it in the best manner, for indeed Allah Almighty is doer of good and loves those who do good."""
"495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you swears an oath (or states something with certainty), let him not say: 'What Allah willed and you willed,' but rather let him say: 'What Allah willed, then what you willed.'"""
"496","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees a bad dream, let him not tell people about this play of Satan with him in his sleep."""
"497","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has a fever, let him pour cold water over himself at the time of suhur for three nights."""
"498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you circumcise (women), do not cut (the skin) excessively, for that (method) is more pleasurable for the woman and more beloved to the husband."""
"499","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man, on leaving his house, recites this supplication: 'Bismillah, tawakkaltu 'ala Allah, la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (In the name of Allah, I have put my trust in Allah; there is no power to avoid sins and no strength to do good deeds except by Allah's enabling), it is said to him: That is sufficient for you; you have been guided, you have been sufficed, and you have been protected (from every evil). So Satan moves away from him, and one devil says to another devil: How can you get at a man who has been guided, sufficed and protected?"""
"500","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When three people set out on a journey, they should appoint one of themselves as their amir (leader)."""
"501","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any woman among you goes out to the mosque, she must not go near perfume (that is, she should not go out wearing perfume)."""
"502","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a curse leaves the mouth of a person, it looks (towards the one who was cursed); if it finds a way to reach that person (that is, if he deserves it), then so be it; otherwise it returns to the very person from whose mouth it came."""
"503","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman (wearing perfume) is about to go out to the mosque, she should bathe on account of that perfume (to remove its trace) just as she bathes on account of major ritual impurity (janabah)."""
"504","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the soul of a believing servant departs, two angels receive it and ascend with it (the narrator mentioned its pleasant fragrance), and the angels of the heaven say: 'A pure soul has come from the direction of the earth; may Allah's mercy be upon you and upon the body you used to inhabit.' Then it is taken to its Lord, and the command is given: 'Take it to its final abode.' And when the soul of a disbeliever departs (the narrator mentioned its foul stench), the inhabitants of the heaven say: 'An evil (impure) soul has come from the direction of the earth.' Then it is said: 'Take it to its final abode.'"""
"505","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are about to leave your house, pray two rak'ahs; they will protect you from going out to evil. And when you enter your house, pray two rak'ahs; they will protect you from entering into evil."""
"506","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you sends a marriage proposal to a woman, then if it is possible for him to see something of her (some quality or a glimpse of her) that would encourage him to marry her, let him certainly do so."""
"507","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you proposes marriage to a woman, there is no sin on him in looking at her, provided that he is looking at her solely with the intention of marriage, even if the woman is not aware (of his looking)."""
"508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you circumcise (women), cut only a little and do not cut from the root (that is, do not go to excess), for this is better for the radiance of the face and more pleasing to the husband."""
"509","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you circumcise (women), cut only a small part and do not remove it from the root, for this increases the radiance of the face and is more attractive (and pleasurable) in the husband's eyes."""
"510","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the believers have crossed over (the bridge of) Hell, they will be held back on a bridge between Paradise and Hell, and they will take retribution (qisas) from one another for the wrongs they committed against each other in the world, until, when they have been completely purified and cleansed, they will be given permission to enter Paradise. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! Each one of them will know the way to his home in Paradise better than he knew the way to his home in the world."""
"511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a hide is tanned, it becomes pure."""
"512","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the skin of a dead animal is tanned, that is sufficient for it, so let use be made of it."""
"513","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you enters the mosque, he should not sit down until he has prayed two rak'ahs (tahiyyat al-masjid)."""
"514","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you enters the mosque, he should send salutations of peace upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and recite this supplication: 'Allahumma iftah li abwaba rahmatik (O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy),' and when he leaves, he should send salutations of peace upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and recite this supplication: 'Allahumma i'simni min al-shaytan (O Allah, protect me from Satan).'"""
"515","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you enters the mosque, he should send salutations of peace upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and recite this supplication: 'Allahumma iftah li abwaba rahmatik (O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy),' and when he leaves, he should send salutations of peace upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and recite this supplication: 'Allahumma inni as'aluka min fadlik (O Allah, I ask You of Your bounty).'"""
"516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you enters the mosque, he should send blessings (durood) upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and recite this supplication: 'Allahumma iftah li abwaba rahmatik (O Allah, open for me the gates of Your mercy),' and when he leaves, he should send salutations of peace upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and recite this supplication: 'Allahumma inni as'aluka min fadlik (O Allah, I ask You of Your bounty).'"""
"517","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you comes to a gathering of people and room is made for him, he should sit there, for this is an honour from Allah with which his Muslim brother has honoured him. And if room is not made for him, he should look for the most spacious place and sit there."""
"518","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you visits his Muslim brother and he feeds him some of his food, he should eat it and not ask about it (its nature or whether it is lawful); and if he gives him some of his drink, he should drink it and not ask about it."""
"519","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man enters his house and mentions the name of Allah Almighty upon entering and when eating, Satan says (to his companions): 'There is no place to spend the night for you here, nor any supper.' And when he enters and does not mention the name of Allah upon entering, Satan says: 'You have found a place to spend the night.' And if he does not mention the name of Allah when eating either, Satan says: 'You have found both a place to spend the night and supper.'"""
"520","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the (first) ten days (of Dhul-Hijjah) begin and any of you intends to offer a sacrifice, he should not cut anything from his hair or his body (such as nails or skin)."""
"521","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of Paradise have entered Paradise and the people of Hell have entered Hell, a caller will call out: 'O people of Paradise! You have a promise with Allah which He wishes to fulfil for you.' They will say: 'What is it? Has Allah not made our scales heavy, made our faces bright, admitted us into Paradise and saved us from Hell?' Then the veil will be lifted and they will behold Allah. By Allah! Allah will not have given them anything more beloved to them than beholding Him, nor anything more delightful to their eyes."""
"522","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of Paradise have entered Paradise and the people of Hell have entered Hell, death will be brought in the form of a black-and-white ram and made to stand between Paradise and Hell. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise! Do you recognise this?' They will raise their necks and look, and say: 'Yes, this is death.' And all of them will have seen it. Then it will be called out: 'O people of Hell! Do you recognise this?' They too will raise their necks and look, and say: 'Yes, this is death.' And all of them will have seen it. Then the command will be given and it will be slaughtered, and it will be said: 'O people of Paradise! Now you will remain here forever, and there is no death. And O people of Hell! Now you will remain here forever, and there is no death.'"""
"523","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of Paradise have entered Paradise, Allah Almighty will say: 'Do you want anything more that I may give you in addition?' They will say: 'Have You not made our faces bright? Have You not admitted us into Paradise and saved us from Hell?' Then the veil will be lifted, and they will not have been given anything more beloved to them than beholding their Lord."""
"524","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of Paradise have entered Paradise, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'Do you desire anything, that I may give it to you in addition?' They will say: 'Our Lord! What could be greater than what You have given us?' Then Allah will say: 'My good pleasure is the greatest (blessing).'"""
"525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you return (from a journey) at night, do not go in to your family suddenly, so that the woman whose husband was away may remove her pubic hair and the woman with dishevelled hair may comb her hair."""
"526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you enter a house, greet its occupants with salam, and when you leave, bid its residents farewell with salam."""
"527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you enter a mosque, pray with the people (in congregation), even if you have already prayed (alone)."""
"528","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the month of Ramadan begins, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained."""
"529","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you invites his brother, he should accept the invitation, whether it is a wedding feast (walimah) or some other occasion like it."""
"530","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you supplicates, he should not say: 'O Allah, forgive me if You wish.' Rather, he should ask with firm conviction and keep his longing high, for nothing that Allah gives is difficult or great for Him."""
"531","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you supplicates, he should ask with firm conviction and not say: 'O Allah, if You wish, then give me,' for there is no one who can compel Allah Almighty (that is, force Him)."""
"532","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man calls his wife to his bed and she refuses to come, and the husband spends the night angry with her, the angels curse that woman until morning."""
"533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man calls his wife to his bed, she should respond to him at once, even if she is (riding) on the saddle of a camel."""
"534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man calls his wife for his (physical) need, she should come to him at once, even if she is (working) at the oven."""
"535","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person supplicates for someone in his absence, the angel says to him: 'And for you the like of that.'"""
"536","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is invited to a wedding feast (walimah), he should certainly attend it."""
"537","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is invited to a meal, he should accept, and then if he wishes he may eat, and if he wishes he may not eat."""
"538","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is invited to a meal, he should accept; then if he is not fasting he should eat, and if he is fasting he should supplicate for blessing (for the host)."""
"539","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is invited to a meal, he should accept; if he is not fasting he should eat, and if he is fasting he should supplicate for him."""
"540","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is invited to a meal while he is fasting, he should say: 'I am fasting.'"""
"541","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is invited to a wedding feast (walimah), he should accept."""
"542","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is invited to a wedding feast (walimah), he should accept, even if he is fasting."""
"543","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you is called and he comes along with the messenger, then that (coming along with him) is his permission (to enter)."""
"544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are invited even to (a humble meal such as goat's) trotters, accept the invitation."""
"545","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When my Companions are mentioned (critically), restrain (your tongues); when the stars (and their supposed influence) are mentioned, remain silent; and when predestination (qadar) is debated, refrain from it."""
"546","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are restrained from something by being reminded of Allah (adjured by Allah), stop at once."""
"547","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you goes to relieve himself, he should take three stones with him with which to clean himself, for indeed they will suffice for him."""
"548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you sees a good dream, he should interpret it (favourably) and tell (others) about it; and when he sees a bad dream, he should neither interpret it nor tell anyone about it."""
"549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you sees a dream that he likes, it is indeed from Allah Almighty; he should praise Allah for it and relate it (to others). And when he sees something other than that, a dream that he dislikes, it is from Satan; he should seek refuge in Allah and not mention it to anyone, and then that dream will certainly not harm him."""
"550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees a dream that he likes, it is indeed from Allah Almighty; let him praise Allah for it and let him relate it (to others). And when he sees something other than that, a dream that he dislikes, it is from Satan; let him seek refuge with Allah from its evil and not mention it to anyone, and then it will not harm him at all."""
"551","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees a dream that he dislikes, let him spit (lightly) to his left three times, seek refuge with Allah from Satan (and his evil) three times, and turn over from the side on which he was lying."""
"552","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees a woman who attracts him, let him return at once to his wife and have intercourse with her, for what that (unrelated woman) has, the same is with (his wife) as well."""
"553","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees a funeral procession and he is not walking with it, let him stand up until it passes ahead, or he leaves the funeral behind, or it is placed (on the ground) before it passes him."""
"554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees a dream that he dislikes, let him turn over, spit (lightly) to his left three times, ask Allah Almighty for the good of that dream, and seek refuge with Allah from its evil."""
"555","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees someone afflicted (or sick) and says: 'Al-hamdu lillahil-ladhi 'afani mimmab-talaka bihi wa faddalani 'alayka wa 'ala kathirin min 'ibadihi tafdila' (All praise is for Allah who has kept me safe from that with which He has afflicted you, and has greatly favoured me over you and over many of His servants), then that is the thanks for that blessing (of well-being)."""
"556","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sees something in himself, in his wealth, or in his brother that pleases him, let him pray for blessing for it, for the evil eye is real."""
"557","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the believer sees the spaciousness (and blessings) of his grave, he says: 'Let me go so that I may give this good news to my family.' It is said to him: 'Rest here in peace (now).'"""
"558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman sees (a wet dream) and has a discharge (of sexual fluid), ritual bath (ghusl) becomes obligatory upon her."""
"559","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you goes to the Friday prayer, let him take a ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"560","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see a slave woman giving birth to her mistress, and you see the builders vying with one another in pride and arrogance in raising tall buildings, and you see the barefoot, hungry and destitute becoming the chiefs (rulers) of the people, then that is among the signs and portents of the Hour."""
"561","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see Allah Almighty granting a servant the worldly blessings that he loves, while he (the servant) persists in his disobedience (sins), then know for certain that this is only Allah giving him respite (istidraj)."""
"562","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see madhi (the fluid that comes out at the time of arousal), wash your private part and perform ablution as you do for prayer; and when you see the water (i.e. semen) spurting out, take a ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see people in a state where their covenants and pledges have become corrupted, their trusts have become light (honesty has disappeared), and they have become entangled with one another like this"" and he (peace and blessings be upon him) interlaced his fingers to show it, ""then keep to your house, control your tongue, adopt what you recognise as right (according to the Shariah) and leave what you know to be wrong, concern yourself especially with your own personal affairs, and leave aside the affairs of the general public."""
"564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see a sign (of Allah's power that warns), fall down in prostration."""
"565","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see a funeral procession, stand up; and whoever walks with the funeral should not sit down until it has been placed (on the ground)."""
"566","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see a funeral procession, stand up for it until it passes ahead of you or it is placed (on the ground)."""
"567","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see a man boasting in the manner of the Days of Ignorance (and calling out by the names of his forefathers), tell him in plain words to bite his father's private part, and do not use any allusion or veiled words in this."""
"568","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see that the night has come from this direction (the east), then the fasting person has broken his fast (i.e. the time for breaking the fast has come)."""
"569","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see those who praise (flatteringly and excessively), throw dust in their faces."""
"570","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see people in a state where their covenants and pledges have become corrupted, their trusts have become light (honesty has disappeared), and they have become entangled with one another like this"" and he (peace and blessings be upon him) interlaced his fingers to show it, ""then keep to your house, control your tongue, adopt what you recognise as right (according to the Shariah) and leave what you know to be wrong, concern yourself especially with your own personal affairs, and leave aside the affairs of the general public."""
"571","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see the new moon (of Ramadan), fast; and when you see it (the new moon of Shawwal), break the fast (i.e. celebrate Eid); and if the moon is hidden from you (because of clouds), then estimate it (i.e. complete thirty days of Sha'ban)."""
"572","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see the new moon (of Ramadan), fast; and when you see it (the new moon of Shawwal), break the fast; and if clouds cover it (the moon) from you, then complete the count of thirty days."""
"573","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see someone buying or selling in the mosque, say to him: 'May Allah not make your trade profitable.' And when you see someone announcing his lost property in it, say to him: 'May Allah not return your lost property to you.'"""
"574","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see the new moon of Dhul-Hijjah and one of you intends to offer a sacrifice, let him refrain from (cutting) his hair and his nails (until he has sacrificed)."""
"575","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you see me in a state like this, that is, relieving myself, do not greet me with salam, for even if you do so, I will not reply to you."""
"576","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you ride these dumb animals, move swiftly on them; and when there is a year of drought, move swiftly on them; and keep to travelling by night, for Allah Almighty folds up the distance of the land at night."""
"577","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you bow, place both your palms on your knees until you are at rest (in bowing); and when you prostrate, place your forehead firmly on the ground until you feel the firmness of the ground."""
"578","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah (the big pillar), everything (that was restricted in ihram) becomes lawful for him except women (i.e. marital relations)."""
"579","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you shoot an arrow at game and find it after three nights with your arrow still in it, eat it, provided it has not begun to smell."""
"580","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you throw the mi'rad (a sharp-edged stick or an arrow without an arrowhead) at game and it pierces it (with its edge), eat it; but if it strikes it with its broad side (or blunt part), do not eat it, for it has died from a blow (and is carrion)."""
"581","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you shoot your arrow and it (the game) remains out of (your) sight for three days and then you find it, eat it as long as it has not begun to smell."""
"582","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are able to give your family their fill of milk (i.e. lawful provision) in the evening, then avoid what Allah has forbidden, such as carrion (i.e. when lawful provision is available, keep strictly away from the unlawful)."""
"583","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you visits his brother and sits with him, let him not get up (to leave) until he has sought his permission."""
"584","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you visits a people, let him not lead them in prayer; rather, a man from among them should lead them in prayer."""
"585","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you decorate your mosques with ornamentation and adorn your copies of the Qur'an (with gold, silver or other embellishments), then ruin and destruction will be your fate."""
"586","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant commits adultery (zina), faith leaves (his heart) and hangs over his head like a canopy (shade); then when he desists (from that sin), faith returns to him."""
"587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the slave woman of one of you commits zina and her zina is established, let him flog her (the prescribed punishment) and not taunt or reproach her. Then if she commits zina (again), let him flog her and not reproach her. Then if she commits zina a third time, let him sell her, even for a rope made of hair."""
"588","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the two of you travel, give the call to prayer (adhan) and the iqamah (when the time of prayer comes), and let the elder of you lead you in prayer."""
"589","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you travel in times of greenery and plenty, give the camels their share of the land (for grazing); and when you travel in a year of drought, hasten your journey on them; and when you halt in the last part of the night, rest away from the road (to one side), for these common thoroughfares are the paths of beasts and the dwelling places of vermin (insects and creeping things) at night."""
"590","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty sends you some provision that you did not ask for and did not greedily covet in your heart, then take it, for Allah has given it to you."""
"591","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you asks (Allah Almighty), let him ask abundantly, for he is asking none other than his Lord."""
"592","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you ask Allah Almighty (for Paradise), ask Him for Firdaws, for it is the very best part (or the middle) of Paradise."""
"593","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you supplicate to Allah Almighty, ask Him with the inner side (i.e. the palms) of your hands, and do not ask Him with the backs of your hands."""
"594","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man reviles you for some fault of yours that he knows, do not revile him for some fault of his that you know; thus the reward (for patience) will be yours and the burden (of the sin) will be upon him."""
"595","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prostrates, let him not kneel down (to the ground) the way a camel kneels; rather, he should place both his hands (on the ground) before his knees."""
"596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prostrates, let him keep balance (in prostration), and let him not spread his forearms (on the ground) the way a dog spreads them."""
"597","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant prostrates, seven of his limbs prostrate with him: his face, his two palms, his two knees and his two feet."""
"598","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you prostrate, place both your palms (on the ground) and keep both your elbows raised (off the ground)."""
"599","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you travel through green and fertile land, give the animals their share (of fodder); and when you pass through drought-stricken (barren) land, hasten your journey on them; and when you halt at night, do not stop in the middle of the road, for it is the dwelling place of every creature (and creeping thing)."""
"600","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When your good deed pleases you and your bad deed grieves you, then (know that) you are a true believer."""
"601","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove the dirt (dust and the like) from it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan. And let each of you wipe the bowl (or plate) clean with his fingers, for you do not know in which part of your food the blessing lies."""
"602","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a morsel of one of you falls, let him remove whatever dirt is on it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan. And let him not wipe his hand with a towel (or napkin) until he has licked his fingers or had them licked (by his wife or the like), for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing has been placed."""
"603","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you drinks an intoxicant, flog him; then if he drinks again, flog him; then if he drinks a third time, flog him again; and if he does it a fourth time as well, kill him."""
"604","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you draws a sword from its sheath to look at it and then wants to hand it to his brother, let him first put it back in its sheath and then hand it to him (in its sheath)."""
"605","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of the People of the Book (the Jews and Christians) greets you with salam, then say (only this in reply): 'Wa 'alaykum' (and upon you too)."""
"606","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the Jews greet you, one of them says (instead of 'As-salamu 'alaykum'): 'As-samu 'alayk' (death be upon you), so say (in reply): 'Wa 'alayk' (and upon you too)."""
"607","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you hears the (Fajr) call to prayer while the vessel (of food or drink for suhur) is in his hand, let him not put it down until he has fulfilled his need from it."""
"608","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear a man saying, 'The people are ruined (or destroyed),' then in reality he is the most ruined of them (or, by spreading this despair, the one who ruins them)."""
"609","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the call to prayer, respond to the one who calls to Allah (the muezzin) (that is, go to the mosque for the prayer)."""
"610","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear your neighbours saying (about you), 'You have done well,' then you have truly done well; and when you hear them saying, 'You have done wrong,' then you have certainly done wrong."""
"611","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the crowing of roosters, ask Allah Almighty for His bounty, for they have seen an angel; and when you hear the braying of donkeys, seek refuge with Allah from the accursed Satan, for they have seen a devil."""
"612","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear a hadith from me which your hearts recognise, at which your hair and skin soften, and which you feel is close to you (that is, in accordance with the truth), then I am more entitled to it than you (that is, it is indeed my word). And when you hear a hadith from me which your hearts reject, from which your hair and skin recoil, and which you feel is far from you (that is, remote from reason and the Shariah), then I am even farther from it than you (that is, I have nothing to do with it)."""
"613","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the muezzin (calling the adhan), say the same as he says. Then send blessings upon me, for whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah Almighty sends down ten mercies upon him in return. Then ask Allah for al-Wasilah for me, for it is a station in Paradise that befits only one servant among the servants of Allah, and I hope that I will be that servant. So whoever asks for al-Wasilah for me, my intercession becomes due for him."""
"614","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the muezzin calling to the prayer (reciting the adhan or the iqamah), then you too say just as he says."""
"615","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the call to prayer, say just as the muezzin says."""
"616","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear of the plague (spreading) in a land, do not go there; and if it breaks out in a land where you are, do not leave it fleeing from it."""
"617","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear of the plague (epidemic) in a land, do not enter it; and if it breaks out in a land where you are, do not leave it in flight from it."""
"618","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear of a people who have been swallowed up by the earth nearby, here, then (know that) the Hour has drawn very near."""
"619","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear someone boasting in the manner of the Days of Ignorance (and displaying tribal partisanship in the name of his forefathers), then shame him in plain words (by telling him to bite his father's private part), and do not use any allusion or veiled words in this."""
"620","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear the barking of dogs and the braying of donkeys at night, seek refuge with Allah from Satan, for they see things (devils) that you do not see. And when the sound of footsteps has died down (people have gone to sleep), go out less at night, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, spreads at night whatever He wills of His creation. And close the doors and mention the name of Allah over them, for Satan does not open a door that has been closed and over which the name of Allah has been mentioned. And cover the jars, tie up the mouths of the water-skins, and turn the vessels upside down."""
"621","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you have fixed the measure (and weight), then measure it out in full."""
"622","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you forgets in his prayer and does not remember whether he has prayed one rak'ah or two, let him build on one (that is, count it as only one); and if he does not remember whether he has prayed three or four, let him build on three, and let him perform two prostrations (of forgetfulness) before giving the salam."""
"623","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the imam forgets and stands up fully straight (instead of sitting for the tashahhud), two prostrations of forgetfulness are required of him; and if he has not stood fully straight (and sits back down), no prostration of forgetfulness is obligatory on him."""
"624","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you drinks water (or any drink), let him not breathe into the vessel. Then if he wants to drink again, let him move the vessel away (from his mouth), and then drink again if he wishes."""
"625","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you drinks something, let him not breathe into the vessel; and when he goes to relieve himself, let him not touch his private part with his right hand, nor clean himself (istinja) with his right hand."""
"626","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you drinks (something), let him not drink it in a single breath."""
"627","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog drinks (by putting its mouth) from the vessel of one of you, let him wash that vessel seven times."""
"628","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you drink milk, rinse your mouth (with water) afterwards, for it contains fat."""
"629","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When people drink wine, flog them; then if they drink again, flog them; then if they drink (a third time), flog them; and if they drink (again after that), kill them."""
"630","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in doubt between two rak'ahs and one, let him count it as one; when he is in doubt between two and three, let him count it as two; and when he is in doubt between three and four, let him count it as three, so that the doubt lies on the side of excess. Then let him complete the rest of his prayer, and then perform two prostrations (of forgetfulness) while sitting, before giving the salam."""
"631","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in doubt in his prayer and does not know whether he has prayed two rak'ahs or three, let him cast aside the doubt and build on what is certain (that is, the lower number)."""
"632","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in doubt in his prayer and does not know how many he has prayed, three rak'ahs or four? Let him cast aside the doubt and build on what he is certain of, then perform two prostrations (of forgetfulness) before giving the salam. If he had prayed five, they (the prostrations) will make his prayer even; and if he had prayed a complete four, the two prostrations will be a cause of humiliation and disgrace for Satan."""
"633","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in doubt in his prayer, let him cast aside the doubt and build on what is certain. Then when he is certain of the prayer's completion, let him perform two prostrations. If his prayer was complete, the (extra) rak'ah and the two prostrations will be voluntary; and if the prayer was incomplete, that rak'ah will complete the prayer and the two prostrations will be a cause of rubbing Satan's nose in the dust (humiliating him)."""
"634","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you women attends the Isha prayer (in the mosque), let her not apply perfume."""
"635","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim points a weapon at his brother, the angels of Allah continue to curse him until he lowers it away from him."""
"636","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of Paradise have gone into Paradise and the people of Hell have gone into Hell, death will be brought until it is placed between Paradise and Hell, and then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will call out: O people of Paradise! Now it is eternity, no death; and O people of Hell! Now it is eternity, no death. So the joy of the people of Paradise will increase even further, and the grief of the people of Hell will increase even further."""
"637","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays facing a sutrah (barrier), let him stand close to it, so that Satan cannot pass between him and the sutrah."""
"638","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays facing something that screens him from people, and someone wants to pass in front of him, let him stop him; and if he refuses, let him deal with him firmly (pushing him to the point of fighting), for he is nothing but a devil."""
"639","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has prayed the Friday prayer, let him not pray any (voluntary or Sunnah) prayer after it until he has spoken or gone out (of the mosque)."""
"640","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has prayed the Friday prayer, let him pray four rak'ahs (Sunnah) after it."""
"641","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him pray facing a sutrah (barrier) and stand close to it, and let him not allow anyone to pass in front of him. If someone comes to pass, let him deal with him firmly, for he is nothing but a devil."""
"642","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has prayed the two rak'ahs (Sunnah) of Fajr, let him lie down on his right side."""
"643","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays and takes off his sandals, let him not cause anyone harm with them; let him place them between his feet or else pray wearing them."""
"644","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him not spit in front of him or to his right; rather, let him spit to his left or beneath his foot."""
"645","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him not place his sandals on his right or on his left, where they would be on someone else's right, unless there is no one on his left. And let him place them between his feet."""
"646","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays and does not know how he has prayed (that is, he has doubt about the number of rak'ahs), let him perform two prostrations (of forgetfulness) while sitting."""
"647","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him wear a lower garment and also put on an upper wrap (that is, his dress should be complete and dignified)."""
"648","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him begin by praising Allah Almighty and extolling Him, then send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and then after that supplicate for whatever he wishes."""
"649","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him complete his bowing (ruku') (and do it calmly), and let him not peck (like a crow) in his prostration. For the likeness of this (one who pecks) is like a hungry person who eats one or two dates; what benefit can they give him (that is, how will they satisfy his hunger)?"""
"650","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him pray facing a sutrah (a barrier) and stand close to his sutrah, so that Satan cannot interrupt (spoil) his prayer."""
"651","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him pray facing a sutrah (a barrier) and stand close to it, and let him not allow anyone to pass in front of him. If someone tries to pass, let him deal with him firmly, for he is a devil."""
"652","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him wear his two garments (the lower wrap and the upper sheet), for Allah Almighty is most deserving that one should adorn oneself for Him."""
"653","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays, let him pray wearing his shoes, or else take them off and place them between his feet, and let him not cause anyone else harm with them."""
"654","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has prayed in his house and then enters the mosque while the people are praying (in congregation), let him pray with them; it will be a voluntary (nafl) prayer for him."""
"655","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays in a single garment, let him cross its two ends over his shoulders (that is, the right end over the left shoulder and the left end over the right)."""
"656","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you prays in a single garment, let him tie it firmly around his waist (and hips), and do not wrap yourselves in the garment the way the Jews do (leaving the shoulders bare)."""
"657","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has prayed at his lodging and then finds the imam, while he (the imam) has not yet prayed, let him pray with him, for it will be a voluntary (nafl) prayer for him."""
"658","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you leads the people in prayer, let him keep it light (short), for among them are the weak, the sick and the elderly. And when one of you prays by himself, let him lengthen it as much as he wishes."""
"659","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the leader (that is, the imam) leads the prayer sitting, then you too should pray sitting."""
"660","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman prays her five (daily) prayers, fasts her month (Ramadan), guards her private parts and obeys her husband, it will be said to her: Enter Paradise by whichever of the gates of Paradise you wish."""
"661","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman prays her five (daily) prayers, fasts her month (Ramadan), guards her private parts and obeys her husband, she will enter Paradise."""
"662","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When people pray the funeral prayer over someone and speak well of him (the deceased), the Lord says: I have accepted their testimony as far as what they know, and I forgive him what they do not know."""
"663","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you have prayed the morning (Fajr) prayer, refrain from praying until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of Satan. When it has risen, then pray, for the prayer at that time is attended by the angels and is accepted, until the sun stands straight over your head like a spear. Then refrain (from prayer), for that is the time when Hell is stoked and its gates are opened, until the sun declines towards your right eyebrow (that is, after the zenith). When it has declined to the right side, then pray, for this prayer too is attended by the angels and is accepted, until you pray the Asr prayer. Then leave off prayer until the sun sets."""
"664","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you pray, do not ever spit in front of you or to your right; rather, spit to your left if that place is empty, otherwise spit under your left foot and rub it away."""
"665","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you pray, do not spread your forearms out (on the ground, in prostration) the way a beast of prey does; rather, support yourself on your palms and keep your elbows away from your sides."""
"666","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you two have prayed at your lodgings and then come to the imam, pray with him as well; this (second prayer) will be voluntary (nafl) for you, and the one you prayed at your lodgings will be the obligatory one."""
"667","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you two have prayed at your lodgings and then come to a mosque where the congregation prays, pray with them as well, for it will be voluntary (nafl) for you."""
"668","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you have prayed the Friday (Jumu'ah) prayer, pray four rak'ahs (sunnah) after it."""
"669","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you pray (the funeral prayer) over the deceased, supplicate for him with sincerity of heart."""
"670","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you send blessings upon me, say: 'O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and upon the family of Ibrahim; and bestow Your favour upon Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and upon the family of Muhammad, as You bestowed Your favour upon Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and upon the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Most Praiseworthy, Most Glorious.'"""
"671","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you pray, tie on a lower wrap and put on an upper sheet, and do not imitate the Jews."""
"672","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you pray, straighten your rows, then let one of you lead you in prayer. When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he recites, remain silent; and when he says: 'Ghayril-maghdubi 'alayhim wa lad-dallin (not of those who have earned anger, nor of those who go astray)' [Surah Al-Fatihah: 7], say: 'Amin', and Allah will love you. When he says the takbir and bows, say the takbir and bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you, so this makes up for that. When he says: 'Sami'allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears the one who praises Him)', say: 'Allahumma Rabbana lakal-hamd (O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs all praise)', and Allah will hear you. When he says the takbir and prostrates, say the takbir and prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you, so this makes up for that. And when it is time for the sitting (tashahhud), let the first words of each of you be: 'All greetings, good words and prayers are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.'"""
"673","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you fast three days of the month, fast the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth."""
"674","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you strikes (punishes) his servant, let him avoid striking (his) face."""
"675","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When people become miserly with dinars and dirhams, trade through 'inah (a form of usury), follow the tails of cattle (that is, become absorbed in farming and worldly wealth) and abandon jihad in the path of Allah, Allah Almighty will bring upon them a humiliation that He will not lift from them until they return to their religion."""
"676","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you cooks a pot, let him add plenty of broth to it, then give some of it to his neighbour."""
"677","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you cook meat, add plenty of broth, for it brings more abundance (in blessing) and is better suited for reaching the neighbours."""
"678","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When dawn (Fajr) has broken, there is no (voluntary) prayer except the two rak'ahs (sunnah) of Fajr."""
"679","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When fornication and usury (riba) become widespread in a town, its people have made the punishment of Allah lawful upon themselves."""
"680","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When evil and sin become widespread on the earth, Allah Almighty sends down His punishment upon the people of the earth, even if there are righteous people among them. The affliction that befalls the people in general befalls them (the righteous) as well, then they (the righteous) return to the mercy of Allah and His forgiveness."""
"681","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you visits a sick person, let him say: 'O Allah, heal Your servant, so that he may inflict harm on an enemy for Your sake, or walk to a prayer for You.'"""
"682","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man goes to visit his sick Muslim brother, he remains among the paths of Paradise (or among the picking of its fruits) until he sits down (with him). When he sits, mercy envelops him. If he went in the morning, seventy thousand angels pray for his forgiveness until the evening, and if he went in the evening, seventy thousand angels pray for his forgiveness until the morning."""
"683","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sneezes and praises Allah (that is, says Al-hamdu lillah), respond to him (by saying Yarhamukallah), and if he does not praise Allah, then do not respond to him."""
"684","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sneezes, let the person sitting with him respond to him. If he sneezes more than three times, he has a cold, so he is not to be responded to after three times."""
"685","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sneezes, let him place his two palms (or a cloth) over his face and lower his voice."""
"686","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sneezes, let him say: 'Al-hamdu lillahi Rabbil-'alamin (All praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds)', and let (the listener) say to him: 'Yarhamukallah (May Allah have mercy on you)', and let him (the one who sneezed, in reply) say: 'Yaghfirullahu lana wa lakum (May Allah forgive us and you)'."""
"687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sneezes, let him say: 'Al-hamdu lillahi 'ala kulli hal (All praise is for Allah in every situation)', and let those around him say to him: 'Yarhamukallah (May Allah have mercy on you)', and let him say (in reply) to those around him: 'Yahdikumullahu wa yuslihu balakum (May Allah guide you and set your affairs right)'."""
"688","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you sneezes, let him say: 'Al-hamdu lillah (All praise is for Allah)'. When he has said it, let his brother or companion say to him: 'Yarhamukallah (May Allah have mercy on you)'. When he says 'Yarhamukallah' to him, let him (the one who sneezed, in reply) say: 'Yahdikumullahu wa yuslihu balakum (May Allah guide you and set your affairs right)'."""
"689","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a sin is committed on the earth, whoever is present there and detests it is like one who was absent from it (that is, he is safe from the consequences of that sin), and whoever is absent from it but is pleased with it (the sin) is like one who was present there."""
"690","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you commit an evil deed (a sin), follow it immediately with a good deed; that good deed will wipe it out."""
"691","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you make broth, add plenty of water to it, and then give some of it to your neighbours as well."""
"692","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the sun sets, keep your children (from going outside), for that is the time when the devils spread out."""
"693","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you becomes angry, let him fall silent."""
"694","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you becomes angry while standing, let him sit down. If the anger leaves him (then well and good); otherwise, let him lie down."""
"695","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man becomes angry and says: 'A'udhu billah (I seek refuge with Allah)', his anger subsides."""
"696","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you become angry, sit down."""
"697","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Persia and Rome (their lands and treasures) are opened up to you, what kind of people will you be? It was said: We will remain as Allah has commanded us. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Or otherwise? You will compete with one another (in greed for the world), then you will envy one another, then you will turn your backs on one another (cutting off relations), then you will hate one another, then you will go to the dwellings of the Muhajirun and set some of them over the necks of others."""
"698","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Egypt is conquered, accept my counsel to treat the Copts well, for they have (from us) a covenant of protection as well as ties of kinship."""
"699","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you finishes the final tashahhud, he should seek refuge with Allah from four things, saying: 'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min adhabi jahannam, wa min adhabil-qabr, wa min fitnatil-mahya wal-mamat, wa min sharri fitnatil-masihid-dajjal' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of life and death, and from the evil of the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal)."""
"700","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you finishes his prayer (that is, its tashahhud), he should supplicate (for refuge) from four things, and after that he may supplicate for whatever he wishes: 'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min adhabi jahannam, wa adhabil-qabr, wa fitnatil-mahya wal-mamat, wa fitnatil-masihid-dajjal' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, the punishment of the grave, the trial of life and death, and the trial of the Masih al-Dajjal)."""
"701","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is startled with fear in his sleep, he should say: 'A'udhu bi-kalimatillahit-tammati min ghadabihi wa 'iqabihi wa sharri 'ibadihi, wa min hamazatish-shayatini wa an yahdurun' (I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His anger and His punishment, from the evil of His servants, and from the whisperings of the devils and from their coming to me), and it (the dream or fear) will certainly never harm him."""
"702","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the people of Syria (al-Sham) become corrupt (fall into corruption), there will be no good left in you. And a group from my Ummah will always remain victorious upon the truth; whoever tries to disgrace (or abandon) them will not be able to harm them until the Hour is established."""
"703","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you fights his brother (or strikes him), he should avoid (striking) the face."""
"704","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you says Amin in prayer and the angels in the heaven also say Amin, and the (saying) of one of them coincides with the other, the past sins of that (person who said Amin) are forgiven."""
"705","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the imam says Sami'allahu liman hamidah, then say Allahumma Rabbana lakal-hamd, for whoever's words coincide with the words of the angels, his past sins are forgiven."""
"706","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the imam says Sami'allahu liman hamidah, then say Allahumma Rabbana wa lakal-hamd."""
"707","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the imam says: Ghayril-maghdubi 'alayhim wa lad-dallin (not of those who have earned anger, nor of those who go astray) [Surah al-Fatihah: 7], then say Amin, for whoever's words coincide with the words of the angels, his past sins are forgiven."""
"708","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person says to his brother: Jazakallahu khayran (May Allah reward you with good), then he has indeed fully discharged the right of praising him."""
"709","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person says to his brother: 'O disbeliever!', then one of the two certainly becomes deserving of it (the verdict of disbelief) (that is, if the other is not truly a disbeliever, the one who said it himself falls under that disbelief)."""
"710","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person says to his brother: 'O disbeliever!', it is like killing him, and cursing a believer is also like killing him."""
"711","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person calls a hypocrite Ya sayyidi (O my master or chief), he has certainly angered his Lord."""
"712","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person says, 'The people are ruined,' he is the most ruined of them all (or he is the one who ruins them by spreading his despair)."""
"713","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the servant says: La ilaha illallahu wallahu akbar (There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest), Allah Almighty says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, and I am the Greatest. Then when he says: La ilaha illallahu wahdahu, Allah says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, I am alone. Then when he says: La ilaha illallahu la sharika lahu, Allah says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, and I have no partner. Then when he says: La ilaha illallahu lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamd, Allah says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, the dominion is Mine alone and all praise is for Me alone. Then when he says: La ilaha illallahu wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah, Allah says: My servant has spoken the truth; there is no god but Me, and the power to avoid sins and the strength to do good come only through My enabling. Whoever is granted (the recitation of) these words at the time of his death, the Fire of Hell will not touch him."""
"714","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the muezzin says: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, and one of you says (in response): Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; then the muezzin says: Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah, and he says: Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah; then the muezzin says: Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah, and he says: Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasulullah; then the muezzin says: Hayya 'alas-salah, and he says: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah; then the muezzin says: Hayya 'alal-falah, and he says: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah; then the muezzin says: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, and he says: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar; then the muezzin says: La ilaha illallah, and he too says from the sincerity of his heart: La ilaha illallah, then he will enter Paradise."""
"715","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you stands for prayer, he should not spit in front of him, for as long as he is at his place of prayer he is conversing intimately with Allah, the Blessed and Exalted; nor should he spit to his right, for on his right there is an angel. Rather, he should spit to his left or under his foot and bury it (in the soil)."""
"716","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you gets up from his bed and then returns to it, he should dust it off three times with the edge of his lower garment, for he does not know what came onto the bed after he left it. And when he lies down, he should recite this supplication: 'Bismika Rabbi wada'tu janbi wa bika arfa'uhu, fa-in amsakta nafsi farhamha, wa in arsaltaha fahfazha bima tahfazu bihi 'ibadakas-salihin' (O my Lord, with Your name I have laid down my side and by Your help I will raise it; so if You withhold my soul (in the state of sleep), have mercy on it, and if You release it (by giving it life again), protect it in the same way that You protect Your righteous servants). Then when he wakes up, he should recite this supplication: 'Alhamdu lillahil-ladhi 'afani fi jasadi wa radda 'alayya ruhi wa adhina li bi-dhikrihi' (All praise is for Allah who granted me well-being in my body, returned my soul to me, and enabled me to remember Him)."""
"717","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you stands at night (for tahajjud) and the Qur'an falters on his tongue (that is, he cannot recite properly because sleep overcomes him) and he does not understand what he is reciting, he should lie down."""
"718","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you wakes up from sleep and intends to perform ablution, he should not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night or on what he placed it."""
"719","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you stands to pray, if there is something in front of him equal to the back post of a camel's saddle, it serves as a sutrah (barrier) for him. But if there is nothing in front of him equal to the back post of the saddle, then a donkey, a woman and a black dog cut off his prayer. It was asked: What is special about the black dog, when red (or other coloured) dogs do not do this? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The black dog is a devil."""
"720","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you stands to pray at night, he should use the miswak, for when one of you recites in his prayer, an angel places its mouth on his mouth, and whatever (letter of the Qur'an) comes out of his mouth enters directly into the angel's mouth."""
"721","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the imam, after praying two rak'ahs, begins to stand up (forgetfully, instead of sitting), then if he remembers before standing fully upright, he should sit down; and if he has stood fully upright, he should not sit down, and he should perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness (sajdah al-sahw) (at the end of the prayer)."""
"722","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person gets up from his sitting place (for some task) and then returns to the same place, he has more right to it (the place)."""
"723","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person stands to perform ablution by night or by day, performs the ablution well and uses the miswak, then stands and prays, the angel circles around him and comes so close to him that it places its mouth on his mouth, so whatever he recites goes into its (the angel's) mouth. And if he does not use the miswak, the angel circles around him but does not place its mouth on his mouth."""
"724","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the deceased is buried in the grave, two angels come to him, black in complexion and with blue eyes; one of them is called Munkar and the other Nakir. They both ask: What did you used to say about this man (that is, Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him))? He says what he used to say (in the world): He is the servant of Allah and His Messenger; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger. The angels say: We knew that you would say this. Then his grave is widened for him, seventy cubits long and seventy cubits wide, then it is illuminated for him, and it is said to him: Sleep. He says: I want to go back to my family and give them this good news. The angels say: Sleep like the bride who is woken only by the one among her family who is most beloved to her, until Allah Almighty raises him from this resting place of his. And if he (the deceased) was a hypocrite, he says: I heard the people saying something, so I said the same; I (in reality) knew nothing. The angels say: We knew that you would say this. Then the earth is commanded: Close in upon him. So it becomes so tight upon him that his ribs interlock with one another, and he continues to suffer punishment in it until Allah Almighty raises him from this resting place of his."""
"725","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you returns (from a journey) at night, he should not come to his family suddenly at night, so that the woman whose husband was away may remove her pubic hair and the woman with dishevelled hair may comb her hair."""
"726","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the evening meal has been served and the time of prayer has come, eat before you pray the Maghrib prayer, and do not hurry in your meal."""
"727","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the son of Adam recites a verse of prostration and prostrates, Satan withdraws weeping and says: Woe to me! The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate and he prostrated, so Paradise is his; and I was commanded to prostrate and I disobeyed, so the Fire of Hell is mine."""
"728","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the imam recites, remain silent."""
"729","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you recite Alhamdu lillah, then also recite Bismillahir-Rahmanir-Rahim, for it (Surah al-Fatihah) is Umm al-Qur'an, Umm al-Kitab and the seven oft-repeated verses (al-Sab' al-Mathani), and Bismillahir-Rahmanir-Rahim is one of its verses."""
"730","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When land has been divided and boundaries have been fixed, then no right of pre-emption (shuf'ah) remains in it."""
"731","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has performed his (obligatory) prayer in the mosque, he should also keep a portion of his prayers (the voluntary and sunnah prayers) for his home, for Allah Almighty will bring about good in his home through the blessing of his prayer."""
"732","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has completed his Hajj, he should hasten to return to his family, for this is a means of increasing his reward."""
"733","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has completed his prayer in the mosque and then returns to his home, he should pray two rak'ahs in his home and also set aside a portion of his prayers for his home, for Allah Almighty will bring about good in his home through the blessing of his prayer."""
"734","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty decrees a matter in the heaven, the angels beat their wings in submission to His word, making a sound as though a chain were being dragged over a smooth, clean rock. Then when fear is removed from their hearts, they ask one another: Madha qala Rabbukum (What did your Lord say?) The angels reply: Qalul-haqqa wa huwal-'aliyyul-kabir (He said the truth, and He is the Most High, the Most Great). [Surah Saba: 23] Then the stealthy eavesdroppers (the devils) hear this word, and these stealthy eavesdroppers are layered one above another in this way. Sometimes the flame of fire (the shooting star) overtakes the one listening before he can pass the word on to his companion below him, and burns him to ashes; and sometimes the flame does not reach him until he has passed the word on to the one below him, until they convey it to the earth. Then the word is cast into the mouth of the sorcerer (or soothsayer), and he relates it mixed with a hundred lies. Then (when that one word turns out true) he is believed, and the people say: Did he not tell us on such-and-such a day that such-and-such would happen? And we found it true. And this is because of that one word which was heard from the heaven."""
"735","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty decrees for a servant that he will die in a particular land (or region), Allah Almighty creates for him some need (or task) in that place (so that he reaches it)."""
"736","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man sits between the four limbs (hands and feet) of the woman and the circumcised part touches the circumcised part (that is, the private parts meet), then ghusl becomes obligatory."""
"737","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On Friday, while the imam is delivering the sermon, if you so much as say to your companion, 'Be quiet,' then you too have engaged in idle talk."""
"738","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you stand for prayer, perform ablution thoroughly and completely, then face the qiblah and say the takbir, then recite whatever of the Qur'an is easy for you, then bow until you are at rest in bowing, then rise until you stand upright, then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration, then rise until you stand upright, then do likewise throughout your whole prayer."""
"739","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you stand for prayer, perform ablution thoroughly and completely, and make the water reach between the fingers of your hands and the toes of your feet (by running your fingers through them)."""
"740","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you stand for prayer, perform ablution as Allah has commanded you, then stand and face the qiblah, then say the takbir. If you know some of the Qur'an, recite it; and if you do not know any of the Qur'an, then praise Allah (say Alhamdu lillah), declare His oneness (say La ilaha illallah) and declare His greatness (say Allahu akbar). Then when you bow, bow with composure, then raise your head and stand upright, then prostrate with balance and stillness in your prostration, then raise your head and sit upright, until you complete your prayer. If you have done this, your prayer is complete; and if you have left out any of it, you have in fact diminished your own prayer."""
"741","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you stand for prayer, say the takbir, then recite whatever of the Qur'an is easy for you, then bow until you are at rest in bowing, then rise until you stand upright, then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration, then rise until you are sitting at rest, then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration, then do likewise throughout your whole prayer."""
"742","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you stand in your prayer, pray like one who is bidding farewell (that is, one praying the last prayer of his life), do not say anything for which you will (later) have to apologise, and give up all hope in what is in the hands of people (that is, place your hope in Allah alone)."""
"743","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you stand in prayer, do not go ahead of your reciter (that is, the imam) in bowing and prostration; rather, he should do so before you."""
"744","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two people are conversing privately, do not come in between them (that is, do not interfere in their private conversation)."""
"745","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the appointed time of death of one of you is set in a (particular) land, some need (or task) is created for him there; then when he reaches the last of his footsteps, Allah Almighty takes his soul, and on the Day of Resurrection that land will say: O my Lord, this is the trust that You entrusted to me."""
"746","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is fasting, he should break his fast with dates; and if he does not find dates, then he should break it with water, for water is purifying."""
"747","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is poor (or in need), he should begin (in charity and spending) with himself; then if anything is left over, on his dependants; then if anything is left over, on his relatives; and if something is still left over, then he should spend it here and there (that is, on other deserving people)."""
"748","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is sitting in the sun and the shade moves away from him, so that part of him is in the shade and part of him is in the sun, he should get up from there."""
"749","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in prayer, he should not raise his gaze to the sky, lest his sight be snatched away (that is, taken from him)."""
"750","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in prayer and feels some movement in his back passage (anus) and is in doubt whether his ablution has been broken or not, then when the matter is unclear to him, he should not turn away (leaving the prayer) until he hears a sound or perceives a smell."""
"751","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in the mosque and senses wind (being passed) between his buttocks, he should not go out (of the mosque) until he hears a sound or perceives a smell."""
"752","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is in prayer, he is conversing intimately with his Lord, so each one of you should consider what he is saying in his prayer; and do not raise your voices, lest you cause harm to the (other) believers."""
"753","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is praying, he should not spit in front of his face, for when he prays, Allah Almighty is in front of his face."""
"754","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is praying, he should not let anyone pass in front of him, and he should push him back as much as he can. If he refuses, then let him deal with him sternly, for he is nothing but a devil."""
"755","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is praying, he should not let anyone pass in front of him, and he should push him back as much as he can. If he refuses, then let him deal with him sternly, for there is a devil (his qarin, companion) with him."""
"756","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you is praying, he should not raise his gaze to the sky, lest it be snatched away (that is, lest his sight be taken)."""
"757","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If (my life) remains until next year, we will also fast on the ninth (of Muharram)."""
"758","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When water amounts to two qullahs (a particular large measure), it does not become impure (najis)."""
"759","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the first night of the month of Ramadan, the devils and the rebellious jinn are chained, and the gates of Hell are closed, so not one of its gates is opened, and the gates of Paradise are opened, so not one of its gates is closed. And every night a caller calls out: 'O seeker of good, come forward! And O seeker of evil, desist!' And Allah frees many people from the Fire, and that happens every night."""
"760","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When there is strife (and civil war) among the Muslims, make yourself a sword of wood (that is, take no part at all in their fighting among themselves)."""
"761","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man has two wives and does not treat them justly, he will come on the Day of Resurrection with half of his body fallen (paralysed)."""
"762","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When three people are together, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third."""
"763","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When three people are on a journey, they should appoint one of themselves as their leader (amir)."""
"764","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the first darkness of night begins to fall, keep your children (from going out), for the devils spread out at that time. Then when an hour of the night has passed, let them go. Close the doors and mention the name of Allah, for the devil does not open a closed door. Tie up the mouths of your waterskins and mention the name of Allah, and cover your vessels and mention the name of Allah, even if you only place something across them, and put out your lamps."""
"765","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is menstrual blood, it is black blood that is recognisable. So when that comes, refrain from prayer; and when it is the other kind (istihadah, that is, blood of illness), perform ablution (for each prayer) and pray, for it is only the blood of a vein."""
"766","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the month of Ramadan comes, perform Umrah in it, for performing Umrah in this month carries a reward equal to a Hajj."""
"767","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is some matter of your worldly affairs, you understand it better; and when it is some matter concerning your religion, then bring it to me (that is, follow me)."""
"768","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has two garments, he should pray wearing both of them (the lower wrap and the upper sheet). If he has only one garment, he should tie it as a lower wrap and should not wrap himself in it the way the Jews do (leaving the shoulders bare)."""
"769","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the servant of one of you has borne the toil (of preparing food) for him and brought it, he should feed him from it as well. If he does not do so (by seating him with him), then let him at least hand him a morsel or two (from it)."""
"770","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you has hair (on his head), he should honour it and look after it (that is, wash it, oil it and keep it groomed)."""
"771","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the night of the middle (the fifteenth) of Sha'ban, Allah Almighty looks upon His creation with a special manifestation. He forgives the believers, gives respite to the disbelievers, and leaves the people of rancour in their state because of their rancour until they abandon it (the harbouring of rancour)."""
"772","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When there are three people (together), two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third."""
"773","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When there are three people, one of them should lead them in prayer, and the one most entitled to lead is the one among them with the most knowledge of the Noble Qur'an."""
"774","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is Friday, the angels sit at the doors of the mosque and record the people who come according to their ranks (that is, the time of their arrival). So one man is like the one who offers a camel in sacrifice, another like the one who offers a cow in sacrifice, another like the one who offers a goat in sacrifice, another like the one who offers a hen, another like the one who offers a sparrow, and another like the one who offers an egg. Then when the muezzin gives the call to prayer and the imam sits on the pulpit, they (the angels) roll up their registers, enter the mosque and listen to the remembrance (the sermon)."""
"775","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is Friday, at every one of the doors of the mosque there are angels who record the people according to their ranks, the first and then the one after him. Then when the imam sits (on the pulpit), they roll up their registers and come to listen to the remembrance (the sermon). The one who comes early (for the Friday prayer) is like one who offers a camel (in charity), then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a ram, then like one who offers a hen, and then like one who offers an egg."""
"776","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is Friday and the night of Friday, send abundant blessings (durud) upon me."""
"777","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the Day of Resurrection, the sun will be brought so close to the servants that it will be at a distance of one or two miles. The sun will scorch them, and people will be immersed in sweat according to their deeds: among them will be one whose sweat reaches his ankles, one whose sweat reaches his knees, one whose sweat reaches his waist, and one whom the sweat will have bridled (that is, it will reach his mouth)."""
"778","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the Day of Resurrection, Allah Almighty will give every individual of this (Muhammadan) Ummah a man from among the disbelievers, and it will be said to him: 'This is your ransom from the Fire of Hell.'"""
"779","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the Day of Resurrection, Allah Almighty will send to every believer an angel with whom there will be a disbeliever. The angel will say to the believer: 'O believer, take this disbeliever; this is your ransom from the Fire of Hell.'"""
"780","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the Day of Resurrection, I will intercede and say: 'O my Lord, admit into Paradise everyone who has in his heart faith even the size of a mustard seed.' So they will enter Paradise. Then he says: 'Admit into Paradise also everyone who has in his heart the least thing (of faith, even less than that).'"""
"781","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the Day of Resurrection, I will be the imam of all the prophets, their spokesman, and their intercessor, and I say this without pride."""
"782","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the Day of Resurrection, a caller will call out: 'Whoever did a deed for anyone other than Allah, let him seek his reward from the one for whom he did it.'"""
"783","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When it is the day of fasting for one of you, he should neither speak obscenely nor behave ignorantly (with clamour). If someone abuses him or fights with him, he should say (to him): 'I am fasting, I am fasting.'"""
"784","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the imam says the takbir, you also say the takbir; when he bows, you also bow; when he prostrates, you also prostrate; when he raises his head from bowing, you also raise your heads; and when he leads the prayer sitting, all of you pray sitting."""
"785","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When two parties both dislike taking the oath, or both like it (that is, both are claimants), they should cast lots over it."""
"786","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you are three, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the other until you mingle with (other) people, for that will grieve him (the third)."""
"787","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you dress and when you perform ablution, begin with your right side."""
"788","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the devil plays with one of you in his sleep (that is, shows him a bad or frightening dream), he should not tell people about it."""
"789","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you meets his brother, he should greet him with salam. Then if a tree, a wall or a stone comes between them and he meets him (again), he should greet him with salam (again)."""
"790","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man meets his Muslim brother, he should say: As-salamu alaykum wa rahmatullah (Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah)."""
"791","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you meet the polytheists on the road, do not initiate the greeting of salam with them, and compel them to the narrowest part of the road."""
"792","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you dies, his abode is presented to him morning and evening: if he is among the people of Paradise, then (his place) among the people of Paradise, and if he is among the people of Hell, then among the people of Hell. And it is said to him: 'This is your abode, until Allah Almighty raises you to it on the Day of Resurrection.'"""
"793","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person dies, his deeds are cut off except for three things: an ongoing charity (sadaqah jariyah), or knowledge from which benefit is derived, or a righteous child who prays for him."""
"794","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a companion of yours dies, leave him alone, and do not speak ill of him."""
"795","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant's child dies, Allah Almighty says to His angels: 'Have you taken the soul of My servant's child?' They say: 'Yes.' Then Allah says: 'Have you taken the fruit (the piece) of his heart?' They say: 'Yes.' Then Allah says: 'So what did My servant say?' They say: 'He praised You and said: Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un (We belong to Allah and to Him we return).' Then Allah Almighty says: 'Build for My servant a house in Paradise and name it Bayt al-Hamd (the House of Praise).'"""
"796","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you passes through our mosque or our marketplace carrying arrows, he should hold their heads in his fist, so that he does not wound any Muslim."""
"797","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When forty-two nights have passed over the drop of fluid (after its settling in the mother's womb), Allah Almighty sends an angel to it who shapes it and creates its hearing, its sight, its skin, its flesh and its bones. Then he says: 'O my Lord, will it be male or female?' And your Lord decrees what He wills, and the angel writes it down. Then he says: 'O my Lord, what is its term of life?' And your Lord says what He wills, and the angel writes it down. Then he says: 'O my Lord, what is its provision?' And your Lord decrees what He wills, and the angel writes it down. Then the angel goes out with the scroll (the record of destiny) in his hand, and he neither adds to the command nor takes anything away from it."""
"798","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When some men pass by a group of people and one of those passing greets those sitting with salam, and one of these (sitting) returns the greeting, it suffices on behalf of these (passing) and on behalf of these (sitting)."""
"799","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant falls ill or goes on a journey, Allah Almighty records for him a reward equal to the (good) deeds he used to do while healthy and resident."""
"800","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a servant falls ill, Allah Almighty says to the Kiraman Katibin (the noble angels who record deeds): 'Keep writing for My servant a reward like that of the deeds he used to do (while healthy), until I take his soul or grant him recovery.'"""
"801","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When my Ummah walks with a swagger (out of arrogance) and the sons of kings, that is, the princes of Persia and Rome, serve them, then the worst of the Ummah will be given power over its best."""
"802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When half of the night or two thirds of it has passed, Allah Almighty descends to the lowest heaven and says: 'Is there anyone asking, that he may be given? Is there anyone supplicating, that his supplication may be answered? Is there anyone seeking forgiveness, that he may be forgiven?' (Allah Almighty continues to call out in this way) until the true dawn breaks."""
"803","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the caller (the mu'adhdhin) calls the adhan, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered."""
"804","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you goes to sleep with the grease (or smell) of meat on his hand and has not washed his hand, and then some harm befalls him, let him blame no one but himself."""
"805","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you stops at a place to camp, let him say: 'A'udhu bi-kalimatillahit-tammati min sharri ma khalaq' (I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created), and nothing will harm him until he departs from that place."""
"806","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you forgets to mention the name of Allah over his food and then remembers, let him say: 'Bismillahi awwalahu wa akhirahu' (In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end)."""
"807","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you forgets a prayer or sleeps through it, let him pray it when he remembers it."""
"808","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you looks at someone who has been given more than him in wealth and physical form (or status), let him also look at someone who is below him (in these things)."""
"809","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you becomes drowsy while sitting in the mosque, let him get up from that place and move to another."""
"810","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you becomes drowsy while praying, let him sleep until his sleepiness leaves him, for when one of you prays while drowsy, he does not know; perhaps instead of asking for forgiveness he may (by mistake) end up cursing himself."""
"811","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you becomes drowsy during the prayer, let him leave the prayer and sleep until he understands what he is saying."""
"812","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you becomes drowsy on Friday, let him move to his companion's seat, and let his companion move to his seat."""
"813","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man becomes drowsy while praying, let him leave the prayer, lest he end up supplicating against himself without realising it."""
"814","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a slave marries without the permission of his master, his marriage is void."""
"815","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you go to sleep, put out the lamp, for the mouse drags away the (burning) wick and burns the people of the house. Also, close the doors, tie up the mouths of the waterskins and cover the drinks."""
"816","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you go to sleep, put out your lamps, for Satan guides things like this (mouse) to this (burning lamp), and so it burns you."""
"817","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the call to prayer is made, Satan turns his back and flees, breaking wind, so that he does not hear the adhan. Then when the adhan is finished he comes back, until when the iqamah for the prayer is called he again turns his back and flees. And when the iqamah is finished he comes back again, until he comes between a person and his heart, casting whispers and saying: 'Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such,' that is, things he had not remembered before, until the person no longer knows how many rak'ahs he has prayed."""
"818","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the adhan is called for prayer, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered."""
"819","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a donkey brays, seek refuge with Allah from Satan the accursed."""
"820","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you feels pain, let him place his hand where he feels the pain and say seven times: 'A'udhu bi-'izzatillahi wa qudratihi 'ala kulli shay'in min sharri ma ajid' (I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power over all things from the evil of the pain I feel)."""
"821","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you finds that, meaning madhi (sees it coming out), let him wash his private part and perform ablution like the ablution done for prayer."""
"822","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you feels some disturbance in his stomach and is in doubt whether something (wind) has come out of him or not, let him not leave the mosque at all until he hears a sound or perceives a smell."""
"823","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you, during his prayer, perceives the sound of passing wind or a disturbance in his stomach, let him withdraw (from the prayer) and perform ablution."""
"824","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a woman sees in a dream what a man sees (that is, she has a wet dream), then taking a ritual bath (ghusl) is obligatory upon her."""
"825","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you weigh (something), weigh so that the scale tips (that is, give a little extra)."""
"826","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When affairs are entrusted to those who are unfit for them, then wait for the Hour."""
"827","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you places in front of him (for prayer) something the size of the back post of a camel saddle (as a sutrah), let him pray and not mind who passes beyond that (sutrah)."""
"828","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the sword is placed among my Ummah (that is, when killing among themselves begins), it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection."""
"829","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the food is laid out, eat from the edges of the dish and leave its middle, for blessing descends in the middle of the dish."""
"830","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the bier is made ready and set down, and men lift it onto their shoulders, then if the deceased was righteous it says: 'Take me forward quickly,' and if it was not righteous it cries out to its family: 'Oh, woe to it! Where are you taking it?' Everything hears its voice except man, and if man were to hear that voice he would fall down unconscious."""
"831","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the evening meal of one of you has been brought and set down and the iqamah for the prayer has also been called, eat first, and do not hasten (to go to the prayer) until you have finished eating."""
"832","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you lower your dead into their graves, recite this supplication: 'Bismillahi wa 'ala sunnati Rasulillah' (In the name of Allah and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah)."""
"833","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you treads on some filth with his shoes, then indeed the (clean) earth (of the road) purifies it."""
"834","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a person treads on some filth with his leather socks, then what purifies them both is earth."""
"835","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him immerse it (completely in the drink), for in one of its wings there is disease and in the other there is cure. And when it falls it puts forward the very wing that carries the disease, so let him immerse it completely and then take it out and throw it away."""
"836","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him dip it thoroughly into it (the drink), for in one of its wings there is poison and in the other there is cure. And it puts the wing with the poison forward and keeps the wing with the cure back."""
"837","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a fly falls into the drink of one of you, let him immerse it and then take it out, for in one of its wings there is disease and in the other there is cure."""
"838","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the boundaries of the property have been marked out and the paths have been separated, then the right of pre-emption (shuf'ah) no longer remains."""
"839","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a man enters his house, let him recite this supplication: 'Allahumma inni as'aluka khayral-mawlaji wa khayral-makhraji, bismillahi walajna wa bismillahi kharajna wa 'alallahi rabbina tawakkalna' (O Allah, I ask You for the good of entering and the good of leaving. In the name of Allah we have entered, and in the name of Allah we have left, and upon Allah, our Lord, we have relied). After that, let him greet his family with salam."""
"840","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog laps from a vessel, wash it seven times, and the eighth time scrub it well with earth."""
"841","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog laps from the vessel of one of you, let him pour out (what is in it) and then wash it seven times."""
"842","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog laps from the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times."""
"843","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a dog laps from the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times, the first of them with earth."""
"844","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you takes charge of preparing and shrouding his brother, let him shroud him in a good shroud."""
"845","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you takes charge of preparing and shrouding his brother, let him shroud him in a good shroud, for they (the dead) will be raised in their shrouds and will visit one another in those very shrouds."""
"846","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Chosroes perishes, there will be no Chosroes after him, and when Caesar perishes, there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, you will certainly spend the treasures of these two (kings) in the way of Allah."""
"847","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When one of you intends to do some (important) matter, let him pray two rak'ahs other than the obligatory prayer, then let him supplicate: 'Allahumma inni astakhiruka bi-'ilmika wa astaqdiruka bi-qudratika wa as'aluka min fadlikal-'azim, fa-innaka taqdiru wa la aqdiru wa ta'lamu wa la a'lamu wa anta 'allamul-ghuyub. Allahumma fa-in kunta ta'lamu hadhal-amra (and he names it) khayran li fi dini wa ma'ashi wa 'aqibati amri faqdurhu li wa yassirhu li thumma barik li fihi. Allahumma wa in kunta ta'lamuhu sharran li fi dini wa ma'ashi wa 'aqibati amri fasrifni 'anhu wasrifhu 'anni waqdur liyal-khayra haythu kana thumma raddini bihi' (O Allah, I seek good from You by means of Your knowledge, and I ask You for strength by means of Your power, and I ask You of Your immense bounty, for You have power and I have none, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of all things unseen. O Allah, if You know that this matter (here he names the matter) is good for me in my religion, my worldly affairs, my life and my final outcome, then decree it for me, make it easy for me, and then bless me in it. And O Allah, if You know that this matter is bad for me in my religion, my worldly affairs and my final outcome, then turn me away from it and turn it away from me, and decree good for me wherever it may be, and then make me pleased with it)."""
"848","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Slaughter for the sake of Allah in whatever month it may be, do good deeds for Allah, and feed people."""
"849","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remember death in your prayer, for when a man remembers death in his prayer, it is very likely that he will perform his prayer well. And pray the prayer of a man who is not certain that he will pray any other prayer after it (that is, consider it the last prayer of your life). And guard yourself against every deed for which one has to make an apology."""
"850","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Announce among the people that whoever (has eaten or drunk something) should remain like those who are fasting for the rest of his day, and whoever has not yet eaten anything should fast, for today is the day of Ashura."""
"851","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Announce among the people that whoever bears witness with sincerity of heart that there is no true god except Allah, He is alone and He has no partner, will enter Paradise."""
"852","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The sign of my permission for you to come in is that the curtain is raised and that you can hear my voice (or my private talk), until I forbid you from it (at some particular time)."""
"853","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been permitted to tell about one of the angels who carry the Throne: his feet are in the lowest earth and the Throne is upon his horn (head), and the distance between the lobe of his ear and his shoulder is as much as a flying bird covers in seven hundred years. And that angel keeps repeating this glorification: ""Subhanaka haythu kunta"" (You are free of all imperfection, O Allah, wherever You are)."""
"854","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been permitted to tell about one of the angels of Allah Almighty who carry the Throne: the distance between the lobe of his ear and his shoulder is a journey of seven hundred years."""
"855","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite this supplication: ""Adhhibil-ba'sa Rabban-nas, ishfi Antash-Shafi, la shifa'a illa shifa'uka, shifa'an la yughadiru saqaman"" (O Lord of the people, remove this affliction and grant healing; You are the Healer, there is no healing except Your healing; grant a healing that leaves behind no illness of any kind)."""
"856","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Both of you go and make every effort (to reach what is right), then divide (the shares) by casting lots, and then let each of you ask his companion for pardon and so make (the matter) lawful."""
"857","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take these two sandals of mine, and whoever you meet behind this garden who bears witness, with firm certainty in his heart, that there is no true god except Allah, give him the glad tidings of Paradise."""
"858","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go and take a ritual bath (ghusl) with water and lote-tree leaves, and shave off from your body the hair of (the time of) disbelief."""
"859","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go and look at her (the woman you wish to marry), for doing so is more likely to create love and harmony between the two of you."""
"860","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go, in that house there are three people, among whom is a slave boy who has prayed. Take him, and do not beat him, for we have been forbidden from beating those who pray."""
"861","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go, I have given her to you in marriage on the basis of the Qur'an that you have (memorised)."""
"862","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go and tell your master (Badhan, the governor of Yemen) that my Lord has killed his lord, that is, Kisra, tonight."""
"863","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take this (leftover ablution) water, then when you reach your town, demolish your church (or temple), sprinkle this water on its site, and make it a mosque."""
"864","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take this embroidered cloak to Abu Jahm bin Hudhayfah and bring me his coarse (plain) cloak, for this (embroidered cloak) distracted me in my prayer just now."""
"865","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take him, that is, Abu Quhafah, to one of his wives so that she may change the colour of his (hair) with something (a dye), but keep him away from black."""
"866","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My view is that you should distribute it (this garden) among your close relatives (as charity)."""
"867","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I see that your dreams (concerning Laylat al-Qadr) have agreed on the last seven nights, so whoever is seeking it (Laylat al-Qadr) should seek it in the last seven nights (of Ramadan)."""
"868","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most compassionate of my Ummah towards my Ummah is Abu Bakr, the sternest (firmest) in the matter of Allah's religion is Umar, the one among them with the truest modesty is Uthman, the best of them in giving judgement is Ali, the greatest expert in the knowledge of inheritance shares (fara'id) is Zayd bin Thabit, the best reciter among them is Ubayy bin Ka'b, and the most knowledgeable about the lawful and the unlawful is Mu'adh bin Jabal. Behold! Indeed every Ummah has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this Ummah is Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah."""
"869","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tonight I saw myself (in a dream) near the Ka'bah, and I saw a man of wheat-brown complexion, the most handsome of wheat-brown men you could ever see. He had hair reaching down to his earlobes, the most beautiful of such hair; he had combed it and water was dripping from it. He was leaning on two men and performing tawaf around the House. I asked: Who is this? I was told: This is the Messiah, son of Maryam (peace be upon them both). Then suddenly I saw a man with extremely curly hair, blind in his right eye, as if it were a protruding (swollen) grape. I asked: Who is this? I was told: This is the Messiah, the Dajjal."""
"870","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw in a dream that I was cleaning my teeth with a miswak, then two men came to me, one of them older than the other. I handed the miswak to the younger of them, and it was said to me: Give it to the older one. So I gave that miswak to the older of them."""
"871","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you see this night of yours? At the completion of one hundred years from tonight, not a single one of those who are on the face of the earth will remain alive."""
"872","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The worst degree of usury (riba) is attacking people's honour (without right) (by speaking against them)."""
"873","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are four traits which, if they are found in you, then you have no cause for regret (loss) over whatever of this world passes you by: speaking the truth, safeguarding trusts, having good character, and purity in one's sustenance (food and drink) (taking care that it is lawful)."""
"874","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four phrases are the best of speech, and there is no harm in whichever of them you begin with: ""Subhan Allah"" (Glory be to Allah), ""Al-hamdu lillah"" (All praise is for Allah), ""La ilaha illallah"" (There is no god but Allah) and ""Allahu Akbar"" (Allah is the Greatest)."""
"875","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four things of the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah) have remained in my Ummah which people will not abandon: boasting about one's lineage, taunting the lineage of others, seeking rain from the stars, and wailing over the dead. And indeed, the wailing woman, if she does not repent before her death, will come on the Day of Resurrection wearing a garment of sulphur (tar) and a shirt of flames of fire."""
"876","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four of the rivers of Paradise (among the waters sent into the world) are these: Sayhan, Jayhan, the Nile and the Euphrates."""
"877","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are four people whose reward continues for them even after death: the one who died guarding the frontiers (ribat) in the path of Allah; the one who taught someone (religious) knowledge, for as long as that knowledge is acted upon he will continue to receive its reward; the one who gave some charity, for as long as that charity remains (as ongoing charity) he will continue to receive its reward; and the one who left behind a righteous child who supplicates (for forgiveness) for him."""
"878","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are four (kinds of) dinars (that are spent): a dinar you gave to a poor person, a dinar you spent on freeing a slave, a dinar you spent in the path of Allah (for jihad), and a dinar you spent on your family. The best of them all (and the most rewarding) is the dinar you spent on your family."""
"879","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four among the animals (and birds) are not to be killed (for killing them is forbidden): the ant, the honeybee, the hoopoe and the surad (a kind of bird of prey)."""
"880","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are four kinds of people whom Allah Almighty intensely hates (and dislikes): the trader who sells his goods by swearing many oaths, the arrogant poor (needy) person, the old man who commits adultery, and the tyrannical ruler."""
"881","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four people will present their argument (excuse) on the Day of Resurrection: a deaf man who could hear nothing, a foolish (insane) man, an extremely old man, and a man who died during the fatrah (the interval between two messengers). The deaf man will say: O Lord, Islam came but I could not hear anything. The foolish man will say: O Lord, Islam came but I understood nothing, and children used to throw dung at me. The extremely old man will say: O Lord, Islam came but my mind did not function. And the one who died during the fatrah will say: O Lord, no messenger of Yours came to me. Then Allah Almighty will take a covenant from them that they will surely obey Him, and He will send a message to them: Enter the Fire. Whoever enters it, it will become cool and safe for him, and whoever does not enter it will be dragged into it."""
"882","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four rak'ahs before Zuhr are equal (in reward) to the prayer at the time of suhur (tahajjud)."""
"883","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are four practices of the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah) in my Ummah which people will not abandon: boasting about lineage and descent, taunting the lineage of others, seeking rain through the stars, and wailing (over the dead)."""
"884","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are four things of the Days of Ignorance (Jahiliyyah) in my Ummah which people will not give up: taunting lineage, wailing over the dead, attributing rain to the stars, saying that it rained on us because of such and such a star, and the belief in contagion, that one camel gets mange and it infects a hundred camels with mange. (If that is so,) then who gave mange to the first camel?!"""
"885","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The four rak'ahs before Zuhr in which the salam is not given in between (that is, they are prayed together), the gates of the heaven are opened for them."""
"886","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four kinds of animals are not valid for sacrifice: the one-eyed animal whose one-eyedness is evident, the sick animal whose sickness is evident, the lame animal whose lameness is evident, and the emaciated (weak) animal that has no marrow left in its bones."""
"887","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four things are part of happiness: a righteous wife, a spacious house, a righteous neighbour and a comfortable mount. And four things are part of misery: a bad wife, a bad neighbour, a bad mount and a cramped house."""
"888","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the deeds of the living, four (are such that their reward) continues for the dead: a man who left behind righteous children who supplicate for him, so their supplication benefits him; a man who gave an ongoing charity to continue after him, so he will receive its reward for as long as it continues; and a man who taught knowledge which was then acted upon after him, so he will receive a reward equal to that of the one who acts upon it, without anything being reduced from the reward of the one who acts upon it."""
"889","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has four traits will be a pure hypocrite, and whoever has one of these traits will have a trait of hypocrisy until he abandons it: when he is entrusted with something, he betrays; when he speaks, he lies; when he makes a covenant, he acts treacherously; and when he quarrels, he uses abusive language."""
"890","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever has four traits will be a pure hypocrite, and whoever has one of these traits will have a trait of hypocrisy until he abandons it: when he speaks, he lies; when he makes a promise, he breaks it; when he makes a covenant, he acts treacherously; and when he quarrels, he uses abusive language."""
"891","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are forty good traits, the highest of which is giving someone a she-goat to drink its milk. Any servant who acts upon any one of these traits, hoping for its reward and believing in the promise made for it, Allah Almighty will admit him into Paradise because of it."""
"892","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Go back to your parents and ask their permission (to go for jihad). If they give you permission, then fight in jihad; otherwise, treat them with kindness."""
"893","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Return to your families and stay among them, teach them (the religion) and command them (to do good), and pray just as you have seen me praying. Then when the time of prayer comes, let one of you call the adhan for you, and let the eldest of you lead you in prayer."""
"894","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take care of your close relatives, take care of your close relatives (that is, be diligent in maintaining ties of kinship)."""
"895","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most compassionate of my Ummah towards my Ummah is Abu Bakr, the sternest (firmest) of them in the matter of Allah (His religion) is Umar, the one among them with the truest modesty is Uthman, the best reciter among them of the Book of Allah is Ubayy bin Ka'b, the greatest expert in the knowledge of inheritance shares (fara'id) is Zayd bin Thabit, and the most knowledgeable about the lawful and the unlawful is Mu'adh bin Jabal. And every Ummah has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this Ummah is Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah."""
"896","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Show mercy to those who are on the earth, and the One who is in the heaven will show mercy to you."""
"897","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Show mercy (to people) and you will (also) be shown mercy, and forgive and you will (also) be forgiven. Woe to those who merely hear speech and let it pass straight out, and destruction to those who stubbornly persist (the obstinate ones), who knowingly persist in what (sins) they have done."""
"898","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Angel of Death was sent to Musa (peace be upon him). When he came to him, he slapped him and knocked out his eye. He returned to his Lord and said: You sent me to a servant who does not want to die. Allah Almighty restored his eye and said: Go back to him and tell him to place his hand on the back of a bull, and for every hair that his hand covers he will be given one year of life. He asked: O my Lord, then what will happen? Allah said: Then death. He said: Then now (give me death). So he supplicated to Allah Almighty to bring him as close to the Holy Land (Bayt al-Maqdis) as the distance of a stone's throw. If I were there, I would certainly show you his grave beside the road, beneath the red sand dune."""
"899","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The land of Paradise will be (like) white bread (that is, on the Day of Resurrection Allah Almighty will turn the earth into one enormous loaf, which the people of Paradise will eat)."""
"900","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give (in the way of Allah) little by little as much as you can, and do not hoard (your wealth) by counting it out, or else Allah Almighty will also withhold from you."""
"901","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep those who collect your charity (zakah) pleased."""
"902","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Raise your izar (lower garment or trousers) (above the ankles) and fear Allah."""
"903","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep away from the low-lying part of the valley of Uranah, and keep away from the low-lying part of the valley of Muhassir as well."""
"904","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep away from the low-lying part of the valley of Muhassir, and use small pebbles (for stoning) of the kind flicked between the fingers."""
"905","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take care of your subordinates (slaves), take care of your subordinates! Feed them from what you yourselves eat and clothe them from what you yourselves wear. And if they commit a sin (or mistake) that you do not wish to forgive, then sell these servants of Allah, but do not punish (torment) them."""
"906","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You may perform ruqyah (for treatment), as long as it contains no associating of partners with Allah (shirk)."""
"907","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ride the sacrificial animals in a reasonable manner as need requires, until you find another mount."""
"908","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ride these mounts while they are sound and leave them while they are sound, and do not make them into chairs for your conversations in the streets and markets (that is, do not sit on them talking at length), for many a ridden animal is better than its rider and remembers Allah more than he does."""
"909","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray these two rak'ahs, that is, the sunnah prayer after Maghrib, in your homes."""
"910","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stone the Jamrah (during the stoning rites) with pebbles like the small pebbles flicked between the fingers."""
"911","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O descendants of Isma'il! Practise archery, for indeed your father (Sayyiduna Isma'il (peace be upon him)) was also an excellent archer."""
"912","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The souls of the believers are in the bellies of green birds that keep eating from the fruit of the trees of Paradise, until Allah Almighty returns those souls to their bodies on the Day of Resurrection."""
"913","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was shown Paradise, and I saw in it the wife of Abu Talhah. Then I heard the sound of footsteps ahead of me, and it was Bilal."""
"914","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was shown some people of my Ummah travelling on the surface of the sea, seated like kings upon their thrones."""
"915","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You were shown to me twice in a dream. An angel was carrying you in a piece of silk and saying, 'This is your wife.' When I uncovered her, it was you. Upon that I would say, 'If this (dream) is from Allah Almighty, He will surely bring it to pass.'"""
"916","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was shown the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr), but then I was made to forget it. However, I saw myself prostrating in water and mud on its morning."""
"917","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was shown the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr), then one of my family woke me and I forgot it. So seek it in the remaining last ten nights (of Ramadan)."""
"918","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was shown the conditions my Ummah will face after me, and that they will shed one another's blood. This had already been decreed by Allah, just as it was for the nations before them. So I asked Allah to grant me the right of intercession for them on the Day of Resurrection, and He granted my request."""
"919","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lower garment (izar, or trousers) of the believer should reach to the middle of his shins."""
"920","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lower garment of the believer should reach to the muscle (fleshy part) of his shin, and then to the ankles. Whatever hangs below that will be in the Fire."""
"921","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lower garment of the believer should reach to the middle of the shin, and there is no harm in keeping it anywhere between that and the ankles; but whatever hangs below the ankles will be in the Fire. Whoever drags his lower garment on the ground out of arrogance, Allah Almighty will not look at him with mercy (on the Day of Resurrection)."""
"922","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be indifferent to the world and Allah will love you; and be indifferent to what people possess and people will love you."""
"923","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be indifferent to the world and Allah will love you. As for people, leave their things to them (be indifferent to what they have), and they will love you."""
"924","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usamah is the dearest of people to me."""
"925","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Performing ablution (wudu) thoroughly is half of faith; Alhamdulillah (all praise is for Allah) fills the Scale; tasbih and takbir (Subhan Allah and Allahu Akbar) fill the space between the heavens and the earth; prayer is light; zakah is a proof (of faith); patience is illumination; and the Qur'an is a proof either for you or against you. Every person sets out in the morning and sells his soul, then he either frees it (by doing good) or destroys it (by sinning)."""
"926","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Performing ablution thoroughly despite hardship, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for one prayer after another prayer: these deeds wash away sins completely."""
"927","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform ablution thoroughly, pass (water) between the fingers, and be thorough in drawing water into the nose, unless you are fasting."""
"928","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform ablution thoroughly."""
"929","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(O women!) Move back, for it is not proper for you to walk in the middle of the road; keep to the edges of the road."""
"930","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek the permission of women regarding (the matters of) their marriage."""
"931","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Establish that the wombs of these captive women (slave women) are clear by means of one menstrual cycle (that is, wait until one menstrual period occurs so that it is certain there is no pregnancy)."""
"932","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, for the punishment of the grave is true."""
"933","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have modesty, for Allah Almighty is not shy of stating the truth: do not approach women in their back passage (anus)."""
"934","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have modesty, for Allah Almighty is not shy of the truth: it is not lawful to approach women in the place of their excrement (the anus)."""
"935","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be modest before Allah Almighty with the modesty that is His due. Whoever wishes to fulfil the due of modesty before Allah, let him guard the head and what it contains (that is, the eyes, ears, tongue and so on), guard the belly and what it holds, and remember death and (the body's) decay (in the grave). Whoever intends the Hereafter abandons the adornment of the life of this world. So whoever does these things has truly fulfilled the due of modesty before Allah."""
"936","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep revising the Qur'an repeatedly, for it escapes from the breasts of men so swiftly that even animals tied with ropes do not run away as fast."""
"937","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have ruqyah performed for this girl, for she has been afflicted by the evil eye."""
"938","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the evil eye, for the evil eye is true."""
"939","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah Almighty from poverty (want), from destitution, and from wronging someone or being wronged."""
"940","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the evil of a bad neighbour where you permanently reside, for a neighbour on a journey can part whenever he wishes."""
"941","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of Hell, seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the False Messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal), and seek refuge with Allah from the trials of life and death."""
"942","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave, for the dead are punished in their graves with a punishment that the animals hear."""
"943","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek help in accomplishing your needs (and aims) through secrecy, for everyone who has a blessing is envied."""
"944","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek forgiveness from your Lord; indeed I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him a hundred times every day."""
"945","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek forgiveness for your (Muslim) brother and ask for steadfastness for him, for he is now being questioned (in the grave by Munkar and Nakir)."""
"946","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray for forgiveness for Ma'iz bin Malik. He has certainly made such a (sincere) repentance that, if it were divided among the whole Ummah, it would suffice them all."""
"947","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be independent of people, even if it is in the matter of the shavings of a tooth-stick (miswak) (or a used miswak)."""
"948","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek a ruling (guidance) from your own heart, even if those who give rulings have given you a ruling."""
"949","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Repeat your prayer, for there is no prayer for the one who prays alone behind the row."""
"950","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Learn the Qur'an from four people: from Abdullah bin Mas'ud, Salim the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, Ubayy bin Ka'b and Mu'adh bin Jabal."""
"951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remain steadfast (in the religion) and make your character good towards people."""
"952","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remain steadfast (in the religion), and you will never be able to count (its full reward). Know that the best of all your deeds is the prayer, and none maintains ablution (wudu) except a believer."""
"953","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remain steadfast (in the religion), and how excellent it will be if you remain steadfast. The best of your deeds is the prayer, and none will maintain ablution (wudu) except a believer."""
"954","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Use sandals often (that is, keep them on when walking), for as long as a man is wearing sandals it is as though he is riding (he suffers less fatigue and hardship)."""
"955","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Benefit from this House (the Ka'bah) (that is, perform its tawaf and visit it frequently), for it has been demolished twice and will be raised up (taken away) the third time."""
"956","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Draw water into the nose and blow it out thoroughly, twice or three times."""
"957","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust and the final outcome of your deeds."""
"958","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I entrust you to Allah, with whom the things entrusted are never lost."""
"959","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Accept my counsel to treat the Ansar well (that is, always treat them kindly)."""
"960","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Accept the counsel to treat women well, for woman has been created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its upper part. If you go to straighten it you will break it, and if you leave it as it is, it will remain crooked. So accept the counsel to treat women well."""
"961","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stand straight (in the rows of prayer) and do not stand unevenly, or else your hearts will differ. Let those of you who are mature and possess understanding stand close to me, then those who come after them, then those who come after them."""
"962","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The quickest of the Arab tribes to perish (come to an end) will be Quraysh. Soon a woman will pass by a sandal and, on seeing it, say: This is the sandal of a Qurayshi."""
"963","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The quickest of you (the Mothers of the Believers) to join me will be the one of you with the longest hands (that is, the one who gives the most in charity)."""
"964","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hasten with the funeral, for if the deceased was righteous, you are hastening him to something good, and if he was otherwise (evil), you are putting an evil off your necks."""
"965","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man wronged himself greatly (through sins). When death approached him, he gave instructions to his sons, saying: When I die, burn me, then grind my bones, then scatter me over the sea, for by Allah, if my Lord gets hold of me, He will punish me with a punishment He has not given anyone. So they did that with him. Then Allah Almighty commanded the earth: Give back what you have taken. And at once he was standing. Allah Almighty asked: What made you do what you did? He said: O my Lord, fear of You. So Allah forgave him because of that."""
"966","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The worst thief among people is the one who steals from his prayer, that is, he does not complete its bowing (ruku') or its prostration (sujud). And the most miserly of people is the one who is miserly with giving the greeting of peace (salam)."""
"967","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The happiest of people with my intercession on the Day of Resurrection will be the one who said, sincerely and from his heart, that there is no true god except Allah."""
"968","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform the sa'i (between Safa and Marwah), for Allah Almighty has indeed made the sa'i obligatory upon you."""
"969","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform the Fajr prayer in the light of dawn, until the people can see (in the light) the places where their arrows fall."""
"970","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform the Fajr prayer when the dawn has become well lit, for there is a very great reward in it."""
"971","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The (other) people (merely) became Muslim, whereas Amr bin al-As believed."""
"972","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have embraced Islam by virtue of the good deeds you did before (in the time of ignorance)."""
"973","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""First accept Islam, then fight (in jihad)."""
"974","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Accept Islam, even if it is (naturally) displeasing to you."""
"975","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has kept the tribe of Aslam safe, and Allah has forgiven the tribe of Ghifar. Listen! By Allah, it was not I who said this; rather, Allah Almighty said it."""
"976","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tribes of Aslam, Ghifar, Ashja', Muzaynah, Juhaynah and the people of Banu Ka'b are my allies and friends, to the exclusion of other people, and Allah and His Messenger are their protectors and helpers."""
"977","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tribes of Aslam and Ghifar, and some of the people of Muzaynah and Juhaynah, are better in the sight of Allah than the tribes of Asad, Tamim, Hawazin and Ghatafan."""
"978","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The tribes of Aslam, Ghifar and Muzaynah are better than Banu Tamim, Asad, Ghatafan and Amir bin Sa'sa'ah."""
"979","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Greatest Name of Allah Almighty, by which, if He is supplicated, He responds, is in three surahs of the Qur'an: Surah al-Baqarah, Surah Al Imran and Surah Ta Ha."""
"980","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Greatest Name of Allah is in these two verses: 'And your God is one God; there is no true god except Him, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.' [Surah al-Baqarah: 163] and in the opening verses of Surah Al Imran: 'Alif Lam Mim. Allah, there is no true god except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer (of all).' [Surah Al Imran: 1-2]"""
"981","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be lenient (and gentle with others), and leniency will be shown to you."""
"982","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be gentle and generous (with others), and generosity and gentleness will be shown to you."""
"983","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen (to your leader) and obey, even if he is an Abyssinian slave with mutilated limbs."""
"984","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen (to the rulers) and obey them, for they are responsible for what they have been charged with, and you are responsible for what you have been charged with."""
"985","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen (to your leader) and obey, even if an Abyssinian slave whose head is like a raisin (in being black and small) is appointed over you."""
"986","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The worst of people in stealing is the one who steals from his prayer, that is, he does not complete its bowing (ruku'), nor its prostration (sujud), nor does he observe humility and devotion in it."""
"987","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of those I have seen, the one who most resembles Jibril (peace be upon him) is Dihyah al-Kalbi."""
"988","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The anger of Allah is most severe against the one who claimed that he is the King of kings, whereas there is no true king except Allah."""
"989","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man bought a piece of land (property) from another man. The man who bought the land found in his land a jar full of gold. The man who bought the land said (to the seller): Take your gold from me; I only bought the land from you, I did not buy the gold. The (former) owner of the land said: I sold you the land and everything in it. Then the two of them went to a third man to have the matter judged. The man to whom they went for judgement asked: Do you have any children? One of them said: I have a son. And the other said: I have a daughter. He (the arbiter) ruled: Marry the boy to the girl, spend from it (the gold) on yourselves, and give (the rest) in charity."""
"990","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Fire of Hell complained to its Lord and said: O my Lord, part of me has devoured another part. So Allah Almighty permitted it two breaths, one breath in winter and one breath in summer. So the most intense heat you feel and the most intense cold you feel is because of that."""
"991","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Fire of Hell complained to its Lord and said: O my Lord, part of me has devoured another part. So Allah Almighty appointed two breaths for it, one breath in winter and one breath in summer. As for its breath in winter, it is the bitter cold, and as for its breath in summer, it is the scorching hot wind (heat)."""
"992","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people who face the severest trials are the Prophets, then, rank by rank, those closest to them (in righteousness). A person is tried according to his religion: if he is firm (strong) in his religion, his trial is made severe, and if there is softness (weakness) in his religion, he is tried according to the level of his religion. Afflictions and trials continue to befall the servant until they leave him walking on the earth with no sin upon him."""
"993","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people with the severest trials are the Prophets, then those closest to them, then those closest to them. People are tried according to their religion: whoever's religion is solid, his trial is also severe, and whoever's religion is weak, his trial is also light. Indeed, a man continues to be afflicted by hardships until he walks among the people with no sin remaining upon him."""
"994","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people with the severest trials are the Prophets and the righteous, then, rank by rank, those who come after them (in status)."""
"995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people with the severest trials are the Prophets, then the righteous. Indeed, one of them would be tried with poverty to such an extent that he would find nothing but a woollen cloak, so he would cut it open and wear it; and they would be tried with lice until they killed him. And each of them was more pleased with trial than any of you is when he receives wealth."""
"996","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people with the severest trials are the Prophets, then those who come after them (in virtue), then those who come after them."""
"997","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people with the severest punishment in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection will be those who imitate the creation of Allah (that is, those who make images of living beings)."""
"998","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who inflicts the severest torment (suffering) on people in this world will be the one who receives the severest punishment from Allah on the Day of Resurrection."""
"999","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are the makers of images (of living beings). It will be said to them: Bring to life what you created."""
"1000","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one among people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection is a man who killed a prophet or was killed by a prophet, or a man who misleads people without knowledge, or an image-maker who makes statues (of living beings)."""
"1001","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one among people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection is a tyrannical ruler."""
"1002","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most modest of my Ummah is Uthman bin Affan."""
"1003","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those of my Ummah who love me most will be people who come after me; each one of them will wish that he could give up his family and wealth, everything, and see me just once."""
"1004","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The finest poetic saying the Arabs have uttered is this line of Labid: Behold! Everything besides Allah is vain (bound to perish)."""
"1005","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say the phrases of the Adhan in even number (twice each) and the phrases of the Iqamah in odd number (once each)."""
"1006","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Intercede (in permissible matters), and you will be rewarded."""
"1007","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Intercede so that you may be rewarded, and Allah Almighty carries out on the tongue of His Prophet whatever decision He wills."""
"1008","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most grateful of people to Allah is the one who is most grateful to people."""
"1009","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I bear witness that there is no true god except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. No servant meets Allah with these two, believing in them without any doubt, except that he will certainly enter Paradise."""
"1010","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Announce (and publicise) marriage."""
"1011","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Announce marriage and make it publicly known."""
"1012","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The fingers of the hands and the toes of the feet are equal (in blood money or retaliation)."""
"1013","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The truest saying ever spoken by a poet is this line of Labid: Behold! Everything besides Allah is vain (perishing)."""
"1014","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Turn your gaze away (that is, when your eyes suddenly fall upon a non-mahram, look away)."""
"1015","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for such a grief has befallen them that it has kept them occupied."""
"1016","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do as you wish (that is, regarding coitus interruptus), but whatever Allah Almighty has decreed will come to be; and besides, a child does not come from every drop of water (sperm)."""
"1017","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty led those before us astray from Friday, so the Jews had Saturday and the Christians had Sunday. Then Allah Almighty brought us and guided us to Friday, and thus He made the order Friday, Saturday and Sunday. Likewise, on the Day of Resurrection they will follow behind us. We are the last of the people of this world, but on the Day of Resurrection we will be the first, those whose judgement will be passed before all of creation."""
"1018","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guarantee me six things on your part, and I guarantee you Paradise: speak the truth when you speak, fulfil it when you make a promise, render it back when something is entrusted to you, guard your private parts, lower your gazes, and restrain your hands (from oppression and wrongdoing)."""
"1019","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Speak good and pure words, spread the greeting of peace (salam), maintain ties of kinship, and pray (Tahajjud) at night while people are asleep; then you will enter Paradise in peace."""
"1020","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The sky is creaking (that is, groaning under its load), and it has every right to creak. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! There is not a span's worth of space in the sky except that there is the forehead of an angel in prostration, glorifying Allah with His praise."""
"1021","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Feed (people) and speak pure words."""
"1022","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Feed (the poor and the needy) and spread the greeting of peace (salam), and you will be made heirs of the Gardens of Paradise."""
"1023","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The (young, deceased) children of the believers are on a mountain in Paradise, where Ibrahim and Sarah (peace be upon them both) are taking care of them until they hand them over to their parents on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1024","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The (young, deceased) children of the polytheists will be servants of the people of Paradise."""
"1025","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you go to sleep, put out the lamps, shut the doors, tie up the mouths of the waterskins, and cover food and drink, even if only by placing a stick across it."""
"1026","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek the acceptance of supplication at the time when armies clash (in jihad), when the prayer is established, and when rain falls."""
"1027","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights (of Ramadan); then if you become weak (due to illness or sleep), do not by any means slacken in the remaining seven nights."""
"1028","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights: when nine nights remain, when seven nights remain, when five nights remain, and when three nights remain."""
"1029","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of Ramadan."""
"1030","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I looked into Hell and saw that most of its inhabitants were women."""
"1031","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, those with the longest necks among people will be the mu'adhdhins (callers to prayer)."""
"1032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of perfumes is musk."""
"1033","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The purest earning is a man's working with his own hand, and every trade that is free of deceit and sin."""
"1034","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Obey me as long as I am among you, and it is binding upon you to hold fast to the Book of Allah: regard as lawful what it makes lawful and regard as unlawful what it makes unlawful."""
"1035","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trials like pieces of the dark night have overshadowed you. The safest of people from them will be a man on a mountain peak who lives on the milk of his goats, or a man at the frontiers holding the reins of his horse, who earns his provision from the shade of his sword (that is, he is engaged in jihad)."""
"1036","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I think you have heard that Abu Ubaydah has come from Bahrain with some wealth. So rejoice and hope for what will please you. By Allah! It is not poverty that I fear for you; rather, I fear for you that the world will be spread open for you just as it was spread open for those before you, and then you will compete with one another to acquire it just as they did, and it (greed for the world) will destroy you just as it destroyed them."""
"1037","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Worship Allah as though you see Him, and if you cannot see Him, then (be certain that) He surely sees you. Count yourself among the dead, and beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for it is certainly answered."""
"1038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Worship Allah as though you see Him, count yourself among the dead, and beware of the supplications of the oppressed, for they are certainly answered. The Fajr and Isha prayers are binding upon you, so attend them both; for if you knew how much reward lies in them, you would certainly come to them, even if you had to crawl on your knees."""
"1039","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Worship Allah, do not associate anything with Him, establish the obligatory prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, perform Hajj and Umrah, and fast in Ramadan. Look at the treatment you would like people to give you, and give them that same treatment; and the conduct you dislike for yourself, keep people safe from it too (that is, do not treat them that way)."""
"1040","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him. Act for Allah as though you see Him, count yourself among the dead, and remember Allah Almighty at every stone and every tree (that is, in every state and every place). When you commit an evil deed, do a good deed right alongside it: a secret good deed for a secret evil deed, and a public good deed for a public evil deed."""
"1041","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Worship the Most Merciful, spread (make common) the greeting of peace (salam), and feed people; you will enter the Gardens of Paradise (in peace)."""
"1042","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be balanced in prostration (that is, adopt a moderate posture), and let none of you spread his forearms on the ground the way a dog spreads them."""
"1043","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Delay this prayer (that is, Isha), for by virtue of this prayer you have been granted superiority over all other nations, and no nation before you prayed it."""
"1044","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most incapable (and helpless) of people is the one who is incapable of making supplication, and the stingiest of people is the one who is stingy with the greeting of peace (salam)."""
"1045","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Count six signs before the Hour comes: my death; then the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis; then a deadly plague that will spread rapidly among you just as disease spreads among goats and kills them; then such an abundance of wealth that if a man is given even a hundred dinars he will remain displeased, considering it little; then a tremendous trial will appear, leaving no Arab household it does not enter; then a truce that will be between you and Banu al-Asfar (the Romans/Christians), but they will betray it and come to attack you, gathered under eighty (80) banners, with an army of twelve thousand under each banner."""
"1046","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Be just among your children in giving gifts (presents), exactly as you would like them to be equal and fair towards you in kind treatment and gentleness."""
"1047","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has left no excuse for a person whose death He kept postponing until he reached sixty years of age."""
"1048","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Present your ruqyahs (the words with which you recite over the sick) to me. There is no harm in ruqyah as long as it contains no words of shirk."""
"1049","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Turn away from (prying into the private and hidden affairs of) people. Do you not know that if you go searching for people's faults and suspicions, you will corrupt their character, or you will come close to corrupting them?"""
"1050","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take careful note of the number of it (the lost item), its container (or pouch) and the string used to tie it, then announce it (publicly) for one year. If its owner comes (then return it to him); otherwise it will be like your own property."""
"1051","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Know your lineages (your family tree and family ties) so that through them you may maintain the ties of kinship, for if kinship is severed, its closeness is of no benefit, however close it may be; and if kinship is maintained, its distance means nothing, however distant it may be."""
"1052","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remove harmful things from the path of the Muslims."""
"1053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you wish, practise withdrawal ('azl) with her (the slave woman or wife), that is, discharge the semen outside; but know for certain that whatever child has been decreed for her will come to her regardless."""
"1054","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give every surah its full due in bowing and prostration (that is, according to the length of the surah, spend a proportionate amount of time in bowing and prostration as well)."""
"1055","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give the labourer his wage before his sweat dries."""
"1056","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been given five distinctions which were not given to any prophet before me: (1) I have been helped by awe (cast into the hearts of enemies) from a distance of a month's journey. (2) The whole earth has been made for me a place of prostration (a mosque) and a means of purification, so whichever man of my Ummah the time of prayer overtakes, wherever he is, let him pray right there. (3) The spoils of war have been made lawful for me, whereas they were not lawful for anyone before me. (4) I have been given the intercession (the great station of intercession). (5) Every prophet before me was sent specifically to his own people alone, whereas I have been sent to all people in general."""
"1057","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been given seventy thousand of my Ummah who will enter Paradise without any reckoning. Their faces will shine like the moon on the night of the full moon, and all their hearts will be like the heart of a single man (united and loving one another). Then I asked my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, for more, and He (at my request) added a further seventy thousand with each one of them."""
"1058","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been given the openings of speech, its comprehensive expressions (jawami' al-kalim, that is, concise words that are brief in wording but vast in meaning) and the excellences of its conclusions."""
"1059","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In place of the Torah I have been given the seven long surahs (al-Sab' al-Tiwal); in place of the Psalms (Zabur) I have been given the surahs of about a hundred verses (al-Mi'in); in place of the Gospel (Injil) I have been given the oft-repeated surahs (al-Mathani); and I have been granted excellence and superiority over all the prophets in particular through the short surahs (al-Mufassal)."""
"1060","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These final verses of Surah al-Baqarah have been given to me from a treasure (a special treasure of Allah) beneath the Throne; they were not given to any prophet before me."""
"1061","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give (in the way of Allah) and do not hoard (your wealth) by counting it out or by tying up the mouth of your pouch, otherwise (the door of provision from Allah) will be closed on you as well."""
"1062","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yusuf (peace be upon him) was given half of (the world's) beauty."""
"1063","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yusuf (peace be upon him) and his mother were given half of (the world's) beauty."""
"1064","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The greatest of days in the sight of Allah Almighty is the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr, that is, 10 Dhul-Hijjah), and after it the Day of Settling (Yawm al-Qarr, 11 Dhul-Hijjah, the day of staying in Mina)."""
"1065","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the matter of prayer, the greatest reward goes to the person who covers the longest distance (to come to the mosque), then after him the one who is at a shorter distance than that. And the one who waits for the prayer until he performs it in congregation with the imam has a far greater reward than the one who prays it (alone) and then goes to sleep."""
"1066","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The greatest liars (and slanderers) among people are of two kinds: a poet who satirises (disparages and condemns) an entire tribe in its entirety, and a man who disowns his lineage from his (real) father."""
"1067","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let your beards grow, trim your moustaches, change the whiteness of your hair (with dye), and do not imitate the Jews and the Christians."""
"1068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""First tie the knee of it (your she-camel), and then put your trust (in Allah)."""
"1069","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Know that you do not make any prostration to Allah except that, by virtue of it (that prostration), Allah Almighty raises you by one degree and erases one sin from you."""
"1070","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Know that there is none among you except that the wealth of his heir is dearer to him than his own wealth. (In reality) your wealth is only what you have sent ahead (by spending it in the way of Allah), and the wealth you leave behind is the wealth of your heir."""
"1071","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Mas'ud! Know that Allah Almighty has far more power and authority over you than the control you have over this slave."""
"1072","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Announce marriage (openly)."""
"1073","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lifespans of the people of my Ummah will (generally) be between sixty and seventy years, and very few of them will go beyond that (limit)."""
"1074","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep doing deeds, for each person is made easy for that for which he was created."""
"1075","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(O Allah!) I seek refuge in Your might, besides which there is no god worthy of worship, lest You lead me astray. You are the Ever-Living who will never die, while the jinn and mankind will all die."""
"1076","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take a bath (ghusl) on Friday and wash your heads, even if the ritual bath for major impurity (janabah) is not obligatory on you, and also apply some perfume."""
"1077","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take advantage of five things before five: your life before your death, your health before your sickness, your free time before your preoccupation, your youth before your old age, and your prosperity (wealth) before your poverty."""
"1078","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fight in the name of Allah and in the way of Allah, and fight against whoever disbelieves in Allah. Fight, but do not embezzle from the spoils of war, do not break your covenant, do not mutilate (bodies by cutting off limbs to disfigure them), and do not kill any child. And when you meet your enemies among the polytheists, invite them to three things; whichever of them they accept, accept it from them and refrain (from fighting) them: first, invite them to Islam; if they accept, accept it from them and do not fight them. Then invite them to leave their land and emigrate to the land of the Muhajirun, and tell them that if they do so, they will have the same rights as the Muhajirun and the same obligations as the Muhajirun. If they refuse to emigrate, tell them that they will be like the Bedouin Muslims: the same command of Allah that applies to the believers in general will apply to them, but they will receive nothing from the spoils of war (ghanimah) and the fay' unless they wage jihad together with the Muslims. If they refuse (even to accept Islam), then demand the jizyah (tax) from them; if they agree, accept it from them and refrain from fighting. But if they refuse that as well, then seek the help of Allah and fight them. And when you besiege the people of a fortress and they want you to grant them the protection (covenant and security) of Allah and of His Prophet, do not by any means grant them the protection of Allah and of His Prophet; rather, grant them your own protection and that of your companions, for if the protection given by you or your companions is broken, that is far lighter than your breaking the covenant of Allah and His Messenger. And when you besiege a fortress and they want you to bring them down on the judgement of Allah, do not bring them down on the judgement of Allah, but bring them down on your own judgement, for you do not know whether you will arrive at Allah's (intended) judgement concerning them or not."""
"1079","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wash him (this deceased person who was in the state of ihram) with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his own two garments (the sheets of ihram), do not apply any perfume to him, do not cover his head, and do not apply hanut (the fragrance applied to the dead) to him, for Allah Almighty will raise him on the Day of Resurrection in the state of calling out the Talbiyah (Labbayk)."""
"1080","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Close the doors (of your houses), cover your vessels, put out your lamps and tie up the mouths of your waterskins, for Satan does not open a closed door, nor uncover a covered vessel, nor untie a tied knot; and also because the little mischief-maker (that is, the mouse) can set the house on fire and burn it to ashes over its occupants."""
"1081","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the man who will be the greatest target of the wrath of Allah Almighty, and the most wicked and evil in His sight, will be the one who used to be called (in the world) the King of Kings (the king of all kings). In reality there is no king but Allah."""
"1082","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Jews split into seventy-one (71) sects, of which one will be in Paradise and seventy (70) in Hell. The Christians split into seventy-two (72) sects, of which seventy-one (71) will be in Hell and one in Paradise. And by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! My Ummah will certainly split into seventy-three (73) sects, of which one will be in Paradise and seventy-two (72) in Hell."""
"1083","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Jews split into seventy-one (71) sects, the Christians divided into seventy-two (72) sects, and my Ummah will split into seventy-three (73) sects."""
"1084","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most knowledgeable of my Ummah in the science of inheritance shares (fara'id, the rules of inheritance) is Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"1085","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spread the greeting of peace (salam), feed (people), maintain the ties of kinship (treat your relatives well), and stand in prayer (tahajjud) at night while people are asleep; you will enter Paradise in peace."""
"1086","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spread the greeting of peace among yourselves; love will arise between you."""
"1087","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spread the greeting of peace; you will remain safe."""
"1088","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spread the greeting of peace so that you may be exalted."""
"1089","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spread the greeting of peace, feed (people), and become brothers to one another as Allah has commanded."""
"1090","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best religion is the upright religion (al-Hanifiyyah), which has breadth and ease."""
"1091","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent deed is faith in Allah alone, then jihad, then an accepted Hajj (Hajj mabrur), which surpasses all other deeds by as much as the distance between the east and the west."""
"1092","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of deeds are faith in Allah alone, then jihad, and then an accepted Hajj, which surpasses all other deeds by as much as the distance between the place where the sun rises (the east) and the place where it sets (the west)."""
"1093","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent deed is performing the prayer at the beginning of its time."""
"1094","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of deeds are performing the prayer at its (appointed) time and treating one's parents with kindness."""
"1095","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of deeds are performing the prayer at its time, being good to one's parents, and waging jihad in the way of Allah."""
"1096","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of deeds are that you bring happiness into the heart of your believing brother (make him happy), or pay off a debt for him, or feed him bread (food)."""
"1097","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best faith is patience and forbearance (generosity of heart)."""
"1098","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent of days in the sight of Allah Almighty is Friday."""
"1099","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent jihad is that a person strives against his own self and his desires."""
"1100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent jihad is to speak a word of truth before a tyrannical king (or ruler)."""
"1101","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best Hajj is the one in which the Talbiyah is called out in a loud voice (al-'ajj) and the blood of sacrificial animals is shed (al-thajj)."""
"1102","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best supplication is the supplication on the Day of Arafah, and the best words that I and the prophets before me have said are: La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah (There is none worthy of worship except Allah, He is alone, He has no partner)."""
"1103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best dinar is the one a person spends on his family, and the dinar a person spends on his mount (animal) in the path of Allah, and the dinar a person spends on his companions in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"1104","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent remembrance is La ilaha illallah (There is none worthy of worship except Allah), and the most excellent supplication is Alhamdulillah (All praise is for Allah)."""
"1105","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best slave (to set free) is the one whose price is highest and who is the most excellent and valuable in the eyes of his owners."""
"1106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best hours (for acceptance) are the last part of the night (its final watch)."""
"1107","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent martyrs are those who fight in the front row (in jihad) and do not turn their faces away (from the enemy) until they are killed. These are the people who will live in delight in the lofty mansions of Paradise. Your Lord smiles at them, and when your Lord smiles at a servant in any place, there is no reckoning for him."""
"1108","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent martyr is the one whose blood is shed (in the path of Allah) and whose horse is hamstrung."""
"1109","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the best acts of charity are providing the shade of a tent in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, or giving a servant in the path of Allah, or giving a young she-camel (for jihad) in the path of Allah."""
"1110","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent charity is spending on a close relative who harbours enmity and rancour in his heart."""
"1111","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent charity is that you give charity while you are healthy and eager for wealth, hoping to become rich and fearing poverty. And do not delay giving charity until, when the soul reaches the throat, you begin to say: 'Give so much to so-and-so, and give so much to so-and-so,' when that wealth has by then already become the property of so-and-so (that is, the heirs)."""
"1112","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent charity is that of a person of little wealth giving to the full extent of his effort and means, and begin giving charity with those whose support is your responsibility."""
"1113","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent charity is giving water to drink."""
"1114","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best charity is that after which wealth still remains (that is, the person does not make himself needy), and the upper hand (the giver) is better than the lower hand (the receiver), and begin spending with those whose upkeep is your responsibility. (For the wife says: 'Either feed me or divorce me'; the slave says: 'Feed me and make use of me'; and the son says: 'Feed me; to whom are you leaving me?')"""
"1115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best charity is that which is given after wealth (that is, after needs have been met), and the upper hand (the giver) is better than the lower hand (the receiver), and begin charity with those whose support is your responsibility."""
"1116","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After the obligatory prayer, the most excellent prayer is the prayer in the last part of the night (Tahajjud), and after the month of Ramadan, the most excellent fasts are the fasts of Allah's month, Muharram."""
"1117","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A person's best prayer is the one he offers in his home, except the obligatory prayer (which should be offered in congregation in the mosque)."""
"1118","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent prayer is the one in which the standing (qunut) is long."""
"1119","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of all the prayers, the most excellent prayer in the sight of Allah Almighty is to offer the Fajr prayer in congregation on Friday."""
"1120","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent fasting is the fasting of my brother Dawud (peace be upon him). He used to fast one day and break his fast the next (that is, not fast), and when he faced the enemy on the battlefield, he would not turn his back."""
"1121","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After Ramadan, the most excellent fasts are those of the month which you call Muharram."""
"1122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent act of worship is supplication."""
"1123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent deed is offering the prayer at its (appointed) time and jihad in the path of Allah."""
"1124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent deed is believing in Allah and jihad in the path of Allah."""
"1125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent surah of the Qur'an is 'All praise is for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds.'"" [Surah al-Fatihah: 2]"
"1126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best earning is trade in which there is no deception, fraud or sin, and a person's working with his own hand."""
"1127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best words are: Subhanallah, walhamdulillah, wa la ilaha illallah, wallahu akbar (Glory be to Allah, all praise is for Allah, there is none worthy of worship except Allah, and Allah is the Greatest)."""
"1128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent of the believers is the one whose character is the best."""
"1129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent of the believers in terms of Islam is the one from whose tongue and hand the other Muslims are safe; the most excellent of the believers in terms of faith is the one whose character is the best; the best emigrant is the one who abandons what Allah Almighty has forbidden; and the best jihad is that a person strives against his own self for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"1130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent of people is a believer who is between two noble and righteous (parents)."""
"1131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent of people is a believer who strives in the path of Allah with his life and his wealth, then a believer who lives in one of the mountain passes, fearing Allah and keeping people safe from his evil."""
"1132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The better of the two emigrations is the Hijrah al-Bannah, and the Hijrah al-Bannah is that you remain permanently with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), whereas the emigration of the desert dweller is that you return to your desert. And it is binding upon you to listen to and obey (the ruler), whether in your hardship or your ease, in what you dislike or what pleases you, and even if others are given preference over you."""
"1133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best days of this world are the (first) ten days (of Dhul-Hijjah)."""
"1134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your best prayer is the one you offer in your homes, except the obligatory prayer."""
"1135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most excellent of the women of Paradise are Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh."""
"1136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who applies cupping (the cupper) and the one who has it applied have both broken their fast."""
"1137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May those who are fasting break their fast with you, may the righteous eat your food, and may the angels pray for mercy upon you."""
"1138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Successful is the one who was granted guidance to Islam, whose provision was according to his need (kafaf), and who was content with it."""
"1139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Establishing one of the prescribed punishments (hudud) of Allah is better than forty nights of rain falling upon Allah's land."""
"1140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Accept (her) garden and give her one divorce."""
"1141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Come from the front or from behind, but avoid the place of excrement (the anus) and (intimacy during) the state of menstruation."""
"1142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Follow these two after me: Abu Bakr and Umar."""
"1143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Follow these two after me: Abu Bakr and Umar; take guidance from the way of Ammar; and whatever Ibn Mas'ud narrates to you, accept it."""
"1144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Follow these two of my Companions after me: Abu Bakr and Umar; take guidance from the way of Ammar; and hold firmly to the covenant (counsel) of Ibn Mas'ud."""
"1145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour has drawn near, and people's distance (heedlessness) is only increasing."""
"1146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour has drawn near, and people's greed for this world only keeps growing, and they only keep growing more distant from Allah."""
"1147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kill the two black things even while in prayer: the snake and the scorpion."""
"1148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kill snakes, for we have not made peace with them since we began hostilities with them."""
"1149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kill all snakes; whoever fears their revenge is not of us."""
"1150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kill snakes and dogs, and especially kill the snake with two white stripes on its back and the short-tailed snake, for these two (through their venom) take away eyesight and cause (women) to miscarry."""
"1151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kill the snake and the scorpion, even if you are in the state of prayer."""
"1152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kill the snake with two white stripes on its back, for it (through its venom) takes away eyesight and causes (women) to miscarry."""
"1153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kill the snake with two stripes and the short-tailed snake, for these two blot out eyesight and cause miscarriage."""
"1154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Complete the Qur'an in forty days."""
"1155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you are able, complete the Qur'an in three days."""
"1156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite (complete) the Qur'an in five days."""
"1157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Complete the Qur'an every month, (or) recite it in twenty-five days, recite it in fifteen days, recite it in ten days, recite it in seven days; and whoever recites it in less than three days will not understand it."""
"1158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite (complete) the Qur'an every month, complete it in twenty nights, complete it in ten nights, complete it in seven days, and do not go beyond that (in speed)."""
"1159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite the surahs of seeking refuge (al-Mu'awwidhat: Surah al-Ikhlas, al-Falaq and an-Nas) after every prayer."""
"1160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite al-Mu'awwidhatayn (Surah al-Falaq and Surah an-Nas), for you will never recite anything like them (for seeking refuge)."""
"1161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""At the time of your sleep, recite {Say: O disbelievers}, for it is a declaration of freedom (deliverance) from associating partners with Allah (shirk)."" [Surah al-Kafirun: 1]"
"1162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) taught me to recite the Qur'an in one harf (mode of recitation). Then I went back to him, and I kept asking him for more and he kept giving me more, until it reached seven ahruf (modes of recitation)."""
"1163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an in seven ahruf (modes); whichever of them you recite in, you will be correct. And do not dispute about it, for disputing about it is disbelief (kufr)."""
"1164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an, for you will be rewarded for it. Indeed, I do not say that Alif-Lam-Mim is one letter; rather, for Alif there are ten good deeds, for Lam ten and for Mim ten, so altogether that makes thirty good deeds."""
"1165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an, for it will come on the Day of Resurrection as an intercessor for those who recite it. Recite the two radiant surahs, Surah al-Baqarah and Surah Al Imran, for on the Day of Resurrection these two will come as though they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds with outspread wings, pleading on behalf of those who recite them. Recite Surah al-Baqarah, for reciting it is a source of blessing and abandoning it is a source of regret, and the sorcerers cannot withstand it (its power)."""
"1166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep reciting the Qur'an as long as your hearts are attentive and united upon it; and when you begin to differ over it (its meanings or its recitation), then stand up (that is, stop the recitation)."""
"1167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an and seek only the pleasure of Allah Almighty through it, before there come people who will straighten it as an arrow is straightened (that is, they will polish its outward words); they will seek its worldly reward (praise, acclaim or money) in haste and will not defer it for the Hereafter."""
"1168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an and act upon it; do not turn away from it, do not go to extremes (exceed the bounds) in it, do not make it a means of eating (earning a livelihood), and do not seek to amass much worldly wealth through it."""
"1169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite the Qur'an and ask Allah Almighty through it, before there comes a people who will recite the Qur'an and then ask people (for worldly wealth) through it."""
"1170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite Surah al-Baqarah in your houses, for Satan does not enter a house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited."""
"1171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite (the Qur'an) just as you have been taught, for what destroyed those before you was nothing but their differing with their own prophets."""
"1172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite these two verses at the end of Surah al-Baqarah, for my Lord granted me both of these verses from beneath the Throne."""
"1173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Lord Almighty is closest to His servant in the last part of the night; so if you are able to be among those who remember Allah at that hour, then be so."""
"1174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The servant is closest to Allah when he is in the state of prostration."""
"1175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The servant is closest to his Lord when he is in prostration, so supplicate abundantly (in prostration)."""
"1176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, those of you who will sit closest to me will be those of you who are best in character."""
"1177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave the birds in their nests (that is, do not make them fly away in order to draw omens from them)."""
"1178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Divide the wealth (of the deceased) among those entitled to fixed shares according to the Book of Allah; then whatever remains after the fixed shares belongs to the nearest male relative ('asabah)."""
"1179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Reduce your belching (that is, do not eat until you are overfull), for those who eat their fill the most in this world will be the hungriest in the Hereafter."""
"1180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pay the debt owed to Allah (that is, vows, fasts, Hajj and the like), for Allah is most deserving that His due be fulfilled."""
"1181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cut off the hand for (the theft of) a quarter of a dinar, and do not cut it off for what is of lesser value than that."""
"1182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Very few people of my Ummah will reach the age of seventy."""
"1183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those in my Ummah who reach the age of seventy will be very few."""
"1184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When people have gone to sleep (and the stillness of night has set in), reduce your going out, for at that time Allah Almighty has many creatures which He spreads out over the earth."""
"1185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pardon the slips of noble and honourable people, except for those sins for which a (legal) hadd punishment is prescribed."""
"1186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform the bowing (ruku') and prostration fully (in accordance with the Sunnah). By Allah! When you bow and when you prostrate, I see you even from behind my back."""
"1187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your rows straight, for you form rows like the rows of the angels. Keep your shoulders level, fill the gaps, be gentle with the hands of your brothers, and do not leave gaps for Satan. Whoever joins a row, Allah Almighty will join him, and whoever breaks a row, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will cut him off."""
"1188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your rows straight in prayer, for keeping the row straight is part of the beauty and perfection of prayer."""
"1189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Establish prayer, give zakah, perform Hajj and Umrah, and remain firm (in the religion); your affairs too will be set right and made firm."""
"1190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Enforce the prescribed punishments (hudud) of Allah Almighty upon those far and near (that is, strangers and your own), and let not the blame of any blamer ever hold you back in the matter of Allah."""
"1191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Straighten your rows. By Allah! You will certainly keep your rows straight, or else Allah Almighty will put discord (and division) between your hearts."""
"1192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your rows straight, lest the devils slip in among you like the young of the hadhaf."" It was asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, what are the young of the hadhaf?"" It was said: ""They are black, hairless goats found in the land of Yemen."""
"1193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your rows straight and stand close together, for I see you even from behind my back."""
"1194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your rows straight and stand close together. By the One in whose Hand is my soul! I see the devils slipping in between your rows as though they were dust-coloured goats."""
"1195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The greatest of the major sins are: associating partners with Allah, killing a (innocent) soul, disobedience to parents, and false testimony."""
"1196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Write! By the One in whose Hand is my soul, nothing comes out of it (this tongue) except the truth."""
"1197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Use ithmid (antimony kohl), for it sharpens the eyesight and makes the eyelashes grow."""
"1198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Supplicate abundantly for well-being (safety and protection)."""
"1199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who eat their fill the most in this world will be the longest hungry in the Hereafter."""
"1200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have urged you very much regarding the use of the miswak."""
"1201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Most of the mistakes and sins of the son of Adam (a human being) are because of his tongue."""
"1202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Most of the punishment of the grave is because of urine (not guarding against its splashes)."""
"1203","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Most of the hypocrites of my Ummah will be its reciters (that is, those who recite the Qur'an for show)."""
"1204","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prostrate much, for there is no Muslim who performs a single prostration for Allah Almighty but that Allah Almighty raises him a rank in Paradise by it and wipes away a sin from him by it."""
"1205","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recite 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no might and no power except with Allah) abundantly, for it is one of the treasures of Paradise."""
"1206","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After the decree and predestination of Allah Almighty (that is, His decision and destiny), most of the deaths in my Ummah will be due to the evil eye."""
"1207","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Send abundant blessings (durood) upon me, for Allah Almighty has appointed an angel at my grave, so when a man from my Ummah sends blessings upon me, that angel says to me: 'O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! So-and-so, son of so-and-so, has just now sent blessings upon you.'"""
"1208","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Send abundant blessings upon me on the day of Friday, for whoever sends blessings upon me on the day of Friday, his blessing is (duly) presented to me."""
"1209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Send abundant blessings upon me on the day of Friday and the night of Friday, for whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah Almighty sends ten mercies upon him."""
"1210","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remember abundantly the destroyer (and ender) of pleasures, that is, death."""
"1211","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remember abundantly the ender of pleasures, that is, death, for whoever remembers it at a time of hardship in livelihood, it (the remembrance of death) makes that hardship spacious (and light) for him, and whoever remembers it in abundance and prosperity, it makes it (the spaciousness of this world) narrow for him (that is, it makes him aware of the impermanence of this world)."""
"1212","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Bear abundant witness that 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah), before death is made to come between you and it (this declaration), and prompt your dying ones (that is, those close to death) to say it."""
"1213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Plant the saplings of Paradise abundantly, for its water is sweet and its soil is excellent and fertile, so plant its saplings abundantly, and that (sapling) is saying 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no might and no power except with Allah)."""
"1214","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Say 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no might and no power except with Allah) abundantly, for it is among the treasures of Paradise."""
"1215","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make much use of shoes (that is, keep shoes on), for as long as a person keeps his shoes on, it is as if he remains riding (that is, because of the shoes he feels less of the hardship and fatigue of walking on foot)."""
"1216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most honoured of people is the one who is the most God-fearing (pious) among them."""
"1217","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most honoured and noble of people is Yusuf bin Ya'qub bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim (peace be upon them)."""
"1218","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Honour your hair and look after it well (by washing and oiling it) and keep it groomed."""
"1219","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Honour bread (that is, protect it from being wasted or falling, and value it)."""
"1220","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Honour the hair (that is, keep it clean and groomed)."""
"1221","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In it (that is, in the time of tribulation), break your bows, cut their strings, cling to the inner parts of your houses (that is, stay confined within them), and in it be like the better of the two sons of Adam (peace be upon him) (that is, like Habil, who accepted being killed but could not bear to kill)."""
"1222","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Lord of mankind! Remove the affliction."""
"1223","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Lord of mankind! O God of mankind! Remove the affliction."""
"1224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Lord of mankind! Remove the affliction, for none besides You can remove this distress and hardship."""
"1225","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Guarantee me six things, and I guarantee you Paradise: (1) when one of you speaks, let him not lie; (2) when something is entrusted to him, let him not betray the trust; (3) when he makes a promise, let him not break the promise; (4) lower your gazes; (5) restrain your hands (from wronging anyone); and (6) guard your private parts."""
"1226","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May the righteous eat your food, may the angels pray for mercy upon you, and may those who are fasting break their fast at your place."""
"1227","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eating any predatory animal with fangs (canine teeth) is forbidden."""
"1228","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take on only as much of (good) deeds as you are able to bear, for Allah Almighty does not grow weary (of giving reward) until you grow weary (of doing deeds), and indeed the most beloved deed to Allah Almighty is the one done constantly, even if it is little."""
"1229","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take on only as much of (good) deeds as you are able to bear, for the best deed is the one done constantly, even if it is little."""
"1230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most complete of the believers in faith is the one whose character is the best."""
"1231","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most complete of the believers in faith are those whose character is the best, who are gentle-natured and humble, who love and are familiar with people and whom people love and are familiar with; and there is no good in the one who neither is familiar with anyone nor is anyone familiar with him."""
"1232","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most complete in faith among the believers is the one whose character is the best, and the best of you are those who are best towards their women (wives)."""
"1233","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The milk of the cow is a cure, its ghee is a medicine, and its meat is a disease."""
"1234","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wear new clothes, live a praiseworthy (and righteous) life and die the death of a martyr, and may Allah grant you the coolness of the eyes in this world and the Hereafter."" (He (peace and blessings be upon him) made this supplication for Sayyiduna Umar bin al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him).)"
"1235","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wear white clothes, for they are very pure and fine, and shroud your dead in them as well."""
"1236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of your clothes, wear the white ones, for they are among the best of your clothes, and shroud your dead in them as well; and indeed the best of your kohl is ithmid: it sharpens the eyesight and makes the hair (of the eyelashes) grow."""
"1237","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek the hour on the day of Friday in which (the acceptance of supplication) is hoped for, from after Asr until the sun sets."""
"1238","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek Laylat al-Qadr (the Night of Decree) in the last night of Ramadan."""
"1239","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the odd nights of the last ten days of Ramadan, for this night was shown to me, then I was made to forget it."""
"1240","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the twenty-seventh night."""
"1241","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Look (for something as a dowry), even if it is only an iron ring."""
"1242","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek it (that is, Laylat al-Qadr) in the last ten days; then if one of you becomes weak or unable, let him by no means slacken in the remaining seven nights."""
"1243","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek it (Laylat al-Qadr) in the last ten days: when nine nights remain, or seven remain, or five remain, or three remain, or on the last night."""
"1244","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek it (that is, Laylat al-Qadr) in the last ten days of Ramadan: when nine nights remain, and when seven nights remain, and when five nights remain."""
"1245","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seek it in the last ten days of Ramadan, and seek it on the ninth (remaining), the seventh and the fifth (night)."""
"1246","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give the fixed shares to those entitled to them, then whatever remains is the right of the nearest male relative (asabah)."""
"1247","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cling to your house (that is, remain confined to your home in times of tribulation)."""
"1248","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cling to her (your mother's) feet (that is, serve her well), for Paradise is there."""
"1249","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to her (that is, remain devoted to her service), for Paradise is beneath her feet."" (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this with reference to the mother.)"
"1250","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hold fast to 'Ya Dhal-Jalali wal-Ikram' (O Possessor of Majesty and Honour) (that is, repeat this phrase often in your supplications)."""
"1251","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remove the hair of (the time of) disbelief, then get yourself circumcised."""
"1252","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah alone is the Physician."""
"1253","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty is with the judge as long as he does not act unjustly; when he acts unjustly, Allah abandons him and Satan attaches himself to him."""
"1254","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah and His Messenger are the guardian of the one who has no guardian, and the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir."""
"1255","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, place my most abundant provision in my old age and in the last part of my life."""
"1256","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, place in Madinah twice the blessing that You have placed in Makkah."""
"1257","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad in this world a bare sufficiency (only as much as is enough to get by)."""
"1258","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, make the death of my Ummah martyrdom in Your path, by the thrust of the spear and by the plague."""
"1259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, place light in my heart, place light in my tongue, place light in my sight, place light in my hearing, place light on my right, place light on my left, place light above me, place light beneath me, place light in front of me, place light behind me, and place light within my soul, and make the light great for me."""
"1260","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, protect me through Islam while standing, protect me through Islam while sitting, and protect me through Islam while lying down, and do not let any enemy or envier rejoice over me. O Allah, I ask You for every good whose treasures are in Your hand, and I seek refuge in You from every evil whose treasures are in Your hand."""
"1261","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, keep me alive as a poor, humble person, cause me to die as a poor, humble person, and raise me among the company of the poor and humble."""
"1262","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, conceal my faults, turn my fear into security, and settle my debt for me."""
"1263","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, set right for me my religion, which is the safeguard of my affairs; set right for me my worldly life, in which is my livelihood; and set right for me my Hereafter, to which I must return. Make life a means of increase for me in every good, and make death a relief for me from every evil."""
"1264","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, forgive me my sin, my ignorance and my excess in my affairs, and forgive me what You know better than I do. O Allah, forgive me my mistakes, what I did intentionally, my jesting and my seriousness; all of this is present in me. O Allah, forgive me what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have made public. You are the One who brings forward and You are the One who puts back, and You have power over all things."""
"1265","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, forgive me my sin, make my home spacious for me, and bless me in my provision."""
"1266","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, forgive all my sins and my errors. O Allah, revive me, remedy my weakness, and guide me to good deeds and good character, for none guides to their good and none turns away their evil except You."""
"1267","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, and join me with the Highest Companion."""
"1268","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, grant us such fear of You as will stand between us and disobedience to You, such obedience to You as will bring us to Your Paradise, and such certainty as will make the calamities of this world easy for us. Let us benefit from our hearing, our sight and our strength for as long as You keep us alive, and make it the heir from us. Take our revenge on those who have wronged us, and help us against those who show enmity towards us. Do not place our calamity in our religion, do not make this world our greatest concern or the limit of our knowledge, and do not give power over us to those who will show us no mercy."""
"1269","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, let me benefit from my hearing and my sight until You make them my heir, grant me well-being in my religion and in my body, and help me against whoever has wronged me until You show me my revenge upon him. O Allah, I have surrendered myself to You, entrusted my affair to You, placed my back under Your support and turned my face towards You. There is no place of refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Messenger whom You sent and in Your Book which You revealed."""
"1270","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, You created my soul and You will take it in death; its death and its life belong to You. If You keep it alive, protect it, and if You cause it to die, forgive it. O Allah, I ask You for well-being."""
"1271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, Ibrahim (peace be upon him) made Makkah a sanctuary and declared it sacred, and I have declared Madinah sacred between its two mountain passes: no blood is to be shed in it, no weapon is to be carried in it for fighting, and none of its trees is to be cut for any purpose other than fodder. O Allah, bless us in our city; O Allah, bless us in our sa'; O Allah, bless us in our mudd; O Allah, grant two blessings along with the blessing. By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no mountain pass or road of Madinah but that two angels are appointed over it to guard it, until you advance to it."""
"1272","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was Your servant and Your intimate friend; he supplicated to You for blessing for the people of Makkah. And I am Muhammad, Your servant and Your Messenger; I supplicate to You for the people of Madinah, that You bless them in their mudd and their sa' as much as You blessed the people of Makkah, indeed, two blessings along with the blessing."""
"1273","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, I make a covenant with You which You will never break: I am only a human being, so whichever believer I have hurt, or reviled, or flogged, or cursed, make it for him a mercy, a purification and a means of nearness by which You bring him near to Yourself on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1274","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, I ask You for chastity and well-being in my worldly life, my religion, my family and my wealth. O Allah, conceal my faults, turn my fear into security, and protect me from in front of me, from behind me, from my right, from my left and from above me, and I seek refuge in You from being seized unawares from beneath me."""
"1275","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity and self-sufficiency."""
"1276","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni as'aluka mina al-khayri kullihi, 'ajilihi wa ajilihi, ma 'alimtu minhu wa ma lam a'lam, wa a'udhu bika mina ash-sharri kullihi, 'ajilihi wa ajilihi, ma 'alimtu minhu wa ma lam a'lam. Allahumma inni as'aluka min khayri ma sa'alaka bihi 'abduka wa nabiyyuka, wa a'udhu bika min sharri ma 'adha bihi 'abduka wa nabiyyuka. Allahumma inni as'aluka al-jannata wa ma qarraba ilayha min qawlin aw 'amal, wa a'udhu bika mina an-nari wa ma qarraba ilayha min qawlin aw 'amal, wa as'aluka an taj'ala kulla qada'in qadaytahu li khayra' (O Allah, I ask You for every kind of good, whether it comes soon or late, what I know of it and what I do not know. And I seek refuge in You from every kind of evil, whether it comes soon or late, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your servant and Your Prophet asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your servant and Your Prophet sought refuge. O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and for every word and deed that brings one near to it, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and from every word and deed that brings one near to it, and I implore You to make every decree You have decreed for me good for me)."""
"1277","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni as'aluka mina al-khayri kullihi ma 'alimtu minhu wa ma lam a'lam, wa a'udhu bika mina ash-sharri kullihi ma 'alimtu minhu wa ma lam a'lam' (O Allah, I ask You for every kind of good, whether I know it or do not know it, and I seek refuge in You from every kind of evil, whether I know it or do not know it)."""
"1278","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni as'aluka min fadlika wa rahmatik, fa innahu la yamlikuha illa ant' (O Allah, I ask You of Your bounty and Your mercy, for no one but You has any control over them)."""
"1279","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni as'aluka wa atawajjahu ilayka bi-nabiyyika Muhammadin nabiyyi ar-rahmah. Ya Muhammad, inni tawajjahtu bika ila rabbi fi hajati hadhihi li-tuqda li. Allahumma fa-shaffi'hu fiyya' (O Allah, I ask You and turn to You through Your Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), the Prophet of mercy. O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), I have turned through you to my Lord concerning this need of mine, so that it may be fulfilled for me. O Allah, accept his intercession on my behalf)."""
"1280","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bi-ridaka min sakhatik, wa bi-mu'afatika min 'uqubatik, wa a'udhu bika mink, la uhsi thana'an 'alayk, anta kama athnayta 'ala nafsik' (O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your displeasure, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot fully enumerate Your praise; You are as You have praised Yourself)."""
"1281","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina al-barasi wal-jununi wal-judhami wa min sayyi'i al-asqam' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from leprous white patches, madness, leprosy and all evil diseases)."""
"1282","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina at-taraddi wal-hadmi wal-gharaqi wal-haraq, wa a'udhu bika an yatakhabbatani ash-shaytanu 'inda al-mawt, wa a'udhu bika an amuta fi sabilika mudbira, wa a'udhu bika an amuta ladigha' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from falling from a height, from being crushed beneath something, from drowning and from burning. And I seek refuge in You from Satan confounding me at the time of death, and I seek refuge in You from dying in Your path while turning my back and fleeing, and I seek refuge in You from dying from the sting or bite of a venomous creature)."""
"1283","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina al-ju'i fa innahu bi'sa ad-daji', wa a'udhu bika mina al-khiyanati fa innaha bi'sati al-bitanah' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from hunger, for it is an evil companion, and I seek refuge in You from treachery, for it is an evil inner trait)."""
"1284","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina al-'ajzi wal-kasali wal-jubni wal-bukhli wal-haram, wa a'udhu bika min 'adhabi al-qabr, wa a'udhu bika min 'adhabi an-nar, wa a'udhu bika min fitnati al-mahya wal-mamat' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness and extreme old age; I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave; I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire; and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death)."""
"1285","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina al-'ajzi wal-kasali wal-jubni wal-bukhli wal-harami wal-qaswati wal-ghaflati wal-'aylati wadh-dhillati wal-maskanah, wa a'udhu bika mina al-faqri wal-kufri wal-fusuqi wash-shiqaqi wan-nifaqi was-sum'ati war-riya', wa a'udhu bika mina as-samami wal-bakami wal-jununi wal-judhami wal-barasi wa sayyi'i al-asqam' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, extreme old age, hardness of heart, heedlessness, destitution, humiliation and wretchedness. And I seek refuge in You from poverty and want, disbelief, disobedience, opposition to the truth, hypocrisy, seeking fame and showing off. And I seek refuge in You from deafness, dumbness, madness, leprosy, leprous white patches and all evil diseases)."""
"1286","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina al-'ajzi wal-kasali wal-jubni wal-bukhli wal-harami wa 'adhabi al-qabri wa fitnati ad-dajjal. Allahumma ati nafsi taqwaha, wa zakkiha anta khayru man zakkaha, anta waliyyuha wa mawlaha. Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min 'ilmin la yanfa', wa min qalbin la yakhsha', wa min nafsin la tashba', wa min da'watin la yustajabu laha' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, extreme old age, the punishment of the grave and the trial of the Dajjal. O Allah, grant my soul its piety and purify it, for You are the best of those who purify it; You are its Guardian and its Master. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, from a heart that has no fear of You, from a soul that is never satisfied, and from a supplication that is not answered)."""
"1287","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu mina al-faqri wal-qillati wadh-dhillah, wa a'udhu bika min an azlima aw uzlam' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty, scarcity and humiliation, and I also seek refuge in You from wronging anyone or being wronged)."""
"1288","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina al-kasali wal-harami wal-ma'thami wal-maghram, wa min fitnati al-qabri wa 'adhabi al-qabr, wa min fitnati an-nari wa 'adhabi an-nar, wa min sharri fitnati al-ghina, wa a'udhu bika min fitnati al-faqr, wa a'udhu bika min fitnati al-masihi ad-dajjal. Allahumma ighsil 'anni khatayaya bil-ma'i wath-thalji wal-barad, wa naqqi qalbi mina al-khataya kama yunaqqa ath-thawbu al-abyadu mina ad-danas, wa ba'id bayni wa bayna khatayaya kama ba'adta bayna al-mashriqi wal-maghrib' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, extreme old age, sin and debt. I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the grave, from the trial of Hell and the punishment of Hell, and from the evil of the trial of wealth; I seek refuge in You from the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Masih ad-Dajjal. O Allah, wash away my sins with water, snow and hail, and cleanse my heart of sins as a white garment is cleansed of dirt, and put as great a distance between me and my sins as You have put between the East and the West)."""
"1289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika mina al-hammi wal-hazani wal-'ajzi wal-kasali wal-bukhli wal-jubni wa dala'i ad-dayni wa ghalabati ar-rijal' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from miserliness and cowardice, and from the burden of debt and the domination and control of people)."""
"1290","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min jari as-saw'i fi dari al-muqamah, fa inna jara al-badiyati yatahawwal' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a bad neighbour in the place of permanent residence, that is, in one's own neighbourhood or settlement, for the neighbour of the desert and of travel moves on)."""
"1291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min zawali ni'matik, wa tahawwuli 'afiyatik, wa fuj'ati niqmatik, wa jami'i sakhatik' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the loss of the blessing You have given, from the change of the well-being You have granted, from Your sudden punishment, and from every kind of Your displeasure)."""
"1292","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min sharri sam'i wa min sharri basari wa min sharri lisani wa min sharri qalbi wa min sharri maniyyati' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my hearing, from the evil of my sight, from the evil of my tongue, from the evil of my heart and from the evil of my death)."""
"1293","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min sharri ma 'amiltu wa min sharri ma lam a'mal' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of every deed that I have done and from the evil of every deed that I have not done)."""
"1294","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min 'adhabi al-qabr, wa a'udhu bika min 'adhabi an-nar, wa a'udhu bika min fitnati al-mahya wal-mamat, wa a'udhu bika min fitnati al-masihi ad-dajjal' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire, I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Masih ad-Dajjal)."""
"1295","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min 'ilmin la yanfa', wa 'amalin la yurfa', wa du'a'in la yusma'' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, from a deed that is not raised up to Your presence, and from a supplication that is not heard)."""
"1296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min ghalabati ad-dayni wa ghalabati al-'aduwwi wa shamatati al-a'da'' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from being overwhelmed by the burden of debt, from the domination and control of the enemy, and from the gloating of enemies, that is, a misfortune over which enemies rejoice)."""
"1297","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min qalbin la yakhsha', wa min du'a'in la yusma', wa min nafsin la tashba', wa min 'ilmin la yanfa', a'udhu bika min ha'ula'i al-arba'' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a heart that has no fear of You, from a supplication that is not answered, from a soul that is never satisfied, and from knowledge that does not benefit. I seek refuge in You from these four things)."""
"1298","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min munkarati al-akhlaqi wal-a'mali wal-ahwa'i wal-adwa'' (O Allah, I seek refuge in You from evil character, evil deeds, evil desires and evil diseases)."""
"1299","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min yawmis-su', wa min laylatis-su', wa min sa'atis-su', wa min sahibis-su', wa min jaris-su' fi daril-muqamah' (O Allah! I seek refuge in You from an evil day, from an evil night, from an evil hour, from an evil companion, and from an evil neighbour in the place of permanent residence.)"""
"1300","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma barik li-ummati fi bukuriha' (O Allah! Bless my Ummah in its early hours, that is, in the morning time.)"""
"1301","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma bi-'ilmikal-ghayba wa qudratika 'alal-khalqi ahyini ma 'alimtal-hayata khayran li, wa tawaffani idha 'alimtal-wafata khayran li. Allahumma wa as'aluka khashyataka fil-ghaybi wash-shahadah, wa as'aluka kalimatal-ikhlasi fir-rida wal-ghadab, wa as'alukal-qasda fil-faqri wal-ghina, wa as'aluka na'iman la yanfad, wa as'aluka qurrata 'aynin la tanqati', wa as'alukar-rida bil-qada', wa as'aluka bardal-'ayshi ba'dal-mawt, wa as'aluka ladhdhatan-nazari ila wajhik, wash-shawqa ila liqa'ik, fi ghayri darra'a mudirrah, wa la fitnatin mudillah. Allahumma zayyinna bi-zinatil-iman, waj'alna hudatan muhtadin' (O Allah! By Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, I ask You to keep me alive as long as, according to Your knowledge, life is better for me, and to give me death when death is better for me. O Allah! I ask You for fear of You in every state, hidden and open; I ask You for the word of truth and sincerity in both states, contentment and anger; I ask You for moderation in both states, poverty and wealth; I ask You for a blessing that never ends; I ask You for a coolness of the eyes that is never cut off; I ask You for contentment with Your decrees; I ask You for a tranquil life after death; and I ask You for the delight of looking at Your Face and for longing to meet You, without any harmful affliction and without any misleading trial. O Allah! Adorn us with the adornment of faith, and make us rightly guided and a means of guidance for others.)"""
"1302","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma hajjatun la riya'a fiha wa la sum'ah' (O Allah! This is a Hajj in which there is no showing off and no seeking of fame.)"""
"1303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma rabban-nas, mudhhibal-ba's, ishfi antash-shafi, la shafiya illa ant, ishfi shifa'an la yughadiru saqama' (O Allah! O Lord of mankind! Remover of affliction! Grant healing, You are the Healer; there is no healer but You. Grant a healing that leaves behind no illness at all.)"""
"1304","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma rabba Jibrila wa Mika'ila wa Israfila wa Muhammadin sallallahu 'alayhi wa sallam, na'udhu bika minan-nar' (O Allah! Lord of Jibril, Mika'il, Israfil and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! We seek refuge in You from the Fire of Hell.)"""
"1305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma rabba Jibrila wa Mika'ila wa rabba Israfil, a'udhu bika min harrin-nari wa min 'adhabil-qabr' (O Allah! Lord of Jibril and Mika'il, and Lord of Israfil! I seek refuge in You from the heat of the Fire of Hell and from the punishment of the grave.)"""
"1306","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! 'Our Lord, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter as well, and save us from the punishment of the Fire.' [Surah al-Baqarah: 201]"""
"1307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma kama hassanta khalqi fa-hassin khuluqi' (O Allah! Just as You have made my form and creation beautiful, so make my character and conduct beautiful as well.)"""
"1308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma la 'aysha illa 'ayshul-akhirah' (O Allah! True and lasting life is only the life of the Hereafter.)"""
"1309","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma laka aslamtu, wa bika amantu, wa 'alayka tawakkaltu, wa ilayka anabtu, wa bika khasamtu. Allahumma inni a'udhu bi-'izzatika, la ilaha illa anta, an tudillani. Antal-hayyul-ladhi la yamutu, wal-jinnu wal-insu yamutun' (O Allah! To You alone I have submitted, in You alone I have believed, upon You alone I have relied, to You alone I have turned, and with Your help alone I have contended with my enemies. O Allah! I seek refuge in Your might, there is no true god but You, from Your leading me astray. You are the Ever-Living who will never die, while all jinn and humans must die.)"""
"1310","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""'Allahumma matti'ni bi-sam'i wa basari, waj'alhumal-waritha minni, wansurni 'ala man zalamani, wa khudh minhu bi-tha'ri' (O Allah! Let me benefit from my hearing and my sight, and make them both my heir (that is, keep them sound until my last breath); help me against whoever wrongs me, and take my revenge on him.)"""
"1311","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Whoever believes in You and bears witness that I am Your Messenger, place in his heart love of meeting You, make Your decree easy for him, and lessen his desire for this world. And whoever does not believe in You and does not bear witness that I am Your Messenger, do not place in his heart love of meeting You, do not make Your decree easy for him, and give him an abundance of this world."""
"1312","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Whoever is put in charge of any affair of my Ummah and is harsh with them, be harsh with him; and whoever is put in charge of any affair of my Ummah and treats them gently, treat him gently."""
"1313","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have you not seen a person when he dies, how his eyes remain open and staring? That happens when his gaze follows the soul leaving his body."""
"1314","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have you not seen what your Lord has said? Allah Almighty said: 'Whenever I bestow any blessing upon My servants (such as sending down rain), a group of them becomes ungrateful for it; they say: ""It is such-and-such a star, and the rain came through the influence of such-and-such a star.""'"""
"1315","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know what befell a man of the Children of Israel? It was their practice (the Children of Israel) that when urine got on any part of their body or clothing, they would cut off the place the urine had touched. This man forbade them from doing that, and because of it he was punished in his grave."""
"1316","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did this second man not live one more year after the first man (who had been martyred), and did he not reach the month of Ramadan and fast it, and perform so many prostrations (prayers) over the year? The difference between the ranks of the two of them is greater than the distance between the heavens and the earth."""
"1317","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this son of yours will not be held responsible for any crime of yours, nor will you be held responsible for any crime of his."""
"1318","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! Had you recited this supplication in the evening, 'A'udhu bi-kalimatillahit-tammati min sharri ma khalaq' (I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of everything He has created), it (the scorpion's sting) would not have harmed you."""
"1319","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Had you not given him (the child) anything, a lie would have been recorded against you in your record of deeds."""
"1320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Soon you will have carpets and cushions (for better and more spacious living)."""
"1321","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! If he has sworn a false oath in order to consume (someone's) wealth unjustly, he will meet Allah Almighty while Allah Almighty is displeased with him and turning away from him."""
"1322","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! The nations before you were destroyed only when they fell into a misguidance like this: they began to strike one part of the Book of Allah against another (and to set its parts in contradiction). It is necessary for you to regard what is lawful as lawful, to hold what is unlawful as unlawful, and simply to believe in what is ambiguous (whose meaning is not fully clear)."""
"1323","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remember! Had he said 'Bismillah' (In the name of Allah) before eating, that food would have been sufficient for all of you. So when any of you eats food, let him say 'Bismillah'; and if he forgets to say it at the beginning, let him say: 'Bismillahi awwalahu wa akhirahu' (In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end)."""
"1324","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remember! Had he recited this supplication in the evening, 'A'udhu bi-kalimatillahit-tammati min sharri ma khalaq' (I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of everything He has created), a scorpion's sting would never have harmed him until morning."""
"1325","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remember! The people who come after you will never attain the blessing and virtue of your sa' (a particular measure) and your mudd (a quarter of a sa')."""
"1326","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Has it not reached you that I have cursed the one who brands an animal on its face or strikes it on its face?"""
"1327","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Are you not pleased that they (the disbelievers) should have the goods of this world, and we should have the Hereafter (with its everlasting blessings)?"""
"1328","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did you not see the one (the angel) who appeared before me a short while ago? He was one of the angels who had never descended to the earth before this night. He sought permission from his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, to greet me with salam and to give me the glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) are the leaders of the youth of the people of Paradise, and that Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) is the leader of the women of the people of Paradise."""
"1329","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know that embracing Islam demolishes all the sins that came before it, that emigrating (hijrah) wipes out the sins that came before it, and that performing Hajj also erases all the sins that came before it?"""
"1330","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know that the angels do not enter a house in which there is a picture (of a living being), and that those who make pictures will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: 'Now bring to life what you have created'?"""
"1331","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know that you and your wealth are part of your father's earnings?"""
"1332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know that an angel calls out in the heavens, making this supplication: 'O Allah! Give the one who spends in the way of Allah the best replacement, and bring ruin upon the wealth of the miser'?"""
"1333","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Could this man not find anything with which to tidy his dishevelled hair? Could this man not find anything (water and the like) with which to wash his clothes?"""
"1334","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Have you not passed by the valley of your people when it was completely barren and drought-stricken, then passed by it and found it green and flourishing, then passed by it and it was barren, then passed by it and it was green? (Life after death will come in exactly the same way, as Allah Almighty says:) 'Thus does Allah bring the dead to life.' [Surah al-Baqarah: 73]"""
"1335","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! By Allah, I am indeed the one among you who fears Allah the most and who is the most mindful of Him."""
"1336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! By Allah, I am the one among you who fears Allah the most and is the most mindful of Him, yet (despite this) I fast and I also leave off fasting, I pray (voluntary prayer at night) and I also sleep, and I have married women. So whoever turns away from my Sunnah has nothing to do with me."""
"1337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! By Allah, I am trustworthy (amin) in the sight of the inhabitants of the heavens, and trustworthy in the sight of the inhabitants of the earth."""
"1338","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! By Allah, had Usamah been a girl, I would surely have adorned her with jewellery and beautified her so that I could send her off (that is, give her in marriage)."""
"1339","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! By Allah, were it not the rule that envoys (ambassadors) are not killed, I would have struck off both your necks."""
"1340","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does not any of you fear that, when he raises his head (towards the sky) during prayer, his sight may not be returned to him (that is, it may be taken away)?"""
"1341","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does not any of you fear that, when he raises his head (from bowing or prostration) before the imam, Allah Almighty may change his head into the head of a donkey, or Allah Almighty may make his form the form of a donkey?"""
"1342","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for Ibrahim (peace be upon him), look at your companion (that is, me; I resemble him). As for Musa (peace be upon him), he was of a wheatish complexion with curly hair. It is as if I can see him descending into the valley, riding a red camel and reciting the Talbiyah, its nose-rein made of a rope of palm fibre."""
"1343","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The man should (when taking the ritual bath) loosen the hair of his head thoroughly and wash it until the water reaches the roots of the hair. As for the woman, it is not necessary for her to undo her braided hair; she need only pour three handfuls of water over her head, and that is sufficient for her."""
"1344","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for me, I take water three times with the palms of both my hands and pour it over my head, then I pour water over the rest of my body."""
"1345","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for me, I pour water over my head three times (when taking the ritual bath)."""
"1346","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for me, I do not eat while reclining."""
"1347","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ja'far! You resemble me in both my appearance and my character. O Ali! You are from me and I am from you. O Zayd! You are our brother and our mawla (friend). And this girl will stay with her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt is like a mother."""
"1348","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Ja'far! Your appearance is like my appearance, and my character is like your character, and you are from me and from my family tree. O Ali! You are my son-in-law and the father of my grandchildren; I am from you and you are from me. O Zayd! You are my mawla (freed slave), you are from me and belong to me, and you are the most beloved to me of all these people."""
"1349","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first of the signs of the Hour will be a fire that will come out from the east and drive the people to the west. The first thing the people of Paradise will be given to eat will be the caudate lobe of the fish's liver (i.e., its choicest piece). As for the child's resemblance to its father or mother: when the man's fluid precedes the woman's fluid, the child is drawn towards the father (i.e., resembles him), and when the woman's fluid precedes the man's fluid, the child resembles the mother."""
"1350","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for the permanent inhabitants of Hell who are deserving of it, they will neither die in it nor live (rather, they will remain in continuous punishment). However, there will be some people whom the Fire will touch because of their sins, and it will burn them until they die, until, when they have become charcoal, permission for intercession will be given. Then they will be brought group after group and spread out upon the rivers of Paradise. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise, pour water over them.' So they will sprout just as a seed sprouts in the debris carried by a flood."""
"1351","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: O people, listen! I am only a human being, and soon the messenger of my Lord (the angel of death) will come to me and I will respond to his call. I am leaving among you two weighty things. The first of them is the Book of Allah, in which there is guidance and light. Whoever holds fast to it and acts upon it will remain upon guidance, and whoever strays from it will go astray. So hold fast to the Book of Allah. And (the second is) my family (Ahl al-Bayt). I remind you of Allah concerning my family; I remind you of Allah concerning my family."""
"1352","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: O people, the number of people will keep increasing, but the Ansar will keep decreasing, until they become among the people like salt in food. So whoever among you is put in charge of an affair in which he is able to harm someone or benefit someone, let him accept the good from those among them (the Ansar) who do good, and overlook the faults of those among them who err."""
"1353","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: Indeed, the most truthful speech is the Book of Allah, the best way is the way of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and the worst of affairs are newly invented matters (in the religion). Every newly invented matter is an innovation (bid'ah), every innovation is misguidance, and every misguidance leads to the Fire. The Hour will come upon you suddenly. I and the Hour have been sent together like these two (fingers). The Hour has come upon your heads. I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever dies leaving wealth, it belongs to his family, and whoever leaves a debt or helpless children, the responsibility for it is upon me and they are to come to me. And I am the guardian and patron of the believers."""
"1354","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: Indeed, Allah Almighty has revealed in His Book: 'O people, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul' [Surah an-Nisa: 1], to the end of the verse. And He said: 'O you who believe, fear Allah, and let every soul look to what it has sent forth for tomorrow' [Surah al-Hashr: 18], and he recited up to 'they are the successful' [Surah al-Hashr: 20]. Then he said: Give charity before the time comes when you will be unable to give charity. Let a man give charity from his dinar, let a man give charity from his dirham, let a man give from his wheat, from his dates, and from his barley. Never regard any charity as insignificant, even if it is only a piece of a date."""
"1355","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: Your state and eagerness last night were not hidden from me (that you were waiting to pray with me), but I feared that the night prayer (Tarawih) would be made obligatory upon you and that you would then be unable to perform it."""
"1356","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that have no basis in the Book of Allah? Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is utterly void, even if there are a hundred conditions. The decree of Allah is most deserving of being followed, and the condition of Allah is the most binding. And wala' (the right of inheritance that comes from freeing a slave) belongs only to the one who sets free."""
"1357","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: What is the matter with the official (who collects zakah) whom we appoint to a task, and then he comes to us and says: 'This is the wealth from your work (i.e., the zakah), and this was given to me as a gift'? Why did he not sit in the house of his father and mother and then see whether he would be given gifts or not? By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! None of you misappropriates anything from it except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying it on his neck. If it is a camel, it will be groaning; if it is a cow, it will be lowing; and if it is a sheep, it will be bleating. Indeed, I have conveyed (the message of Allah)."""
"1358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: By Allah, I give wealth to one man and leave another, even though the one I leave is more beloved to me than the one I give to. But I give to some people because I see impatience and anxiety in their hearts, and I entrust other people to the self-sufficiency (contentment) and goodness that Allah has placed in their hearts. Among these (patient and content) people is Amr bin Taghlib."""
"1359","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To proceed: O people of Quraysh! You are the rightful holders of this matter (i.e., the caliphate and leadership) as long as you do not disobey Allah. But when you disobey Him, He will set over you people who will strip you just as this stick is stripped (of its bark)."""
"1360","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for your going out from your house intending the Sacred House (the Ka'bah), for every step your mount places on the ground Allah Almighty writes a good deed for you in return and erases a sin from you in return. As for your standing at Arafah, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of them (the pilgrims) before the angels, saying: 'These are My servants who have come to Me with dishevelled hair and covered in dust from every distant path, hoping for My mercy and fearing My punishment, though they have not seen Me. So how would they be if they saw Me?' So even if you had sins equal to the grains of sand of Alij (a particular place), or equal to the days of the world, or equal to the drops of rain from the sky, Allah Almighty will wash them away from you (i.e., forgive them). As for your stoning of the Jamarat, that is stored up for you. As for the shaving of your head, for every hair that falls you have a good deed. Then, when you perform tawaf of the House, you come out of your sins as pure as on the day your mother gave birth to you."""
"1361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for the trial of the Dajjal, there has been no prophet who did not warn his nation about him, but I will warn you about him by telling you something that no prophet told his nation: he is one-eyed, and Allah Almighty is certainly not one-eyed. Between the Dajjal's eyes will be written 'Kafir' (disbeliever), which every believer will be able to read. As for the punishment of the grave (the trial of the grave), it is on account of me that you will be tried, and it is about me that you will be questioned. When a righteous man is seated in his grave, he sits without any fear. Then it is said to him: 'Who is this man who was sent among you?' He says: 'Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. He came to us with clear proofs from Allah, and we believed him.' Then a window is opened for him towards Hell, and he sees it, parts of it crushing other parts. Then it is said to him: 'Look at what Allah has saved you from.' Then a window is opened for him towards Paradise, and he sees its splendour and the blessings within it. Then it is said to him: 'This is your abode.' It is also said to him: 'You remained upon complete certainty, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised again, if Allah wills.' And when an evil man is seated in his grave, he is terrified. He is asked: 'What did you used to say?' He says: 'I do not know.' Then he is asked: 'Who is this man who was sent among you?' He says: 'I heard people saying something, so I said the same.' Then a window is opened for him towards Paradise, and he sees its splendour and its blessings. Then it is said to him: 'Look at what Allah has turned away from you.' Then a window is opened for him towards Hell, and he sees it, parts of it crushing other parts, and it is said to him: 'This is your abode. You remained upon doubt, upon it you died, and upon this doubt you will be raised again, if Allah wills.' Then he is punished."""
"1362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for the cutting off of the roads (lawlessness), only a little time will pass over you before trade caravans travel to Makkah without any guard. As for poverty and need, the Hour will not be established until one of you goes about with his charity and finds no one who will accept it from him. Then each one of you will surely stand before Allah, with no veil between him and Allah, nor any interpreter to translate for him. Then Allah Almighty will say to him: 'Did I not give you wealth?' He will say: 'Yes.' Then He will say: 'Did I not send a messenger to you?' He will say: 'Yes.' Then that person will look to his right and see nothing but fire, then he will look to his left and see nothing but fire. So let each one of you protect himself from the Fire of Hell, even if only by means of a piece of a date, and if he cannot find even that, then by means of a good and kind word."""
"1363","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As for what you mentioned about the vessels of the People of the Book: if you find other vessels, do not eat from them, and if you do not find any other vessels, then wash them well and eat from them. Whatever you hunt with your bow and mention the name of Allah over, eat it; and whatever you hunt with your trained dog and mention the name of Allah over, eat that too; and whatever you hunt with your untrained dog, but you find it alive and slaughter it, eat that as well."""
"1364","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ahead of you is a Pond (Hawd) whose width is equal to the distance between Jarba and Adhruh (two places)."""
"1365","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best of the things with which you treat yourselves is cupping (hijamah) and sea costus (qust bahri, a medicinal root)."""
"1366","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Adam has been commanded to prostrate (in prayer) on seven bones (i.e., limbs)."""
"1367","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The messengers were commanded to eat only what is pure and to do only righteous deeds."""
"1368","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to give Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) the glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl, in which there will be neither noise nor fatigue and toil."""
"1369","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones (limbs): on the forehead, on both hands, on both knees, and on the tips of both feet; and (I have also been commanded) that we do not gather up (i.e., tuck up) our clothes or hair in prayer."""
"1370","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no true god except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. When they say it, they have protected their lives and their wealth from me, except by the right of Islam, and their (inner) reckoning is with Allah Almighty."""
"1371","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no true god except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and they establish the prayer and pay the zakah. When they do that, they have protected their lives and their wealth from me, except by the right of Islam, and their reckoning is with Allah Almighty."""
"1372","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no true god except Allah, and believe in me and in the Shari'ah that I have brought. When they do that, they have certainly protected their lives and their wealth from me, except by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"1373","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah). So whoever says 'La ilaha illallah' has certainly protected his life and his wealth from me, except by its right, and his reckoning is with Allah Almighty."""
"1374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to recite the Qur'an in seven ahruf (i.e., seven different modes of recitation), each of which is healing and sufficient."""
"1375","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was commanded to use the miswak so emphatically that I began to fear that my teeth would fall out (from using it so much)."""
"1376","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was commanded to use the miswak so emphatically that I began to fear that it would be made obligatory upon me."""
"1377","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was commanded to use the miswak so emphatically that I began to fear for my teeth (that they would wear down)."""
"1378","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded (to emigrate) to a town that will devour all other towns (i.e., prevail over them). People call it Yathrib, but it is Madinah. It expels the (evil) people from within it just as the bellows remove the impurities of iron."""
"1379","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your affair after me is among the things that concern me, and in fulfilling your rights only those who are patient will remain steadfast."""
"1380","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We have been commanded to perform ablution (wudu) completely and well (by washing the limbs fully)."""
"1381","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We have been commanded to say after the prayers 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times, 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is for Allah) thirty-three times, and 'Allahu Akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) thirty-four times."""
"1382","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) commanded me to say the takbir."""
"1383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) commanded me to use the miswak so emphatically that I began to think I would lose my teeth (from using it so much)."""
"1384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) commanded me to raise my voice when calling out the Talbiyah after entering ihram, for it is indeed one of the prominent rites of Hajj."""
"1385","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wipe away the nasal mucus of the sheep and goats, keep their pens clean, and pray on one side of their pens, for they are among the animals of Paradise."""
"1386","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wipe over the leather socks for three days."""
"1387","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep some of your wealth for yourself; that is better for you."""
"1388","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your wealth for yourselves and do not waste it, for whoever gives someone a lifelong gift ('umra), it belongs to that person and his descendants, in his lifetime and after his death."""
"1389","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Walk in front of me, and leave (the area behind) my back free for the angels."""
"1390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remove harmful things from the road, for that too is a charity for you."""
"1391","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your tongue under your control."""
"1392","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your tongue under your control, let your house be spacious enough for you (i.e., do not leave your house without need), and weep over your sins."""
"1393","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your hand under your control."""
"1394","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Umm al-Qur'an (Surah al-Fatihah) is the Seven Oft-Repeated (verses) (the seven verses recited again and again) and the Mighty Qur'an."""
"1395","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of my Ummah will be (on the Day of Resurrection) the ones with radiant faces and shining limbs (due to ablution)."""
"1396","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This Ummah of mine is an Ummah that has been shown mercy. There will be no punishment upon it in the Hereafter; its punishment is only in this world, in the form of trials, earthquakes, killing and afflictions."""
"1397","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the people of my Ummah will have radiant faces because of their abundant prostrations and shining limbs because of ablution."""
"1398","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Lead your people in prayer. Whoever leads people in prayer should keep the prayer light, for among them are the elderly, the sick, the weak and those with needs. But when one of you prays alone, let him pray as long as he wishes."""
"1399","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(The person most entitled to good treatment is) your mother, then your mother, then your mother, after that your father, and then whoever is a closer relative is entitled to that same degree."""
"1400","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(Treat well) your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, and then (treat well) each relative in order of how close they are to you."""
"1401","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When (this verse of the Qur'an) 'not of those who have earned (Your) anger, nor of those who go astray' is recited, say Amin."" [Surah al-Fatihah: 7]"
"1402","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) led me in prayer at the House (of Allah) twice. He led me in the Zuhr prayer when the sun had passed its zenith and the shadow was the length of a sandal strap; he led me in the Asr prayer when the shadow of everything was equal to its length; he led me in the Maghrib prayer at the time the fasting person breaks his fast; he led me in the Isha prayer when the twilight had disappeared; and he led me in the Fajr prayer at the time when food and drink become forbidden for the fasting person. Then, when the next day came, he led me in the Zuhr prayer when the shadow of everything was equal to its length; he led me in the Asr prayer when the shadow of everything was twice its length; he led me in the Maghrib prayer at the same time, when the fasting person breaks his fast; he led me in the Isha prayer up to one third of the night; and he led me in the Fajr prayer when the light had spread. Then he turned to me and said: 'O Muhammad, this is the time of the prophets before you, and the (prayer) time is between these two times.'"""
"1403","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The trustees of the Muslims over their prayers and their suhur are the mu'adhdhins."""
"1404","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give some respite (that is, wait) so that we enter (our homes) at night, so that the woman with dishevelled hair may comb it, and the woman whose husband was away on a journey may remove her unwanted hair."""
"1405","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Remove this curtain of yours from us, for its pictures keep appearing before me in my prayer."""
"1406","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The trustworthy one of this Ummah is Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"1407","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you cannot refrain from sitting on the roads, then guide the one who has lost his way, return the greeting of salam, and help the wronged."""
"1408","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you keep your hair, then honour it (that is, keep it clean and comb it)."""
"1409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you would love for Allah Almighty and His Messenger to love you, then when something is entrusted to you, give it back; when you speak, speak the truth; and treat well whoever is your neighbour."""
"1410","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you want your heart to become soft, then feed the poor and pass your hand over the head of the orphan."""
"1411","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Even if a black slave with his nose and ears cut off is made your leader, as long as he leads you according to the Book of Allah, listen to him and obey."""
"1412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you overpower him (the enemy), kill him, but do not burn him with fire, for none may punish with fire except the Lord of the fire (Allah Almighty)."""
"1413","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you sold dates to your brother and then some calamity struck those dates (and they were ruined), it is not lawful for you to take anything from him. On what basis would you take your brother's wealth unjustly?!"""
"1414","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you are attacked suddenly at night, then your watchword (secret password of recognition) should be 'Ha Mim, la yunsarun' (Ha Mim, they will not be helped)."""
"1415","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you are true to Allah, He will be true to you in fulfilling His promise."""
"1416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you criticise his leadership (that is, of Usamah bin Zayd), then before this you criticised the leadership of his father. By Allah, he was certainly worthy of leadership, and he was among the people most beloved to me, and after him this one (Usamah bin Zayd) too is among the people most beloved to me. I enjoin you to treat him well, for he is one of the righteous among you."""
"1417","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, if You forgive, You forgive abundantly, and which servant of Yours is there who has not committed a sin?"""
"1418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you wish, keep its principal (that is, the land or property) withheld (that is, make it an endowment) and give its produce in charity."""
"1419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you two wish, I will give you (from the charity), but there is no share in it for a rich person, nor for a strong, healthy person able to earn."""
"1420","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you wish, I will tell you what leadership is. Its beginning is blame, its second stage is regret, and its third stage is punishment on the Day of Resurrection, except for the one who acted justly."""
"1421","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I live, in sha' Allah, I will certainly forbid my Ummah from giving the names Nafi', Aflah and Barakah."""
"1422","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If any of them (the sacrificial animals) becomes exhausted and breaks down (or is close to dying), then slaughter it (by nahr), then dip its neck-marker in its own blood and strike it on its side, and leave it for the people so that they may eat it."""
"1423","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If any of them (the sacrificial animals) breaks down and you fear it will die, then slaughter it, then dip its neck-marker in its own blood and strike it on its side. But neither you yourself nor anyone of your travelling companions should eat any of that meat; rather, distribute it (among the people)."""
"1424","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the Hour begins to be established while one of you has a small palm seedling in his hand, then if he is able to plant it before the Hour is established, let him plant it."""
"1425","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you are killed in the path of Allah while being steadfast, seeking the reward, advancing (towards the enemy) and not turning your back, Allah Almighty will forgive all your sins except debt. Jibril (peace be upon him) told me this just a little while ago."""
"1426","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If Allah Almighty has decreed something (the creation of a child), it will certainly come to be, even if the man practises withdrawal ('azl)."""
"1427","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If ill omen were in anything, it would be in the house, the woman and the horse."""
"1428","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If he has gone out striving to earn a living for his young children, he is in the path of Allah; if he has gone out to provide for his elderly, frail parents, he is in the path of Allah; if he has gone out to work to keep himself (from the humiliation of begging), he is in the path of Allah; but if he has gone out for show and boasting, then he is in the path of Satan."""
"1429","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you have water that has been kept overnight in an old waterskin, give us some to drink; otherwise we will drink (directly from the stream) with our mouths."""
"1430","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If there is good in anything among your methods of treatment, it is cupping (hijamah)."""
"1431","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If there is healing in anything among your remedies, it is in the incision of the cupper, or a drink of honey, or cauterisation with fire suited to the illness, but I do not like to be cauterised."""
"1432","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If that (pollinating the date palms) benefits them, then let them do it. I merely expressed an assumption, so do not hold me to account for my assumption. But when I tell you something from Allah, hold firmly to it, for I will never lie against Allah."""
"1433","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you have committed a sin, then seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty and repent to Him, for true repentance from sin is (in fact) remorse and seeking forgiveness."""
"1434","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you want to keep (voluntary) fasts, then fast the Ayyam al-Bid (the 13th, 14th and 15th of the lunar month)."""
"1435","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you want to fast, then keep to the days of the bright moonlit nights: that is, the 13th, 14th and 15th."""
"1436","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you truly are a servant of Allah, then raise your lower garment (above the ankles)."""
"1437","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Just a little while ago you were doing what the people of Persia and Rome do: they stand over their kings while the kings are sitting. Never do that. Follow your imams: if he leads the prayer standing, then pray standing, and if he leads the prayer sitting, then you too should pray sitting."""
"1438","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you love the ornaments of Paradise and its silk, then do not wear them in this world."""
"1439","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you find no other place (for prayer) except sheep pens and the resting places of camels, then pray in the sheep pens, but do not pray in the camel enclosures, for they were created from devils (that is, they share their traits)."""
"1440","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you find nothing to give the beggar except a burnt hoof, then place that in his hand."""
"1441","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you stay as guests with a people and they provide for you all that is fitting for a guest, then accept it. But if they do not do so, then take from them the right of the guest that is due from them."""
"1442","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you find vessels other than theirs (that is, the People of the Book), then do not eat from theirs. And if you do not find (any other vessels), then wash them well and then eat from them."""
"1443","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If this boy lives, it may be that he will not reach old age before the Hour (that is, the time of your death) is established."""
"1444","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If he is the one (that is, the Dajjal), you will never be able to overpower him (for killing him is the task of Isa, peace be upon him), and if he is not the one, then there is no good for you in killing him."""
"1445","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If one of you gives his (Muslim) brother his land (for cultivation) free of charge, that is better for him than taking a fixed payment (rent) from him for it."""
"1446","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am the son of the Awatik (that is, the women named Atikah) of the tribe of Banu Sulaym."""
"1447","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am Abu al-Qasim. It is Allah who (truly) gives, while I am merely the one who distributes."""
"1448","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am the one among you who fears Allah the most and who knows the limits set by Allah best."""
"1449","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A vessel for a vessel, and food for food."""
"1450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, I will have the most followers of all the Prophets, and I will be the first to knock at the gate of Paradise."""
"1451","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am the Prophet, there is no lie in this; I am the son of Abd al-Muttalib."""
"1452","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am the closest of all people to Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon them both) in this world and the Hereafter; no other Prophet came between me and him. All the Prophets are paternal half-brothers (that is, the children of one father and different mothers); their mothers (their laws) are different, while their religion (Tawhid) is one and the same."""
"1453","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am closer to the believers according to the Book of Allah. So whoever among you dies leaving a debt or weak and helpless dependants, let them call me, for I am his guardian. And whoever dies leaving wealth, let his wealth be given to his paternal heirs (asabah), whoever they may be."""
"1454","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am closer to the believers than their own selves. So whoever among the believers passes away and leaves a debt owing, its payment is my responsibility; and whoever leaves wealth, it is the right of his heirs."""
"1455","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am closer to every believer than his own self. So whoever leaves a debt or weak dependants, their responsibility is upon me; and whoever leaves wealth, it is the right of his heirs. And I am the heir (guardian) of the one who has no heir: I will inherit his wealth and pay the ransom of his captive. And the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir: he inherits his wealth and pays the blood money (diyah) on his behalf."""
"1456","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am closer to every believer than his own self. So whoever dies leaving a debt, its payment is my responsibility; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs."""
"1457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be the first to intercede in the matter of Paradise, and I am the one with the most followers of all the Prophets."""
"1458","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am the first intercessor for Paradise. No Prophet has been believed as much as I have been believed; and indeed, among the Prophets there was a Prophet whom only a single man of his nation believed (and accepted his faith)."""
"1459","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be the first person to take hold of the ring (knocker) of the gate of Paradise and knock on it."""
"1460","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am free of the one who (in grief at a calamity or bereavement) shaves his head, wails loudly and tears his clothes."""
"1461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am free (disassociated) from every Muslim who resides among the polytheists. The fires of the two of them (that is, the Muslim and the polytheist) should not be visible to each other (that is, they should live at such a distance)."""
"1462","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am at war with whoever you are at war with, and at peace with whoever you are at peace with."""
"1463","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am the supplication of (my forefather) Ibrahim (peace be upon him), and the last of those who gave the glad tidings of my coming was Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon them both)."""
"1464","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I guarantee a house on the outskirts of Paradise for the one who gives up arguing even when he is in the right; a house in the middle of Paradise for the one who gives up lying even in jest; and a house in the highest level of Paradise for the one who makes his character good."""
"1465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the one who believes in me, accepts Islam and emigrates, I guarantee a house on the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise and a house in the highest of the upper chambers of Paradise. And for the one who believes in me, accepts Islam and strives (performs jihad) in the path of Allah, I guarantee a house on the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise and a house in the highest of the upper chambers of Paradise. So whoever does that has left no means of attaining good untried and no way of escaping evil untaken; he may now die wherever (and in whatever state) he wishes."""
"1466","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be the leader of all people on the Day of Resurrection, and do you know why that will be? Allah Almighty will gather the first and the last on a single plain; the voice of the caller will reach them all and the sight will see them all, and the sun will come very close to them. People will be afflicted with such grief and distress as they have no strength to bear. So people will say to one another: 'Do you not see what state you have reached? Will you not look for someone to intercede for you with your Lord?' Then some people will say to others: 'Go to Adam (peace be upon him).' They will come to Adam (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Adam! You are our father, you are the father of mankind. Allah created you with His own Hand, breathed into you of His spirit, and commanded the angels and they prostrated to you. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in? Do you not see what affliction we have reached?' Adam (peace be upon him) will say to them: 'Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been before and never will be after. And He forbade me from (eating of) the tree, but I disobeyed Him. Today I am concerned only for myself: myself, myself, myself. Go to someone other than me; go to Nuh (peace be upon him).' So they will come to Nuh (peace be upon him) and say: '(O Nuh!) You are the first Messenger sent to the people of the earth, and Allah named you ""a most grateful servant"" [Surah al-Isra: 3]. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in? Do you not see what affliction we have reached?' Nuh (peace be upon him) will say to them: 'Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been before and never will be after. I was granted one supplication, which I made against my people. I am concerned only for myself: myself, myself, myself. Go to someone other than me; go to Ibrahim (peace be upon him).' So they will come to Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Ibrahim! You are the Prophet of Allah and His intimate friend (Khalil) from among the people of the earth. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in? Do you not see what affliction we have reached?' Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will say to them: 'Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been before and never will be after. I told three lies (in my life). I am concerned only for myself: myself, myself, myself. Go to someone other than me; go to Musa (peace be upon him).' So they will come to Musa (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Musa! You are the Messenger of Allah; Allah favoured you above people with His messages and His speech. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in? Do you not see what affliction we have reached?' He will say: 'Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been before and never will be after. I killed a person whom I had not been commanded to kill. I am concerned only for myself: myself, myself, myself. Go to someone other than me; go to Isa (peace be upon him).' So they will come to Isa (peace be upon him) and say: 'O Isa! You are the Messenger of Allah and His Word which He conveyed to Maryam (peace be upon her), and a spirit from Him, and you spoke to people in the cradle. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in? Do you not see what affliction we have reached?' Isa (peace be upon him) will say to them: 'Indeed, my Lord is angry today with an anger such as He has never been before and never will be after. I am concerned only for myself: myself, myself, myself. Go to someone other than me; go to Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him).' So they will come to me and say: 'O Muhammad! You are the Messenger of Allah and the Seal of the Prophets, and Allah has forgiven you all your past and future sins. Intercede for us with your Lord. Do you not see the state we are in? Do you not see what affliction we have reached?' Then I will set off and come beneath the Throne and fall down in prostration before my Lord. Then Allah Almighty will open to me words of His praise and the finest glorification of Him that He has not opened to anyone before me. Then it will be said: 'O Muhammad! Raise your head; ask and you will be given, and intercede and your intercession will be accepted.' So I will raise my head and say: 'O my Lord! My Ummah, my Ummah.' Then it will be said: 'O Muhammad! Admit those of your Ummah who have no reckoning against them through the right-hand gate among the gates of Paradise; and they share with the rest of the people in the other gates besides that.' By the One in whose Hand is my soul! The distance between two of the door-leaves of the gates of Paradise is like the distance between Makkah and Hajar, or like that between Makkah and Busra."""
"1467","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be the leader of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, and the first person whose grave will be split open (that is, I will be the first to rise from the grave), and I am the first to intercede and the first whose intercession will be accepted."""
"1468","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be the leader of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, and I say this without pride; in my hand will be the Banner of Praise, and I say this without pride; and on that day Adam (peace be upon him) and all the Prophets besides him will be beneath my banner; and I will be the first to intercede and the first whose intercession will be accepted, and I say this without pride."""
"1469","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will reach the Pond (al-Kawthar) before you and be your forerunner there."""
"1470","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be your forerunner at the Pond (al-Kawthar). I will wait for you until some men from among you are brought before me; then, when I recognise them, they will be pulled away from me. So I will say: 'O my Lord! These are my companions! O my Lord! These are my companions!' Then it will be said: 'You do not know what new things they invented (in the religion) after you.'"""
"1471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be your forerunner at the Pond (al-Kawthar), and I will contend (to save) some people, then I will be overpowered regarding them (that is, they will be taken away from me). So I will say: 'O my Lord! These are my companions! These are my companions!' Then He (Allah) will say: 'You do not know what new things they fabricated after you.'"""
"1472","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abd al-Muttalib. Indeed, Allah Almighty created the creation and placed me in the best group of them; then He divided them into two parts and placed me in the best part of them; then He divided them into tribes and made me be born in the best tribe of them; then He divided them into households and made me be born in the best household of them. So I am the best of you in household and the best of you in person."""
"1473","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Muqaffi (the one who comes after all the others), and I am al-Hashir (the one who gathers the people), and I am the Prophet of repentance, and I am the Prophet of mercy."""
"1474","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am the heir of the one who has no heir: I pay the ransom of his captive on his behalf and I inherit his wealth. And the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir: he pays the ransom of his captive on his behalf and inherits his wealth."""
"1475","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I and the one who looks after an orphan will be in Paradise like this (together)."""
"1476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I and the one who looks after an orphan, whether his own or someone else's, will be in Paradise (together like this); and the one who strives to meet the needs of the widow and the poor person is like the one who strives (performs jihad) in the path of Allah."""
"1477","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soak it (the nabidh) in the morning and drink it at night, and soak it at night and drink it in the morning; and soak it in waterskins and do not soak it in earthenware jars, for when time passes over it, it turns into vinegar."""
"1478","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have more right than I do to the front part of your mount (that is, to sit at the front), unless you give that place to me."""
"1479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are our brother and our mawla (freed slave and friend)."" (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to Sayyiduna Zayd bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him).)"
"1480","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are their imam, so lead them in prayer taking into account the weakest among them, and appoint a muezzin who does not take any payment for his call to prayer (adhan)."""
"1481","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are (merely) one who comforts and treats gently, and the true Physician (the Giver of cure) is Allah alone."""
"1482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are one freed by Allah from the Fire of Hell."" (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him).)"
"1483","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will be (on the Day of Resurrection) with the one you loved."""
"1484","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are to me in the position that Harun (peace be upon him) held in relation to Musa (peace be upon him), except that there is no Prophet after me."""
"1485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are from me and I am from you."" (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him).)"
"1486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You and your wealth belong to your father."""
"1487","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You and your wealth belong to your father. Indeed, your children are among the purest of your earnings, so eat from the earnings of your children."""
"1488","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You know best the affairs of your worldly life."""
"1489","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, you will have radiant faces and shining limbs because of performing ablution (wudu) completely and thoroughly."""
"1490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are Allah's witnesses on the earth, and the angels are Allah's witnesses in the heaven."""
"1491","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has taken responsibility for the one who goes out in His path, whom nothing brings out of his home except faith in Me and belief in My messengers, that He will bring him back with reward or spoils of war, or else admit him into Paradise. And were it not that I fear hardship for my Ummah, I would not stay behind any army unit. And I truly wish that I could be killed in the path of Allah, then be brought back to life, then be killed, then be brought back to life, then be killed and then be brought back to life."""
"1492","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the time of Musa (peace be upon him), two men declared their lineage. One of them said: 'I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so,' until he had counted nine (of his disbelieving forefathers). Then he said: 'Who are you? May you have no mother!' The other replied: 'I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, and I am a son of Islam.' So Allah Almighty revealed to Musa (peace be upon him): Say to these two who boast of their lineage: 'O you who traced your lineage to nine forefathers who are in the Fire! You are the tenth of them in the Fire. And O you who traced your lineage to two who are in Paradise! You are the third of them in Paradise.'"""
"1493","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wear sandals, and wear leather socks (khuffs), and act contrary to the People of the Book."""
"1494","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Abd al-Muttalib! Draw the water (of Zamzam). Were it not that I fear people would overpower you in this service of giving water to drink (and, taking it to be a Sunnah, take this right away from you), I would have drawn water along with you."""
"1495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an was revealed in seven ahruf (modes of recitation)."""
"1496","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Qur'an was revealed from seven gates in seven ahruf (modes of recitation), and all of them are healing and sufficient."""
"1497","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Scriptures of Ibrahim (peace be upon him) were revealed on the first night of Ramadan; the Torah was revealed when six days of Ramadan had passed; the Injil was revealed when thirteen days of Ramadan had passed; the Zabur was revealed when eighteen days of Ramadan had passed; and the Qur'an was revealed when twenty-four days of Ramadan had passed."""
"1498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A surah has just been revealed to me a short while ago: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar. So pray to your Lord and sacrifice. Indeed, it is your enemy who is cut off.' [Surah al-Kawthar: 1-3] Do you know what al-Kawthar is? It is a river which my Lord has promised me; upon it is abundant good. It is my Pond, to which my Ummah will come to drink on the Day of Resurrection; its vessels are as numerous as the stars. Then a servant from among them will be pulled away, and I will say: 'O my Lord! He is indeed from my Ummah.' Then He will say: 'You do not know what new things he invented (in the religion) after you.'"""
"1499","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Verses have been revealed to me the like of which have never been seen: they are ""Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak"" [Surah al-Falaq: 1] and ""Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind"" [Surah an-Nas: 1]."""
"1500","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Get down from it (the camel), and do not remain in our caravan with something accursed. Do not invoke curses upon yourselves, nor invoke curses upon your children, nor invoke curses upon your wealth, lest your curse coincide with that hour of acceptance from Allah in which whatever is asked for is granted, and so that curse of yours is answered."""
"1501","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. If he is an oppressor, stop him from committing oppression, and if he is oppressed, help him (in getting his right)."""
"1502","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or oppressed."" It was asked: ""How should I help him when he is an oppressor?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stop him from committing oppression; that (in reality) is helping him."""
"1503","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abu Mas'ud! Go (and do your work). Let me never find you on the Day of Resurrection coming with a groaning camel from the camels of charity (sadaqah) upon your back, one that you stole through misappropriation."""
"1504","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Three men from among those who were before you set out on a journey, until they took shelter in a cave to spend the night and entered it. Suddenly a rock fell from the mountain and blocked the mouth of the cave upon them. They said to one another: 'Nothing can save you from this rock except that you call upon Allah by means of your righteous deeds.' One of them said: 'O Allah! I had elderly parents, and I would not give the evening milk to my family or my slaves before them. One day I went far away in search of something, and when I returned they had already fallen asleep. I milked their evening milk for them but found them asleep. I disliked giving milk to my family or my property (slaves) before them, so I kept waiting for them to wake up with the cup of milk in my hand until dawn broke. Then they woke up and drank their milk. O Allah! If I did this solely to seek Your pleasure, then remove from us the distress of this rock.' The rock shifted a little, but they could not get out. The second said: 'O Allah! I had a cousin (my paternal uncle's daughter) who was the most beloved of all people to me. I desired her for evil, but she refused me, until a year of famine befell her and she came to me. I gave her one hundred and twenty dinars on condition that she would be alone with me. She did so, until, when I had gained power over her, she said: ""I do not make it lawful for you to break the seal except by its right (marriage)."" Hearing this, I refrained from going to her and moved away from her, even though she was the most beloved of people to me, and I also left the gold that I had given her. O Allah! If I did this solely for Your pleasure, then remove this distress of ours.' The rock shifted further, but they still could not get out of it. The third said: 'O Allah! I hired some labourers and gave them their wages, except for one man who left what was due to him and went away. I invested his wages in trade and increased them, until much wealth accumulated from them. After some time he came to me and said: ""O servant of Allah! Give me my wages."" I said to him: ""These camels, cows, goats and slaves that you see are all your wages."" He said: ""O servant of Allah! Do not mock me."" I said: ""I am not mocking you."" Then he took all of it and drove it away, leaving nothing of it. O Allah! If I did this solely for Your pleasure, then relieve us of this difficulty of ours.' The rock moved away completely, and they all came out walking."""
"1505","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Look! You are by no means better than anyone red or black, unless you surpass him through piety (taqwa)."""
"1506","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(O women!) Look carefully at who your (foster) brothers are, for (valid) suckling is only that which satisfies hunger (that is, which takes place during the period of suckling in infancy)."""
"1507","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Look at those who are below you and do not look at those who are above you (the wealthy), for it is more fitting that you do not belittle the blessings of Allah upon you."""
"1508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Look to Quraysh: take from their words, and leave their (bad) deeds."""
"1509","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(O woman!) Keep watching where you stand with regard to him (your husband) and his rights, for he is your Paradise and your Hell."""
"1510","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I advise you to use cotton, for it will absorb and remove the (istihadah) blood."""
"1511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Proceed calmly until you descend into their open ground, then invite them to Islam and inform them of what is obligatory upon them of the right of Allah. By Allah! If Allah Almighty guides even one man through you, it is better for you than red camels."""
"1512","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Bilal! Spend, and do not fear that the Lord of the Throne (Allah) will cause you want."""
"1513","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep spending (in the way of Allah) and do not count out what you keep, or else Allah too will count out what He gives you; and do not hoard wealth (in sacks or vessels), or else Allah too will withhold (His blessings) from you."""
"1514","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Marry, for I will take pride in your great numbers (over the other nations on the Day of Resurrection)."""
"1515","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, even your footprints are recorded."""
"1516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Adam (peace be upon him) was created from three kinds of soil: black, white and red."""
"1517","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the family of such-and-such a tribe are not my friends (or patrons); my friend and supporter is only Allah and the righteous believers."""
"1518","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The family of Ja'far have become occupied with grief for their deceased, so prepare food for them."""
"1519","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The greatest miser among people is the one who is miserly with the greeting of salam, and the most helpless of people is the one who is too helpless to make supplication (du'a)."""
"1520","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Ibrahim is my son, and he has died at the age of suckling. Now in Paradise he has two wet-nurses who will complete his period of suckling."""
"1521","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Ibrahim (peace be upon him) made the House of Allah sacred and a place of security, and I have declared Madinah sacred between its two lava plains: its thorny trees are not to be cut and its game is not to be hunted."""
"1522","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah a sanctuary, and I have declared it (Madinah) a sanctuary between its two lava plains."""
"1523","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Ibrahim (peace be upon him) made Makkah sacred and supplicated for it, and I have made Madinah sacred just as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred, and I have supplicated for (blessing in) its mudd and sa' (measures) just as Ibrahim supplicated for Makkah."""
"1524","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was thrown into the fire, there was no creature on the face of the earth that was not extinguishing the fire, except the gecko, for it was blowing on the fire."""
"1525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the greatest act of righteousness is that a man treats his father's friends kindly after the father has gone (passed away)."""
"1526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Iblis places his throne upon the water and then sends out his troops. The closest of them to him in rank is the one who causes the greatest mischief. One of them comes and says: 'I did such-and-such,' and Iblis says: 'You have done nothing.' Then another of them comes and says: 'I did not leave him until I had caused separation between him and his wife.' Then Iblis brings him close to himself and says: 'Yes, you (have done a great job)!'"""
"1527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the son of Adam feels heat, he says: 'Ouch!' and when he feels cold, he says: 'Ouch!'"""
"1528","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this son of mine (Hasan) is a sayyid (leader), and it is hoped that Allah Almighty will bring about reconciliation through him between two great groups of the Muslims."""
"1529","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these two sons of mine (Hasan and Husayn) are my two flowers in this world."""
"1530","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the gates of Paradise are beneath the shade of swords."""
"1531","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the sin of usury (riba) has seventy-two (72) doors; the least of them in degree is like a person committing adultery with his own mother in Islam."""
"1532","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the gates of heaven are opened as soon as the sun passes its zenith, and they are not closed until the Zuhr prayer has been prayed, so I love that a good deed of mine should ascend through them (while they are open)."""
"1533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one among you who fears Allah the most and knows Allah better than all of you is I."""
"1534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the most beloved of your names to Allah Almighty are Abdullah and Abdur-Rahman."""
"1535","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the most beloved of you to me and the closest to my gathering in the Hereafter will be those of you who are best in character; and the most hateful of you to me and the farthest from me in the Hereafter will be those of you who are worst in character: those who talk excessively, those who speak with arrogance and wide-open mouths, and the chatterers."""
"1536","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it."""
"1537","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when any one of you stands in his prayer, he is conversing intimately with his Lord, and his Lord is between him and the qiblah, so let none of you ever spit towards his qiblah; rather, let him spit to his left or beneath his foot."""
"1538","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when any one of you stands to pray, he converses intimately with his Lord, so let him consider how he is conversing with Him."""
"1539","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when any one of you stands to pray, Satan comes and confuses him with whisperings until he does not know how many rak'ahs he has prayed. So when any of you experiences that, let him perform two prostrations (of forgetfulness) while sitting."""
"1540","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when any one of you is in prayer, Allah Almighty is in front of his face, so let none of you ever spit (or clear his throat) in front of his face (that is, towards the qiblah) during prayer."""
"1541","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when any one of you is in his prayer, he is conversing intimately with his Lord, so let him never spit in front of him nor to his right, but rather to his left and beneath his foot."""
"1542","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you and says: 'Who created you?' He answers: 'Allah.' Then he (Satan) says: 'Then who created Allah?' So when any one of you experiences this (whispering), let him say: 'Amantu billahi wa rasulihi' (I believe in Allah and His Messenger), for saying this will drive it (the whispering) away from him."""
"1543","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the creation of each one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty days in the form of a drop of fluid (nutfah); then for the same number of days it remains a clot of blood ('alaqah); then for the same number of days it remains a lump of flesh (mudghah). Then Allah Almighty sends to it an angel who is commanded with four things, and it is said to him: 'Write down his deeds, his provision, his appointed time of death (lifespan), and whether he will be wretched or blessed.' Then the soul is breathed into it. So indeed, a man among you keeps doing the deeds of the people of Paradise until there remains between him and Paradise only the distance of an arm's length, then what has been written overtakes him, and he begins doing the deeds of the people of Hell and enters Hell. And indeed, a man keeps doing the deeds of the people of Hell until there remains between him and Hell only the distance of an arm's length, then what has been written overtakes him, and he begins doing the deeds of the people of Paradise and enters Paradise."""
"1544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the noble lineage of the people of this world is this wealth towards which they rush (that is, the people of the world regard wealth alone as the standard of honour and nobility)."""
"1545","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a man returns from a journey, the best time for him to come to his family is the early part of the night."""
"1546","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best of the things with which you change this whiteness of old age (white hair) are henna and katam (a kind of plant whose dye is a blackish red)."""
"1547","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the condition most deserving of being fulfilled by you is that through which you made private parts lawful for yourselves (that is, the conditions of marriage)."""
"1548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the thing most deserving of your taking a wage for it is the Book of Allah (that is, taking a wage for teaching the Qur'an or for performing ruqyah with it)."""
"1549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your brother al-Najashi has passed away, so stand and offer the funeral prayer for him."""
"1550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your brother is held back (from entering Paradise) because of his debt, so pay it off on his behalf."""
"1551","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, what I fear most for my Ummah is misguiding leaders."""
"1552","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, what I fear most for my Ummah is the deed of the people of Lut (homosexuality)."""
"1553","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, what I fear most for my Ummah in its last age is the stars (belief in their influence), denial of divine decree (qadar), and the injustice of the ruler."""
"1554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, what I fear most for my Ummah is every hypocrite who is highly skilled with his tongue (smooth-tongued)."""
"1555","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, what I fear most for you is the lesser shirk, that is, showing off (riya'). On the Day of Resurrection, when people are recompensed for their deeds, Allah Almighty will say: 'Go to those for whom you used to show off in the world, then see whether you find any reward with them.'"""
"1556","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, what I fear most for you after me is every hypocrite who is very smooth-tongued."""
"1557","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one of lowest rank among the people of Paradise will be a man whose face Allah Almighty turns away from the Fire towards Paradise. A shady tree will be made to appear before him, and he will say: 'O my Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may be in its shade.' Allah Almighty will say: 'Is it not likely that, if I give you this, you will ask Me for something else?' He will say: 'No, by Your Might!' So Allah Almighty will bring him near it. Then another tree, shady and bearing fruit, will be made to appear before him, and he will say: 'O my Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may be in its shade and eat of its fruit.' Allah Almighty will say: 'Is it not likely that, if I grant you this, you will ask Me for something else?' He will say: 'No, by Your Might!' So Allah Almighty will bring him near it. Then Allah Almighty will make another tree appear before him, shady, bearing fruit and with water (a spring), and he will say: 'O my Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may be in its shade, eat of its fruit and drink of its water.' Allah Almighty will say to him: 'Is it not likely that, if I do this, you will ask Me for something else?' He will say: 'No, by Your Might! I will not ask You for anything else.' So Allah Almighty will bring him near it. Then the gate of Paradise will be opened to him, and he will say: 'O my Lord, bring me near the gate of Paradise so that I may be under the curtain of Paradise and see its people.' So Allah Almighty will bring him near it, and he will see Paradise and its blessings. He will say: 'O my Lord, admit me into Paradise.' So he will be admitted into Paradise, and when he enters Paradise he will say: 'Is all this for me?' Allah Almighty will say to him: 'Make your wishes (ask for whatever you want).' So he will wish, and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will remind him: 'Ask for such-and-such as well,' until, when all his wishes are exhausted, Allah Almighty will say: 'All this is yours, and ten times as much besides.' Then Allah Almighty will admit him into his palace in Paradise, and his two wives from the wide-eyed houris will come to him and say: 'All praise is for Allah, who brought you to life for us and brought us to life for you.' He will say: 'No one has been given anything like what I have been given today.' And the one who receives the lightest punishment among the people of Hell will be a man who is made to wear two sandals of fire, from the heat of which his brain will boil."""
"1558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the souls of the martyrs are inside the bellies of green birds. They have lanterns hanging beneath the Throne; they roam freely in Paradise wherever they wish, then return to rest in those lanterns. Their Lord casts a glance upon them and says: 'Do you desire anything?' They say: 'What could we desire when we roam (freely) in Paradise wherever we wish?' Allah Almighty repeats this question to them three times. When they see that they will not be left (without asking) (but will certainly be asked), they say: 'O our Lord, we wish that You return our souls to our bodies so that we may go back to the world and be killed in Your path once more!' When Allah Almighty sees that they have no other need (except that they wish to go back to the world, which is impossible), they are left alone."""
"1559","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the souls of the martyrs are in green birds that hang from the fruits of Paradise (that is, they take their provision from them)."""
"1560","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the souls of the believers are in green birds that hang from the trees of Paradise."""
"1561","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the wives of the people of Paradise will sing to their husbands in the most beautiful and enchanting voices that no one has ever heard. Among what they will sing is: 'We are the good and beautiful ones, wives of an honourable people, gazing with eyes full of delight.' And among the words of their songs will also be: 'We are the everlasting, so we shall never die; we are the secure, so we shall never fear; we are the ever-abiding, so we shall never depart from here.'"""
"1562","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people who face the severest trials are the Prophets, then those who are nearest to them in rank, then those who come after them."""
"1563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are the makers of images (or statues)."""
"1564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the most modest of this Ummah after its Prophet is Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"1565","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the makers of these images (or statues) will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: 'Now bring to life what you have created.'"""
"1566","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the purest thing you eat is from your own earnings, and indeed your children are also part of your earnings."""
"1567","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the gravest sins in the sight of Allah is that a man marries a woman, then when he has fulfilled his desire with her, he divorces her and usurps her dowry (mahr); and another is a man who employs a labourer and withholds his wages; and a third is the one who kills an animal without right (merely for sport)."""
"1568","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The greatest wrongdoer among the Muslims against the Muslims is the one who asks about something that had not been made unlawful for the Muslims, and then, because of his probing and questioning, it is made unlawful for them."""
"1569","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the greatest slanderer among people in the sight of Allah is a man who satirises (disparages) another man and then disparages his entire tribe, and a man who disowns his own father and accuses his own mother of fornication."""
"1570","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the deeds of the servants are presented (before Allah Almighty) on Monday and Thursday."""
"1571","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best servants of Allah on the Day of Resurrection will be those who praise Allah abundantly (that is, al-hammadun)."""
"1572","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best of the things with which you treat yourselves are cupping (hijamah) and sea costus (al-qust al-bahri, a marine herb), so do not torment your children by pressing their throats (as a treatment)."""
"1573","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those of you who will be closest to me in station on the Day of Resurrection are those of you with the best character in the world."""
"1574","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the inhabitants of Paradise, women will be the fewest in number."""
"1575","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there are some people in Madinah who have stayed behind us, yet we do not pass through any mountain pass or valley except that they are with us (in reward); only a (legitimate) excuse has held them back there."""
"1576","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some people will be brought out of the Fire, having been burned in it except for the round areas of their faces, until they enter Paradise."""
"1577","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those who eat their fill the most in this world will be the ones who remain hungry the longest on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1578","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the most complete of the believers in faith is the one with the best character, and indeed good character brings a person to the rank of fasting and prayer."""
"1579","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, camels were created from devils, and behind every camel there is a devil."""
"1580","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Islam began as something strange and it will soon return to being strange just as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers (that is, those who remain steadfast upon it)."""
"1581","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Islam began as something strange and it will soon return to being strange just as it began, and it will retreat between the two mosques (of Makkah and Madinah) just as a snake retreats into its hole."""
"1582","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when the people of the Ash'ari tribe run short of provisions during a military expedition, or the food of their families in Madinah runs low, they gather whatever they have in a single cloth, then divide it equally among themselves from a single vessel. So they are from me and I am from them."""
"1583","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, deeds are raised (before Allah Almighty) on Monday and Thursday, so I love that my deeds be raised while I am fasting."""
"1584","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, trustworthiness (amanah) (at first) descended into the depths of people's hearts. Then the Qur'an was revealed, and they learned (trustworthiness) from the Qur'an and learned it from the Sunnah. (Then the time will come for trustworthiness to be taken away, when) a man will sleep a single sleep and trustworthiness will be taken from his heart, and its trace will remain only like a faint spot. He will sleep again and the (remaining) trustworthiness will be taken from his heart, and its trace will remain like a blister, as when you roll an ember over your foot and it blisters; you see it swollen, though there is nothing inside it. Then people will get up in the morning and trade with one another, but hardly anyone will fulfil the trust, until it will be said: 'In such-and-such a tribe there is a trustworthy man.' And it will even be said of a man (judging by appearances): 'How brave he is! How pleasant he is! How intelligent he is!' yet there will not be in his heart faith equal to a mustard seed."""
"1585","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a ruler seeks out suspicion (and faults) among people, he corrupts them."""
"1586","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Prophets will vie in pride over which of them has the most followers from his Ummah, and I hope that on that Day those of my Ummah who come to the Pond will be more than all of theirs. And indeed on that Day each one of them (the Prophets) will stand at his full Pond with a staff in his hand, calling those of his Ummah whom he recognises, and every Ummah will have a distinctive mark by which its Prophet will recognise them."""
"1587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Ansar have fulfilled the responsibility that was upon them, and what remains is the responsibility that is upon you (that is, to fulfil their rights). So accept the good from those of them who do good, and overlook the faults of those of them who err."""
"1588","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, vessels do not make anything unlawful, so prepare nabidh (a drink made by steeping dates or raisins in water) in whatever vessel you wish, but avoid everything that intoxicates."""
"1589","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, faith will retreat to Madinah just as a snake retreats to its hole."""
"1590","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, faith wears out (and becomes worn) within one of you just as a garment wears out, so ask Allah Almighty to renew the faith in your hearts."""
"1591","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, blessing descends in the middle of the food, so eat from its edges and do not eat from its middle."""
"1592","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, trials come to the one who loves me faster than floodwater flows to its final destination (or low ground)."""
"1593","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels (of mercy) do not enter a house in which there are images (or statues)."""
"1594","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the merchants (who adopt unlawful practices and deceive) are the wicked ones (fujjar)."""
"1595","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, (in sacrifice) a jadha'ah (a young animal of six months to a year) suffices for what a thaniyyah (an animal that has shed its two front teeth) suffices for."""
"1596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a jadha' of sheep (a young one of six months to a year) suffices for what a thani of goats (an animal that has shed its two front teeth) suffices for."""
"1597","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection the hornless goat will certainly be given retribution from the horned goat."""
"1598","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Paradise yearns for three people: Ali, Ammar and Salman (may Allah be pleased with them)."""
"1599","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Hajj and Umrah are in the path of Allah (part of jihad), and indeed, an Umrah performed in Ramadan carries a reward equal to a Hajj."""
"1600","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Hasan and Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) are my two flowers from this world."""
"1601","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, by saying 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is for Allah), 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah) and 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest), the sins of a servant fall away just as the leaves of this tree are falling."""
"1602","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the wide-eyed and beautiful Hur will sing in Paradise, saying: 'Nahnu al-huru al-hisan, khubbi'na li-azwajin kiram' We are the beautiful Hur, kept hidden (and preserved) for noble husbands."""
"1603","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, modesty and faith are joined together, so when one of them is taken away, the other is taken away as well."""
"1604","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, wine is made from (grape) juice, raisins, dates, wheat, barley and corn, and I forbid you from every intoxicant."""
"1605","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one who guides to good is like the one who does it (in earning reward)."""
"1606","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Dajjal will be blind in his left eye, over which there will be a thick growth (a lump of flesh), and between his eyes will be written 'Kafir' (disbeliever)."""
"1607","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Dajjal will emerge from the direction of the east, from a land called Khurasan. He will be followed by people whose faces are like layered shields (broad and flat)."""
"1608","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this world is sweet and green. So whoever takes something from it in a lawful way, blessing is placed for him in it. And how many people there are who wrongfully plunge into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger (misappropriating it); for them on the Day of Resurrection there will be nothing but the Fire."""
"1609","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this world is accursed, and whatever is in it is accursed (far from the mercy of Allah), except the remembrance of Allah, and whatever brings one close to obedience to Allah, and a scholar or a student of religious knowledge."""
"1610","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the religion is sincere goodwill in its entirety: to Allah, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the rulers of the Muslims and to their common people."""
"1611","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the religion is easy, and whoever is harsh with the religion, the religion will overpower him. So adopt moderation, stay as close as possible to what is right (if you cannot attain perfection), be of good cheer, and seek help through worship in the morning, after midday and in part of the night."""
"1612","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a dream comes to pass according to the interpretation given to it, and its example is that of a man who has raised his foot and is waiting for when to put it down. So when one of you sees a (good) dream, he should not relate it to anyone except a well-wisher or a scholar."""
"1613","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man has the greater right to the front of his mount and the head of his bed, and he also has the greater right to lead the prayer himself in his own dwelling (home)."""
"1614","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a person begins his prayer, Allah Almighty turns towards him in a manner befitting His majesty, and He does not turn His attention away from him until he finishes the prayer or does something bad (that breaks his ablution)."""
"1615","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a man keeps praying with the imam until he (the imam) finishes, the reward of a whole night of worship (standing in prayer) is written for him."""
"1616","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a person dies somewhere other than his place of birth, the distance from his place of birth to his place of death is measured for him in Paradise, and that much space (in Paradise) is given to him."""
"1617","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man's rank is raised in Paradise and he asks: 'How did I get this station?' He is answered: 'Because of your children's supplicating for forgiveness on your behalf.'"""
"1618","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person utters a word in which he sees no harm, yet because of that one word he falls into the fire of Hell to a depth of seventy years' distance."""
"1619","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person speaks a word pleasing to Allah Almighty which he does not even imagine will reach as far as it does, and because of that one word Allah Almighty writes His good pleasure for him until the Day of Resurrection. And indeed, a person speaks a word displeasing to Allah Almighty which he cannot even imagine will reach as far as it does, and because of that word Allah Almighty writes His displeasure against him until the Day of Resurrection."""
"1620","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, by his excellent character a person attains the ranks of one who prays tahajjud at night and fasts during the day."""
"1621","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, through his good character a man attains the rank of one who stands in prayer at night and stays thirsty (fasting) in the intense heat of midday."""
"1622","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man asks me for something and I hold it back from him so that you may intercede and be rewarded for it."""
"1623","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man does the deeds of the people of Paradise for a long time, then his end comes upon a deed of the people of Hell; and a man does the deeds of the people of Hell for a long time, then his end comes upon a deed of the people of Paradise."""
"1624","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person outwardly does the deeds of the people of Paradise in the eyes of people while he is one of the people of Hell, and a person outwardly does the deeds of the people of Hell in the eyes of people while he is one of the people of Paradise."""
"1625","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person has a special station (appointed) with Allah which he cannot reach through any deed of his, so Allah Almighty keeps testing him with things he dislikes until Allah brings him to that station."""
"1626","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person returns (after praying) and nothing is written for him (as reward) except a tenth of his prayer, a ninth, an eighth, a seventh, a sixth, a fifth, a quarter, a third or a half."""
"1627","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man from the people of Paradise will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, desire and intercourse, and their need (to relieve themselves) will only be in the form of sweat that comes out of their skin, by which their stomachs become light (and slim)."""
"1628","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man from the people of Hell will be made so large for the Fire that one of his molars will be like Mount Uhud."""
"1629","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the womb (kinship) is a branch that has taken hold of the waist-wrapper of the Most Merciful. It joins whoever joins it (kinship) and it cuts off whoever cuts it off."""
"1630","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a servant's provision seeks him out more intensely than his death seeks him."""
"1631","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, messengership and prophethood have come to an end, so after me there is no messenger and no prophet. However, glad tidings remain, and that is the (true) dream of a Muslim man, which is one of the parts of prophethood."""
"1632","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, (polytheistic) incantations, amulets and love charms (spells to create love between husband and wife) are shirk."""
"1633","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Black Stone and the Station of Ibrahim are two rubies from the rubies of Paradise. Allah Almighty has dimmed their light; had He not dimmed their light, they would have illuminated everything between the east and the west."""
"1634","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when the soul is taken, the sight follows it (which is why the eyes of the dead remain open)."""
"1635","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Hour will not be established until ten signs appear: the smoke, the Dajjal, the beast of the earth, the rising of the sun from its place of setting, three sinkings of the earth: one in the east, one in the west and one in the Arabian Peninsula, the descent of Isa (peace be upon him), the emergence of Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and a fire that will come out of the depths of Aden and drive people to the place of gathering; where people spend the night, this fire will spend the night with them, and where people take their midday rest, it will rest with them."""
"1636","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, eating suhur is a blessing that Allah Almighty has granted you, so do not abandon it."""
"1637","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the fortunate one is he who is kept safe from trials, and he who is put to a test and remains patient."""
"1638","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, As-Salam is one of the names of Allah Almighty, so spread it (abundantly) among yourselves."""
"1639","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, As-Salam is one of the names of Allah Almighty which has been placed on earth, so spread the greeting of salam among yourselves."""
"1640","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, lending (to someone) holds the rank of (the reward of) half a charity."""
"1641","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one who is present sees what the absent one cannot see."""
"1642","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of Allah; they are not eclipsed for the death or the life of anyone. So when you see this (eclipse), supplicate to Allah, say the takbir, pray and give charity. O Ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! By Allah, there is no one more jealous (of His honour) than Allah when His male servant commits adultery or His female servant commits adultery. O Ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much. O Allah, have I conveyed the message?"""
"1643","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the sun and the moon will be two hamstrung bulls in the Fire."""
"1644","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death or the life of anyone; rather, they are two of the signs of Allah by which Allah Almighty frightens His servants. So when you see it, pray and supplicate until the state you are in is lifted."""
"1645","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the month can also be twenty-nine days."""
"1646","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, an old man has control over himself (his desires)."""
"1647","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Satan hears the call to prayer (adhan), he turns his back and flees passing wind so that he may not hear its sound. Then when the adhan ends, he comes back and whispers. Then when he hears the iqamah, he flees so that he may not hear its sound, and when the iqamah ends, he comes back again and whispers."""
"1648","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Satan hears the call to prayer (adhan), he flees so far that he reaches the place of al-Rawha."""
"1649","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan appeared before me and pressed hard against me in order to break my prayer, but Allah Almighty gave me power over him, so I choked him. And I had intended to tie him to one of the pillars of the mosque so that you could see him in the morning, but I remembered this saying of Sulayman (peace be upon him): 'My Lord! Grant me a kingdom such as will not befit anyone after me.' [Surah Sad: 35] So Allah sent him back humiliated and disgraced."""
"1650","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan said: 'O my Lord! By Your Might, I will keep on leading Your servants astray as long as their souls remain in their bodies.' So the Lord, the Exalted, said: 'By My Might and My Majesty! I will keep on forgiving them as long as they keep seeking My forgiveness.'"""
"1651","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray (in the Arabian Peninsula), but (he has hope) in stirring up quarrels, strife and discord among them."""
"1652","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan sits in wait for the son of Adam on his paths to lead him astray. He sat in wait for him on the path of Islam and said: 'Will you accept Islam and abandon your religion and the religion of your forefathers?' But the man disobeyed him and became a Muslim. Then he sat in wait for him on the path of emigration (hijrah) and said: 'Will you emigrate and leave your land and your sky (your homeland)? The example of the emigrant is like that of a horse tied to a tether.' But he disobeyed him and emigrated. Then he sat in wait for him on the path of jihad and said: 'Will you fight in jihad, when it is a toil of both life and wealth? You will fight and be killed, then someone else will marry your wife and your wealth will be divided up?' But he disobeyed him and fought in jihad. So whoever does that, it is a right upon Allah that He admit him into Paradise; whoever is killed (in jihad), it is a right upon Allah that He admit him into Paradise; if he drowns, it is a right upon Allah that He admit him into Paradise; and if his mount throws him and kills him, then too it is a right upon Allah that He admit him into Paradise."""
"1653","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan considers lawful for himself the food over which the name of Allah (Bismillah) has not been mentioned. When he brought this Bedouin in order to make the food lawful for himself through him, I took hold of his (the Bedouin's) hand; then he brought this girl in order to make it lawful through her, so I took hold of her hand as well. By the One in whose Hand is my soul! Satan's hand was indeed in my hand along with both of their hands."""
"1654","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Umar! Indeed, Satan fears you."""
"1655","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you during his prayer and confuses him until he does not know how many units (rak'ahs) he has prayed. So when any of you experiences this, let him perform two prostrations (the prostrations of forgetfulness) while sitting, before saying the salam, and then let him say the salam."""
"1656","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you and says: 'Who created the sky?' He replies: 'Allah.' Then he says: 'Who created the earth?' He replies: 'Allah.' Then he says: 'Who created Allah?!' So when any of you experiences such a whisper, let him say: 'I believe in Allah and His Messenger.'"""
"1657","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan comes to one of you and asks: 'Who created you?' He says: 'Allah.' Then he says: 'Then who created Allah?' So when any of you feels this, let him say: 'I believe in Allah and His Messengers.' Indeed, saying this will drive that whisper away from him."""
"1658","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan circulates within the human being (the son of Adam) just as blood circulates."""
"1659","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Satan is present with you at every one of your affairs, so much so that he is present even when you eat. So when a morsel falls from any of you, let him remove whatever dirt (dust and the like) is on it and then eat it, and not leave it for Satan. And when he finishes eating, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies."""
"1660","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, trials are made severe for the righteous. And no calamity befalls a believer, whether the prick of a thorn or anything greater than that, except that because of it one of his sins is forgiven and he is raised one degree in rank."""
"1661","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""True patience is only that which is shown at the first blow of a calamity (the initial shock)."""
"1662","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, if a huge rock were thrown from the edge of Hell, it would keep falling into it for seventy years and still would not reach its bottom."""
"1663","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, charity (zakah) is not lawful for us, and indeed the freed slave of a people is counted as one of them."""
"1664","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is not permissible for the family of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) to accept charity, for it is nothing but the dirt of people."""
"1665","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise; and a man keeps on speaking the truth until he is recorded with Allah as a great truthful one (siddiq). And indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire of Hell; and a man keeps on lying until he is recorded with Allah as a great liar (kadhdhab)."""
"1666","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, clean earth is a means of purification as long as you do not find water, even if (you do not find water) for ten years. Then when you find water, apply it to your skin (that is, perform ghusl or wudu)."""
"1667","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, clean earth is the ablution (and purification) of the Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years. So when he finds water, let him pour it over his body (skin), for that is better for him."""
"1668","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the five prayers remove sins just as water washes away dirt."""
"1669","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, oppression will be a cause of many darknesses on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1670","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a servant commits a sin, a black spot is placed upon his heart. If he refrains from that sin, seeks forgiveness and repents, his heart is cleaned and polished. But if he returns to sin, that blackness is increased until it covers his whole heart. And this is the rust that Allah Almighty has mentioned (in this verse): 'No! Rather, the rust of what they used to earn has covered their hearts.' [Surah al-Mutaffifin: 14]"""
"1671","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a servant stands to pray, all his sins are brought and placed on his head and his two shoulders. Then every time he bows or prostrates, those sins fall away from him."""
"1672","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a servant curses something, that curse goes up toward the sky, but the gates of the sky are shut against it. Then it descends to the earth, and the gates of the earth are also shut against it. Then it seeks a way to the right and to the left, and when it finds no way, it returns to the person (or thing) that was cursed. If that one deserves it, (it falls upon it); otherwise it returns to the one who uttered it."""
"1673","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a servant falls ill, Allah Almighty reveals to His angels: 'I have bound My servant with one of My fetters. So if I take his life (in this state), I will forgive him; and if I restore him to health, he will rise up with no sin upon him.'"""
"1674","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a slave is sincere toward his master and also worships his Lord well, he will have a double reward."""
"1675","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a servant is placed in his grave and his companions turn away and leave him, so much so that he hears the sound of their footsteps, two angels come to him, sit him up and ask him: 'What did you used to say about this man (that is, Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him))?' As for the believer, he says: 'I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger.' Then it is said to him: 'Look at your place in Hell; Allah has indeed given you in exchange for it a place in Paradise.' So he sees both places, and his grave is widened for him by seventy cubits, and it is made green and lush for him until the Day of Resurrection. As for the disbeliever or the hypocrite, when he is asked: 'What did you used to say about this man?' he replies: 'I do not know; I used to say what the people said.' Then it will be said to him: 'You neither tried to know for yourself nor followed those who read (the Qur'an).' Then he will be struck between his two ears with such a forceful blow from an iron hammer that he will let out a terrible scream, which everything around him will hear except humans and jinn, and his grave will be made so narrow for him that his ribs will interlock with one another."""
"1676","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when the believing servant is about to depart from this world and turn toward the Hereafter, angels with white faces descend to him from the sky, their faces shining like the sun. They have with them one of the shrouds of Paradise and one of the perfumes of Paradise, and they sit around him as far as the eye can see. Then the Angel of Death comes and sits at his head and says: 'O good soul! Come out to forgiveness from Allah and His pleasure.' So the soul comes out as easily as a drop of water flows from the mouth of a waterskin. Then he (the angel) takes hold of it, and when he takes hold of it, the other angels do not leave it in his hand even for the blink of an eye, until they take it and place it in that shroud and that perfume. And there comes from it a fragrance like the finest musk ever found on the face of the earth. Then they ascend with it, and they do not pass by any gathering of angels except that they ask: 'Whose is this good soul?' So they tell them, calling him by the best of his names in this world: 'This is so-and-so, son of so-and-so.' Until they reach with it the lowest heaven and ask for the gate to be opened, and it is opened for them. The angels nearest to Allah in every heaven escort it to the next heaven, until they reach the seventh heaven. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: 'Write the record of My servant in Illiyyin, and return My servant to the earth, for from it I created them, into it I will return them, and from it I will bring them out once again.' So his soul is returned to his body. Then two angels come to him, sit him up and ask: 'Who is your Lord?' He says: 'My Lord is Allah.' They ask: 'What is your religion?' He says: 'My religion is Islam.' They ask: 'Who is this man who was sent among you?' He says: 'He is the Messenger of Allah.' They ask: 'How did you come to know?' He says: 'I read the Book of Allah, believed in it and affirmed it.' Then a caller calls out from the sky: 'My servant has spoken the truth, so spread for him a bed from Paradise, clothe him with the garments of Paradise, and open for him a door to Paradise.' So its breezes and fragrances keep coming to him from there, and his grave is widened for him as far as the eye can see. Then a man with a handsome face, fine clothes and a pleasant fragrance comes to him and says: 'Rejoice at what will delight you; this is your day which you were promised.' The servant asks him: 'Who are you? Yours is the face that brings good.' He says: 'I am your righteous deeds.' The servant says: 'O my Lord! Establish the Hour! O my Lord! Establish the Hour! So that I may return to my family and my wealth.' And indeed, when the disbelieving servant is about to depart from this world and turn toward the Hereafter, angels with black faces descend to him from the sky, carrying sackcloth (coarse cloth), and they sit around him as far as the eye can see. Then the Angel of Death comes and sits at his head and says: 'O wicked soul! Come out to the displeasure and wrath of Allah.' So the soul hides throughout his whole body, and the angel drags it out just as an iron skewer is pulled out of wet wool. Then he takes hold of it, and when he takes hold of it, the other angels do not leave it in his hand even for the blink of an eye, until they wrap it in that sackcloth. And there comes from it a stench like the foulest stench of a rotting corpse ever found on the face of the earth. Then they ascend with it, and they do not pass by any gathering of angels except that they say: 'Whose is this wicked soul?' So they tell them, calling him by the worst of his names in this world: 'This is so-and-so, son of so-and-so.' Then the gate is asked to be opened for him, but it is not opened for him. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: 'The gates of heaven will not be opened for them.' [Surah al-A'raf: 40] Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: 'Write his record in Sijjin, in the lowest earth.' Then his soul is flung down violently. So his soul is returned to his body. And two angels come to him, sit him up and ask: 'Who is your Lord?' He says: 'Alas, alas! I do not know.' They ask: 'What is your religion?' He says: 'Alas, alas! I do not know.' They ask: 'Who is this man who was sent among you?' He says: 'Alas, alas! I do not know.' Then a caller calls out from the sky: 'My servant has lied, so spread for him a bed of fire and open for him a door to Hell.' So its heat and scorching wind keep coming to him from there, and his grave is made so narrow for him that his ribs interlock with one another. Then an extremely ugly man with foul clothes and a putrid smell comes to him and says: 'Receive the tidings of what will grieve you; this is your day which you were promised.' He asks: 'Who are you? Yours is the face that brings evil.' He says: 'I am your wicked deeds.' Then he says: 'O my Lord! Do not establish the Hour.'"""
"1677","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a servant is rewarded for all of his spending except for constructing buildings (for extravagance and show)."""
"1678","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a servant (thoughtlessly) utters a word whose consequences he does not reflect upon, and because of that one word he falls into the Fire of Hell a distance farther than that between the east and the west."""
"1679","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection (people's) sweat will go down into the earth to a depth of seventy arm-spans, and it will indeed (rise and) reach up to people's mouths or their ears."""
"1680","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when all the scholars are brought before their Lord, Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) will be ahead of them all by the distance of a stone's throw."""
"1681","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the evil eye, by the permission of Allah Almighty, pursues a man until he climbs to some high place and then falls down from it."""
"1682","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection a banner will be raised for the betrayer (the one who breaks his pledge), and it will be said: 'Behold! This is (the mark of) the betrayal of so-and-so, son of so-and-so.'"""
"1683","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the thigh is part of the awrah (the area that must be covered)."""
"1684","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the grave is the first of the stages of the Hereafter. If a person is saved from it, the stages after it will be easier than it; and if he is not saved from it, the stages after it will be even harder than it."""
"1685","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the hearts (of people) are between two of the fingers of Allah Almighty; He turns them about (however He wills)."""
"1686","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one, is Yusuf bin Ya'qub bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim (peace be upon them). And had I remained in prison for as long as Yusuf (peace be upon him) remained, and then the summoner had come to me, I would have accepted his call at once (and come out). And may the mercy of Allah be upon Lut (peace be upon him); he was indeed seeking refuge in a strong support when he said: 'If only I had strength against you, or could take refuge in a strong support.' [Surah Hud: 80] So after him, every prophet that Allah Almighty sent was sent only from among the honoured and powerful of his people."""
"1687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the One who made them walk on their feet in this world is fully able to make them walk on their faces on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1688","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the One who sent down the disease has also sent down its cure."""
"1689","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the One who has forbidden drinking it has also forbidden buying and selling it. (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this about wine.)"""
"1690","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one who does not pay the zakah on his wealth, on the Day of Resurrection his wealth will take the form of a bald (venomous) snake with two black spots above its eyes. It will cling to him or become a collar around his neck, saying: 'I am your treasure, I am your treasure.'"""
"1691","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever has intercourse with his wife in her back passage (anus), Allah Almighty will not look at him with mercy on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1692","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever eats or drinks from vessels of silver and gold is in fact gulping the fire of Hell down into his belly."""
"1693","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever drags his garment (on the ground) out of arrogance, Allah Almighty will not look at him with mercy on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1694","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever lies about me, a house is built for him in Hell."""
"1695","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those who make these images (or statues) will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: 'Now bring to life what you have made.'"""
"1696","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those who cut down (shade-giving) lote trees will be flung headlong into the Fire of Hell."""
"1697","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah and His Messenger have disliked for you (the People of the Household) that the dirt of people's hands (that is, zakah and charity) should be assigned to you."""
"1698","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has refused my intercession three times concerning the one who kills a believer (unjustly)."""
"1699","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has closed the door of repentance to every person of innovation (until he abandons his innovation)."""
"1700","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has issued this new command regarding the prayer: that you do not speak in it except for the remembrance of Allah and what is appropriate for you, and that you stand before Allah in reverence and obedience."""
"1701","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty took the covenant from the back of Adam (peace be upon him) at Na'man (a valley of Arafat) on the Day of Arafah, and He brought forth from his loins all of his offspring that He was to create, then He scattered them before Him like tiny ants. Then He spoke to them face to face, saying: 'Am I not your Lord? They all answered: Yes indeed! (You are our Lord).' [Surah al-A'raf: 172]"""
"1702","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty brought forth the offspring of Adam (peace be upon him) from his back, then 'made them testify concerning themselves, asking: Am I not your Lord? They answered: Yes indeed!' [Surah al-A'raf: 172] Then He took them in His two handfuls and said: These will go to Paradise and these will go to Hell. So the people of Paradise are eased towards the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the people of Hell are eased towards the deeds of the people of Hell."""
"1703","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty brought me forth through (lawful) marriage, and He did not bring me forth through fornication (the path of indecency). (That is, my lineage is pure and rests upon lawful, Shari'ah-sanctioned marriage.)"""
"1704","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty loves the people of a household, He instils gentleness and kindness among them."""
"1705","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty loves a servant, He calls Jibril (peace be upon him) and says: I love so-and-so, so you love him too. So Jibril loves him too. Then he calls out among the inhabitants of the heavens: Indeed, Allah Almighty loves so-and-so, so you love him too. So the inhabitants of the heavens love him too, and then acceptance is placed for him in the hearts of the people of the earth as well. And when Allah hates a servant, He calls Jibril (peace be upon him) and says: I hate so-and-so, so you hate him too. So Jibril hates him too. Then he calls out among the inhabitants of the heavens: Indeed, Allah Almighty hates so-and-so, so you hate him too. So they all hate him too, and then aversion and hatred are placed for him in the hearts of the people of the earth as well."""
"1706","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty loves a people, He afflicts them with trials. So whoever is patient (in those trials) will have (the excellent reward of) patience, and whoever shows impatience will have (the burden of) impatience."""
"1707","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty intends mercy for a nation from among His servants, He takes its Prophet in death before it, and makes him a forerunner and one who goes ahead to prepare for that nation. And when Allah intends the destruction of a nation, He punishes them while their Prophet is alive, so He destroys them before his eyes and cools that Prophet's eyes with their destruction, because they rejected him and disobeyed his command."""
"1708","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when something is entrusted to Allah Almighty for safekeeping, He guards it (in the best way)."""
"1709","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty grants a Prophet some provision (property or wealth), it belongs (after his death) to the one who succeeds him after him (that is, his caliph) (inheritance does not apply to it)."""
"1710","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty sends down His punishments upon those deserving of His wrath, and at that same time the appointed hour of death of some righteous people also arrives, they too are destroyed along with them. Then (on the Day of Resurrection) they will be raised according to their intentions and their deeds."""
"1711","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves that the trace of His blessing be seen upon that servant. He dislikes wretchedness and deliberately displaying poverty, He hates the beggar who clings and asks insistently, and He loves the modest, chaste one who refrains from asking."""
"1712","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty sends down one of His blessings upon a servant, He loves that the trace of His blessing be visible upon His servant."""
"1713","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection, when Allah Almighty descends in His majesty to judge between His servants, and every nation is fallen on its knees, then among the first to be called will be a man who memorised the Qur'an, a man who was killed in the path of Allah, and a man who had much wealth. Allah Almighty will say to the reciter of the Qur'an: Did I not teach you what I sent down upon My Messenger? He will say: Yes indeed, O my Lord! Allah will ask: What did you do with your knowledge? He will say: I used to stand (in prayer) with it through the hours of the night and the day. Then Allah will say to him: You have lied. And the angels will also say to him: You have lied. Allah Almighty will say: Rather, your intention was that it be said that so-and-so is a great reciter, and that has been said. Then the wealthy man will be brought, and Allah will ask him: Did I not give you such abundance that I did not leave you in need of anyone? He will say: Yes indeed, O my Lord! Allah will ask: What did you do with what I gave you? He will say: I used to maintain ties of kinship and give in charity. Allah will say: You have lied. And the angels will also say: You have lied. Allah will say: Rather, your intention was that it be said that so-and-so is very generous, and that has been said. Then the man who was killed in the path of Allah will be brought, and Allah will ask him: For what were you killed? He will say: You commanded jihad in Your path, so I fought until I was killed. Allah will say: You have lied. The angels will also say to him: You have lied. Allah will say: Rather, you wanted it to be said that so-and-so is very brave, and that has been said. (Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said:) O Abu Hurayrah! These are the three kinds of people with whom the Fire of Hell will be kindled first on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1714","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has permitted me to tell about a rooster (an angel in the form of a rooster) whose feet have pierced through the depths of the earth and whose neck is bent beneath the Throne, and it is saying: 'Subhanaka ma a'zamak' ((O Allah!) Glory be to You, how immense is Your greatness!). Then it is answered (by Allah): The one who swears falsely by Me does not know this reality."""
"1715","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has sent me as a conveyor (of the message of the religion), and He did not send me as one who puts people into hardship (or who imposes needless severity)."""
"1716","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty turned my face towards al-Sham and my back towards Yemen, and said to me: O Muhammad! I have made what is in front of you a source of spoils and provision for you, and what is behind your back a source of support for you. Islam will continue to increase, and shirk and the polytheists will continue to decrease, until two women will travel together fearing nothing except injustice. And by the One in whose hand is my soul! The days and nights will not come to an end until this religion reaches as far as this star reaches."""
"1717","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty chose Kinanah from the descendants of Isma'il (peace be upon him), chose Quraysh from Kinanah, chose Banu Hashim from Quraysh, and chose me from Banu Hashim."""
"1718","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has chosen four phrases from all speech: 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), 'wal-hamdu lillah' (and praise be to Allah), 'wa la ilaha illallah' (and there is no god but Allah), and 'wallahu akbar' (and Allah is the Greatest). So whoever says 'Subhan Allah', twenty good deeds are written for him and twenty of his sins are erased. Whoever says 'wallahu akbar' has the same reward, and whoever says 'wa la ilaha illallah' has the same as well. And whoever says 'al-hamdu lillahi rabbil-'alamin' (praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds) sincerely from his heart, thirty good deeds are written for him and thirty of his sins are erased."""
"1719","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty looked at the state of the hearts of the people of Badr (those who took part in the Battle of Badr) and said: Do whatever you wish, for I have certainly forgiven you."""
"1720","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has given every rightful claimant his due, so there is no (valid) bequest for an heir; the child belongs to the (marital) bed (that is, the husband), and for the fornicator is the stone (that is, deprivation)."""
"1721","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has given you one third of your wealth at the time of your death (to bequeath), so that your (good) deeds may be increased."""
"1722","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made five prayers obligatory upon His servants in every day and night."""
"1723","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has commanded me to name Madinah 'Taybah' (the pure one)."""
"1724","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty commanded Yahya bin Zakariyya (peace be upon them both) with five things: that he himself act upon them and that he command the Children of Israel to act upon them. It seemed that he delayed somewhat in this, so Allah Almighty revealed to Isa (peace be upon him): Either you convey them, or else he (Yahya, peace be upon him) conveys them. So Isa (peace be upon him) came to him and said: You were commanded with five things, to act upon them and to command the Children of Israel to act upon them; so either you convey them or I will convey them. Yahya (peace be upon him) said to him: O Spirit of Allah! I fear that if you go ahead of me, I will be punished or made to sink into the earth. Then Yahya (peace be upon him) gathered the Children of Israel in Bayt al-Maqdis until the mosque was filled; he sat on a raised place, praised and extolled Allah, and then said: Indeed, Allah has commanded me with five things, that I act upon them and command you to act upon them. The first of them is that you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, for the example of one who associates partners with Allah is like a man who bought a slave with his own pure wealth, gold or silver, then settled him in a house and said: Work and bring (the earnings) to me. So the slave began to work and take the earnings to someone other than his master. Which of you would be pleased for his slave to be like that? And indeed Allah created you and provided for you, so worship Him alone and do not associate anyone with Him. And He has commanded you to pray, so when you stand for prayer, do not look here and there, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, keeps His attention turned towards His servant as long as he does not look here and there. And He has commanded you to fast; its example is that of a man who has a pouch of musk in the midst of a group, and everyone is sensing the fragrance of the musk; and indeed, the smell of the fasting person's mouth is purer in the sight of Allah than the fragrance of musk. And He has commanded you to give charity; its example is that of a man whom the enemy has taken captive, tied his hands to his neck and brought forward to kill him, and he says to them: Would you agree to let me ransom my life from you and free myself? Then he ransoms himself from them with little and much until he frees himself from them. And He has commanded you to remember Allah abundantly; its example is that of a man whom the enemy is pursuing swiftly, and he comes to a strong fortress and secures himself within it; and indeed, a servant is most protected from Satan when he is engaged in the remembrance of Allah Almighty. And I command you with five things which Allah has commanded me: al-Jama'ah (holding fast to the community of the Muslims), listening and obeying (the leader), emigration (hijrah), and jihad in the path of Allah. For indeed, whoever leaves the community even by a handspan has removed the collar of Islam from his neck, unless he returns (to the community). And whoever calls with the call of the Days of Ignorance (tribal partisanship and the like) is among those who fall on their knees in Hell, even if he fasts, prays and claims that he is a Muslim. So call with the call given by Allah, who has named you Muslims, believers and servants of Allah."""
"1725","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has revealed to me that you should treat one another with humility, so that no one boasts over another and no one transgresses against another."""
"1726","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has revealed to me that you should adopt humility and that none of you should transgress against another."""
"1727","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has revealed to me that whoever travels a path in search of knowledge, I make the path to Paradise easy for him; and whoever I deprive of his two precious things (that is, his eyes), I make Paradise obligatory for him in return for them; and excellence in knowledge is better than excellence in worship; and the foundation of the religion is scrupulous piety."""
"1728","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has sent me to every red and black (that is, all humans and jinn); I have been helped with awe (cast into the hearts of the enemy); the spoils of war have been made lawful for me; the whole earth has been made for me a place of prostration and a means of purification (tahur); and I have been granted (the right of) intercession for the sinners of my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1729","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has pardoned my Ummah for the whisperings that arise in their hearts, as long as they do not act upon them or express them with the tongue, and (He has also pardoned) that which they are forced into."""
"1730","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has pardoned my Ummah for the thoughts (whisperings) that come into their hearts, as long as they do not express them with the tongue or act upon them."""
"1731","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty, for my sake, has pardoned my Ummah for mistakes, forgetfulness, and that which they are forced into."""
"1732","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty, for my sake, has pardoned my Ummah for the whisperings that arise in their hearts, as long as they do not act upon them or express them with the tongue."""
"1733","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has bestowed upon you, as charity at the time of your death, one third of your wealth (that is, He has permitted you to make a bequest), and has made it a means of increase in your (good) deeds."""
"1734","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has shown grace and generosity to this gathering of yours: He has forgiven the sinners among you for the sake of the righteous among you, and He has given the righteous among you what they asked for. Now depart (from here) with the name of Allah."""
"1735","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has placed blessing in the pre-dawn meal (suhur) and in measuring."""
"1736","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made the truth flow upon the tongue and heart of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"1737","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty made the whole world little, and now only a very little of it remains, like a small pool whose clear water has been drunk and only muddy water remains."""
"1738","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has placed the punishment of this Ummah in this world, in the form of killing and bloodshed (and tribulations)."""
"1739","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made that which comes out of the belly of the son of Adam (as waste) an example for this world."""
"1740","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made these new moons a means of fixing times. So when you see it (the moon of Ramadan), fast; and when you see it (the moon of Shawwal), end the fast (that is, celebrate Eid). And if the sky is overcast (that is, the moon is not sighted), complete the count of thirty days."""
"1741","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Jamil (Beautiful) and loves beauty."""
"1742","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Beautiful and loves beauty, and He loves that the trace of His blessing be seen upon His servant, and He dislikes wretchedness and deliberately making oneself appear wretched."""
"1743","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Beautiful and loves beauty, and He loves lofty character while He dislikes base and lowly character."""
"1744","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Generous and loves generosity, and He loves lofty character while He dislikes base and lowly character."""
"1745","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty held back the elephant from Makkah and gave His Messenger and the believers dominance over it. Behold! It (Makkah) was not made lawful (for fighting) for anyone before me, nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me. Listen! It was made lawful even for me only for an hour of a day. Listen! It is sacred even in this hour of mine: its thorns are not to be broken, its trees are not to be cut, and its fallen property is not to be picked up except by one who will announce it. And whoever has one of his people killed has a choice between two things: either he accepts the blood money, or the heirs of the slain person take retaliation (qisas)."""
"1746","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made wine unlawful, has made carrion and its price unlawful, and has made swine and its price unlawful as well."""
"1747","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made unlawful for my Ummah wine, gambling, barley liquor (al-mizr), the drum (al-kubah) and millet liquor (al-ghubayra'), and He has granted me the additional Witr prayer."""
"1748","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made unlawful for you wine, gambling, barley wine (al-mizr) and the drum (al-kubah), and every intoxicant is unlawful."""
"1749","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made unlawful for you disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, withholding (the rights that are due) and demanding (what is not due). And He has disliked for you idle talk (qil wa qal, that is, pointless gossip), asking too many questions and wasting wealth."""
"1750","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made charity unlawful for me and for my household."""
"1751","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty made Makkah sacred (inviolable) on the day He created the heavens and the earth, so it is sacred by the sanctity Allah Almighty has granted it until the Day of Resurrection. It was not made lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me, and even for me it was made lawful for only one hour in my whole life. Its game is not to be startled, its thorns are not to be cut, its grass is not to be uprooted, and its lost property may only be picked up by one who will announce it."""
"1752","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made unlawful through suckling (that is, the bond of nursing) all those relationships that He has made unlawful through birth (that is, lineage)."""
"1753","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made unlawful through suckling all those relationships that He has made unlawful through lineage."""
"1754","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, wherever Allah Almighty created a disease, He also created its cure, so seek treatment."""
"1755","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty created the creation, He wrote with His Hand upon Himself (in a book with Him): 'Indeed, My mercy prevails over My wrath.'"""
"1756","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Most Modest and One who conceals much; He loves modesty and concealment. So when one of you takes a bath, let him screen himself."""
"1757","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Most Modest and Most Generous and Noble. When a man raises his hands to Him (in supplication), He is too modest to return those hands empty and disappointed."""
"1758","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty created Adam (peace be upon him), then He brought out all of creation from his back and said: 'These will be in Paradise and I do not care, and these will be in Hell and I do not care.'"""
"1759","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty created Adam (peace be upon him) from a handful of soil that He took from the whole of the earth, so the children of Adam came according to the nature of that earth. Among them are the red, the white and the black, and those in between these colours (such as wheat-coloured). Likewise, among them are the gentle-natured and the harsh-natured, the wicked and the pure, and those of a temperament in between."""
"1760","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty created Paradise and created Hell, then He created dwellers for Paradise and created dwellers for Hell."""
"1761","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty created the creation until, when He had finished creating His creation, the womb (kinship) stood up. Allah Almighty said: 'What is it?' It said: 'This is the station of one who seeks refuge with You from being severed.' Allah Almighty said: 'Yes. Are you not pleased that I will maintain ties with whoever maintains ties with you, and sever whoever severs you?' It said: 'Of course, O my Lord!' Allah Almighty said: 'Then that (station) is (granted) to you.'"""
"1762","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty created both the disease and the cure, so seek treatment, but do not seek treatment with unlawful things."""
"1763","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the day Allah Almighty created mercy, He made it into one hundred parts. He kept ninety-nine parts with Himself and sent only one mercy among all His creation. So if the disbeliever knew how much mercy is with Allah, he would never despair of Paradise, and if the believer knew how much punishment is with Allah, he would never feel safe from Hell."""
"1764","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty created His creation in darkness, then He cast His light upon them. So whoever was reached by that light on that day was guided, and whoever was missed by it went astray."""
"1765","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty created one hundred parts of mercy. He distributed one part of them among the creation, and He kept ninety-nine parts for the Day of Resurrection."""
"1766","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty created one hundred mercies. Then He spread only one mercy among His creation, by which they show mercy to one another, and He has stored up ninety-nine mercies with Himself for His righteous servants."""
"1767","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the day Allah Almighty created the heavens and the earth, He also created one hundred mercies, each mercy equal to the distance between the heaven and the earth. Then He placed only one of them on the earth; because of it a mother shows tenderness to her child, and wild animals and birds show kindness to one another. He deferred ninety-nine mercies, and when the Day of Resurrection comes, He will complete them (to one hundred) with this one mercy."""
"1768","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Most Merciful, Most Modest and Most Generous. He is too modest before His servant, when he raises his hands to Him, to then place no good in them (that is, to turn them away empty)."""
"1769","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has approved ease for this Ummah and has disliked hardship for it."""
"1770","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Gentle; He loves gentleness and is pleased with it, and He grants for gentleness what He does not grant for harshness. So when you ride these speechless animals, let them stop at their halting places (that is, give them rest). If the land is barren, travel quickly on them, for the earth is folded up by night (that is, the journey is covered easily) in a way it is not folded up by day. And beware of stopping for the night in the middle of the road, for it is the path of animals and the shelter of snakes."""
"1771","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Gentle; He loves gentleness, and He grants for gentleness what He does not grant for harshness."""
"1772","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has added a prayer for you, so guard it, and it is the Witr prayer."""
"1773","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty folded up the earth for me, so I saw its easts and its wests, and the dominion of my Ummah will surely reach as far as what was folded up for me of it. I was given the two treasures, the red and the white (that is, gold and silver, or the empires of Rome and Persia). I asked my Lord for my Ummah that they not be destroyed by a general famine, and that no enemy other than from among themselves be given power over them who would destroy their core. And my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, said: 'O Muhammad, when I issue a decree, it is not turned back. I have granted you for your Ummah that I will not destroy them by a general famine, and that I will not give power over them to any enemy other than from among themselves who would destroy their core, even if people gathered against them from all the regions of the earth, until some of them destroy one another.' I fear for my Ummah only the misguiding leaders (rulers and scholars). When the sword is placed among my Ummah (that is, when bloodshed among themselves begins), it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection. The Hour will not be established until tribes of my Ummah join the polytheists, and until tribes of my Ummah worship idols. There will surely be in my Ummah thirty great liars, each of them claiming that he is a prophet, whereas I am the Seal of the Prophets; there is no prophet after me. And a group of my Ummah will always remain upon the truth, prevailing; those who oppose them will not harm them, until the command of Allah (the Hour) comes."""
"1774","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will ask every shepherd about the flock that was placed in his charge: did he guard it or did he neglect it? Even a man will be asked about his household."""
"1775","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has named Madinah 'Tabah' (the pure one)."""
"1776","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection Allah Almighty will single out a man from my Ummah before all of creation, and ninety-nine registers (of sins) will be unrolled before him, each register stretching as far as the eye can see. Then Allah Almighty will say: 'Do you deny anything of this? Have My guardian scribes wronged you?' The servant will say: 'No, O my Lord.' Allah Almighty will say: 'Do you have any excuse?' He will say: 'No, O my Lord.' Allah Almighty will say: 'Rather, you have a good deed with Us, and no injustice will be done to you today.' So a card will be brought out on which is written: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan abduhu wa rasuluh' (I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger). Allah Almighty will say: 'Be present for your weighing.' The servant will say: 'O my Lord, what is this one card compared to these huge registers?' It will be said to him: 'Surely you will not be wronged.' Then all the registers will be placed in one pan of the scale and the card in the other pan; the registers will fly up (being light) and the card will be heavy, for nothing can be heavier than the name of Allah Almighty."""
"1777","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is the Maker of every maker and of his craft."""
"1778","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made the food of the son of Adam a parable for this world, and has made this world a parable for the food of the son of Adam, however much spice and salt he may add to it."""
"1779","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Most Pardoning and He loves pardoning."""
"1780","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has favoured me over the other prophets with four things: I have been sent to all of mankind (as a Messenger); the whole earth has been made a means of purification and a place of prostration for me and my Ummah, so wherever the time of prayer reaches a man of my Ummah, there is his mosque and there is his means of purification (tayammum); I have been helped by awe (cast into the enemy) from a month's distance; and spoils of war have been made lawful for me."""
"1781","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has said: 'We sent down wealth for establishing the prayer and giving the zakah. If the son of Adam had one valley (of wealth), he would love to have a second, and if he had two valleys, he would love to have a third along with them. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust (that is, his greed ends only after death).' Then Allah Almighty accepts the repentance of whoever repents."""
"1782","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'Whoever shows enmity to a friend (wali) of Mine, I have declared war against him. My servant does not draw near to Me with anything more beloved to Me than what I have made obligatory upon him, and My servant continues to draw near to Me with voluntary acts of worship until I love him. When I love him, I become his hearing with which he hears, his sight with which he sees, his hand with which he grasps, and his foot with which he walks (that is, his limbs become subject to My will). If he asks Me for something, I will surely give it to him, and if he seeks My protection, I will surely protect him. I do not hesitate in anything I do as much as I hesitate in taking the soul of the believer; he dislikes death and I dislike hurting him.'"""
"1783","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty took your souls when He willed (that is, caused you to sleep) and returned them to you when He willed. O Bilal, stand up and call the people to prayer with the adhan."""
"1784","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty took a handful (of creation) and said: 'These will go to Paradise by My mercy.' And He took another handful and said: 'These will go to Hell, and I do not care.'"""
"1785","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has taken me as His Khalil (intimate friend)."""
"1786","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has protected my Ummah from ever uniting (agreeing) upon misguidance."""
"1787","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has removed from you the arrogance of the Days of Ignorance and its boasting about forefathers. Now people are of only two kinds: a God-fearing believer and a wretched sinner. You are all the children of Adam, and Adam was created from dust. Let people give up boasting about those peoples (forefathers) who have become coals from among the coals of Hell, or else they will be more contemptible in the sight of Allah Almighty than the dung beetle that pushes filth with its nose."""
"1788","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has given everyone who has a right his due right, so there is now no bequest (permissible) for an heir."""
"1789","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has given everyone who has a right his due right, so making a bequest for an heir is not permissible. The child belongs to the (husband who owns the) bed, and for the fornicator is the stone (deprivation), and their reckoning is with Allah. Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father, or a freed slave who attributes himself to other than his patrons, upon him is the continuous curse of Allah until the Day of Resurrection. And no woman should spend anything from her husband's house without her husband's permission."" It was asked: ""Not even food?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That is the best of our wealth."""
"1790","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has extended the period for sighting it (the moon) (that is, He has made its sighting necessary), so if the horizon is clouded over for you, complete the count."""
"1791","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has set his reward according to his intention."""
"1792","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has given Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) two wings stained with blood, with which he flies along with the angels (in Paradise)."""
"1793","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made the Fire of Hell unlawful for the one who said 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah) seeking thereby purely the pleasure of Allah Almighty."""
"1794","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has appointed for every heir his share of the inheritance, so making a bequest for an heir is not permissible. The child belongs to the (husband who owns the) bed, and for the fornicator is the stone (deprivation). Whoever deliberately claims to belong to someone other than his father, or a freed slave who turns away from his patrons and attributes himself to others, upon him is the curse of Allah Almighty, the angels and all the people, and Allah Almighty will not accept from him any obligatory or voluntary deed."""
"1795","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has prescribed excellence (ihsan, gentleness and good conduct) in everything. So when you kill, kill in a good manner, and when you slaughter an animal, slaughter in a good manner. Let each of you sharpen his blade well and let him give ease to the animal he slaughters."""
"1796","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has written down the good deeds and the bad deeds and then made them clear. So whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, Allah Almighty writes it down with Himself as one complete good deed. If he intends it and then does it, Allah Almighty writes it down with Himself as ten good deeds up to seven hundred times, and even many times more than that. If he intends a bad deed but does not do it, Allah Almighty writes it down with Himself as one complete good deed. But if he intends a bad deed and does it, Allah Almighty writes it down as only one bad deed. And none is destroyed before Allah except one who is truly bound for destruction."""
"1797","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has written for the son of Adam his share of zina (fornication), which he will inevitably attain. The zina of the eye is looking (with an unlawful gaze), and the zina of the tongue is (obscene) speech. The self wishes and desires, and the private part confirms it or denies it."""
"1798","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has made the sa'i (between Safa and Marwah) obligatory upon you, so perform the sa'i."""
"1799","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty wrote a Book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and it is with the Throne. And He sent down from it two verses with which Surah al-Baqarah was concluded. In whatever house they are recited for three nights, Satan cannot come near that house."""
"1800","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Generous and loves those who are generous; He is Most Bountiful and loves bounty; He loves lofty manners and dislikes base and vile manners."""
"1801","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Generous and loves generosity (liberality and nobility), and He loves lofty manners and dislikes base and vile manners."""
"1802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has cursed wine, the one who presses it, the one who has it pressed, the one who drinks it, the one who serves it, the one who carries it, the one to whom it is carried, the one who sells it, the one who buys it, and the one who consumes its price."""
"1803","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Allah Almighty created the creation, He wrote with His Hand upon Himself (in a Book): Indeed, My mercy prevails over My wrath."""
"1804","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has not commanded us, concerning the provision He has granted us, to clothe the stones, bricks and clay (of houses)."""
"1805","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty did not send any prophet, nor appoint any caliph, except that he had two kinds of advisers (confidants): one group of advisers who command him to do good and forbid him from evil, and another group of advisers who spare no effort in bringing him to ruin. And whoever is protected from evil advisers has truly been saved."""
"1806","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty did not send me to cause hardship or to be harsh; rather, He sent me as a teacher and one who makes things easy."""
"1807","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has not given any transformed (people whose forms were disfigured) any lineage or offspring, and monkeys and pigs existed even before those transformed people."""
"1808","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has not sent down any disease without sending down its cure. So hold fast to cow's milk, for it grazes from every kind of tree (and plant)."""
"1809","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has not sent down any disease without sending down its remedy; those who know it know it, and those who do not know it remain unaware of it, except al-Sam, and that is death."""
"1810","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has not sent down any disease without sending down its cure, except old age. So make use of cow's milk, for it grazes from every kind of tree (and herb)."""
"1811","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will not leave me helpless regarding my Ummah by not granting it a respite of half a day, that is, five hundred years."""
"1812","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, had Allah Almighty willed that He not be disobeyed, He would not have created Iblis at all."""
"1813","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty supports this religion even through a wicked (sinful) man."""
"1814","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty protects His believing servant from the world (and its allurements) while He loves him, just as you keep your sick one away from (harmful) food and drink because you fear for his life."""
"1815","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty nurtures (the charity of) a date or a morsel for one of you, just as one of you nurtures his foal or young camel, until it (the charity, having grown) becomes the size of Mount Uhud."""
"1816","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is pleased with the servant when he eats something or drinks something and then praises Allah for it."""
"1817","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty increases the punishment of the disbeliever because of his family's weeping (and wailing) over him."""
"1818","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will question the servant on the Day of Resurrection, until He asks him: 'When you saw evil, what prevented you from stopping it?' Then, when Allah Almighty teaches that servant his argument, he will say: 'O my Lord, I placed my hope in You and I feared the people.'"""
"1819","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty manifests Himself (in a special way to His creation) on the fifteenth night of Sha'ban and forgives all His creation, except a polytheist or one who harbours rancour (hatred)."""
"1820","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is greatly pleased with prayer offered in congregation."""
"1821","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is greatly pleased with the servant's words when he says: 'La ilaha illa anta, inni qad zalamtu nafsi, faghfir li dhunubi, innahu la yaghfiru al-dhunuba illa anta' (There is no god but You; indeed I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins except You). Allah Almighty says: 'My servant has recognised that he has a Lord who both forgives and punishes.'"""
"1822","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty keeps giving respite to the wrongdoer, until, when He seizes him, He does not let him go."""
"1823","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is benevolent, so you too should act with excellence (gentleness and kindness)."""
"1824","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is benevolent and loves excellence. So when you kill, kill in a good manner, and when you slaughter, slaughter in a good manner. Each of you should sharpen his blade well and then give ease to the animal he slaughters."""
"1825","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is with the debtor (in helping him) until he repays his debt, provided that his debt was not incurred for something Allah dislikes."""
"1826","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is with the judge (the one who decides cases) so long as he does not deliberately commit injustice (unfairness). But when he commits injustice, Allah Almighty entrusts him to himself (that is, He withdraws His help)."""
"1827","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is with the judge so long as he does not commit injustice. But when he commits injustice, Allah Almighty disowns him and attaches Satan to him."""
"1828","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is with the judge so long as he does not deliberately commit wrong and transgression."""
"1829","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Witr (One) and loves what is odd (in number)."""
"1830","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Witr (One) and loves what is odd, so when you perform istinja (using clods or stones), use an odd number."""
"1831","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is Witr (One) and loves what is odd, so O people of the Qur'an, you too should pray the Witr (odd-numbered prayer)."""
"1832","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of wine, carrion, swine and idols."""
"1833","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah and His Messenger forbid you from eating the meat of domestic donkeys, for it is impure and a deed of Satan."""
"1834","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has placed the truth upon the tongue of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he speaks in accordance with it."""
"1835","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has relieved the traveller of fasting (temporarily) and of half the prayer (by way of shortening it)."""
"1836","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has pardoned my Ummah for mistakes, forgetfulness, and whatever they are forced to do."""
"1837","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has appointed an angel over the womb, who says: 'O my Lord, (now) it is a drop of fluid. O my Lord, (now) it is a clinging clot. O my Lord, (now) it is a lump of flesh.' Then, when Allah Almighty wishes to decree its creation, the angel asks: 'O my Lord, will it be wretched or blessed? Male or female? What will its provision be? And what will its lifespan be?' So all of this is written while it is still in its mother's womb."""
"1838","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty, His angels, and even the ants in their holes and the fish in the sea send blessings upon the one who teaches people goodness."""
"1839","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty and His angels send mercy upon those in the first row."""
"1840","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty and His angels send mercy upon those in the first row. Straighten your rows, align your shoulders, be gentle in the hands of your brothers, and fill the gaps, for Satan enters between you like small black lambs."""
"1841","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty and His angels send mercy upon those in the front row. The mu'adhdhin is forgiven (by its blessing) as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing that hears his voice affirms him, and he (the mu'adhdhin) receives a reward equal to the reward of all those who pray with him."""
"1842","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty and His angels send mercy upon those in the front rows."""
"1843","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty and His angels send mercy upon those who join the rows, and whoever fills a gap in the row, Allah Almighty raises him a degree in return for it."""
"1844","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty and His angels send mercy upon those who eat suhur."""
"1845","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty alone is al-Hakam (the Judge), and to Him belongs the judgement (the authority to decide)."""
"1846","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty alone is the Creator, the One who restricts, the One who expands, the Provider, and the One who sets prices. And I hope to meet Allah Almighty in a state where none of you has any claim against me for a wrong done to him in life or property."""
"1847","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty alone is al-Salam (the Giver of peace). So when one of you sits in the prayer, let him say: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibat, as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh, as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin' (All verbal, physical and financial worship belongs to Allah; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon all the righteous servants of Allah). For when you say this, it reaches every righteous servant of Allah in the heavens and the earth. Then let him say: 'Ashhadu an la ilaha illallah, wa ashhadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluh' (I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is His servant and Messenger). Then, after that, let him ask for whatever supplication he wishes."""
"1848","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will never gather my Ummah upon misguidance, and the Hand of Allah (that is, His help) is over the community."""
"1849","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not love disobedience to parents."""
"1850","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not love anyone who is shameless and given to obscene speech."""
"1851","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is not pleased, for His believing servant, when He takes away someone dear to him (a beloved person) from among the people of the earth and he bears it with patience and hopes for reward, to give him any reward less than Paradise."""
"1852","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is not shy of stating the truth: do not approach women in their back passages (the anus)."""
"1853","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not wrong a believer even a single good deed; he is given its reward in this world and will also be rewarded for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is fed in this world in return for his good deeds, until, when he reaches the Hereafter, he will have no good deed left for which he could be given any good."""
"1854","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will not take away knowledge by snatching it from (the hearts of) His servants; rather, He will take away knowledge by taking away the scholars (through death), until, when no scholar remains, people will take ignorant men as their leaders. They will then be asked questions and will give rulings without knowledge, so they will go astray themselves and lead others astray."""
"1855","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not accept any prayer without purification (purity), nor does He accept any charity from wealth gained through misappropriation."""
"1856","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not accept any deed except that which is purely for Him and through which only His pleasure is sought."""
"1857","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not sanctify a nation in which the weak person cannot take his right from the strong without any fear or hesitation."""
"1858","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not sanctify a nation that does not give its weak their right."""
"1859","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not grow weary (of giving reward) until you grow weary (of doing deeds)."""
"1860","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not sleep, nor is it befitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the scale (of justice or provision) and raises it. The deeds of the night are raised up to Him before the deeds of the day, and the deeds of the day before the deeds of the night. His veil is light. If He were to remove it, the splendours of His Face would burn everything of His creation as far as His sight reaches."""
"1861","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will not snatch knowledge away from you after having given it to you; rather, He will take the scholars along with their knowledge (cause them to die), and ignorant people will remain. They will then be asked questions and will give rulings, so they will go astray themselves and lead others astray."""
"1862","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not look at your forms and your wealth; rather, He looks at your hearts and your deeds."""
"1863","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not look (with the gaze of mercy) at the one who (out of arrogance) lets his lower garment hang below his ankles."""
"1864","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty does not look (with the gaze of mercy) at the one who drags his lower garment (or clothing) on the ground out of pride and arrogance."""
"1865","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty supports Hassan (bin Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him) through Jibril the Trustworthy (the Holy Spirit) for as long as he defends the Messenger of Allah."""
"1866","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty supports this religion even through people who have no share (in the Hereafter)."""
"1867","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty boasts of the people of Arafat before the inhabitants of the heavens (the angels), and says to them: Look at these servants of Mine; they have come to Me dishevelled and covered in dust."""
"1868","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty, on the evening of the Day of Arafah, boasts before His angels about the people of Arafat, and says: Look at these servants of Mine; they have come to Me dishevelled and covered in dust."""
"1869","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty tests a servant in what He has given him. If he is content with what Allah has apportioned for him, he is blessed in it and it is made ample for him; and if he is not content, he is not blessed in it, and he is given nothing more than what was decreed for him."""
"1870","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty afflicts His believing servant with illness until it becomes an expiation for all his sins."""
"1871","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty stretches out His Hand at night so that the one who sinned during the day may repent, and He stretches out His Hand during the day so that the one who sinned at night may repent, (and this will continue) until the sun rises from the west."""
"1872","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection Allah Almighty will raise the days in their original form, and He will raise Friday for its people in a radiant and shining form. They will gather around it (Friday) just as a bride is escorted to her noble groom. It will give light for them and they will walk in its light. Their colours will be white like snow, and their fragrance will spread like musk. They will be walking through mountains of camphor. The jinn and mankind will be watching them in amazement, unable to lower their gaze, until they enter Paradise. No one else will be mixed in with them except the muezzins who used to call the adhan seeking reward."""
"1873","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will send a wind from the direction of Yemen, softer than silk, and it will not leave anyone who has even a grain's weight of faith in his heart without taking his soul."""
"1874","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will send for this Ummah, at the head of every hundred years, someone (or a group) who will renew its religion for it."""
"1875","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty detests those eloquent (glib-tongued) men who (out of affectation and artificiality in speech) twist their tongues around just as a cow twists its tongue (while eating fodder)."""
"1876","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty detests the one who begs importunately (with persistence)."""
"1877","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty detests the one who is shameless and given to obscene speech."""
"1878","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty detests every person who is ill-tempered, arrogant, and clamorous in the marketplaces; a corpse by night (sleeping heedlessly like the dead), a donkey by day (absorbed like a donkey only in earning worldly gain); well-versed in the affairs of this world and ignorant of the affairs of the Hereafter."""
"1879","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty detests every person who is well-versed in the affairs of this world but utterly ignorant of the affairs of the Hereafter."""
"1880","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves that when any of you does a piece of work, he does it with perfection (and excellence)."""
"1881","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves gentleness in every matter."""
"1882","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves the servant who is God-fearing, self-sufficient (that is, rich of heart) and inconspicuous (far from showing off)."""
"1883","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves sneezing and dislikes yawning."""
"1884","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. So when any of you sneezes and says 'Alhamdulillah' (All praise is for Allah), it is a right upon every Muslim who hears him to say to him in reply 'Yarhamuk Allah' (May Allah have mercy on you). As for yawning, it is from Satan, so when any of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can, for when a person says 'haa' (while yawning), Satan laughs at him."""
"1885","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves that His concessions (allowances) be acted upon, just as He loves that His firm commands (obligations) be acted upon."""
"1886","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves that His concessions be acted upon, just as He dislikes that He be disobeyed."""
"1887","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves to see the effect of His blessing upon His servant."""
"1888","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves the person who is lenient when selling, lenient when buying, and lenient when demanding repayment of a debt."""
"1889","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves lofty manners and dislikes base manners."""
"1890","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves lofty and noble matters and dislikes their base aspects."""
"1891","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty loves that when a worker does a job, he does it really well."""
"1892","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty introduces by His command whatever new ruling He wills, and indeed Allah Almighty has introduced this new ruling: that you should not speak during the prayer."""
"1893","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will bring some people out of Hell in such a state that nothing of them will remain except their faces, and then He will admit them into Paradise."""
"1894","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will bring the believer close to Himself, place His covering over him and screen him from the people, and make him confess his sins. He will say: Do you remember such-and-such a sin? Do you remember such-and-such a sin? He will say: Yes, O my Lord! Until, when He has made him confess all his sins and he thinks within himself that he is now ruined, Allah Almighty will say: I concealed these sins of yours in the world, and today I forgive them for you. Then the record of his good deeds will be given to him in his right hand. As for the disbeliever and the hypocrite, the witnesses will call out: These are the ones who lied against their Lord. Behold! The curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers."""
"1895","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty is pleased with three things for you and dislikes three things for you. He is pleased for you: that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him; that you all hold firmly together to the rope of Allah and do not become divided; and that you sincerely wish well for the one whom Allah has put in charge of your affairs. And He dislikes for you: idle talk ('it was said' and 'he said'), asking too many questions, and wasting wealth."""
"1896","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty raises some people through this Book and lowers others through it."""
"1897","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty increases the punishment of the disbeliever because of some of his family's weeping over him."""
"1898","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty looks upon His servants with mercy on the fifteenth night of Sha'ban, and He forgives the believers, gives respite to the disbelievers, and leaves the people of rancour with their rancour until they abandon it."""
"1899","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will punish the image-makers because of the images they made."""
"1900","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will, on the Day of Resurrection, punish those who torment people in this world."""
"1901","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has protective jealousy (ghayrah), and the believer too has protective jealousy; and Allah's jealousy is that the believer should commit what Allah Almighty has forbidden him."""
"1902","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty accepts charity and takes it in His right hand, then He nurtures and grows it for you just as one of you raises his foal, until even a single morsel becomes (grows) as large as the mountain of Uhud."""
"1903","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty accepts the repentance of a servant as long as the throes of death have not come upon him (that is, as long as the soul has not reached the throat)."""
"1904","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'When I take back in this world My servant's two beloved things (that is, his eyes) (and he is patient over it), then there is no reward for him with Me other than Paradise.'"""
"1905","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'I am near to the opinion My servant holds of Me; so if he holds a good opinion, there is good for him, and if he holds a bad opinion, there is bad for him.'"""
"1906","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'I am with My servant as long as he remembers Me and his lips move with My remembrance.'"""
"1907","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'Fasting is exclusively for Me, and I Myself will reward it.' The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast he rejoices, and when he meets Allah Almighty he will rejoice at the reward his Lord grants him. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! The smell of the fasting person's mouth is purer and more pleasing to Allah than the fragrance of musk."""
"1908","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'Might is My lower garment and grandeur (majesty) is My cloak; so whoever contends with Me regarding either of them (that is, claims equality with Me in them), I will punish him.'"""
"1909","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'Indeed, a servant whose body I have kept healthy and whose livelihood I have made ample, then five years pass over him and he does not come to Me (to My House for Hajj or Umrah), is surely deprived.'"""
"1910","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'Indeed, My believing servant is, in My sight, at the station of every good; I am drawing out his soul from between his sides while he is praising Me.'"""
"1911","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will say to the people of Paradise: 'O people of Paradise!' They will say: 'Our Lord, here we are at Your service; all felicity is in Your hands and all good is with You alone.' Allah Almighty will say: 'Are you pleased?' They will say: 'Why should we not be pleased, when You have given us what You have not given to anyone else of Your creation?' Allah will say: 'Shall I not give you something even better than that?' They will say: 'O our Lord, what could be better than that?' Allah Almighty will say: 'I make My good pleasure binding upon you forever, so after this I will never be displeased with you.'"""
"1912","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will say to the person in Hell with the lightest punishment: 'If you had everything on the earth, would you give it as a ransom to be released (from this punishment)?' He will say: 'Yes.' Allah Almighty will say: 'When you were in the loins of Adam, I asked of you something far easier than this: that you associate nothing with Me; but you refused everything except associating partners with Me.'"""
"1913","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'O son of Adam, take care to pray four rak'ahs for Me in the early part of the day, and through their blessing I will suffice you in all your affairs until the end of the day.'"""
"1914","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty says: 'O son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship (that is, with undivided attention), and I will fill your chest with contentment (freedom from want) and remove your poverty; and if you do not do so, I will fill your hands with work and preoccupations, and I will not remove your poverty either.'"""
"1915","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'Where are those who loved one another for the sake of My majesty and glory? Today I will shade them in My shade, on the day when there is no shade but My shade.'"""
"1916","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'O son of Adam, I was sick and you did not visit Me.' The servant will say: 'O my Lord, how could I visit You when You are the Lord of all the worlds?' Allah will say: 'Did you not know that My servant so-and-so fell sick, yet you did not visit him? Do you not know that had you gone to visit him, you would have found Me with him? O son of Adam, I asked you for food, but you did not feed Me.' The servant will say: 'O my Lord, how could I feed You when You are the Lord of the worlds?' Allah will say: 'Did you not know that My servant so-and-so asked you for food, but you did not feed him? Do you not know that had you fed him, you would have found its reward with Me? O son of Adam, I asked you for water, but you did not give Me to drink.' The servant will say: 'O my Lord, how could I give You to drink when You are the Lord of all the worlds?' Allah will say: 'My servant so-and-so asked you for water, but you did not give him to drink. Know that had you given him water, you would have found its reward with Me.'"""
"1917","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty gives respite until, when half or two-thirds of the night has passed, He says: 'Let My servants ask of Me alone and of no one else. Whoever supplicates to Me, I will answer him; whoever asks of Me, I will give him; whoever seeks My forgiveness, I will forgive him.' And this continues until dawn breaks."""
"1918","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty gives respite until, when the last third of the night remains, He descends to the lowest heaven and calls out: 'Is there anyone seeking forgiveness? Is there anyone repenting? Is there anyone asking? Is there anyone supplicating?' (This calling continues in this way) until dawn breaks."""
"1919","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty sends down help in proportion to one's expenses and needs, and sends down patience in proportion to one's trial and affliction."""
"1920","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty creates the clouds, and they speak in the best manner (that is, they thunder) and laugh in the best manner (that is, lightning flashes in them)."""
"1921","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty forbids you from approaching women in their back passages (anus)."""
"1922","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty forbids you from swearing by your forefathers."""
"1923","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty forbids you from swearing by your forefathers; so whoever must swear, let him swear by Allah, or else remain silent."""
"1924","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty enjoins you to treat your mothers well (he said this three times); indeed, Allah Almighty enjoins you to treat your fathers well (he said this twice); indeed, Allah Almighty enjoins you to treat well your closest relatives, and then those who are next closest after them."""
"1925","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, water is purifying; nothing makes it impure."""
"1926","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, water does not take on major ritual impurity (janabah), and nothing makes it impure."""
"1927","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, water does not become affected by janabah (that is, it does not become impure through use by a person in a state of major ritual impurity)."""
"1928","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, nothing makes water impure."""
"1929","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the muezzin is forgiven his sins as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing that hears his voice testifies to his truth; and the one who is present with him (that is, who attends the prayer with him) has the reward of twenty-five degrees."""
"1930","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when the believer is placed in his grave, an angel comes to him and says to him: 'Whom did you worship?' If Allah has guided him, he says: 'I used to worship Allah.' Then the angel asks him: 'What did you used to say about this man (that is, Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him))?' He says: 'He is the servant of Allah and His Messenger.' So he is not asked about anything besides this. Then he is taken to a house that was in the Fire, and it is said to him: 'This was your abode in Hell, but Allah protected you and had mercy on you, so He has exchanged it for you with a house in Paradise.' He says: 'Let me go so that I may give this glad tidings to my family.' It is said to him: 'Stay here in peace.' And indeed, when the disbeliever is placed in his grave, an angel comes to him, rebukes him and asks: 'Whom did you worship?' He says: 'I do not know.' It is said to him: 'You neither knew yourself nor followed those who read.' Then he is asked: 'What did you used to say about this man?' He says: 'I used to say what the people said.' So the angel strikes him between his two ears with an iron hammer, and he lets out a scream that all creatures hear except jinn and mankind."""
"1931","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the soul of the believer departs from between his sides while he is praising Allah Almighty."""
"1932","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the believer, through his good character, attains the rank of one who fasts continually and stands in prayer all night."""
"1933","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the believer does not become impure."""
"1934","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the believer strives (performs jihad) with his sword and with his tongue (both)."""
"1935","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, hardships (trials) are made severe upon the believers because no calamity befalls a believer, whether the prick of a thorn or anything greater, nor any pain, except that Allah Almighty raises him a degree by it and removes a sin from him."""
"1936","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the buyer and the seller both have the option in their transaction as long as they have not separated from each other, or unless the sale itself was made with a stipulated option."""
"1937","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those who love one another for the sake of Allah will be (on the Day of Resurrection) in the shade of the Throne."""
"1938","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the women who seek khul' and who demand divorce (without a valid Shari'ah reason) are the hypocrites."""
"1939","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a woman comes forward, she comes in the form of a devil; so when one of you sees a woman and she attracts him, let him go to his wife, for what that (other) woman has, his wife has the same."""
"1940","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a woman comes forward in the form of a devil, and when she turns away she is also in the form of a devil; so when one of you sees a woman and she attracts him, let him go to his wife, for this will repel what is in his heart."""
"1941","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a woman is married for her religion, her wealth and her beauty; so hold fast to the religious woman, may your hands be covered in dust (that is, may good befall you)."""
"1942","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, woman was created from a rib; if you set about straightening her, you will break her, and if you leave her as she is, there will remain a crookedness in her, and with that you will get by."""
"1943","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, woman was created from a rib; she will never be straight for you in one way. So if you wish to benefit from her, you may benefit from her with that crookedness; and if you set about straightening her, you will break her, and breaking her is divorcing her."""
"1944","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, woman was created from a rib, and if you try to straighten the rib you will break it; so treat her with gentleness and wisdom, and you will live happily with her."""
"1945","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a woman too may grant protection on behalf of the people."" That is, she may grant protection on behalf of the Muslims."
"1946","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the return is to Allah alone, to Paradise or to Hell, where there is eternal abiding without death and residence without departure."""
"1947","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, begging (asking people) is a wound with which a man wounds his own face, except when a man asks a ruler (authority), or asks in a matter for which there is no alternative."""
"1948","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a Muslim visits his sick Muslim brother, he remains in the gardens of Paradise until he returns."""
"1949","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Muslim who keeps to the right path attains, through his good character and noble disposition, the rank of one who fasts often and stands at night (in prayer) with the verses of Allah."""
"1950","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a Muslim is rewarded for everything he spends, except for what he puts into this dust (i.e. unnecessary construction)."""
"1951","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one praying is in intimate conversation (whispering) with his Lord, so let him consider what he is saying to Him in that conversation; and do not raise your voices over one another in reciting the Qur'an."""
"1952","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, help comes to the servant from Allah Almighty in proportion to his expenses (and burden), and patience comes down from Allah in proportion to the affliction."""
"1953","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those who act justly will be, on the Day of Resurrection, with Allah Almighty upon pulpits of light at the right hand of the Most Merciful, and both of His hands are right hands. They are those who are just in their judgements, with their families, and in whatever they have been placed in charge of."""
"1954","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those who have much (wealth in this world) are the very ones who will have little (in reward) on the Day of Resurrection, except the one whom Allah Almighty has blessed with wealth and he spends it to his right, to his left, in front of him and behind him (in the way of Allah), and does good deeds with that wealth."""
"1955","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels descend into the clouds and mention the matter that has been decreed in the heavens; the devils then stealthily overhear it and cast it into the hearts of the soothsayers (fortune-tellers), and those soothsayers then relate it, mixing a hundred lies of their own into it."""
"1956","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels, pleased with what the seeker of knowledge does, spread their wings for him."""
"1957","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels curse any one of you who points a piece of iron (i.e. a weapon or the like) at his brother, even if he is his full brother."""
"1958","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on Friday the angels stand at the doors of the mosque with scrolls in which they keep recording the people who arrive in order, first, second and third, until, when the imam comes out (for the sermon), the scrolls are rolled up."""
"1959","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels do not come near a person in a state of major ritual impurity, nor one smeared with khaluq (a perfume mixed with saffron), until they take a ritual bath (ghusl)."""
"1960","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever with any good, nor do they come near one smeared with saffron or a person in a state of major ritual impurity."""
"1961","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels do not enter a house in which there are statues or a picture of a living being."""
"1962","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels (of mercy) do not enter a house in which there is a dog."""
"1963","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels (of mercy) do not enter a house in which there is a dog, nor a house in which there is a picture."""
"1964","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one who spends on horses in the way of Allah (for jihad) is like a person who has stretched out his hands to give charity and does not close them."""
"1965","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the dead are punished in their graves, to the extent that even the animals hear their (screaming) voices."""
"1966","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, death is something of great terror, so when you see a funeral procession, stand up."""
"1967","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when the deceased is buried, he hears the sound of the footsteps of the (departing) people as they turn their backs on him and go away."""
"1968","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the angels come to the dying person. If he is a righteous man, (the angel) says: 'O pure soul that was in a pure body! Come out; come out praiseworthy, and receive the glad tidings of rest, fragrant flowers (or provision), and a Lord who is not angry with you.' This continues to be said to it until it comes out; then it is taken up to the heaven. The gate is asked to be opened for it, and it is asked: 'Who is this?' The angel says: 'It is so-and-so.' It is said: 'Welcome to the pure soul that was in a pure body! Enter praiseworthy, and receive the glad tidings of rest and ease, pure provision, and a Lord who is not displeased.' This continues to be said to it until it is brought to the heaven in which Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, is. And if he is an evil man, the angel says: 'O foul soul that was in a foul body! Come out; come out in disgrace, and receive the tidings of boiling water, pus, and ""other (punishments) of its kind"" [Surah Sad: 58].' This continues to be said to it until it comes out; then it is taken up towards the heaven. The gate is asked to be opened for it, and it is asked: 'Who is this?' It is said: 'It is so-and-so.' Then it is said: 'No welcome to the foul soul that was in a foul body! Go back in disgrace, for the gates of heaven will not be opened for you.' So it is cast down from the heaven, and then it comes to the grave. Then the righteous man is made to sit up in his grave, neither alarmed nor terrified. Then he is asked: 'What religion were you on?' He says: 'I was upon Islam.' He is asked: 'Who is this man (Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him)?' He says: 'He is Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He came to us with clear proofs from Allah, and we believed him.' He is asked: 'Have you seen Allah?' He says: 'It is not fitting for any human being to see Allah.' Then a window is opened for him towards Hell, and he sees it, one part of it smashing (devouring) another. He is told: 'Look at that from which Allah Almighty has saved you.' Then a window is opened for him towards Paradise, and he sees its splendour and its blessings. He is told: 'This is your abode.' And he is further told: 'You were (in the world) upon certainty, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised again, if Allah wills.' And the evil man is made to sit up in his grave, extremely alarmed and terrified. He is asked: 'What religion were you on?' He says: 'I do not know.' He is asked: 'Who is this man?' He says: 'I heard the people saying something, so I said it too!' Then a window is opened for him towards Paradise, and he sees its splendour and its blessings, and he is told: 'Look at what Allah has turned away from you (i.e. deprived you of).' Then a window is opened for him towards Hell, and he sees it, one part of it crushing another, and he is told: 'This is your abode. You were upon doubt, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised, if Allah wills.'"""
"1969","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the deceased is punished because of the weeping of the living (i.e. their wailing and lamentation)."""
"1970","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the deceased is punished because of his family's weeping (wailing) over him."""
"1971","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the deceased will be raised in the very clothes (i.e. the shroud or the martyr's garments) in which he dies."""
"1972","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Fire (of Hell) was brought so near to me that I blew to push its heat away from my face, and I saw in it (being punished) the man with the crooked staff, the man who slit the ear of the bahirah (she-camel, in the name of idols), the man of Himyar, and the woman of the cat."""
"1973","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when people see a wrongdoer (committing wrong) and do not seize his hand (i.e. do not stop him from wrongdoing), Allah Almighty is about to send down His punishment upon them all."""
"1974","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when people see evil and do not change it (i.e. do not stop it), Allah Almighty is about to envelop them in His punishment."""
"1975","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the people have prayed and gone to sleep, and as long as you remain waiting for the prayer, you will continue to be counted as being in prayer."""
"1976","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the people have prayed and gone to sleep, while you remain in prayer as long as you are waiting for the prayer. Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the sickness of the sick, I would have ordered that this (Isha) prayer be delayed until half the night."""
"1977","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, people have not been given anything better than good character."""
"1978","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection people will be fallen on their knees; every nation will follow its prophet, saying: 'O so-and-so, intercede! O so-and-so, intercede!' until the matter of intercession reaches Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). That will be the day on which Allah Almighty will raise him (peace and blessings be upon him) to the Praised Station (al-Maqam al-Mahmud)."""
"1979","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, people will migrate to you, and you will not migrate to them. By the One in whose hand is my soul! No man loves the Ansar until he meets Allah except that he will meet Allah while Allah loves him, and no man hates the Ansar until he meets Allah except that he will meet Allah while Allah is displeased with him."""
"1980","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, making a vow neither brings anything forward nor puts it back (i.e. it cannot change destiny); it is only a means by which something (of wealth) is extracted from the miser."""
"1981","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a vow does not bring near to the son of Adam anything that Allah Almighty has not decreed for him; rather, the vow coincides with the decree, and through it something comes out of the miser that the miser did not want to give out."""
"1982","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, vows are of two kinds: the vow made for Allah, its expiation is to fulfil it; and the vow made for Satan (i.e. for a sin) may not be fulfilled, and the expiation of an oath is binding upon him."""
"1983","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, women are the counterparts (and likes) of men."""
"1984","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the drop of fluid remains in the womb for forty days; then the angel who is appointed over its creation descends upon it and says: 'O my Lord, will it be male or female?' So Allah makes it male or female. Then he says: 'O my Lord, will it be sound or defective?' So Allah makes it complete or defective. Then he asks: 'O my Lord, how much is its provision? How long is its lifespan? What will its character be like?' Then Allah records it as wretched or blessed."""
"1985","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the soul whose creation has been decreed will certainly come into being."""
"1986","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, plundered property is no more lawful than carrion (i.e. it is forbidden just like carrion)."""
"1987","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, plunder is not lawful."""
"1988","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, al-Wasilah is a rank with Allah Almighty above which there is no rank, so ask Allah Almighty to grant it to me, above all creation, on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1989","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, children are a cause of miserliness and cowardice."""
"1990","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, children are a cause of making a person miserly, cowardly, ignorant and sorrowful."""
"1991","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, migration (hijrah) will not come to an end as long as jihad continues."""
"1992","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, good conduct and a good manner are one part of the seventy parts of prophethood."""
"1993","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, good conduct, a good manner and moderation (balance) are one part of the twenty-five parts of prophethood."""
"1994","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the two hands prostrate just as the face prostrates, so when one of you places his face (on the ground), let him place his hands as well, and when he raises his face, let him raise them too."""
"1995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, today is the day of Ashura. So whoever has eaten something should not eat anything for the rest of the day, and whoever has not eaten or drunk anything should complete the fast."""
"1996","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when one of the Jews greets you, he actually says 'As-samu 'alaykum' (death be upon you), so (in reply) say only 'Wa 'alaykum' (and upon you too)."""
"1997","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Jews envy you for the greeting of salam and for saying Amin."""
"1998","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Jews and the Christians do not dye (their hair), so be different from them (that is, apply dye)."""
"1999","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, ahead of you there is a Pond whose extent is like the distance between Jarba' and Adhruh (two places). In it are cups as numerous as the stars of the sky. Whoever comes to it and drinks from it will never be thirsty after that."""
"2000","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, ahead of you there is a Pond; the distance between its two sides is like the distance between Jarba' and Adhruh."""
"2001","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, ahead of you there is a hard and difficult mountain pass which the heavily burdened (with sins and worldliness) will not be able to cross."""
"2002","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your affair after me is among the things that worry me, and none will be patient and kind toward you after me except those who are patient. (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to his pure wives.)"""
"2003","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the affair of this Ummah will remain sound and close to the truth as long as they do not engage in (needless) debate about children (of the polytheists) and about divine decree."""
"2004","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a nation of the Children of Israel was transformed into creatures of the earth, and I do not know which creatures they are."""
"2005","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection the people of my Ummah will be called while their faces, hands and feet are shining from the traces of ablution (wudu)."""
"2006","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Umm Mildam (fever) removes the filth of the sins of the son of Adam just as the bellows removes the dross of iron."""
"2007","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among all people the one who has done me the greatest favour with his wealth and his companionship is Abu Bakr. If I were to take anyone (other than Allah) as a khalil (intimate friend), I would take Abu Bakr as a khalil, but the brotherhood of Islam (suffices). Let all the small doors opening into the mosque be closed except the small door of Abu Bakr."""
"2008","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some people of my Ummah will come after me, each of whom will wish that he could see me at the cost of his family and his wealth."""
"2009","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the firmest handhold of Islam is that you love for the sake of Allah and hate for the sake of Allah."""
"2010","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those are the people who, when a righteous man among them died, would build a place of worship (masjid) over his grave and make images of him in it. These people will be the worst of creation in the sight of Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2011","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the closest of people to Allah Almighty is the one who is first to greet them with salam."""
"2012","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the closest of people to me are the pious, God-fearing ones, whoever they may be and wherever they may be."""
"2013","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first of the (major) signs (of the Hour) to appear will be the rising of the sun from the west and the emergence of the Beast of the Earth (Dabbat al-Ard, a creature of strange form) upon the people in the forenoon. Whichever of the two appears first, the other will appear immediately after it."""
"2014","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first person to be judged on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who was martyred. He will be brought, and Allah Almighty will remind him of His blessings, and he will recognise them. Allah will say: 'What did you do with these (in gratitude)?' He will say: 'I fought in Your cause until I was martyred.' Allah will say: 'You have lied. Rather, you fought so that it would be said that you are brave, and so it was said.' Then the command will be given concerning him, and he will be dragged on his face until he is thrown into Hell. The second will be a man who acquired knowledge, taught it to others and recited the Qur'an. He will be brought, and Allah will remind him of His blessings, and he will recognise them. Allah will say: 'What did you do with them?' He will say: 'I acquired knowledge, taught it, and recited the Qur'an for Your pleasure.' Allah will say: 'You have lied. Rather, you acquired knowledge so that it would be said that you are a scholar, and you recited the Qur'an so that it would be said that you are a reciter, and so it was said.' Then the command will be given concerning him, and he will be dragged on his face until he is thrown into Hell. The third will be a man whom Allah gave abundance and granted every kind of wealth. He will be brought, and Allah will remind him of His blessings, and he will recognise them. Allah will say: 'What did you do with them?' He will say: 'I did not leave any path in which You love that wealth be spent without spending in it for Your sake.' Allah will say: 'You are lying. Rather, you spent so that it would be said that you are generous, and so it has been said.' Then the command will be given concerning him, and he will be dragged on his face and thrown into Hell."""
"2015","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the faces of the first group to enter Paradise will shine like the moon on the night of the full moon; then those who come after them will be like the most brilliantly shining star in the sky. They will not urinate, nor defecate, nor spit, nor will mucus run from their noses. Their combs will be of gold, their sweat will be the fragrance of musk, the fuel of their censers will be aloeswood (a fragrant wood), and their wives will be the wide-eyed houris. Their characters will all be like the character of a single man, and they will all be in the form of their father Adam (peace be upon him), sixty cubits tall toward the sky."""
"2016","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first thing Allah Almighty created was the Pen. Then He commanded it, and it wrote everything that is to be (until the Day of Resurrection)."""
"2017","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first thing Allah Almighty created was the Pen, and He said to it: 'Write.' It said: 'What shall I write?' Allah Almighty said: 'Write the decree: what has been and what is to be forever.'"""
"2018","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first thing Allah Almighty created was the Pen. Then He said to it: 'Write.' It said: 'O my Lord, what shall I write?' Allah Almighty said: 'Write the decrees of everything until the Hour is established.' So whoever dies upon a belief other than this has nothing to do with me."""
"2019","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first thing we begin with on this day of ours (the day of Eid al-Adha) is that we first offer the prayer, then return and offer the sacrifice. Whoever does that has attained our Sunnah, and whoever slaughters before that (prayer), it is merely meat which he has prepared early for his family; it has nothing to do with the rites of sacrifice."""
"2020","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first of a servant's deeds for which he will be held to account on the Day of Resurrection is the prayer. If it proves sound, he has succeeded and prospered; and if it proves corrupt, he has failed and lost. If anything is lacking in his obligatory prayers, the Lord will say: 'Look, does My servant have any voluntary prayer?' Then the deficiency in the obligatory prayers will be made up by means of those voluntary prayers, and then all the rest of his deeds will be reckoned in the same way."""
"2021","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first cases to be judged between the servants (on the Day of Resurrection) will be those of blood (that is, unjust killing)."""
"2022","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first question the servant will be asked about blessings on the Day of Resurrection is that it will be said to him: 'Did We not keep your body healthy, and did We not quench your thirst with cool water?'"""
"2023","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first act of worship on this day of ours is offering the (Eid) prayer."""
"2024","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first person to start the custom of setting animals loose in the name of idols, and to worship idols, was Amr bin Amir, the forefather of Banu Khuza'ah, and indeed I saw him in the Fire dragging his intestines."""
"2025","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the people of the Days of Ignorance used to say that the sun and the moon are eclipsed only because of the death of some great person among the people of the earth, whereas the sun and the moon are not eclipsed because of anyone's death or life; rather, they are two creations among the creations of Allah. Allah brings about in His creation whatever He wills. So whenever either of them is eclipsed, pray until the eclipse clears or Allah Almighty brings about some new matter."""
"2026","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the people of Paradise will see the people of the lofty chambers of Paradise (above them) just as you see the stars in the sky."""
"2027","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the people of Paradise will see those who live in the lofty chambers above them just as you see a brilliant distant star on the horizon in the east or the west; this will be because of the difference in ranks and excellence between them."""
"2028","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, for the people of Paradise the deeds of the people of Paradise are made easy, and indeed for the people of Hell the deeds of the people of Hell are made easy."""
"2029","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the people of Paradise will eat and drink in it, but they will not spit, nor urinate, nor relieve themselves, nor blow their noses. Rather, their food will be digested in the form of a belch and sweat like the fragrance of musk, and the glorification (tasbih) and praise (tahmid) of Allah will be inspired into their hearts just as you have been inspired to breathe effortlessly."""
"2030","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those of the high ranks will be seen by those below them just as you see a shining star on the horizon of the sky, and indeed Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent they are!"""
"2031","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, those who do good and kindness in this world are the ones who will receive good in the Hereafter, and those who do evil in this world are the ones who will receive evil in the Hereafter."""
"2032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the people of Hell will weep so much that if ships were sailed in their tears, they would sail; and indeed they will weep blood instead of tears."""
"2033","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one with the lightest punishment among the people of Hell will be the person who is made to wear two sandals and two straps of fire, from whose heat his brain will boil as a cooking pot boils. He will think that no one is being punished more severely than him, whereas he will be the one with the lightest punishment among the people of Hell."""
"2034","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection the one with the lightest punishment among the people of Hell will be a man who is made to wear two sandals of fire, from whose heat his brain will be boiling on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2035","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection the one with the lightest punishment among the people of Hell will be the man under the soles of whose feet two embers of fire will be placed, from which his brain will boil as a cooking pot boils in a copper vessel."""
"2036","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in Madinah there are some people who, whatever journey you made, whatever you spent, and whatever valley you crossed, were with you in it (in terms of reward), even though they are in Madinah; in fact, a legitimate excuse held them back."""
"2037","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in Madinah there are some jinn who have accepted Islam. So if you see any of them (the snakes living in houses), warn it for three days (to leave). Then if it appears to you after that, kill it, for it is a devil."""
"2038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, killing (that is, attaining martyrdom in the cause of Allah) is sufficient for you."""
"2039","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, after me there will be people in my Ummah who will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game, and then they will never return to it. They are the worst of all creation."""
"2040","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Bilal gives the adhan at night (for tahajjud), so keep eating and drinking until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the adhan."""
"2041","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Bilal gives the adhan at night in order to wake those of you who are asleep and to send back those of you who are standing in prayer (tahajjud) (for the pre-dawn meal)."""
"2042","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Children of Israel split into seventy-one (71) sects, and indeed my Ummah will soon split into seventy-two (72) sects. All of them will be in the Fire except one, and that is al-Jama'ah (that is, the group that holds firm to the Sunnah)."""
"2043","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, (such was the state of) the Children of Israel that when urine got on (the clothes or body of) any one of them, he would cut that part off with scissors. So when any one of you intends to urinate, let him look for a (soft) place for his urine."""
"2044","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Children of Israel wrote a book (of their own), then began to follow it and abandoned the Torah."""
"2045","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when the Children of Israel fell into ruin, they had begun (abandoning knowledge and action and merely) telling stories."""
"2046","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Banu Hisham bin al-Mughirah have asked my permission to marry their daughter to Ali bin Abi Talib, but I will never permit it, I will never permit it, I will never permit it, unless Ibn Abi Talib wishes to divorce my daughter and marry their daughter. For she (Fatimah) is a part of me; whatever displeases her displeases me, and whatever hurts her hurts me."""
"2047","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, before the Hour there will be al-Harj, that is, widespread killing. It will not be the killing of the disbelievers, but rather the Ummah killing one another, to the extent that a man will meet his brother and kill him. The minds of the people of that time will be taken away, and in their place will remain foolish and worthless people, most of whom will think that they are on a right path, whereas they will not be on anything true."""
"2048","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, before the Hour there will be thirty great liars (dajjals)."""
"2049","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, before the Hour there will be trials (fitan) like pieces of the dark night. In them a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever by evening, and a believer in the evening and a disbeliever by morning. In these trials the one sitting will be better than the one standing, the one standing will be better than the one walking, and the one walking will be better than the one running. So (in the time of these trials) break your bows, cut their strings and strike your swords against stones (to blunt them). Then if an attacker enters the house of any one of you, let him be like the better of the two sons of Adam (Habil) (that is, let him be killed rather than kill)."""
"2050","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, before the Hour many great liars (extreme liars) will appear, so beware of them."""
"2051","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, before the Hour there will be days in which ignorance will descend, knowledge will be taken away, and al-harj will become widespread in them; and al-harj means killing and bloodshed."""
"2052","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There were three men among the Children of Israel: one a leper, the second bald and the third blind. Allah Almighty willed to test them, so He sent an angel to them. The angel came to the leper and asked: 'What thing do you love most?' He said: 'A good colour and good skin, for people are repulsed by me.' The angel passed his hand over him, and his illness went away, and he was given a beautiful colour and good skin. The angel asked: 'What wealth do you love most?' He said: 'Camels.' So he was given a she-camel ten months pregnant, and the angel said: 'May Allah Almighty bless you in it.' Then the angel came to the bald man and asked: 'What thing do you love most?' He said: 'Beautiful hair, and that this defect of mine be removed, for people are repelled by me.' The angel passed his hand over him, his baldness went away, and he was given beautiful hair. The angel asked: 'What wealth do you love most?' He said: 'Cows.' So he was given a pregnant cow, and the angel said: 'May Allah Almighty bless you in it.' Then the angel came to the blind man and asked: 'What thing do you love most?' He said: 'That Allah Almighty restore my sight to me so that I may see people.' The angel passed his hand over him, and Allah Almighty restored his sight. The angel asked: 'What wealth do you love most?' He said: 'Goats.' So he was given a goat that bore young. Then these two (the she-camel and the cow) produced offspring, and this one (the goat) also gave birth, until one of them had a valley full of camels, the second a valley full of cows and the third a valley full of goats. Then the angel came to the leper in that same form and appearance (of a leper) and said: 'I am a poor man; all my means have been cut off during my journey, and today there is no way for me to reach my destination except with the help of Allah and then with your support. I ask you, by the One who gave you a good colour, beautiful skin and wealth, for a camel so that I may complete my journey.' He replied: 'I have many other obligations.' The angel said to him: 'It is as though I recognise you. Were you not a leper whom people found repulsive? You were poor, and then Allah gave you wealth?' He said: 'This wealth I inherited from my forefathers.' The angel said: 'If you are lying, may Allah return you to the state you were in before.' Then the angel came to the bald man in that same form and appearance (of a bald man) and said to him the same as he had said to the leper, and he too gave the same reply the leper had given. The angel said: 'If you are lying, may Allah return you to the state you were in before.' Then the angel came to the blind man in that same form and appearance (of a blind man) and said: 'I am a poor man and a traveller; all my means have been cut off on my journey, and today there is no way for me to reach my destination except with the help of Allah and then with your support. I ask you, by the One who restored your sight, for a goat so that I may complete my journey.' The blind man said: 'I was indeed blind and Allah restored my sight, and I was poor and He made me rich. Take whatever you wish. By Allah! Whatever you take today for the sake of Allah, I will never hold you back.' The angel said: 'Keep your wealth. You were only being tested. Indeed, Allah is pleased with you and is displeased with your two companions.'"""
"2053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Jibril came to me at the time you saw. He called me and hid it from you, and I answered him and hid it from you. He could not come in to you because you had taken off your clothes, and I thought you had fallen asleep, so I did not like to wake you, and I also feared that you would feel lonely (at my leaving). Then he (Jibril) said: 'Indeed, your Lord commands you to go to the people of al-Baqi' and seek forgiveness for them.'"""
"2054","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Jibril used to review the Qur'an with me once every year, but this year he has reviewed it with me twice, and I can only think that my appointed time (of passing) has come near. And indeed, you will be the first of my household to join me, so fear Allah and be patient, for what an excellent forerunner I am for you."""
"2055","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Jibril dug Zamzam with his heel, the mother of Isma'il (Hajar) began gathering the earth and sand to contain it. May Allah have mercy on Hajar! Had she left it as it was (without containing it), the spring of Zamzam would have become a flowing spring."""
"2056","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, honouring old ties and keeping faith with them is part of faith."""
"2057","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is an established way of Allah Almighty that whatever thing of this world He raises high, He eventually brings it low."""
"2058","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, my Pond (in its breadth) is longer than the distance from Aylah to Aden. It is whiter than snow and sweeter than honey in milk, and its vessels are more numerous than the stars of the sky. And indeed, I will drive people away from it just as a man drives other people's camels away from his own trough."" The Companions said: ""Will you recognise us on that day?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes! You will have a mark that no other nation will have: you will come to me with radiant white foreheads, hands and feet from the traces of ablution."""
"2059","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, my Pond is wider than the distance from Aylah to Aden. By the One in whose hand is my soul! Its vessels are more numerous than the stars of the sky, it is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. By the One in whose hand is my soul! I will drive (others) away from it just as a man drives stray camels away from his trough."" The Companions said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will you recognise us?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Yes! You will come to me at the Pond with radiant white foreheads, hands and feet from the traces of ablution, and this distinction will belong to no one besides you."""
"2060","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, my Pond extends from Aden to Amman of al-Balqa'. Its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, and its drinking cups are as many as the stars. Whoever drinks a single draught from it will never feel thirst after it. The first people to come to it will be the poor among the Muhajirun: those with dishevelled hair and soiled clothes, whom well-off, wealthy women do not marry and for whom the great doors are not opened; those who fulfil the obligations owed by them but are not given what is owed to them."""
"2061","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Your menstruation is not in your hand (that is, in this state the hands do not become impure for cooking or taking part in other matters)."
"2062","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best of Allah's servants are those who fulfil their promises and are pure."""
"2063","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best of you are those who are best in repaying (that is, who settle debts or dues handsomely)."""
"2064","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best of the Tabi'in is a man who will be called Uways. He has a mother to whom he is very dutiful. If he were to swear an oath by Allah, Allah would surely fulfil it. He has a mark of whiteness (leprosy) on his body. So tell him to seek forgiveness for you."""
"2065","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best perfume for men is that whose fragrance is apparent and whose colour is hidden, and the best perfume for women is that whose colour is apparent and whose fragrance is hidden."""
"2066","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best of the days on which you have cupping done are the 17th, 19th and 21st of the month."""
"2067","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Prophet of Allah Dawud (peace be upon him) used to eat only from the earnings (labour) of his own hands."""
"2068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your blood and your wealth are sacred to one another, just like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this city of yours. Beware! Every matter of the Jahiliyyah has been trampled beneath my feet, and all the blood-claims of the Jahiliyyah have been remitted, and the first blood-claim I remit is that of our own family, the blood of Rabi'ah bin al-Harith bin Abd al-Muttalib. And the usury (riba) of the Jahiliyyah has been abolished, and the first usury I abolish is that of our own family, the usury of al-Abbas bin Abd al-Muttalib; it is all remitted. So fear Allah concerning women! For you have taken them with the trust of Allah and made their private parts lawful by the word of Allah. And your right over them is that they do not allow anyone whom you dislike onto your beds; if they do so, then strike them, but in a way that is not severe or harmful. And their right over you is that you provide them with food and clothing according to what is customary. And I have left among you something which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah (the Qur'an). And you will be asked about me, so what will you say?"" The Companions said: ""We bear witness that you have conveyed (the religion), fulfilled (the trust) and given sincere counsel."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah, bear witness."""
"2069","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your Lord marvels at His servant when he says: 'My Lord, forgive me my sins,' while he knows that none forgives sins except Me."""
"2070","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, your Lord is Modest and Generous. He is too modest, when a servant raises his hands to Him, to return them empty (disappointed)."""
"2071","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, my Lord sent word to me: 'Recite the Qur'an in one harf (mode).' I replied to Him: 'Make it easy for my Ummah!' Then Allah sent word to me again: 'Recite it in two ahruf.' I replied again: 'Make it easy for my Ummah!' Then Allah sent word to me (a third time): 'Recite it in seven ahruf, and for each reply you have a request (a promise of acceptance) which you may ask of Me.' I said: 'O Allah, forgive my Ummah! O Allah, forgive my Ummah!' And I have kept back the third for a day on which all of creation, even Ibrahim (peace be upon him), will turn to me."""
"2072","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there are some men among the Arabs, one of whom gives me a gift, and I recompense him for it according to what I have, then he is displeased with it and keeps being angry with me over it. By Allah! After this stand of mine, I will not accept a gift from any man among the Arabs except from a man of Quraysh, of the Ansar, of Thaqif or of Daws."""
"2073","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some men deal with the wealth of Allah without right (use it unjustly); for them is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2074","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, death came to a man, and when he despaired of life he instructed his family: 'When I die, gather a great deal of firewood for me, then light a fire in it, until, when it has eaten my flesh, reached my bones and burnt them, take them and grind them, then watch for a windy day and scatter them into the sea.' They did as he had commanded them. Then Allah gathered his particles and asked him: 'Why did you do that?' He said: 'Out of fear of You!' So Allah forgave him."""
"2075","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man said: 'By Allah! Allah will never forgive so-and-so.' So Allah Almighty said: 'Who is it that swears by Me that I will not forgive so-and-so?! I have indeed forgiven so-and-so and have nullified your (acts of worship) deeds.'"""
"2076","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man killed ninety-nine people, then the thought of repentance came to him, so he asked about the most knowledgeable person on earth, and he was directed to a monk. He came to him and said that he had killed ninety-nine people; was there any repentance for him? He said: 'No!' So he killed him as well, completing a hundred. Then he asked about the most knowledgeable person on earth, and he was directed to a scholar. He said that he had killed a hundred people; was there any repentance for him? He said: 'Yes! And who can come between him and repentance? Go to such-and-such a land, for there are people there who worship Allah; worship Allah with them and do not return to your land, for it is an evil land.' So he set off, until, when he had reached halfway, death came to him. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed over him. The angels of mercy said: 'He came repenting, turning with his heart towards Allah Almighty.' And the angels of punishment said: 'He never did any good.' Then an angel came to them in human form, and they made him judge between them. He said: 'Measure between the two lands; whichever of them he is closer to, he belongs to it.' They measured and found him closer to the land he had intended, so the angels of mercy took his soul."""
"2077","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there was a man before you to whom Allah had given abundant wealth. When his death approached, he said to his sons: 'What kind of father have I been to you?' They said: 'You were the best of fathers.' He said: 'I have never done any good deed, so when I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter me on a stormy day.' They did so. Then Allah gathered him and asked: 'What drove you to this?' He said: 'Fear of You!' So Allah received him with His mercy."""
"2078","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man had never done any good deed except that he used to lend to people, and he would say to his agent (servant): 'Take what is easy, leave what is difficult, and overlook; perhaps Allah will overlook our faults.' When he died, Allah Almighty said: 'Did you ever do any good deed?' He said: 'No, except that I had a servant, and I used to lend to people; when I sent him to collect, I would say to him: Take what is easy, leave what is difficult, and overlook; perhaps Allah will overlook our faults too.' So Allah Almighty said: 'I have overlooked your faults.'"""
"2079","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the Angel of Death came to a man from among those before you to take his soul, and said to him: 'Have you done any good?' He said: 'I do not recall anything like that.' He was told: 'Think carefully.' He said: 'I cannot think of any good deed, except that I used to trade and do business with people, and I would give respite to the one in hardship and forgive (or be lenient with) the well-off.' So Allah admitted him into Paradise."""
"2080","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man from the people of Paradise asked his Lord for permission to farm. Allah said: 'Are you not in whatever you wish?' He said: 'Of course! But I love to farm.' So he sowed seed, and in the blink of an eye it sprouted, stood upright and became ready for harvest, and it became like mountains. Then Allah said: 'Take it, O son of Adam! For nothing satisfies you.'"""
"2081","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man from the Children of Israel asked another man from the Children of Israel to lend him a thousand dinars. He said: 'Bring me witnesses so that I may call them to witness.' He said: 'Allah is sufficient as a Witness.' He said: 'Then bring me a guarantor.' He said: 'Allah is sufficient as a Guardian.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth,' and he gave it to him for a fixed term. The man went out on a sea journey and fulfilled his need, then he looked for a ship to board so that he could return by the term that had been fixed, but he found no ship. So he took a piece of wood, hollowed it out, placed in it a thousand dinars and a letter to his companion, then sealed up the opening, then brought it to the sea and said: 'O Allah! You know that I borrowed a thousand dinars from so-and-so. He asked me for a guarantor and I said: Allah is sufficient as a Guardian, and he was content with You. He asked me for a witness and I said: Allah is sufficient as a Witness, and he was content with You. I have tried hard to find a ship by which to send him what is his, but I have found none, and now I entrust it to You.' Then he threw it into the sea until it went into it. Then he went back, while still looking for a ship to take him to his town. Meanwhile the man who had lent to him went out to see whether some ship had come with his money, and he found the very piece of wood that contained the money. He took it as firewood for his family. When he sawed it open, he found the money and the letter. Then the one who had borrowed arrived, bringing a thousand dinars, and said: 'By Allah! I kept trying hard to find a ship so that I could bring you your money, but I found no ship before the one in which I have come.' He said: 'Did you send me anything?' He said: 'I am telling you that I found no ship before the one in which I came.' He said: 'Indeed, Allah Almighty has delivered on your behalf what you sent in the piece of wood, so go back with your thousand dinars, rightly guided.'"""
"2082","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the nations before you there was a man who developed an ulcer. When it caused him severe pain, he drew an arrow from his quiver and lanced it. Then his blood did not stop until he died. So Allah Almighty said: 'My servant hastened to Me with his own life; therefore I have made Paradise forbidden to him.'"""
"2083","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man called Uways will come to you from Yemen. He will leave no one behind in Yemen except his mother. He had leprosy (white patches), so he supplicated to Allah Almighty and Allah removed the illness from him, except for a spot the size of a dirham. So whoever among you meets him, let him ask him (Uways) to seek forgiveness from Allah for you."""
"2084","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Ruh al-Qudus (that is, Jibril (peace be upon him)) is with you as long as you answer their (the polytheists') satire (with your poetry)."""
"2085","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Ruh al-Qudus (that is, Jibril (peace be upon him)) has put into my heart that no soul will die until it completes its appointed term and receives its provision in full. So fear Allah and be moderate in seeking provision. And let not delay in provision ever drive any of you to seek it through disobedience to Allah, for what is with Allah Almighty can only be attained through obedience to Him."""
"2086","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Ruh al-Qudus (that is, Jibril (peace be upon him)) will continue to support you as long as you defend Allah and His Messenger."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to Sayyiduna Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2087","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Zahir is our desert (friend) and we are his town (friends)."""
"2088","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who gives water to the people drinks last of all."""
"2089","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Subhan Allah, wal-hamdu lillah, wa la ilaha illallah, wallahu akbar (Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest) shake off sins just as a tree sheds its leaves."""
"2090","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when Sulayman bin Dawud (peace be upon them both) built Bayt al-Maqdis, he asked Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for three things: he asked Allah for the ability to judge in a way that accords with His (Allah's) judgement, and he was granted it. And he asked Allah for a kingdom such as would befit no one after him, and he was granted that too. And he asked Allah, when he finished building the mosque, that whoever comes to this mosque with no purpose other than to pray in it, Allah would cleanse him of his sins as on the day his mother bore him. The first two were granted to him, and I hope that the third was also granted to him."""
"2091","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A surah of the Qur'an, which has thirty verses, interceded for a man until he was forgiven, and it is: Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion."" [Surah al-Mulk: 1]"
"2092","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a surah of the Book of Allah (the Qur'an), which has only thirty verses, interceded for a man, so it brought him out of Hell and admitted him into Paradise."""
"2093","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the travel (that is, going out in the land) of my Ummah is jihad in the path of Allah."""
"2094","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the worst shepherd is the one who crushes (his animals through cruelty)."" (That is, the ruler who oppresses and wrongs his subjects.)"
"2095","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the worst person in rank in the sight of Allah Almighty will be the one whom people left alone to protect themselves from his foul tongue (and evil)."""
"2096","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If that were so (that is, if only those who die on the battlefield were martyrs), then the martyrs of my Ummah would be very few! Being killed in the path of Allah is martyrdom, dying of the plague is martyrdom, the woman who dies while pregnant (or in childbirth) dies a martyr, and the death of one who dies by drowning, by burning, or from al-majnub (pleurisy) is also martyrdom."""
"2097","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angel on the left (who records sins) holds back the pen for six hours (or six periods) from the Muslim servant who has erred. Then if he regrets it and seeks Allah's forgiveness for that sin, he discards it (that is, does not record the sin); otherwise, one sin is recorded (in his record of deeds)."""
"2098","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's prayer in congregation is superior to his praying alone by twenty-five degrees."""
"2099","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the food of one person suffices for two, the food of two suffices for three and four, and the food of four suffices for five and six."""
"2100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's lengthening of his prayer and shortening of his sermon is a sign of his understanding (deep understanding of the religion). So lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon, and indeed some eloquence (and speech) has (the effect of) magic."""
"2101","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the day of Ashura (the tenth of Muharram) is one of the days of Allah Almighty. So whoever wishes may fast on it, and whoever wishes may leave it."""
"2102","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, most of the punishment of the grave is because of urine (not guarding against its splashes), so guard yourselves against it."""
"2103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a servant committed a sin and said: My Lord, I have sinned, so forgive it. His Lord said: Has My servant come to know that he has a Lord who forgives sin and also takes to account for it? I have forgiven My servant. Then he remained as long as Allah willed, then he committed another sin and said: My Lord, I have committed another sin, so forgive me. Allah said: Has My servant come to know that he has a Lord who forgives sin and also takes to account for it? I have forgiven My servant. Then he committed another sin and said: My Lord, I have committed another sin, so forgive it. Allah said: Has My servant come to know that he has a Lord who forgives sin and also takes to account for it? I have forgiven My servant; now let him do as he wishes."""
"2104","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Abdullah bin Qays (Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him)) has been given one of the melodious voices of the family of Dawud (peace be upon him)."""
"2105","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What a righteous man Abdullah is! If only he would pray (the tahajjud) prayer abundantly at night."""
"2106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Uthman is extremely modest and one who conceals (faults); even the angels feel shy before him."""
"2107","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Uthman is a modest man, and I feared that if I permitted him to enter while I was in that (informal) state, he would not (fully) convey his need to me."""
"2108","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the enemy of Allah, Iblis, came with a flame of fire to thrust it into my face. So I said three times: I seek refuge with Allah from you. Then I said three times: I curse you with the complete curse of Allah, but he did not retreat. Then I intended to seize him. By Allah! Were it not for the supplication of our brother Sulayman (peace be upon him), he would have woken up tied up, and the children of the people of Madinah would have played with him."""
"2109","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the punishment of this Ummah has been placed in this world."""
"2110","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the greatness of the reward goes with the greatness of the affliction (that is, the greater the trial, the greater the reward), and indeed when Allah Almighty loves a people, He tests them. So whoever is content, for him is (Allah's) pleasure, and whoever is displeased, for him is (Allah's) displeasure."""
"2111","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Last night a rebellious one from among the jinn suddenly attacked me in order to break my prayer, but Allah Almighty gave me power over him and I choked him. I intended to tie him to one of the pillars of the mosque so that in the morning all of you could see him. But then I remembered this supplication of my brother Sulayman (peace be upon him): 'My Lord, forgive me and grant me a kingdom such as will not belong to anyone after me' [Surah Sad: 35], so Allah Almighty sent him (the jinn) back humiliated and disgraced."""
"2112","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, knowledge from which no benefit is derived is like a treasure from which nothing is spent in the way of Allah."""
"2113","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man's paternal uncle is like his father (that is, of the same root and in his place)."""
"2114","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the thickness of the skin of the disbeliever's body will be forty-two cubits by the cubit of al-Jabbar (that is, a man of enormous size), his molar will be the size of (the mountain of) Uhud, and his seat in Hell will be as wide as the distance between Makkah and Madinah."""
"2115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Fatimah is a part of me, and I fear that she will be put to trial in her religion. And indeed I do not make anything lawful unlawful, nor anything unlawful lawful, but by Allah! The daughter of the Messenger of Allah and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will never be joined together in marriage to one man."""
"2116","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the day of the great battle (al-Malhamah al-Kubra), the tent (headquarters) of the Muslims will be in al-Ghutah, beside a city called Damascus, which is one of the best cities of Sham."""
"2117","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The superiority of Aishah over women is just like the superiority of tharid over all other food."""
"2118","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The poor among the Muhajirun will enter Paradise forty years before the rich on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2119","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""So-and-so gave me a she-camel as a gift, and in return I gave him six young she-camels, yet he remained displeased. I have resolved that from now on I will not accept a gift except from a man of Quraysh, of the Ansar, of Thaqif or of Daws."""
"2120","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On Friday there is an hour such that if a Muslim servant finds it while standing in prayer and asks Allah for some good, Allah Almighty will certainly grant it to him."""
"2121","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan. On the Day of Resurrection only those who fast will enter through this gate; no one other than them will enter through it. It will be called out: Where are those who fasted? So they will stand up and enter through it. When they have entered, the gate will be closed, and then no one will enter through it."""
"2122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a sea of water, a sea of honey, a sea of milk and a sea of wine, then after them rivers burst forth (from these very seas)."""
"2123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there are lofty chambers whose outside can be seen from the inside and whose inside can be seen from the outside. Allah Almighty has prepared them for the one who feeds others, speaks gently, fasts regularly, and prays at night while people are asleep."""
"2124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a market to which the people of Paradise will come every Friday. In it there will be mounds of musk. Then the north wind will blow and scatter the musk over their faces and clothes, increasing them further in beauty and splendour. Then they will return to their families, their beauty and splendour having increased. Their families will say to them: By Allah! Since you left us your beauty and splendour have increased. And they will say: By Allah! Since we left you your beauty and splendour have increased too."""
"2125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider on a fast, trained horse could travel for a hundred years and still not cross it."""
"2126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there are a hundred degrees which Allah Almighty has prepared for those who strive (jihad) in His path. Between each two degrees is a distance like that between the heaven and the earth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise and the highest degree of Paradise; above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it the rivers of Paradise gush forth."""
"2127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there are blessings that no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and whose thought has never crossed the heart of any human being."""
"2128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In being cupped (having hijamah done) there is healing."""
"2129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prayer requires full attention (that is, prayer is itself a great occupation)."""
"2130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the night there is an hour such that no Muslim servant finds it and asks Allah Almighty in it for any good of this world or the Hereafter, except that Allah Almighty will certainly grant it to him, and this hour occurs every night."""
"2131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among my Ummah there are twelve hypocrites who will neither enter Paradise nor find its fragrance until a camel passes through the eye of a needle. For eight of them, the abscess called al-Dubaylah will suffice; it will be a lamp (that is, a flame) of fire that appears between their shoulders until it bursts out from their chests."""
"2132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in my Ummah there will be the punishment of being swallowed up (into the earth), of faces being transformed, and of stones raining down (from the sky)."""
"2133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in the tribe of Thaqif there will arise a great liar and a destroyer (that is, a bloodthirsty tyrant)."""
"2134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, at my Pond there will be vessels (cups) as numerous as the stars of the sky."""
"2135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in the ajwah dates of the upper part of Madinah (al-Aliyah) there is healing, and eating them early in the morning on an empty stomach is an antidote to poison."""
"2136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, you have two qualities that Allah Almighty loves: forbearance, and deliberation (that is, not being hasty)."""
"2137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in a man's wealth there is a trial, and in his wife and his children there is a trial as well."""
"2138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the length of my Pond is like the distance between Aylah, a city of Sham, and San'a, a city of Yemen, and indeed there will be in it vessels (cups) as numerous as the stars of the sky."""
"2139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Quraysh are a trustworthy people. Whoever seeks out their stumbles (that is, their downfall), Allah Almighty will throw him on his face (into Hell)."""
"2140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Quraysh have only recently come out of the days of ignorance (Jahiliyyah) and affliction (that is, they are new Muslims), so I wanted to give them (financial) help and win their hearts. Are you (O Ansar!) not content that the people go back with worldly goods, while you return to your homes with the Messenger of Allah? If all the people were to walk in one valley or mountain pass, I would walk in the valley and mountain pass of the Ansar."""
"2141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the hearts of all the children of Adam are between two of the fingers of the Most Merciful like a single heart; He turns it however He wills."""
"2142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, lying about me is not like lying about anyone else. So whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire of Hell."""
"2143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, breaking the bone of a Muslim after his death is just like breaking it during his life."" (That is, the deceased is owed the same respect.)"
"2144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prayer wipes out the sins (that is, minor sins) committed before it."""
"2145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there are some jinn who dwell in your houses, so warn them for three days; if after that any of them appears to you, kill it."""
"2146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one who has a right is entitled to speak (and to be firm)."""
"2147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every Ummah has a trustworthy one, and indeed the trustworthy one of this Ummah is Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"2148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, for every nation there is a trial, and indeed the trial of my nation is wealth."""
"2149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every religion has a distinctive trait, and indeed the distinctive trait of Islam is modesty (haya)."""
"2150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, everything has a reality, and no servant attains the reality of faith until he knows that whatever afflicted him was never going to miss him, and whatever missed him was never going to reach him."""
"2151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, everything has a zeal and fervour, and every zeal is followed by a time of slackness (and rest). So if its possessor (that is, the one doing the deed) keeps to moderation and balance, then have hope of good for him; and if (he shows off until) fingers are pointed at him, then do not count him (that is, he is of no worth)."""
"2152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every deed has a zeal, and every zeal is followed by a time of slackness. So whoever's slackness (and rest) leads to my Sunnah has been guided, and whoever's slackness leads to something else (that is, to innovation or sin) has perished."""
"2153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection every betrayer (deceiver) will have a banner by which he will be recognised, (and it will be planted) at his buttocks."""
"2154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prophet has a trustee (a confidant and trusted one), and my trustee is Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"2155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prophet has a disciple (a special and sincere helper), and my disciple is al-Zubayr (bin al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"2156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prophet has a Pool (Hawd), and they will vie with one another in pride over which of them has the most people coming to drink at his Pool, and I hope that those coming to my Pool will be the most numerous."""
"2157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prophet has a (special) supplication which he made concerning his nation and it was answered for him, but I have kept my supplication hidden (and preserved) as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every prophet has, from among the prophets, some who are his allies (friends and patrons), and indeed my ally is my father and the Intimate Friend of my Lord (Sayyiduna Ibrahim, peace be upon him)."""
"2159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, you will have as much reward as you intended and hoped for (from Allah)."""
"2160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, you will have reward in proportion to your toil and your spending."""
"2161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, for every step (taken towards the mosque) you will have a degree (of elevation)."""
"2162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Islam too has, like the waymarks of a road, certain shining signs and minarets (for guidance)."""
"2163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has vessels among the people of the earth, and the vessels of your Lord are the hearts of His righteous servants, and the dearest of them to Allah are those that are the softest and most tender."""
"2164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has certain servants whom He singles out with special blessings for the benefit of other servants, and He keeps those blessings with them as long as they keep spending them. Then when they withhold them, He takes them away from them and transfers them to others."""
"2165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the people there are some who belong to Allah Almighty. (The Companions asked who they were, and he said:) The people of the Qur'an are the people of Allah and His chosen ones."""
"2166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has ninety-nine names, that is, one hundred less one. Whoever memorises them (and acts upon what they require) will enter Paradise."""
"2167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has ninety-nine names, that is, one hundred less one. Whoever memorises them will enter Paradise. And He is Odd (One), and He loves what is odd."""
"2168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has certain servants who recognise people through insight (and the signs in their faces)."""
"2169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in every day and night Allah Almighty has servants whom He frees (from Hell), and each servant among them has one supplication that is certainly answered."""
"2170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, at every time of breaking the fast, Allah Almighty frees people from the Fire of Hell, and this happens every night (of Ramadan)."""
"2171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, to Allah Almighty belongs what He has taken, and to Him belongs what He has given, and with Him everything has an appointed term."""
"2172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah has one hundred mercies. Of them He has sent down only one mercy among the jinn, humans, animals and insects. Through it they show affection to one another, through it they show mercy to one another, and through it the wild beasts show tenderness to their young. And He has deferred (and preserved) ninety-nine mercies, through which He will show mercy to His servants on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has certain angels, besides the angels who write down the deeds of people, who roam about the earth. They go around the roads searching for the people of remembrance. So when they find a people remembering Allah, they call out to one another: 'Come to what you are seeking.' Then they surround them with their wings up to the lowest heaven. Then their Lord asks them, though He knows better than them: 'What are My servants saying?' The angels say: 'They are glorifying You, proclaiming Your greatness, praising You and extolling Your majesty.' Allah says: 'Have they seen Me?' The angels say: 'No, by Allah! They have not seen You.' Allah says: 'What would their state be if they saw Me?' The angels say: 'If they saw You, they would worship You even more, extol Your majesty even more and glorify You even more.' Allah says: 'Then what do they ask of Me?' The angels say: 'They ask You for Paradise.' Allah says: 'Have they seen it?' The angels say: 'No, by Allah! O Lord, they have not seen it.' Allah says: 'What would their state be if they saw it?' The angels say: 'If they saw it, they would be even more eager for it, seek it even more and have even greater longing for it.' Allah says: 'Then from what do they seek refuge?' The angels say: 'From the Fire (of Hell).' Allah says: 'Have they seen it?' The angels say: 'No, by Allah! O Lord, they have not seen it.' Allah says: 'What would their state be if they saw it?' The angels say: 'If they saw it, they would flee from it even more and fear it even more.' Allah says: 'Then I make you witnesses that I have forgiven them.' One of the angels says: 'Among them is so-and-so, who is not one of them; he only came for some need!' Allah says: 'They are such people that even the one who sits with them is not left wretched.'"""
"2174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has certain angels who roam about the earth; they convey to me the salam (greeting of peace) of my nation."""
"2175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has certain angels on the earth who make the tongues of the children of Adam speak of the good and the evil that is in a person."""
"2176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has an angel to whom He has given the ability to hear the voices of the servants, so no one sends blessings (durud) upon me except that he conveys it to me. And I have asked my Lord that whichever servant sends blessings upon me once, Allah Almighty sends down ten mercies upon him in return."""
"2177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, repentance has a door, the width between its two leaves being as much as the distance between the east and the west. It will not be closed until the sun rises from its place of setting."""
"2178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the prayer has an earliest time and a latest time. The earliest time of the Zuhr prayer is when the sun passes its zenith, and its latest time is when the time of Asr begins. The earliest time of Asr is when its time begins, and its latest time is when the sun turns yellow. The earliest time of Maghrib is when the sun sets, and its latest time is when the twilight (redness) disappears. The earliest time of Isha is when the twilight disappears, and its latest time is when half the night has passed. And the earliest time of Fajr is when the (true) dawn appears, and its latest time is when the sun rises."""
"2179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the one who eats and gives thanks has as much reward as the fasting person who is patient."""
"2180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the grave has a squeezing (a pressing), and if anyone were to be saved from it, Sa'd bin Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) would certainly have been saved from it."""
"2181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man of Quraysh has the strength of two men who are not from Quraysh."""
"2182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in Paradise the believer will have a tent made of a single hollow pearl, sixty miles long. In it the believer will have wives, and the believer will go around to each of them in turn, yet (because of its vastness) they will not see one another."""
"2183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, death has a terror, so when you see a funeral procession, stand up."""
"2184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this stone (the Black Stone) has a tongue and two lips; on the Day of Resurrection it will bear witness in favour of whoever kissed it with sincerity (haqq)."""
"2185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these camels have a wildness and a tendency to bolt like that of wild animals, so if any of them gets the better of you (that is, goes out of control), then treat it like this (that is, bring it under control by shooting it with an arrow)."""
"2186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these houses have certain dwellers (jinn), so when you see any of them (a snake or the like), then strictly warn them (admonish them) for three days; if it goes away, well and good, otherwise kill it, for it is a disbeliever (a rebellious devil)."""
"2187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it contains fat."" (According to the narrator, this refers to milk.)"
"2188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, he has a wet nurse in Paradise."" (This refers to his son, Sayyiduna Ibrahim.)"
"2189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I have five names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Hashir, at whose feet the people will be gathered, I am al-Mahi, through whom Allah will erase disbelief, and I am al-Aqib (the one who comes after all)."""
"2190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the distance between the two leaves of a door of Paradise is equal to a journey of forty years."""
"2191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whatever has been decreed (destined) in the womb will certainly come to be."""
"2192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the example of the one who does evil deeds and then does good deeds is like a man wearing a tight coat of mail that is choking him. Then he does a good deed and one ring (of the mail) comes loose, then he does another good deed and another ring comes loose, until it (comes completely undone and) falls to the ground (that is, he becomes completely free from the burden of sins)."""
"2193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the example of the one who takes back his gift (present) after giving it is like a dog that ate until, when it was full, it vomited, then returned to its vomit and ate it again."""
"2194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, wiping (that is, touching) the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner sheds sins away completely."""
"2195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the food of the son of Adam has been made an example for this world; however much spice and salt he adds to it (however tasty he makes it), just see what it finally turns into (that is, filth)."""
"2196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when the Dajjal emerges, he will have water and fire with him. What people see as fire will in reality be cold water, and what people see as cold water will be burning fire. So whoever among you lives to see him should plunge into what he sees as fire, for it will in fact be sweet, cold water."""
"2197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty made Makkah sacred; it was not people who made it sacred. So it is not lawful for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it, nor to cut down any of its trees. If anyone seeks a concession on the grounds that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fought in Makkah, then say to him: 'Indeed, Allah permitted His Messenger, but He did not permit you.' And even I was permitted only for an hour of a day, then today its sanctity has returned just as it was yesterday. And let the one who is present convey this to the one who is absent."""
"2198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, an angel came to me and said: Indeed, your Lord says to you: Are you not pleased that no one from your Ummah sends blessings (salat) upon you once except that I send ten mercies upon him, and no one sends salutations (salam) upon you once except that I send peace upon him ten times? I said: Certainly (I am pleased)."""
"2199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, part of honouring Allah Almighty is to show respect to the grey-haired Muslim, to show respect to the bearer of the Qur'an who neither goes to extremes in it nor turns away from it, and to show respect to the just ruler."""
"2200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the most beloved of you to me are those of you who are best in character."""
"2201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me in sitting on the Day of Resurrection are those who are best in character. And indeed, among the most hateful of you to me and the farthest of you from me on the Day of Resurrection are those who talk excessively, those who speak affectedly, and al-mutafayhiqun. The Companions asked: O Messenger of Allah, who are al-mutafayhiqun? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The arrogant."""
"2202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the people with the finest voice in reciting the Qur'an is the one who, when you hear him reciting, you feel that he fears Allah."""
"2203","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the worst forms of usury (riba) is to make unjust attacks on the honour of a Muslim with one's tongue."""
"2204","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah (that is, those who make images and statues of living beings)."""
"2205","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the signs of the Hour is that you will fight a people who wear sandals made of hair, and among the signs of the Hour is also that you will fight a people with broad faces, as though their faces were shields covered with layer upon layer of hide."""
"2206","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the signs of the Hour is that (religious) knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will prevail, fornication will become widespread, wine will be drunk, and men will become few while women remain, until fifty women will have only one man to look after them."""
"2207","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the signs of the Hour is that knowledge will be sought from the lesser ones (that is, people of little knowledge and low standing)."""
"2208","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the purest things a person eats is what comes from his own earnings, and his children are also part of his earnings."""
"2209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the greatest forms of jihad is to speak a word of truth (and justice) before a tyrannical ruler."""
"2210","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the greatest of lies are that a person attributes his lineage to someone other than his real father, or makes his eyes see what they did not see (that is, he relates a false dream), or attributes to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) something he (peace and blessings be upon him) did not say."""
"2211","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the greatest of lies is that a man makes his eyes see in a dream what they did not see (that is, he relates a false dream)."""
"2212","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the best of your days is Friday. On it Adam (peace be upon him) was created, on it his soul was taken, on that day the Trumpet will be blown, and on that day everyone will be struck unconscious. So send abundant blessings upon me on that day, for your blessings are presented to me. Indeed, Allah Almighty has forbidden the earth from consuming the bodies of the prophets."""
"2213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the gravest of the major sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and al-yamin al-ghamus (a deliberately false oath). And whoever swears by Allah an oath that he is bound to (or swears it of his own accord), and includes in it (falsehood) even the size of a mosquito's wing, a black spot is placed on his heart until the Day of Resurrection."""
"2214","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the gravest of sins is that a man curses his own parents. (When the Companions asked, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It happens like this:) he abuses another man's father, so that man in return abuses his father; and he abuses his mother, so that man in return abuses his mother."""
"2215","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some eloquent speech (and oratory) has (the effect of) magic, and indeed, some poetry contains (words of) wisdom."""
"2216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some eloquent speech (oratory) truly has (the effect of) magic."""
"2217","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, wine is made from wheat, wine is made from barley, wine is made from dates, wine is made from raisins, and wine is made from honey; and I forbid (the use of) every intoxicant."""
"2218","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the trees there is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and indeed, it is like the Muslim. So tell me, which tree is it?"" (When the people remained silent,) he (peace and blessings be upon him) then said: ""It is the date palm."""
"2219","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom."""
"2220","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, wine is made from grapes, wine is made from dates, wine is made from honey, wine is made from wheat, and wine is made from barley."""
"2221","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there is a kind of protective jealousy (ghayrah) that Allah loves and a kind that Allah dislikes. Likewise, there is a kind of pride (in one's gait) that Allah loves and a kind that Allah dislikes. As for the jealousy that Allah loves, it is jealousy where there is cause for suspicion (when there is fear of something unlawful); and the jealousy that Allah dislikes is jealousy without reason (without any cause for suspicion). And the pride that Allah loves is a man walking proudly on the battlefield and when giving charity; and the pride that Allah dislikes is a man walking proudly out of transgression and arrogance."""
"2222","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the practices of the fitrah (natural disposition) are these: rinsing the mouth, putting water into the nose, using the miswak, trimming the moustache, clipping the nails, plucking the armpit hair, removing the pubic hair, washing the finger joints (thoroughly), sprinkling water (on the clothes after istinja, to ward off doubts about urine), and circumcision."""
"2223","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, some people are keys to good and locks against evil, and indeed, some people are keys to evil and locks against good. So glad tidings to the one in whose hands Allah Almighty has placed the keys of good, and woe and ruin to the one in whose hands Allah Almighty has placed the keys of evil."""
"2224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in my Ummah there will be some people who will be given a reward like that of the first of this Ummah (that is, the noble Companions); they will be those who forbid evil (and wrongdoing)."""
"2225","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, straightening the rows is part of the completeness of the prayer."""
"2226","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the worst of people in the sight of Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection will be the two-faced person (the hypocrite with two faces)."""
"2227","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, from the offspring of this man there will come a people who will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will kill the people of Islam and leave the idol-worshippers alone. They will pass out of Islam as swiftly as an arrow passes through the body of the game. If I live to see them, I will kill them as the people of Ad were killed (uprooting them completely)."""
"2228","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the servants of Allah Almighty are some who, if they were to swear an oath relying on Allah, Allah Almighty would fulfil their oath."""
"2229","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in the direction of the setting of the sun (in the west) there is an open door (of repentance) whose width is equal to a distance of seventy years. That door will remain open until the sun rises from that direction (the west). So when the sun rises from that direction, then 'No soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or had not earned some good through its faith.' [Surah al-An'am: 158]"""
"2230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among what has reached the people from the words of the earlier prophethood is this: If you have no modesty, then do whatever you wish."""
"2231","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the deeds and good works whose reward continues to reach the believer after his death are these: knowledge that he spread, a righteous child whom he left behind, a copy of the Qur'an that he left as inheritance, or a mosque that he built, or a house that he built for travellers, or a stream that he made flow, or charity that he gave from his wealth while in good health and during his lifetime; the reward of all of these continues to reach him even after his death."""
"2232","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the deeds that make forgiveness due are spreading the greeting of salam abundantly and speaking in a good and gentle manner."""
"2233","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, ahead of you are days in which ignorance will descend, knowledge will be taken away, and al-harj, that is, killing and bloodshed, will become widespread."""
"2234","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, after you there will come a time of patience in which the one who holds firmly (to the religion) will have a reward equal to that of fifty martyrs from among you."""
"2235","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the blessings of a woman is that her proposal of marriage is easy, her dowry (mahr) is easy, and her womb (that is, the stage of childbirth) is easy."""
"2236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among you are some men to whom I do not give anything (from wealth to win over their hearts); rather, I entrust them to their faith (that is, I rely on their firm faith). Among them is Furat bin Hayyan (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"2237","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the people of Hell there will be some whom the Fire will seize up to their ankles, some whom the Fire will seize up to their knees, some whom the Fire will seize up to their waists, and some whom the Fire will seize up to their necks."""
"2238","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Musa (peace be upon him) said: O my Lord, show us Adam (peace be upon him), who caused himself and us to be expelled from Paradise. So Allah showed him Adam (peace be upon him). Musa asked: Are you our father Adam? Adam said to him: Yes. Musa said: Are you the one into whom Allah breathed of His spirit, whom He taught all the names, and He commanded the angels, so they prostrated to you? Adam said: Yes. Musa said: Then what led you to cause us and yourself to be expelled from Paradise? At this Adam asked him: Who are you? He said: I am Musa. Adam said: Are you the prophet of the Children of Israel to whom Allah spoke from behind a veil, without making any messenger from His creation an intermediary between Him and you? Musa said: Yes. Adam said: Did you not find that this was written in the Book of Allah before I was created? Musa said: Yes. Adam said: Then why do you blame me for something that Allah Almighty had decreed before I was even created? So Adam (peace be upon him) prevailed over Musa (peace be upon him); so Adam (peace be upon him) prevailed over Musa (peace be upon him)."""
"2239","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Musa (peace be upon him) was a very modest man who kept himself covered; out of modesty, no part of his body could be seen. So those among the Children of Israel who wished to hurt him hurt him, and they began saying: He only covers himself this much because there is some defect in his body: either leprosy (white patches), or a hernia, or some other affliction. And indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, willed to clear him of what they said. One day he went off alone, placed his clothes on a stone and began to bathe. When he had finished bathing, he went towards his clothes to take them, but the stone ran off with his clothes. Musa took hold of his staff and ran after the stone, saying: O stone, my garment! O stone, my garment! until he reached a gathering of the Children of Israel. They saw Musa unclothed, the best of Allah's creation, and Allah cleared him of the defect they used to speak of. Then the stone stopped, so he took his clothes and put them on, and began striking the stone with his staff. By Allah, the marks of his striking are still on that stone, three, four or five of them. And concerning this is the saying of Allah Almighty: 'O you who believe, do not be like those who hurt Musa; then Allah cleared him of what they said, and he was honoured in the sight of Allah.' [Surah al-Ahzab: 69]"""
"2240","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there will be some people from my Ummah whose distinguishing mark will be the shaving of the head. They will recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass out of the religion as swiftly as an arrow passes through the game. They are the worst of all creation and all creatures."""
"2241","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a group of the jinn have accepted Islam in Madinah. So when you see one of them (in your homes, in the form of a snake or the like), warn it three times (for three days) to leave. Then if it still appears to you after that, kill it after those three times."""
"2242","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these two prayers, that is, Isha and Fajr, are the heaviest of prayers upon the hypocrites. If they knew how much reward there is in them, they would certainly come to them, even if they had to crawl on their knees. And hold fast to the first row, for it is like the row of the angels, and if you knew its virtue you would race towards it. And a man's praying together with another man (in congregation) is purer than his praying alone, and his praying with two men is purer than his praying with one man, and the more people there are, the more beloved it is to Allah Almighty."""
"2243","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This man drew my sword from its sheath while I was asleep. Then I woke up, and the drawn sword was in his hand. He said to me: Who will save you from me? I said: Allah! So look, now he is sitting here before you."""
"2244","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this matter (of rule and caliphate) will remain among Quraysh; whoever shows enmity to them, Allah Almighty will throw him down on his face, as long as they keep the religion established."""
"2245","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surely these dinars and dirhams destroyed the nations before you, and they are the very ones that will destroy you too."""
"2246","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this religion is very firm, so proceed in it with gentleness and moderation."""
"2247","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this month has come to you, and in it there is a night better than a thousand months. Whoever is deprived of its blessings has been deprived of all good, and none is deprived of the good of that night except one who is truly deprived and unfortunate."""
"2248","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this plague is a punishment, and it is the remnant of the punishment with which (earlier) peoples were punished. So when this epidemic spreads in a land while you are there, do not leave it to flee from it; and when it spreads in a land where you are not present, do not enter it."""
"2249","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this Qur'an has been revealed in seven modes of recitation (dialects), so recite of it whatever is easy for you."""
"2250","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever acquires it by its right is blessed in it, and whoever acquires it with the greed of the self is not blessed in it, and his example is like one who eats but is never satisfied. And the upper hand is better than the lower hand."""
"2251","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this wealth is green, fresh and sweet. Whoever acquires it by its right, blessing is placed in it. And there are many people who wrongfully deal with the wealth of Allah and His Messenger as their own desires please; on the Day of Resurrection there will be nothing for them except the Fire."""
"2252","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this mosque is not a place to be urinated in; it has been built only for the remembrance of Allah and for prayer."""
"2253","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this epidemic is a punishment by which Allah destroyed the nations before you, and some of it now remains in the earth; it comes at times and goes at times. So when it spreads in a land (region), do not leave it to flee from it; and when you hear about a land that this epidemic is there, do not go there."""
"2254","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is a matter that Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam (women). So take a ritual bath (ghusl), enter the state of ihram for Hajj, and perform all the rites that a pilgrim performs, except that you should not perform tawaf of the House (the Ka'bah) and should not pray."""
"2255","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is a matter that Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam. So perform all the same rites that a pilgrim performs, except that you should not perform tawaf of the House (the Ka'bah)."""
"2256","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this (dry trunk) wept because it no longer heard the remembrance of Allah near it."" (The narrator says that this refers to the palm-tree trunk.)"
"2257","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is an angel who had never descended to the earth before this night. He sought permission from his Lord to greet me with salam and to give me the glad tidings that Fatimah is the leader of the women of the people of Paradise, and that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the leaders of the youth of the people of Paradise."""
"2258","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is a day that Allah has made a day of Eid for the Muslims. So whoever comes to the Friday prayer, let him take a ritual bath (ghusl), and if he has perfume, let him apply some of it; and you must use the miswak (tooth-stick)."""
"2259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is a day on which the people of the Jahiliyyah (pre-Islamic ignorance) used to fast. So whoever likes to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever likes to leave it, let him leave it."" (The narrator says that this refers to the day of Ashura.)"
"2260","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these signs which Allah sends do not occur because of anyone's death or life; rather, Allah sends them to frighten His servants with them. So when you see any of them, hasten in alarm to the remembrance of Allah, to supplicating to Him, and to seeking His forgiveness."""
"2261","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this Ummah is an Ummah shown mercy; its punishment is in its own hands (that is, the afflictions that befall it in this world become its expiation). So when the Day of Resurrection comes, a man from the polytheists will be handed over to every man of the Muslims, and it will be said: 'This is your ransom from the Fire.'"""
"2262","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this Ummah is tested in its graves. Were it not for the fear that you would stop burying one another, I would have supplicated to Allah to make you hear the punishment of the grave that I hear. Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire; seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave; seek refuge with Allah from all trials (whether apparent or hidden); and seek refuge with Allah from the trial of the Dajjal."""
"2263","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these privies and toilets are places frequented by jinn and devils. So when any one of you goes to the toilet, he should say this supplication: 'A'udhu billahi min al-khubuthi wal-khaba'ith' (I seek refuge with Allah from the male and female evil jinn)."""
"2264","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these charities and zakah are like the dirt (impurities) of people, and they are lawful neither for Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) nor for the family of Muhammad."""
"2265","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, nothing of people's ordinary speech is proper in this prayer; it consists only of glorification (tasbih), magnification (takbir) and the recitation of the Qur'an."""
"2266","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this prayer (that is, the Asr prayer) was presented to the nations before you and they neglected it. So whoever among you guards it today will have his reward twice over, and there is no prayer after it until the shahid (a star) appears."""
"2267","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these graves are filled with darkness for the people in them, and indeed Allah Almighty illuminates them for them through the blessing of my prayer (funeral prayer or supplication) over them."""
"2268","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these mosques are not suitable for any kind of filth, urine or impurity; they are built only for the recitation of the Noble Qur'an, the remembrance of Allah and prayer."""
"2269","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this fire is your enemy, so when you go to sleep, extinguish it (so it is away) from you."""
"2270","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is a manner of lying down that Allah Almighty does not love."""
"2271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is a manner of lying down that Allah Almighty intensely detests (that is, lying on the stomach)."""
"2272","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is not menstruation (menstrual blood); rather, it is blood from a vein. So when the days of menstruation have passed, take a ritual bath (ghusl) and pray, and when those days come, leave the prayer during them."""
"2273","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is among the garments of the disbelievers, so do not wear it (that is, mu'asfar clothing, which is dyed yellow with safflower)."""
"2274","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these two things are forbidden to the men of my Ummah and lawful for their women (that is, gold and silk)."""
"2275","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If that is the case, then your pillow is certainly very wide and long (that is, you have taken the matter in far too extended a sense). It is merely the blackness of the night and the whiteness of the day."""
"2276","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Ya'juj and Ma'juj (Gog and Magog) dig through the barrier every day, until, when they are about to see the rays of the sun, the one in charge of them says: 'Go back; we will dig it tomorrow.' Then Allah Almighty restores it (the barrier) stronger than it was before. Until, when their term is complete and Allah wills to send them against the people, they will come to dig, until, when they are about to see the rays of the sun, the one in charge of them will say: 'Go back; we will dig it tomorrow, in sha' Allah (if Allah wills).' (This time) they will make the exception (by saying 'in sha' Allah'). So they will return and find the barrier in the same state in which they left it. Then they will dig through it and come out upon the people. They will drink up all the water, and the people will shut themselves up in their fortresses to protect themselves from them. Then they (Ya'juj and Ma'juj) will shoot their arrows towards the sky, and the arrows will come back stained with blood. They will say: 'We have overpowered the people of the earth and prevailed over the people of the heavens!' Then Allah Almighty will send upon their necks a kind of worm by which they will all die. By the One in whose hand is my soul! Indeed, the animals of the earth will become fat and fully satisfied from eating their flesh and drinking their blood."""
"2277","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the right hand of Allah Almighty is full; continuous spending day and night does not diminish it. Just consider how much He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth! Yet, despite that, nothing has diminished from what is in His right hand. His Throne is upon the water, and in His other hand is the withholding (al-qabd); He raises and lowers."""
"2278","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on Monday and Thursday Allah Almighty forgives every Muslim except two people who have cut off relations with each other. Allah Almighty says (to the angels): 'Leave these two until they reconcile with each other.'"""
"2279","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Friday is the leader of all days and the greatest of them in the sight of Allah Almighty. It is greater in the sight of Allah than the day of Eid al-Adha and the day of Eid al-Fitr. In it there are five characteristics (important matters): on this day Allah Almighty created Adam (peace be upon him); on this day Allah sent Adam (peace be upon him) down to the earth; on this day Allah caused Adam (peace be upon him) to die; on it there is an hour in which the servant does not ask Allah for anything except that Allah certainly grants it to him, provided he does not ask for something forbidden; and on this day the Hour will be established. There is no angel brought near, nor sky, nor earth, nor winds, nor mountains, nor sea, except that it fears Friday, lest the Hour be established on it."""
"2280","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we are the family of Muhammad, and charity (sadaqah) is not lawful for us."""
"2281","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we are the family of Muhammad, and charity (sadaqah) is not lawful for us; and certainly the freed slave of a people is counted as one of them."""
"2282","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we are an unlettered nation; we neither write nor calculate."""
"2283","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we have had a ring made and have had an inscription engraved on it, so let no one else engrave an inscription like it on his ring."""
"2284","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we had forbidden you from eating the meat of the sacrificial animals beyond three days (by storing it) so that it would suffice for all of you. Now Allah Almighty has granted abundance and plenty, so eat it, store it and benefit from it. And listen! Indeed, these days are days of eating, drinking and the remembrance of Allah."""
"2285","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we will never appoint to this (governmental) work of ours anyone who desires (or seeks) it."""
"2286","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we, the community of prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking of the fast, to delay our pre-dawn meal (suhur), and to place our right hands on our left hands in prayer."""
"2287","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we are the community of prophets; our eyes sleep but our hearts do not sleep."""
"2288","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we are the community of prophets; trials and hardships are doubled for us."""
"2289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we are about to deliver the (Eid) sermon. So whoever wishes to sit to listen to the sermon, let him sit, and whoever wishes to leave, let him leave."""
"2290","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we have been forbidden from having our private parts ('awrah) seen."""
"2291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah! We will never appoint to this (governmental) office anyone who has asked for it, nor anyone who covets it."""
"2292","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we do not seek help from polytheists against polytheists."""
"2293","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we do not seek help from a polytheist."""
"2294","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, we do not accept anything (such as gifts) from the polytheists."""
"2295","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, if you pursue people's hidden faults, you will corrupt them, or you will come close to corrupting them."""
"2296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, you are going to a people who are People of the Book. So let the first thing you call them to be the worship of Allah. When they come to know Allah, inform them that Allah has made five prayers obligatory upon them in their day and night. When they do that, inform them that Allah has made zakah obligatory upon them, to be taken from their wealth and returned to their poor. So when they obey in this, take (the zakah) from them, but avoid the choicest and best of people's wealth."""
"2297","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You invited us, five men, and we were five (in it), and this (sixth) man has followed us. So if you wish, give him permission (to come in), and if you wish, he will go back."""
"2298","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are going to a people who are People of the Book. So when you reach them, invite them to bear witness that there is no true god except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. If they accept this from you, then inform them that Allah has made five prayers obligatory upon them in every day and night. Then if they accept this too, inform them that Allah has made charity (zakah) obligatory upon them, which will be taken from their rich and distributed among their poor. So if they obey you in this as well, then beware of (taking as zakah) the finest of their wealth, and fear the supplication of the oppressed, for there is no veil between it and Allah."""
"2299","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, you are like that first man who said: O Allah, find me a friend who is dearer to me than my own self."""
"2300","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you are left behind (in Makkah) after me and do any righteous deed, you will surely increase in rank and elevation because of it. Then perhaps you will remain (in the world for some more time), until some peoples benefit through you and others are harmed. O Allah, complete the emigration of my Companions and do not turn them back on their heels (into apostasy). But the one to be pitied is (Sa'd bin Khawlah) (for he died in Makkah itself)."""
"2301","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You complete seventy (70) nations (that is, you are the seventieth nation); you are the best of them all and the most honoured in the sight of Allah Almighty."""
"2302","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will be gathered here (on the plain of the Gathering) walking on foot, riding on mounts, and being dragged on your faces"", and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed with his hand towards the land of Sham."
"2303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, you are waiting for a prayer that the followers of no religion other than yours wait for. Were it not that I feared it would be a hardship upon my Ummah, I would lead them in this prayer (that is, the delayed Isha prayer) at this very hour."""
"2304","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will soon be intensely eager to attain leadership (office and rule), yet on the Day of Resurrection it will be a cause of regret and sorrow. So it (leadership) is an excellent wet-nurse (that is, giving worldly benefits at first), but a terrible weaner (that is, when it is snatched away at dismissal or death)."""
"2305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me you will soon see unfair preference (the unworthy being preferred over the worthy) and matters that you will disapprove of. (At that time) keep giving them (the rulers) their right, and ask (only) Allah Almighty for your own right."""
"2306","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will soon see your Lord (clearly) just as you see this moon; you will face no difficulty or hindrance of any kind in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in performing the prayer before sunrise (Fajr) and the prayer before sunset (Asr) (that is, to offer them on time), then be sure to do so."""
"2307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will soon conquer Egypt, and it is a land where the qirat (as a measure) is mentioned. So when you conquer it, accept the counsel to treat its people well (be kind to them), for they have a covenant (of protection) and (with us) a bond of kinship. And when you see two men quarrelling over the space of a (mere) brick (there), then leave it."""
"2308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tomorrow you will surely face the enemy, so (for recognition) your watchword and slogan should be: 'Ha Mim, la yunsarun' (They will never be victorious)."""
"2309","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me you will see others being preferred over you (in matters of government), so be patient (with it) until you meet me tomorrow at the Pond (of Kawthar)."""
"2310","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have complained of the drought in your lands and of the rain being delayed from its appointed time, while Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has commanded you (to supplicate) and promised you that He will answer you. 'All praise is for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Recompense' [Surah al-Fatihah: 2-4]. There is no true god except Allah; He does what He wills. 'La ilaha illallahu yaf'alu ma yurid, Allahumma anta Allahu la ilaha illa anta al-Ghaniyyu wa nahnu al-fuqara', anzil 'alayna al-ghaytha waj'al ma anzalta lana quwwatan wa balaghan ila hin' (O Allah, You are Allah, there is none worthy of worship except You; You are the Free of all needs and we are all the needy. Send down rain upon us, and make what You send down for us a source of strength and a means of sustenance until an appointed time)."""
"2311","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will never attain this matter (of government and caliphate) by force and seizing it."""
"2312","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will never see your Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, until you die (that is, seeing Allah is not possible in the life of this world)."""
"2313","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will continue to be counted as in a state of prayer as long as you keep waiting (sitting in the mosque) for the (next) prayer."""
"2314","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tomorrow morning you are going to face your enemy, and breaking the fast will give you more strength, so break your fast (that is, do not keep it)."""
"2315","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your term (of remaining in the world) compared to the nations that have passed before is only like the time from the Asr prayer until sunset. Indeed, the example of you and of the Jews and Christians is like that of a man who hired some labourers and said: Who will work for me from morning until midday for one qirat (wage) each? So the Jews worked. Then he said: Who will work for me from midday until the Asr prayer for one qirat (wage) each? So the Christians worked. Then he said: Who will work for me from the Asr prayer until sunset for two qirats (wage) each? And you are those (workers). At this the Jews and Christians became angry and said: What is wrong with us that we worked more and received less wage? He (the owner) said: Have I wronged you in any way in giving you your agreed wage? They said: No. Then He (Allah) said: This is My bounty; I give it to whomever I will."""
"2316","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What I fear most for my Ummah is misguiding leaders (and rulers)."""
"2317","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What I fear most for you after me is that the splendour of the world and its glitter will be opened up to you (and you will fall into love of it). Indeed, good does not bring evil. Indeed, among what the spring season grows (fresh grass) there is some that kills (the animal) by bloating its belly or brings it close to death, except for the animal that eats greenery, until when both its flanks are full, it turns to face the sun, then it passes dung, urinates, and then starts grazing again. And indeed this wealth is green and sweet. How excellent a companion that wealth is for a Muslim who gives it to the poor, the orphan and the wayfarer. So whoever takes this (wealth) by its right (that is, in a lawful way) and spends it in its right (proper place), then it is an excellent helper. And whoever acquires it without right (in an unlawful way), he is like the one who keeps eating but is never satisfied, and it (the wealth) will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2318","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I regard Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib as one and the same thing (that is, one family); they neither abandoned us in the days of Ignorance nor (left us alone) in Islam."""
"2319","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""True rest is attained only by the one who has been forgiven."""
"2320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, deeds are like a vessel: if its lower part is pure (and sound), its upper part also becomes pure, and if its lower part becomes spoiled, its upper part also becomes spoiled."""
"2321","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Imam (leader or ruler) is but a shield behind which fighting is done."""
"2322","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Imam (ruler) is but a shield behind which fighting is done and by means of which protection (from the enemy) is sought. So if he commands the fear of Allah and acts with justice and fairness, he will have a reward for that (deed), and if he commands something other than that, he will bear its sin."""
"2323","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Buying and selling is valid only with mutual consent."""
"2324","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The religion is entirely sincere goodwill (and sincerity)."""
"2325","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Usury (riba) is only in deferment (that is, delay in payment and an increase for the extension of time)."""
"2326","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ill omen, (if it existed,) could only be in three things: in a horse, in a woman and in a house."""
"2327","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Obedience is only in what is good and right."""
"2328","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Knowledge comes only through learning, and forbearance (the habit of restraining anger) is attained through practising patience. Whoever keeps seeking good is granted good, and whoever strives to avoid evil is protected from it."""
"2329","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Water (that is, the obligation of ritual bath (ghusl)) is only because of water (that is, the emission of semen with desire)."""
"2330","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gatherings (their conversations and secrets) are only a trust."""
"2331","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Madinah is but like a furnace: it expels its impurities (bad people) and refines its pure ones (righteous people)."""
"2332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People are but like a hundred camels, among which you can hardly find a single one fit for riding."""
"2333","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Women are but the counterparts (equals) of men (in rulings and circumstances)."""
"2334","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Maintenance and housing are (due) to a woman only when her husband has the right to take her back."""
"2335","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Witr prayer is (prescribed) only at night."""
"2336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Wala' (the right to inherit from a freed slave) belongs only to the one who sets the slave free."""
"2337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to perform ablution (wudu) only when I stand up to pray."""
"2338","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am only a human being. When I command you to do something related to your religion, then hold firmly to it, and when I tell you something from my own personal opinion, then (remember that) I too am only a human being."""
"2339","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am merely a human being; I forget just as you forget. So when one of you forgets, let him perform two prostrations (the prostration of forgetfulness) while sitting."""
"2340","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am only a human being. The eye sheds tears and the heart grieves, but we do not say anything with our tongue that would displease our Lord. And by Allah, O Ibrahim, we are deeply grieved at your parting."""
"2341","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am only a human being like you, and indeed (human) opinion is sometimes wrong and sometimes right. But when I say to you: Allah Almighty has said, then (remember that) I will never tell a lie against Allah."""
"2342","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am only a human being, and you bring your disputes to me. Perhaps one of you may be more eloquent (and clever) in presenting his argument than the other, and I judge in his favour according to what I hear from him. So whoever I judge to have the right of another Muslim (while in reality it is not his right), it is in truth a piece of the Fire of Hell; now let him take it if he wishes, or leave it."""
"2343","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am only a human being, and I have made a condition (covenant) with my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, that whichever servant among the Muslims I say something harsh to or rebuke, that it becomes a means of purification and reward for him."""
"2344","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am merely a treasurer (one who distributes), and in reality the only Giver is Allah. So whoever I give a gift to with a willing heart, blessing is placed in it for him, and whoever I give because of his greed and excessive asking, he is like the one who eats but his stomach is never filled (that is, he gets no blessing in that wealth)."""
"2345","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am nothing but a mercy, sent as a gift (from Allah to the people of the world)."""
"2346","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am to you in the position of a father, teaching you (the etiquettes of the religion). So when one of you goes to relieve himself, let him neither face the Qiblah nor turn his back towards it, and let him not clean himself (istinja) with his right hand."""
"2347","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In truth, I am only a conveyor (of Allah's message), and it is Allah alone who guides; and I am merely a distributor, while the One who gives (in reality) is Allah alone."""
"2348","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What destroyed those before you was that when a noble (and influential) person among them stole, they would let him go, and when a weak (and poor) person among them stole, they would carry out the prescribed punishment (hadd) upon him."""
"2349","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have only been sent to perfect noble character."""
"2350","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have indeed been sent to make things easy (for people), and you have not been sent to make things difficult (to be harsh)."""
"2351","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has sent me as a conveyor (of His commands), and He has not sent me to burden (people) (or to be needlessly harsh)."""
"2352","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your scattering apart like this in the mountain passes and valleys (when making camp during a journey) is indeed from Satan."""
"2353","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best repayment of a loan is simply praise (of the lender) and settling it (on time and in a good manner)."""
"2354","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seeking permission (before entering someone's house) has in fact been prescribed because of the eyes (to protect them from seeing what is not permitted)."""
"2355","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam has been made a shield (as it were). So when he prays sitting, all of you pray sitting; and when he says 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him), then say 'Allahumma rabbana lakal-hamd' (O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs all praise). For when the words of the people of the earth coincide with the words of the people of the heavens (the angels) (at that moment), his (the follower's) previous sins are forgiven."""
"2356","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam has been appointed only so that he may be followed. So when he prays standing, you too pray standing; and if he prays sitting, you too pray sitting. And do not remain standing while he is sitting, as the people of Persia do with their great men (out of reverence)."""
"2357","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam has been appointed only so that he may be followed. So when he says the takbir, you too say the takbir; when he raises (his head from bowing), you too raise yours; when he says 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him), then say 'Allahumma rabbana wa lakal-hamd' (O Allah, our Lord, and to You belongs all praise); when he prostrates, you prostrate; and when he prays sitting, all of you (too) pray sitting."""
"2358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam has been appointed only so that he may be followed. So when he says the takbir, you too say the takbir; when he recites, listen in silence (attentively); and when he says 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him), then say 'Rabbana lakal-hamd' (Our Lord, to You belongs all praise)."""
"2359","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam has been appointed only so that he may be followed. So when he says the takbir, you too say the takbir; when he recites, remain silent; when he says 'Not of those who have earned anger, nor of those who go astray' [Surah al-Fatihah: 7], say: Amin; when he bows, you bow; when he says 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him), then say 'Allahumma rabbana wa lakal-hamd' (O Allah, our Lord, and to You belongs all praise); when he prostrates, you too prostrate; and when he prays sitting, you too pray sitting."""
"2360","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam has been appointed only so that he may be followed, so do not differ from him (in his actions). When he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he says 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him), then say 'Rabbana lakal-hamd' (Our Lord, to You belongs all praise); when he prostrates, prostrate; and when he prays sitting, all of you together pray sitting."""
"2361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty has given me a choice, and He said: 'Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them; even if you ask forgiveness for them seventy times' [Surah at-Tawbah: 80]. So I will ask forgiveness for them more than seventy times."""
"2362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That was indeed Jibril (peace be upon him). I have never seen him in the (original) form in which he was created except on these two occasions. I saw him descending from the sky, his immense size filling the space between the heavens and the earth."""
"2363","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is only (the blood of) a vein (that is, istihadah). So watch carefully: when the days of your menstrual period come, do not pray; and when the days of your period have passed, purify yourself, then pray during the interval between one period and the next."""
"2364","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Khidr was called Khidr (green) because he once sat on a white patch of dry grass (or ground), and suddenly it began to sway beneath him, turned green."""
"2365","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The heart (qalb) is called qalb because of its turning over and over (taqallub). The likeness of the heart is that of a bird's feather in a barren plain, caught at the root of a tree, which the wind keeps turning over, top to bottom."""
"2366","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fatimah is but a part of my body; whatever hurts her hurts me, and whatever wearies her wearies me."""
"2367","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It would have been enough for you (in tayammum) simply to strike the ground with both your hands, then wipe your face and both your palms with them."""
"2368","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The likeness of a good companion and a bad companion is that of one who carries musk and one who blows on a blacksmith's bellows. The one carrying musk will either give you some as a gift, or you will buy some from him, or (at the very least) you will find a pleasant fragrance from him. And the one blowing the bellows will either burn your clothes, or (at the very least) you will certainly find a foul smell from him."""
"2369","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The likeness of one who prays with the hair of his head tied in a knot (at the back) is that of one who prays with his hands bound."""
"2370","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The likeness of the believer when fever or some pain afflicts him is that of a piece of iron which is put into the fire, so all its rust and impurity is removed and its pure part remains."""
"2371","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The likeness of the one who goes early to the prayer is that of one who offers a camel as a sacrifice in the way of Allah; then the one who comes after him is like one who offers a cow; then the one who comes after him is like one who offers a ram; then the one who comes after him is like one who gives a hen in the way of Allah; then the one who comes after him is like one who gives a single egg in charity."""
"2372","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The likeness of the companion of the Qur'an (the one who memorises it) is that of the owner of camels tied with ropes: if he keeps looking after them (and watching over them), he will keep hold of them, and if he lets them loose, they will run off."""
"2373","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the soul of the believer, in the form of a bird, keeps eating (or hanging) among the trees of Paradise, until Allah Almighty returns it to its body on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those before you were destroyed only because of their differing over their (revealed) Book."""
"2375","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women began wearing these (false hair),"" meaning a lock of hair."
"2376","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, they (people) are in two handfuls: one handful (of people) will go to Hell and one handful (of people) will go to Paradise."""
"2377","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This (waiting period, 'iddah) is only four months and ten days, whereas in the Days of Ignorance your state was such that a woman among you would throw a piece of dung at the end of the year (when leaving her waiting period)."""
"2378","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is only the repentance of a prophet (the prostration of it),"" (by this he (peace and blessings be upon him) meant the prostration of Surah Sad)."
"2379","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection people will be raised according to their intentions."""
"2380","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will only come out because of an intense rage that will seize him."""
"2381","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty shows mercy only to those of His servants who are merciful."""
"2382","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Only three kinds of people may farm: a man who has his own land and cultivates it; a man who has been given land as a gift (on loan) and cultivates what he has been given; and a man who rents land (on lease) for gold or silver (that is, cash)."""
"2383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The urine of a baby girl is to be washed, whereas water is only to be sprinkled on the urine of a baby boy."""
"2384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For any one of you, only as much wealth in this world should suffice as a traveller's provisions for the journey."""
"2385","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is enough for you simply to pour three handfuls of water over your head, then pour water over the rest of your body, and you will be purified."""
"2386","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of amassing wealth, all that suffices you is a servant and a mount for the way of Allah (jihad)."""
"2387","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In this world, only the one who has no share in the Hereafter wears silk."""
"2388","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah Almighty helps this Ummah because of its weak ones, through the blessing of their supplications, their prayers and their sincerity."""
"2389","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a man has followed us who was not with us when we were invited. So if you permit him, he may come in."""
"2390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it has been revealed to me that you will surely be tested in the graves."""
"2391","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, every human being among the children of Adam has been created with three hundred and sixty joints. So whoever proclaims the greatness of Allah, praises Allah, declares the oneness of Allah, glorifies Allah, seeks forgiveness from Allah, removes a stone, a thorn or a bone from people's path, and enjoins good or forbids evil, and makes all these deeds equal to the number of those three hundred and sixty joints, then indeed he will reach the evening of that day having removed himself from the Fire of Hell."""
"2392","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there will soon be division and severe dissension. When that happens, break your sword, make yourself a sword of wood, and sit in your house until a sinful hand (comes to kill) you or your death comes to you."""
"2393","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there will soon be many trials and evils. So whoever intends to divide the affairs of this Ummah while it is united (upon one leader), strike him with the sword, whoever he may be."""
"2394","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there will soon be rulers who will delay the prayers beyond their appointed times. So listen! Pray your prayer at its time, then go to them. If they have already prayed, you will have secured your prayer; and if (they are praying), pray with them as well, and it will be a voluntary (nafl) prayer for you."""
"2395","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there will soon be rulers appointed over you, some of whose deeds you will recognise (as in accordance with the Shari'ah) and some of which you will disapprove of (as contrary to the Shari'ah). So whoever objected (to their evil deeds) is absolved, and whoever disliked them is safe; but the one who is ruined is the one who was pleased (with their deeds) and followed them."""
"2396","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there will soon be people in this Ummah who will transgress the limits in purification (ablution and ritual bath) and in supplication."""
"2397","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, after me men will take charge of your affairs who will make known to you things you disapprove of (because they are contrary to the Shariah), and they will disapprove of the things you know (to be right). So there is no obedience to one who disobeys Allah; therefore do not go astray regarding your Lord."""
"2398","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Paradise and Hell were presented to me. Paradise was brought so close to me that I reached out to take a cluster of fruit from it, but my hand could not reach it. And Hell was presented to me, and I began to draw back for fear that it would engulf me. In it I saw a tall black woman of the tribe of Himyar being punished on account of a cat of hers which she had tied up; she neither gave it food and water nor let it go so that it could eat the vermin of the earth. And in that same Hell I saw Abu Thumamah Amr bin Malik dragging his intestines in the Fire. People used to say: The sun and the moon are eclipsed only for the death of some great man. Indeed, these two are two of the signs of Allah which He shows you, so when they are eclipsed, pray until they become clear."""
"2399","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, he (Abu Talib) is in a shallow part of the Fire of Hell, and had it not been for me (interceding on his behalf), he would have been in the lowest depth of Hell."""
"2400","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there has come to your father that (death) from which Allah Almighty will not spare anyone, so that they appear on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2401","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the women who join (other hair to their own hair) have been cursed."""
"2402","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No prophet has ever had his soul taken until he is shown his place in Paradise; then he is given the choice (between remaining in this world or departing for the Hereafter)."""
"2403","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There was no prophet before me except that it was a duty upon him to guide his nation to the good that he knew for them and to warn them of the evil that he knew for them. And indeed, the well-being of this nation of yours has been placed in its early period, and its later generations will be struck by severe trials and by matters that you will disapprove of. Trials will come, one of them making the other seem light (that is, each later trial will be more severe than the one before). A trial will come and the believer will say: This will be my ruin; then it will pass. Then another trial will come and the believer will cry out: This is my ruin, this is it. So whoever among you loves to be kept away from the Fire of Hell and admitted into Paradise, let his death come to him while he believes in Allah and the Last Day, and let him treat people the way he would love to be treated. And whoever pledges allegiance to an imam (a leader of the Muslims), giving him his hand and accepting him with the full consent of his heart, let him obey him as much as he is able. Then if another comes disputing with (and rebelling against) him (the leader), strike the neck of that other one."""
"2404","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing prevented me from returning your (greeting of) salam except that I was praying."""
"2405","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing prevented me from returning your (greeting of) salam except that I was not in a state of ablution (wudu)."""
"2406","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had anything new (or any change) occurred in the ruling of the prayer, I would certainly have informed you of it. But the fact is that I am a human being like you; I forget just as you forget. So when I forget, remind me. And when one of you is in doubt in his prayer, let him strive for what is correct and complete his prayer on that (correct assumption), then let him make two prostrations (the prostration of forgetfulness)."""
"2407","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection a huge, fat and heavy man will be brought, yet in the sight of Allah Almighty he will not weigh even as much as the wing of a mosquito."""
"2408","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is not a medicine; rather, it is itself a disease."" (By this he (peace and blessings be upon him) meant wine.)"
"2409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there is nothing between the heavens and the earth except that it knows that I am the Messenger of Allah, except the disobedient among the jinn and mankind."""
"2410","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no negligence (or sin) in sleep (when a prayer is missed); negligence is only in (being heedless while) awake. So when one of you forgets to pray a prayer or sleeps through it, let him pray it when he remembers it, and let him also pray that prayer at its appointed time on the following day."""
"2411","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not befitting for a prophet to enter a house that has been adorned (with pictures and decorations)."""
"2412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not befitting for a prophet to make signals (with his eyes)."""
"2413","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, among the people there is none who has done me more favours with his person and his wealth than Abu Bakr bin Abi Quhafah. And if I were to take anyone from among the people as my khalil (intimate friend), I would have taken Abu Bakr, but the bond of Islam (Islamic brotherhood) is superior. Close off every small door opening into this mosque, except the small door of Abu Bakr."""
"2414","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there is no Arabian horse except that it is permitted, at every true dawn, to make two supplications. It says: 'Allahumma innaka khawwaltani man khawwaltani min bani Adam, faj'alni min ahabbi ahlihi wa malihi ilayh' (O Allah, You have given me to whomever You have given me among the children of Adam, so make me the most beloved to him of his family and his wealth)."""
"2415","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a kind of veil (at times) comes over my heart too, and indeed I seek the forgiveness of Allah Almighty a hundred times a day."""
"2416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Anger is shown towards me (or displeasure is expressed at me) because I do not find anything to give him. Whoever among you asks (people) while he has an uqiyah (of silver) or its equivalent in wealth has certainly asked importunately (going beyond the limit)."""
"2417","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever stands (in the night prayer) with the imam until the imam finishes (completing the prayer), the reward of standing in prayer for the whole night is recorded for him."""
"2418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, whoever does not ask of Allah Almighty, Allah becomes angry with him."""
"2419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a walimah (wedding feast) is necessary for a wedding (marriage)."""
"2420","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prayer of any one of you is not complete until he performs ablution thoroughly, as Allah Almighty has commanded him: he washes his face and his hands up to the elbows, wipes over his head, and washes his feet up to the ankles. Then he declares the greatness of Allah (takbir), praises Him and glorifies Him, and recites whatever is easy for him of the Qur'an, of what Allah has taught him and permitted him. Then he says the takbir and bows, placing his hands on his knees and remaining (in bowing) until all his joints are at rest and relaxed. Then he says 'Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him) and stands up straight until every bone settles into its place and he straightens his back. Then he says the takbir and prostrates, placing his forehead firmly on the ground until his joints are at rest and relaxed. Then he says the takbir and raises his head, sitting upright on his seat and keeping his back straight. Then he says the takbir and prostrates until he places his face firmly (on the ground) and is at rest. The prayer of any one of you is not complete until he does this."""
"2421","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A nation in which the weak cannot take his right without fear and hesitation will never attain purity (and blessing)."""
"2422","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, none but a believer will love you, and none but a hypocrite will hate you. (He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him).)"""
"2423","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, none shall enter Paradise except a submitting (Muslim) soul, and indeed Allah Almighty supports this religion even through a wicked (sinful) man."""
"2424","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, none shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, and the days of Mina (the days of Tashriq) are days of eating and drinking."""
"2425","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is not fitting for anyone other than the Lord of the Fire (Allah) to punish (anyone) with fire."""
"2426","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is not befitting for a prophet to make secret signals with the corner of his eye (that is, to have treachery in his eye)."""
"2427","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, from the progeny of this man there will come forth a people who will recite the Book of Allah with great fluency, but it will not go beyond their throats. They will pass swiftly out of the religion just as an arrow passes through the game. If I were to find them, I would certainly kill them as the people of Thamud were killed."""
"2428","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is a safe sanctuary; indeed, it is a safe sanctuary. (By this he (peace and blessings be upon him) meant Madinah.)"""
"2429","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, after me there will be rulers over you whom certain (worldly) matters will distract from offering the prayer at its appointed time, until its time passes. So pray the prayer at its proper time. A man asked: If I also catch the prayer with them, should I pray with them as well? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, if you wish (then pray)."""
"2430","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, there will soon be trials. Listen! Then there will be a trial in which the one lying down will be better than the one sitting, the one sitting will be better than the one standing, the one standing will be better than the one walking, and the one walking will be better than the one rushing towards it. Beware! When it descends or occurs, whoever has camels, let him go to his camels; whoever has sheep and goats, let him go to his sheep and goats; and whoever has land, let him go to his land. And whoever has none of these, let him take his sword and strike its edge with a stone to break it (so that it cannot be used to kill anyone), then let him save himself if he is able to. O Allah, have I conveyed (Your message)? O Allah, have I conveyed (Your message)?"""
"2431","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be a trial in which the one sitting will be better than the one standing, the one standing will be better than the one walking, and the one walking will be better than the one rushing towards it. (The Companions) asked: What do you think if someone forces his way into my house (to kill me)? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then be like the son of Adam (Habil, the wronged one) (and do not raise your hand to kill)."""
"2432","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will be trial, division and severe disagreement. When that happens, take your sword to Mount Uhud (or any rock) and strike it until it breaks, then sit in your house until a sinful hand (comes to kill) you or your death comes to you."""
"2433","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This (prayer that I have just prayed) was a prayer of hope and fear. In it I asked Allah Almighty for three things; He granted me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to bring upon you a (general, destructive) punishment such as befell the nations before you, and He granted me that. And I asked Him not to let an external enemy overpower your heartland and destroy it from the root, and He granted me that too. And I asked Him not to divide you into different factions and make some of you taste the might and warfare of others (that is, that there be no civil war among you), but He withheld that from me."""
"2434","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, this is Tabah (Madinah); it expels (evil) people just as fire removes the impurities of iron."""
"2435","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it (Zamzam water) is greatly blessed; it is excellent nourishment for the one who eats it and a cure for sickness."""
"2436","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it is not a medicine; rather, it is itself a disease. (By this he (peace and blessings be upon him) meant wine.)"""
"2437","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it (the cat) is not najis (impure); it is only one of those, male and female, who go about among you a great deal."""
"2438","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, it (Zamzam water) is greatly blessed; it is excellent nourishment for the one who eats it."""
"2439","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""They (the shooting stars) are not thrown for the death or the life of anyone. Rather, when our Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, decrees a matter, the angels who bear the Throne glorify Him. (Then the other angels ask them:) What did your Lord say? And they inform them of what He said. Then the inhabitants of the heavens ask one another (in the same way) until the news reaches this lowest (first) heaven. Then the jinn (devils) snatch the news by eavesdropping and pass it on to their friends (the soothsayers of the world), and they (the devils) are pelted (with stars). Whatever they bring exactly as it is (without any addition) is true, but they mix lies into it of their own and add to it."""
"2440","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these two (occupants of the graves) are being punished, and they are not being punished for something (that would have been difficult for them to avoid). One of them did not guard himself against (splashes of) urine, and the other used to go about spreading tales."""
"2441","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these two are being punished, and they are not being punished for something very great (or difficult to avoid). One of them is being punished on account of urine (not guarding against its splashes), and the other is being punished for backbiting."""
"2442","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, they (the people of the earlier nations) used to name (their children) after their prophets and the righteous people who had come before them."""
"2443","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, they will all be raised (on the Day of Resurrection) according to their own intentions."""
"2444","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, these people force me to choose between their asking me excessively (importunately and harshly) or (if I do not give) their declaring me a miser, and (you know that) I am not a miser."""
"2445","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I declare before Allah my innocence of having a khalil (intimate friend) from among you. Indeed, Allah Almighty has taken me as His khalil just as He took Ibrahim (peace be upon him) as His khalil. And if I were to take anyone from my nation as a khalil, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a khalil. Beware! Those who came before you used to take the graves of their prophets and righteous people as places of prostration (mosques). Listen! Do not take graves as places of prostration; indeed, I strictly forbid you from doing that."""
"2446","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I narrate a hadith (a saying) to you, so let whoever among you is present convey it to the one who is absent (not here)."""
"2447","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I solemnly warn you regarding the right of the two weak ones (that is, I declare violating their right to be forbidden): the orphan and the woman."""
"2448","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I declare the area between the two lava fields of Madinah (the eastern and western Harrah) a sanctuary, such that its thorny trees may not be cut nor its game hunted. Madinah is far better for them, if only they knew. No one leaves it out of aversion to it except that Allah Almighty brings into it, in his place, someone better than him. And no one remains steadfast through its hardship and difficulty except that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection. And no one intends evil against the people of Madinah except that Allah Almighty will melt him in the Fire as lead melts, or as salt dissolves in water."""
"2449","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I see what you do not see and I hear what you do not hear. The sky is creaking (under the weight of the angels), and it has every right to creak, for there is not a space in it the size of four fingers except that an angel is placing his forehead there in prostration before Allah Almighty. By Allah! If you knew what I know, you would surely laugh little and weep much, you would not take pleasure in women on your beds, and you would go out (leaving your homes) to the open plains and roads, beseeching and crying out to Allah."""
"2450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I see that you love sheep and the open country (the desert). So when you are with your sheep or in your open country and you call the adhan for the prayer, raise your voice in the call, for no jinn, human, stone or anything else within the reach of the mu'adhdhin's voice hears it except that it will surely testify for him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2451","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then I was made to forget it. So seek it in the odd nights of the last ten. And indeed I saw (in a dream) that I was prostrating in water and mud on the morning of it (Laylat al-Qadr)."""
"2452","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I give (more wealth) to some men who have only recently come out of disbelief (that is, new Muslims), in order to win their hearts. Are you not pleased that the people go away with wealth while you return to your tents (and homes) with the Messenger of Allah? By Allah! What you are returning with is far better than what they are returning with. Surely, after me you will see others being given strong preference over you, so be patient (in the face of this injustice) until you meet Allah and His Messenger, for indeed I will be your forerunner (the one who receives you) at the Pond of Kawthar."""
"2453","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I give Quraysh (more from the spoils of war) in order to win their hearts, because they have only recently come out of the Jahiliyyah."""
"2454","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I give (wealth) to some people whose wavering and impatience I fear, and I entrust other people to the goodness and self-sufficiency (contentment) that Allah has placed in their hearts; among these (patient and content) people is Amr bin Taghlib."""
"2455","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I suffer from fever as severely as two men among you (together) suffer."""
"2456","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am your forerunner (the one who will receive you at the Pond of Kawthar), and I am a witness over you. Surely, your meeting place with me is the Pond, and by Allah! I am looking at my Pond from here right now. And indeed I have been given the keys to the treasures of the earth. And by Allah! I do not fear for you that you will associate partners with Allah after me, but I do fear the world for you, that you will fall into (love and greed for) it and start competing and vying with one another."""
"2457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am leaving among you two successors (weighty things): one is the Book of Allah, a rope stretched out (or extended) between the heaven and the earth, and the other is my family, that is, the people of my household. And surely the two will never separate from each other until they come to me at the Pond of Kawthar."""
"2458","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am leaving among you something which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray after me; one of the two is greater and more exalted than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope stretched from the heaven to the earth, and my family, that is, the people of my household. And the two will never separate from each other until they come to me at the Pond of Kawthar. So consider how you will succeed me in fulfilling your duties toward them both."""
"2459","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I have told you so much (in detail) about the Dajjal that I began to fear you might not understand (by mixing these things up). Surely, the Masih al-Dajjal is a short man, bow-legged, with very curly hair, and one-eyed, one of whose eyes is completely wiped out (flat), neither protruding outward nor sunken inward. So if the matter becomes confusing for you (on hearing his claim to divinity), know that your Lord is not one-eyed, and that you will never see your Lord until you die."""
"2460","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I have declared the area between the two lava fields of Madinah a sanctuary (sacred), just as Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah a sanctuary."""
"2461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I came out to inform you about Laylat al-Qadr, but so-and-so and so-and-so (two men) quarrelled with each other, so it (the knowledge of its exact date) was taken away, and perhaps that is better for you. So seek it on the seventh, the ninth and the fifth (odd nights of the last ten)."""
"2462","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am going to mention a matter to you, and there is no harm upon you if you do not hasten until you have consulted your parents, for Allah Almighty has said: 'O Prophet, say to your wives' up to His words 'great' [Surah al-Ahzab: 28-29] (O Prophet, say to your wives, up to: and if you desire Allah, His Messenger and the home of the Hereafter, then indeed Allah has prepared for those of you who do good a great reward)."""
"2463","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While I was in the Asr prayer I remembered some pieces (or particles) of gold that we had with us, and I disliked that they should remain overnight (that is, remain until morning), so I ordered that they be distributed."""
"2464","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tomorrow I am riding out to the Jews, so whoever of you goes with me should not greet them with salam first, and if they greet you with salam, then say (in reply): 'Wa alaykum' (and upon you too)."""
"2465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw in a dream as if Jibril (peace be upon him) were at my head and Mika'il (peace be upon him) at my feet, one of them saying to his companion: 'Strike a parable for him.' So he said: 'Listen, may your ear hear, and may your heart understand. The parable of you and your ummah is like that of a king who took a house, then built a dwelling in it, then set out a feast in it, then sent a messenger inviting people to his food. Some people accepted the messenger's invitation and some ignored him. Allah is the King, the house is Islam, the dwelling is Paradise, and you, O Muhammad, are the messenger: whoever accepts you enters Islam, whoever enters Islam enters Paradise, and whoever enters Paradise attains all its blessings.'"""
"2466","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I prayed a prayer of hope and fear, and I asked my Lord for three things for my ummah; He granted me two and turned one back from me (did not accept it). I asked Him not to set over them an enemy from other than themselves, and He granted me that; I asked Him not to destroy them by drowning, and He granted me that too; and I asked Him to end their fighting and mutual enmity among themselves, but He turned that back from me."""
"2467","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will be at the Pond (of Kawthar) so that I may see who among you comes to me, and some people will be pulled away from me, and I will say: 'O Lord, they are from me and from my ummah!' It will be said in reply: 'Do you know what they did after you? By Allah! After you they kept turning back on their heels.'"""
"2468","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am your forerunner at the Pond (of Kawthar). Whoever passes by me will drink, and whoever drinks will never feel thirst again. And surely people will be brought to me whom I will recognise and who will recognise me, then a barrier will be placed between me and them, and I will say: 'They are my own people!' It will be said: 'You do not know what new things (innovations) they introduced after you.' Then I will say: 'Away, away with whoever made changes (in the religion) after me.'"""
"2469","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am your forerunner at the Pond, and its width is like the distance between Aylah and al-Juhfah. Indeed, I do not fear for you that you will associate partners with Allah after me, but I fear the world for you, that you will compete with one another in it, fight one another and be destroyed as those before you were destroyed."""
"2470","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I have had a silver ring made and have had 'Muhammad Rasul Allah' (Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah) engraved on it, so let no one have an engraving made like its engraving."""
"2471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, my body has become heavy, so when I bow, you bow; when I raise my head, you raise your heads; and when I prostrate, you prostrate. Let me never find a man who gets ahead of me in bowing or in prostration."""
"2472","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I disliked remembering Allah Almighty without being in a state of purity."""
"2473","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I had ordered you to burn so-and-so and so-and-so with fire, but none punishes with fire except Allah. So if you capture the two of them, kill them (with the sword)."""
"2474","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I had forbidden you to eat the meat of the sacrificial animals beyond three days; now eat (it yourselves), feed others and store as much as you wish. And I had forbidden you to make nabidh in vessels, namely gourd vessels, pitch-coated vessels, vessels hollowed out of wood and green earthenware jars; now make nabidh in whatever vessel you wish, but avoid every intoxicant. And I had forbidden you to visit graves, so whoever wishes to visit, let him visit, but do not say anything obscene."""
"2475","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I had forbidden you to visit graves; now visit them, so that visiting them may remind you of good. And I had forbidden you to keep the meat of the sacrificial animals after three days; now eat it yourselves and keep as much as you wish. And I had forbidden you to keep drinks in (certain) vessels; now drink from whatever vessel you wish, but do not drink anything intoxicating."""
"2476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I had forbidden you to eat the meat of the sacrificial animals beyond three days so that there would be enough for all of you. Now Allah Almighty has granted abundance, so eat yourselves, give in charity and store it. Indeed, these days are days of eating, drinking and the remembrance of Allah."""
"2477","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I turn in repentance to Allah Almighty seventy times a day."""
"2478","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I enter the prayer intending to make it long, then I hear a child crying, so I shorten my prayer, because I know how deeply distressed his mother becomes at his crying."""
"2479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I see you from behind me just as I see you (in front of me)."""
"2480","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I hope to depart from this world in such a state that none of you will have a claim against me for any wrong I did to him."""
"2481","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I hope that my ummah will not be so helpless before its Lord that He would not grant them a respite of half a day."""
"2482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I hope, if Allah wills, that no one who took part in the Battle of Badr and the Treaty of Hudaybiyah will enter Hell."""
"2483","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I seek forgiveness from Allah Almighty seventy times a day."""
"2484","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I hear a child crying (during the prayer), so I shorten the prayer."""
"2485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I know well the one who will be the last to be taken out of Hell and the last to enter Paradise. A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: 'Present his minor sins to him and put aside his major ones.' Then it will be said to him: 'On such-and-such a day you did such-and-such things, and on such-and-such a day you did such-and-such deeds?' He will say: 'Yes.' He will not be able to deny it, and all the while he will be fearful of his major sins being presented to him. Then it will be said to him: 'For you, in place of every evil deed, there is a good deed.' On hearing this he will say: 'O my Lord, I did some things that I do not see here.'"""
"2486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I recognise the voices of the company of the Ash'aris reciting the Qur'an when they come in at night, and I know their dwellings from the voices of their Qur'an recitation at night, even if I did not see the places where they encamped during the day."""
"2487","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me with salam before I was sent as a prophet."""
"2488","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surely, I give (wealth) to some men and leave those who are dearer to me than them (and give them nothing), out of fear that they (the ones who are given, if they were not given) might be thrown on their faces into Hell."""
"2489","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surely, I know well the one who will be the last to come out of Hell and the last to enter Paradise. He will be a man who comes out of Hell crawling, and Allah Almighty will say to him: 'Go and enter Paradise.' He will come to Paradise and it will seem to him that it is full. He will go back and say: 'O my Lord, I found it full!' Allah Almighty will say to him (again): 'Go and enter Paradise, for indeed you have the like of the world and ten times as much besides.' The man will say in astonishment: 'Are You mocking me, while You are the True King?'"""
"2490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry with me. When you are pleased with me, you say: 'No, by the Lord of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)!' And when you are angry with me, you say: 'No, by the Lord of Ibrahim (peace be upon him)!'"""
"2491","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I know a word which, if this (angry) man were to say it, what he is feeling would leave him. If he says 'A'udhu billahi min ash-shaytan ir-rajim' (I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan), his present state will go away."""
"2492","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I know a word which no servant says at the time of his death except that it becomes a light for his record of deeds, and surely his body and his soul find comfort and ease through that word at the time of death."""
"2493","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surely, I stand for the prayer intending to make it long, but then I hear a child crying, so I shorten my prayer, disliking to cause hardship to the child's mother."""
"2494","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I also joke (in good humour), but I say nothing except what is true and right."""
"2495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I warn you about him (the Dajjal), and there has been no prophet who did not warn his people about him; Nuh (peace be upon him) too warned his people about him. But I will tell you something about him that no prophet told his people: that he (the Dajjal) will be one-eyed, whereas Allah Almighty is certainly not one-eyed."""
"2496","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I see the devils among the jinn and mankind fleeing in fear of Umar."""
"2497","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I return to my family and find a date fallen on my bed, so I pick it up to eat it, but then I fear that it may be a date of charity (sadaqah), so I leave it."""
"2498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection I will be standing at the center of my Pond; I will push the people back for the sake of the people of Yemen and drive them away with my staff until the water flows for the people of Yemen."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about the width of the Pond, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Its extent is as far as from this place of mine to Amman. Its drink is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Two spouts pour into it from Paradise, supplying it with water; one of them is of gold and the other of silver."""
"2499","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I am not like you; I spend the night in such a state that my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."""
"2500","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I will be your forerunner (the one who arrives before you) at the Pond of Kawthar, so let none of you come to me in such a state that he is being driven away from me as a stray camel is driven away. I will say: 'What is the matter?' And it will be said to me: 'You do not know what innovations they invented after you.' So I will say: 'Away with them, away with them!'"""
"2501","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I was not sent as one who curses."""
"2502","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I was not sent as one who curses; rather, I was sent as a mercy in its entirety."""
"2503","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I was not commanded to search out the secrets of people's hearts, nor to cut open their bellies to look inside."""
"2504","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I forgot to instruct you to cover the two horns (of the sacrificial ram), for there should not be anything in the house that distracts the one who is praying."""
"2505","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I have been forbidden from accepting the gifts and presents of the polytheists."""
"2506","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I have been forbidden from killing those who pray."""
"2507","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah! Allah willing, whenever I swear an oath about something and then see greater good in something else, I expiate my oath and do that which is better."""
"2508","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah! I have not stood in this place to encourage you towards anything or to frighten you; rather, Tamim ad-Dari came to me and gave me a piece of news which, out of joy and delight, kept me from my midday rest (qaylulah), so I wished to share with you the joy of your Prophet. Listen! Tamim ad-Dari told me that a contrary wind drove them to an island they did not know, so they sat in the small boats of the ship until they came out onto the island. There they encountered a creature that was very hairy. They asked it: 'What are you?' It replied: 'I am al-Jassasah.' They said: 'Give us some news.' It said: 'I will neither tell you anything nor ask you anything; but go to this monastery which you can see, for in it there is a man who is eagerly waiting for you to tell him something and for him to tell you something.' So they went to him, and when they entered, there was an old man bound with extremely firm fetters, showing intense grief and great distress. He asked them: 'Where have you come from?' They replied: 'From Syria (Sham).' He asked: 'How are the Arabs?' They said: 'We are people of the Arabs; what are you asking about?' He said: 'How is this man who has appeared among you?' They said: 'Well; he fought against a people and Allah granted him victory over them. Today their affair is united: their God is one and their religion is one.' He asked: 'How is the spring of Zughar?' They said: 'Very well; people irrigate their crops from it and drink water from it.' He asked: 'How are the well of Amman and the date palms of Baysan?' They said: 'They bear fruit every year.' He asked: 'How is the Lake of Tiberias?' They said: 'Its banks are overflowing because of the abundance of water.' At this he heaved three heavy sighs and then said: 'If I am freed from this captivity of mine, I will not leave any land without treading it with these two feet of mine, except Taybah (Madinah), for I will have no power over it.' Here my joy reaches its peak. This is Taybah, and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul! There is not a single road in it, narrow or wide, nor any plain or mountain, except that upon it an angel stands guard with his sword drawn until the Day of Resurrection."""
"2509","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, even though I jest (joke) with you, I say nothing but the truth."""
"2510","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I neither break a covenant nor imprison envoys."""
"2511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I do not know how long I will remain among you, so after me follow these two (persons), namely Abu Bakr and Umar; hold firmly to the way of Ammar; and whatever Ibn Mas'ud narrates to you, accept it as true."""
"2512","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I do not bear witness to oppression (and injustice)."""
"2513","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I do not shake hands with (non-mahram) women."""
"2514","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I do not accept the gift of a polytheist."""
"2515","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I forbid every intoxicant that (by clouding the mind) makes a person heedless of the prayer."""
"2516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I forbid you from falsehood (and false speech)."""
"2517","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I forbid you from fasting on two days: Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha."""
"2518","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I forbid you even a small amount of anything of which a large amount intoxicates."""
"2519","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Make the blood flow (that is, slaughter) with whatever (sharp instrument) you wish, and mention the name of Allah over it."""
"2520","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trim the moustaches closely and let the beards grow (that is, leave them untouched)."""
"2521","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Throne of the Most Merciful shook at the death (that is, the passing) of Sa'd bin Mu'adh."""
"2522","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Satirize the polytheists (compose verses condemning them), for indeed the Holy Spirit (that is, Jibril (peace be upon him)) is with you."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said this to Sayyiduna Hassan (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2523","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Satirize Quraysh, for it (poetry) is harder (and more painful) for them than a volley of arrows."""
"2524","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pour over me seven waterskins whose mouths have not yet been untied (that is, freshly filled), so that I may (bathe, go out and) give the people some instructions."""
"2525","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise will be without body hair, beardless, and with kohl-lined eyes. Their youth will never end, nor will their clothes ever wear out."""
"2526","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise will be in one hundred and twenty rows, of which eighty (80) rows will be from this (my) Ummah, and the remaining forty from all the other nations."""
"2527","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The person of Paradise is the one whose ears Allah Almighty fills with the good reputation and praise that people speak of him while he is listening, and the person of Hell is the one whose ears Allah Almighty fills with the evil that people speak of him while he is listening."""
"2528","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of the Qur'an (that is, those who recite it and act upon it) are the people of Allah and His special, close servants."""
"2529","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Hell are every harsh-tempered, stingy, gluttonous and arrogant person, and the people of Paradise are those who are weak and overpowered (oppressed) (in the eyes of the people of the world)."""
"2530","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Yemen have the softest hearts and the most tender souls, and they are the most obedient."""
"2531","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lowest degree of usury (riba) is like a man (Allah forbid) committing fornication with his own mother, and the greatest usury is a person's unjust attack with his tongue upon the honor and dignity of his Muslim brother."""
"2532","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one with the lightest punishment among the people of Hell will be Abu Talib; he will be made to wear two shoes of fire, from the heat of which his brain will boil."""
"2533","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the one with the lightest punishment among the people of Hell will be a man under the soles of whose feet two embers of fire will be placed, from the heat of which his brain will boil (like a cooking pot)."""
"2534","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If Allah Almighty has removed mercy from your heart, do I have any power over that?"""
"2535","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you really do that ('azl, coitus interruptus)? There is no harm upon you if you do not do it, for any soul that Allah Almighty has decreed to come into being will certainly come into being."""
"2536","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pray the Witr before (the time of) Fajr (begins)."""
"2537","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perform the Witr before the dawn breaks."""
"2538","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people of the Qur'an! Perform the Witr, for indeed Allah Almighty is Witr (odd, that is, One) and He loves what is odd."""
"2539","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The firmest handhold (that is, bond) of faith is to be someone's ally for the sake of Allah, to hold enmity towards someone for the sake of Allah, to love for the sake of Allah, and to hate for the sake of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"2540","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Talhah made (Paradise) obligatory (for himself) when he did for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) the kindness that he did (that is, during the Battle of Uhud he became a shield to save the life of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him))."""
"2541","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I advise you to feel shy before Allah Almighty just as you feel shy before a righteous man of your people."""
"2542","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I advise you not to be one who curses a great deal."""
"2543","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I advise you to have taqwa (mindfulness) of Allah Almighty, for it is the foundation of everything; hold fast to jihad, for it is the monasticism of Islam; and hold fast to the remembrance of Allah Almighty and the recitation of the Qur'an, for it is your repose in the heavens and the cause of your mention on earth."""
"2544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I advise you to fear Allah Almighty in all your affairs, hidden and open; when you commit an evil deed, then (immediately) do a good deed; never ask anyone for anything; do not take anyone's trust into your keeping; and do not judge between two people."""
"2545","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I advise you to fear Allah Almighty and to say the takbir (Allahu Akbar) upon every elevated place."""
"2546","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I advise you concerning (the rights of) my Companions, then those who will come after them; then lying will spread, until a man will swear an oath without being asked to swear, and a witness will testify without being asked to testify. Beware! Let no man ever be alone with a (non-mahram) woman, for the third of them is Satan. It is obligatory upon you to hold fast to the Jama'ah (the united body of the Muslims), and beware of division, for Satan is with the one who is alone and he stays farther away from two. So whoever desires the best, central part of Paradise, let him hold fast to the Jama'ah. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his bad deed, that is the complete believer."""
"2547","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I enjoin you regarding the Ansar, for they are my confidants and my special people. They have fulfilled the responsibility that was upon them, and now what is due to them remains. So accept good from the righteous among them and overlook the wrongdoers among them."""
"2548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I enjoin you regarding the neighbour (fulfilling his rights)."""
"2549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I enjoin you to have taqwa (mindfulness) of Allah Almighty and to listen and obey (the ruler), even if an Abyssinian slave is made ruler over you. For whoever among you lives after me will see much disagreement, so hold to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided Caliphs, who are guided by Allah. Hold fast to it and bite onto it with your molars, and beware of newly invented matters (innovations) in the religion, for every new matter is an innovation and every innovation is misguidance."""
"2550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fulfil your vow."""
"2551","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fulfil your vow; however, it is not permissible to fulfil any vow that involves disobedience to Allah Almighty, nor is it valid to vow something that the son of Adam does not own."""
"2552","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O son of al-Khattab! Do you have any doubt?! These are people whose good things have been hastened for them in the life of this world."""
"2553","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fulfil the alliances of the Days of Ignorance, for Islam has only added to their firmness; but do not create new (such) alliances (pacts) in Islam."""
"2554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is it so that whenever we set out in the path of Allah (for jihad), one of them (the hypocrites) stays behind, making sounds like a billy goat (giving way to lust), and leads one of them (the women) astray by giving her a little milk?! By Allah! If I get hold of any one of them, I will certainly make an exemplary punishment of him."""
"2555","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Does every one of you have two garments?"""
"2556","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Give a wedding feast (walimah), even if only by slaughtering a single sheep."""
"2557","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The friends of Allah Almighty are those who, when they are seen, Allah Almighty is remembered."""
"2558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know what befell a man of the Children of Israel? They were people who, when drops of urine fell on them, would cut that part off with shears. Then a companion of theirs forbade them from doing this, and he was punished in his grave."""
"2559","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not know what covenant I have made with my Lord? I said: O Allah, I am only a human being, so whichever Muslim I curse or revile, make that (word) a means of purification and reward for him."""
"2560","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first of the (major) signs (of the Hour) is the rising of the sun from its west."""
"2561","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first of the people to perish will be Quraysh, and the first of Quraysh to perish will be the people of my household."""
"2562","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first army of my Ummah that will set sail on the sea for jihad has made Paradise obligatory for itself, and the first army of my Ummah that will campaign against the city of Caesar (Constantinople) is forgiven."""
"2563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first two disputants to present their case on the Day of Resurrection will be two neighbours."""
"2564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first group to enter Paradise will be radiant like the moon on the night of the full moon, and the second group will shine like the most beautiful glittering star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives, and each wife will be wearing seventy garments, through which the marrow of her shin will be visible."""
"2565","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first group to enter Paradise will be in the form of the moon on the night of the full moon, and those who come after them will be like the brightest glittering star in the sky. Their hearts will be like the heart of one man; there will be no disagreement, hatred or envy among them. Each one of them will have two wives, whose beauty will be such that the marrow of their shins will be visible through the flesh. They will glorify Allah Almighty morning and evening. They will not fall ill, nor blow their noses, nor spit. Their vessels will be of gold and silver, their combs will be of gold, and the fuel of their censers will be (fragrant) aloeswood."""
"2566","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The faces of the first group to enter Paradise will be like the moon on the night of the full moon. They will not spit there, nor blow their noses, nor relieve themselves. Their vessels there will be of gold, their combs of gold and silver, the fragrance of their censers will be aloeswood, and their sweat will be like musk. Each one of them will have two wives, whose beauty will be such that the marrow of their shins will be visible through the flesh. There will be no disagreement or hatred among them; their hearts will all be like one heart, and they will glorify Allah Almighty morning and evening."""
"2567","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The very first thing the people of Paradise will eat will be the extra (choice) lobe of the fish's liver."""
"2568","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing that will gather the people (to the place of gathering) will be a fire that will drive them from the east to the west."""
"2569","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing to be taken away from this Ummah will be humility (in prayer), until you will not see a single humble person in it."""
"2570","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing of your religion that you will lose will be trustworthiness."""
"2571","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first of people's deeds for which they will be held to account on the Day of Resurrection is the prayer. Our Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, will say to His angels, though He knows best: Look at My servant's prayer; did he complete it or did he fall short in it? If it is complete, it will be recorded for him as complete; and if he fell short in it in anything, Allah Almighty will say: Look, does My servant have any voluntary prayer? If he has any voluntary prayer, He will say: Complete My servant's obligatory prayer (from his voluntary prayers). Then the rest of the deeds will be taken to account in the same way."""
"2572","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing (of his deeds) for which a servant will be held to account is the prayer, and the first thing to be judged between people (in their rights) will be cases of blood (i.e. unjust killing)."""
"2573","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing for which a servant will be held to account on the Day of Resurrection is the prayer. If it turns out sound, all the rest of his deeds will be sound, and if it turns out corrupt, all the rest of his deeds will be corrupt."""
"2574","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing for which a servant will be held to account on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer. If he performed it completely, it will be recorded for him as complete; and if he did not perform it completely, Allah Almighty will say to His angels: Look, do you find any voluntary deed among My servant's deeds, so that you may complete his obligatory duty with it? Then the matter of zakah will be likewise, and then the rest of the deeds will be taken to account according to the same principle."""
"2575","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing to be taken away from the people will be trustworthiness, and the last thing of their religion to remain will be the prayer; and many a person who prays will have no share or portion (of good) with Allah Almighty."""
"2576","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing to be taken away from the people (of their worship) will be humility."""
"2577","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first thing to be judged between people on the Day of Resurrection will be cases of blood (unjust killing)."""
"2578","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As soon as the first drop of the martyr's blood falls, all his sins are forgiven, except debt."""
"2579","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first mosque built on the face of the earth was al-Masjid al-Haram, then al-Masjid al-Aqsa was built, and between the two (in their building) was a gap of forty years. Then after that, wherever the time of prayer comes upon you, pray there, for the virtue lies in that."""
"2580","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first person who changed the religion of Ibrahim (peace be upon him) was Amr bin Luhayy bin Qam'ah bin Khindif, Abu Khuza'ah."""
"2581","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first person from whose tongue clear and eloquent Arabic flowed was Isma'il (peace be upon him), and at that time he was fourteen years old."""
"2582","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first to change my Sunnah will be a man from Banu Umayyah."""
"2583","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first to be called on the Day of Resurrection will be Adam (peace be upon him). His offspring will be presented before him, and it will be said: This is your father Adam. He will say: Here I am at Your service, ready to obey You. Allah Almighty will say: Separate from your offspring the contingent of the people of Hell. He will say: O my Lord, how many shall I take out? Allah Almighty will say: Take out ninety-nine out of every hundred. The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, when ninety-nine out of every hundred of us are taken out, what will remain of us? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Indeed, the example of my Ummah among all the nations is like a single white hair on the body of a black bull."""
"2584","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first of all creation to be clothed (at the place of gathering) will be Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."""
"2585","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The first Prophet to be sent (as a Messenger) was Nuh (peace be upon him)."""
"2586","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The children of the idolaters (who die before maturity) will be servants of the people of Paradise."""
"2587","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The friends of Allah Almighty are those who, when they are seen, Allah Almighty is remembered."""
"2588","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Has Allah Almighty not made for you things which you can give in charity? Indeed, every time you say 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah) is charity, every time you say 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) is charity, every time you say 'Al-hamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah) is charity, every time you say 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah) is charity, enjoining good is charity, forbidding evil is charity, and even one of you having relations with his wife is charity. The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, when one of us fulfils his desire, does he get a reward for that too? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Tell me, if he were to use it in what is unlawful, would there not be a sin upon him? Likewise, when he uses it in a lawful way, there is a reward for him."""
"2589","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the two most wretched men among people? One is the ruddy man of Thamud who hamstrung the she-camel, and the other is the man who, O Ali, will strike you on this (head) until this (beard) is soaked with it (blood)."""
"2590","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of a deed which, if you adopt it, you will catch up with those who have gone ahead of you, no one who comes after you will be able to reach you, and you will become the best of those among whom you live, except for one who does exactly the same deed? That deed is that after every prayer you say 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times, 'Al-hamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah) thirty-three times and 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) thirty-three times."""
"2591","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you something about the Dajjal that no Prophet before me told his people? He will certainly be one-eyed, and a likeness (image) of Paradise and Hell will be brought with him; what he calls Paradise will in reality be the Fire. And I warn you of him just as Nuh (peace be upon him) warned his people."""
"2592","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not inform you of the very best surah of the Qur'an? It is: All praise is for Allah, the Lord of the worlds."" [Surah al-Fatihah: 2]"
"2593","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the best words by which those who seek refuge seek refuge? They are: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak [Surah al-Falaq: 1] and: Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind [Surah an-Nas: 1]."""
"2594","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the people of Hell? Every harsh-tempered, gluttonous, arrogant person who amasses wealth and withholds it from being spent. Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise? Every poor and humble person who, if he swears by Allah (about something), Allah Almighty will certainly fulfil it."""
"2595","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of something whose rank is even higher than (voluntary) fasting, prayer and charity? It is setting right relations between people (making peace), for the corruption of mutual relations is the thing that shaves off (the religion)."""
"2596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the borrowed billy goat? He is the one who performs halalah; so Allah Almighty has cursed both the one who performs halalah and the one for whom halalah is performed."""
"2597","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of a deed which, if you do it, you will catch up with those before you and surpass those after you? Praise Allah after every prayer, glorify Him and proclaim His greatness, that is, thirty-three times, thirty-three times and thirty-four times."""
"2598","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise? Every weak (humble) person whom people regard as weak, yet if he were to swear by Allah, Allah Almighty would surely fulfil it. Shall I not tell you about the people of Hell? Every harsh, gluttonous, coarse and arrogant person."""
"2599","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about your best rulers and your worst rulers? Your best rulers are those whom you love and who love you, for whom you pray and who pray for you. And your worst rulers are those whom you hate and who hate you, whom you curse and who curse you."""
"2600","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the best of witnesses? He is the one who gives his testimony before he is asked for it."""
"2601","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the person who holds the best rank among people? A man who holds the reins of his horse in the path of Allah until he dies or is martyred. Shall I not tell you about the one who comes next to him in rank? A man who lives in seclusion in a mountain pass, establishes the prayer, pays zakah and keeps away from the evils of people. Shall I not tell you about the worst of people? A man who is asked for something in the name of Allah and does not give."""
"2602","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the best households of the Ansar? The household of Banu al-Najjar, then the household of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the household of Banu al-Harith, then al-Khazraj, then the household of Banu Sa'idah; and in all the households of the Ansar there is goodness."""
"2603","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you who is the best among you and who is the worst? The best among you is the one from whom good is hoped and from whose evil people are safe, and the worst among you is the one from whom no good is hoped and from whose evil people are not safe."""
"2604","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about your men who are among the people of Paradise? The prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the truthful one (siddiq) is in Paradise, the child (who dies in infancy) is in Paradise, and the man who visits his (Muslim) brother on the far side of the city purely for the sake of Allah is in Paradise. Shall I not tell you about your women who are among the people of Paradise? The woman who is very loving, bears many children and repeatedly turns back (to her husband), who, when she is wronged (or she herself commits a wrong), says to her husband: 'This is my hand in your hand; I will not taste sleep until you are pleased with me.'"""
"2605","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of a supplication which, when some worldly distress or affliction befalls any of you and he supplicates with it, his affliction is removed? It is the supplication of Dhu al-Nun (Prophet Yunus, peace be upon him): 'La ilaha illa anta subhanaka inni kuntu min al-zalimin' (There is no true deity except You; You are free of all imperfection; indeed I have been among the wrongdoers)."""
"2606","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the prayer of the hypocrite? He delays the Asr prayer so much that when the sun becomes (pale) like the fat of a cow, he then offers it."""
"2607","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about what I fear for you more than the False Messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal)? It is hidden shirk (showing off): that a man stands to pray and beautifies his prayer only because he sees someone looking at him."""
"2608","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of a deed that removes the impurity (and rancour) of the heart? It is fasting three days of every month."""
"2609","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the one for whom the Fire will be forbidden tomorrow (on the Day of Resurrection)? The Fire is forbidden for everyone who is gentle, easygoing, close to people and good-natured."""
"2610","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not guide you to one of the gates of Paradise? It is saying 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no might and no power except with Allah)."""
"2611","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not guide you to a jihad in which there is no thorn (that is, no hardship and fighting)? It is Hajj to the House of Allah."""
"2612","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not guide you to Sayyid al-Istighfar (the master of seeking forgiveness)? It is this: 'Allahumma anta rabbi, la ilaha illa anta, khalaqtani wa ana 'abduka, wa ana 'ala 'ahdika wa wa'dika mastata'tu, a'udhu bika min sharri ma sana'tu, wa abu'u laka bi-ni'matika 'alayya, wa a'tarifu bi-dhunubi, faghfir li dhunubi innahu la yaghfiru al-dhunuba illa anta' (O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no true deity except You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I abide by Your covenant and promise as far as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your favours upon me and I confess my sins, so forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins except You). Whoever says these words in the evening and his appointed time (of death) comes to him before morning, Paradise becomes obligatory for him; and whoever says them in the morning and his appointed time comes to him before evening, Paradise becomes obligatory for him as well."""
"2613","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not guide you to a planting that is far better than this (worldly planting)? Say 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), 'Al-hamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah), 'La ilaha illa Allah' (There is no true deity except Allah) and 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest); for each of these words a tree is planted for you in Paradise."""
"2614","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not guide you to a word from beneath the Throne, from the treasures of Paradise? Say 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah' (There is no might and no power except with Allah), and Allah Almighty says: 'My servant has submitted and surrendered (himself to Me).'"""
"2615","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of a deed that brings more reward than your remembering Allah continuously through the night and the day? Say: 'Al-hamdu lillahi 'adada ma khalaq, al-hamdu lillahi mil'a ma khalaq, al-hamdu lillahi 'adada ma fi al-samawati wa ma fi al-ard, al-hamdu lillahi 'adada ma ahsa kitabuh, wal-hamdu lillahi 'ala ma ahsa kitabuh, wal-hamdu lillahi 'adada kulli shay', wal-hamdu lillahi mil'a kulli shay'' (All praise is for Allah as many times as what He has created; all praise is for Allah filling what He has created; all praise is for Allah as many times as what is in the heavens and what is in the earth; all praise is for Allah as many times as what His Book has recorded; all praise is for Allah for what His Book has recorded; all praise is for Allah as many times as everything; all praise is for Allah filling everything), and likewise glorify Allah (Subhan Allah) in the same measure. Learn them yourself and teach them to your descendants after you."""
"2616","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of something that is better for you than a servant? When you are about to lie down on your bed, glorify Allah, 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), thirty-three times, praise Him, 'Al-hamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah), thirty-three times, and proclaim His greatness, 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest), thirty-four times."""
"2617","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of the deeds by which Allah Almighty wipes away sins and increases good deeds? Performing ablution completely and well despite difficulty (such as intense cold), taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after a prayer."""
"2618","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of the deeds by which Allah Almighty wipes away sins and raises ranks? Performing ablution completely even at times of hardship and difficulty, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after a prayer. That is ribat (that is, true guarding at the frontier), that is ribat, that is ribat."""
"2619","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not guide you both to something better than what you have asked me for? When you are about to lie down on your beds, say 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) thirty-four times, say 'Al-hamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah) thirty-three times and say 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah) thirty-three times, for that is far better for you both than a servant."""
"2620","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Should I not feel modesty before a man before whom even the angels feel modesty?"" (He (peace and blessings be upon him) meant Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him).)"
"2621","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not teach you words which, when you say them, Allah Almighty will forgive you, even if you have already been forgiven? Say: 'La ilaha illa Allah al-'Aliyy al-'Azim, la ilaha illa Allah al-Hakim al-Karim, la ilaha illa Allah, subhan Allah rabbi al-samawati al-sab'i wa rabbi al-'arsh al-'azim, al-hamdu lillahi rabbi al-'alamin' (There is no true deity except Allah, the Most High, the Most Great; there is no true deity except Allah, the Most Wise, the Most Generous; there is no true deity except Allah; glory be to Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne; all praise is for Allah, Lord of the worlds)."""
"2622","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not teach you words to say when you lie down on your bed, so that if you die that very night you will die upon the natural religion (fitrah), and if you reach the morning you will attain good? Say: 'Allahumma aslamtu nafsi ilayk, wa wajjahtu wajhi ilayk, wa fawwadtu amri ilayk, raghbatan wa rahbatan ilayk, wa alja'tu zahri ilayk, la malja'a wa la manja minka illa ilayk, amantu bi-kitabika alladhi anzalt, wa bi-nabiyyika alladhi arsalt' (O Allah, I have submitted myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, out of hope and fear of You, and relied upon You for support; there is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You revealed and in Your Prophet whom You sent)."""
"2623","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not teach you words to say at times of distress and hardship? (They are:) 'Allahu Allahu rabbi, la ushriku bihi shay'an' (Allah, Allah is my Lord; I associate nothing with Him)."""
"2624","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not teach you words that you should recite? (They are:) 'Subhan Allahi 'adada khalqih, subhan Allahi 'adada khalqih, subhan Allahi 'adada khalqih, subhan Allahi rida nafsih, subhan Allahi rida nafsih, subhan Allahi rida nafsih, subhan Allahi zinata 'arshih, subhan Allahi zinata 'arshih, subhan Allahi zinata 'arshih, subhan Allahi midada kalimatih, subhan Allahi midada kalimatih, subhan Allahi midada kalimatih' (Glory be to Allah as many times as the number of His creation, three times; glory be to Allah as much as pleases Him, three times; glory be to Allah as much as the weight of His Throne, three times; glory be to Allah as much as the ink of His words, three times)."""
"2625","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not teach you words such that, even if you owed a debt as large as (the mountain of) Sabir, Allah Almighty would pay it off on your behalf? Say: 'Allahumma-kfini bi-halalika 'an haramik, wa aghnini bi-fadlika 'amman siwak' (O Allah, suffice me with what You have made lawful against what You have made unlawful, and make me independent by Your bounty of all besides You)."""
"2626","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not teach you a deed by which you will catch up with those who have gone ahead of you and surpass those who come after you, and no one will be better than you except one who does the like of what you do? After every prayer, say 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), 'Allahu akbar' (Allah is the Greatest) and 'Al-hamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah) thirty-three times each."""
"2627","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise? They are those who are regarded as weak and the oppressed (in the world)."""
"2628","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you about the greatest of sins (the major sins)? Associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and speaking falsehood."""
"2629","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you of the best of your deeds, the purest in the sight of your King (Allah), the one that raises your ranks the highest, which is better for you than spending gold and silver, and better for you than meeting your enemy so that you strike their necks and they strike your necks? That deed is the remembrance of Allah."""
"2630","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shall I not tell you what slander (and mischief-making) is? It is carrying tales and spreading discord among people."""
"2631","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! The family of so-and-so are not my friends and supporters; rather, my Wali (friend and protector) is only Allah Almighty and the righteous believers."""
"2632","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Indeed, the tribulation will arise from this direction, from where the horn of Satan rises."""
"2633","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Indeed, strength is archery. Beware! Surely, strength is archery. Beware! Surely, strength is archery."""
"2634","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! Soon Allah Almighty will open the land for you and you will be spared the toil (of enemies), so let none of you neglect practising (and playing) with his arrows."""
"2635","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! I declare myself free of the intimate friendship of every intimate friend. If I were to take anyone as an intimate friend (khalil), I would have taken Abu Bakr, but indeed your companion (that is, I myself) is the intimate friend (khalil) of Allah."""
"2636","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! Indeed, the False Messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal) will be blind in the right eye, as though his eye were a swollen grape. Last night I saw myself in a dream near the Ka'bah, and there was a man of brown complexion, more handsome than any brown-complexioned man you have ever seen. His locks (of hair) hung between his shoulders; his hair was straight, and water was dripping from his head. He had placed his hands on the shoulders of two men and was circling the House of Allah between them. I asked: 'Who is this?' They said: 'This is the Messiah, son of Maryam (peace be upon them both).' Then behind him I saw another man whose hair was tightly curled; he was blind in the right eye, and to my eyes he most resembled Ibn Qatan. He had placed his hands on the shoulders of a man and was circling the House of Allah. I asked: 'Who is this?' They replied: 'This is the False Messiah (al-Masih al-Dajjal).'"""
"2637","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! Indeed, my Lord has commanded me to teach you what you do not know of what He has taught me this day: (Allah Almighty says:) 'Every wealth that I have granted to a servant is lawful. Indeed, I created all My servants upright (monotheists); then the devils came to them and led them astray from their religion, and the devils made unlawful for them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I have sent down no authority.' Indeed, Allah Almighty looked at the people of the earth and was intensely angry with all of them, whether Arabs or non-Arabs, except a few remnants of the People of the Book, and He said: 'I have sent you only to test you and to test others through you, and I have revealed to you a Book that water cannot wash away; you recite it asleep and awake.' And indeed, Allah Almighty commanded me to burn Quraysh, so I said: 'O my Lord! Then they will crush my head and break it like bread.' Allah Almighty said: 'Drive them out as they drove you out, and fight them and We will help you, and spend and We will spend on you. Send an army and We will send five like it, and together with those who obey you, fight those who disobey you.' And the people of Paradise are of three kinds: a ruler who is just, gives charity and is granted success in doing good; a man who is merciful and tender-hearted towards every relative and every Muslim; and a man who is chaste and refrains from asking, though he has a family to support. And the people of Hell are of five kinds: the weak person who has no sense (to restrain himself from evil), those among you who are followers of others and seek neither family nor wealth; the treacherous person whose greed is not hidden and who betrays even in the smallest thing; and the man who morning and evening keeps deceiving you about your family and your wealth; and he (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned miserliness, lying, and the foul-mouthed, obscene person."""
"2638","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! Indeed, the blood money for quasi-deliberate killing (shibh al-'amd) with a whip, a stick and the like is one hundred camels, taken in the heavier (aggravated) form, forty of which shall be pregnant she-camels with young in their bellies."""
"2639","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Each one of you is conversing intimately (in munajat) with his Lord, so let none of you harm another, nor raise his voice over another in recitation."""
"2640","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! These are four fundamental things: do not associate anything with Allah, do not kill a soul which Allah has made sacred except by right, do not commit adultery and do not steal."""
"2641","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! Those before you from the People of the Book split into seventy-two (72) sects, and this Ummah will split into seventy-three (73) sects, of which seventy-two (72) will be in Hell and only one will be in Paradise, and that is al-Jama'ah (Ahl al-Sunnah wal-Jama'ah). And indeed, there will emerge from my Ummah people in whom desires will spread just as the poison of a rabid dog spreads through the body of the one it bites; not a vein or a joint of him will remain that it does not enter."""
"2642","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! On the Day of Resurrection a banner will be set up for every deceiver and betrayer, in proportion to his betrayal."""
"2643","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! I have been given the Qur'an and something like it along with it (wisdom and Sunnah). Beware! Soon a man, full-bellied and reclining on his couch, will say: 'Hold fast to this Qur'an; whatever you find lawful in it, treat as lawful, and whatever you find unlawful in it, treat as unlawful.' (Listen!) Indeed, the meat of the domestic donkey is not lawful for you, nor (the meat of) any fanged beast of prey, nor the lost property (luqatah) of a non-Muslim under covenant, unless its owner has no need of it. And whoever comes as a guest to a people, it is binding on them to host him; and if they do not host him, the guest has the right to take from them by force the equivalent of his hospitality."""
"2644","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! I will be your forerunner at the Pond (al-Kawthar). The distance between its two sides is like the distance between San'a and Aylah, and its jugs (or cups) will be like the stars of the sky."""
"2645","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not trust me, when I am the trustee of the One who is in the heaven? News from the heaven comes to me morning and evening."""
"2646","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Will you not pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you worship Allah alone, associate nothing with Him, establish the five prayers, pay zakah, listen and obey (those in authority), and ask people for nothing?"""
"2647","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not hear? Indeed, Allah Almighty does not punish because of the tears of the eye or the grief of the heart; rather, He punishes or shows mercy because of this"" - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed towards his blessed mouth (that is, because of the tongue). ""And indeed, the deceased is punished because of his family's weeping over him."""
"2648","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why do you not form rows as the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord? They complete the front rows first and stand closely joined to one another in the row."""
"2649","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you not wonder how Allah Almighty turns away from me the abuse and curses of Quraysh? They (Allah forbid) abuse and curse 'Mudhammam' (the blameworthy one), whereas my name is 'Muhammad' (the praised one)."""
"2650","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Will you not teach this woman the ruqyah (incantation) for namlah (skin sores), just as you taught her writing?"""
"2651","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did you not cover it, even if only by placing a stick across it?"""
"2652","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is there no one who will give charity to this man (a traveller or one praying alone) by praying (in congregation) with him?"""
"2653","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is there no one who will give a household a she-camel that goes out in the morning with a bowl of milk and comes back in the evening with a bowl of milk? Indeed, its reward is immense."""
"2654","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did you split open his heart so that you would know whether he said it for that reason or not? What will become of you on the Day of Resurrection regarding (the claim of) 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah)?"""
"2655","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! Whoever wrongs a mu'ahid (a non-Muslim living under a covenant of protection), or diminishes his right, or burdens him beyond his capacity, or takes anything from him without his willing consent, then I will be the one to argue against him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2656","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Does any one of you not care that he sets up camp with a flock of goats a mile or two away, then, because the pasture there runs out, he moves further (to higher ground); then Friday comes and he does not come (for the Friday prayer) and does not attend it, then Friday comes and he does not attend it, then Friday comes and he does not attend it, until a seal is set upon his heart?"""
"2657","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! It may be that a man, while reclining on his couch, has a hadith of mine reach him and he says: 'Between us and you there is only the Book of Allah (the Qur'an); whatever we find permissible in it we will treat as permissible, and whatever we find forbidden in it we will treat as forbidden.' (Listen!) Whatever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has forbidden is forbidden just as what Allah has forbidden."""
"2658","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Listen! A person should blame no one but himself (in this case, namely) that he spends the night while the grease and smell of food remain on his hand."""
"2659","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O my brothers! Prepare for a day like this one (the Hereafter)."""
"2660","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Would any one of you like to find, when he returns to his family, three large, fat, pregnant she-camels? For one of you to recite three verses in his prayer is better for him than three large, fat, pregnant she-camels."""
"2661","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Would any one of you like to be spat upon in the face? Indeed, when one of you faces the qiblah, he is in fact facing his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, and the angel is on his right. So let him not spit to his right nor towards the qiblah; rather, let him spit to his left or under his foot. And if something urgent presses upon him, let him spit like this"" - meaning into his garment."
"2662","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is any one of you unable, in the prayer - meaning in the voluntary prayer - to move forward, or step back, or move to his right or his left?"""
"2663","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is any one of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an in one night? Indeed, whoever recites 'Say: He is Allah, the One; Allah, the Eternal Refuge' in a night has recited a third of the Qur'an that night."" [Surah al-Ikhlas: 1-2]"
"2664","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is any one of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an every night? Indeed, Allah Almighty divided the Qur'an into three parts, and He made 'Say: He is Allah, the One' one of the parts of the Qur'an."" [Surah al-Ikhlas: 1]"
"2665","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is any one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day? Let him glorify Allah one hundred times, and Allah Almighty records for him a thousand good deeds in return and erases a thousand of his sins."""
"2666","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The most blessed and the most ill-omened thing for a person is what lies between his two jaws (that is, the tongue)."""
"2667","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Well done, O Ibn al-Khattab! By the One in whose Hand is my soul, Satan has never met you walking on a path except that he took a path other than yours."""
"2668","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of luxury and indulgence, for the true servants of Allah are not accustomed to luxury."""
"2669","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of (harming or neglecting) the milk-giving animal."""
"2670","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of talking late into the night after people have gone to sleep, for you do not know what (decree or matter) Allah is about to bring about among His creation."""
"2671","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of every deed for which you will later have to apologise."""
"2672","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of (going to) the doors of rulers (and their courts), for they have become a most difficult place and one that brings a person down."""
"2673","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of making camp in the middle of the roads and praying there, for they are the dwelling places of snakes and wild beasts; and beware of relieving yourselves there, for they are places of cursing."""
"2674","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of praising one another, for it is (as if it were) slaughter."""
"2675","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of sitting on the roads. And if you must sit there, then give the road its right: lowering the gaze, refraining from causing harm, returning the greeting of peace, enjoining good and forbidding evil."""
"2676","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of khadhf (flicking small pebbles with the fingertips), for it breaks a tooth and puts out an eye, and it does no harm to the enemy."""
"2677","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of entering upon non-mahram women (in private)."""
"2678","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of greed and stinginess, for those before you were destroyed only because of greed. It commanded them to be miserly, so they were miserly; it commanded them to sever ties of kinship, so they severed them; and it commanded them to commit wickedness, so they committed wickedness."""
"2679","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not search for one another's faults, do not eavesdrop, do not vie with one another, do not envy one another, do not hate one another, and do not turn your backs on one another. O servants of Allah, be brothers to one another. And let no man propose marriage over his brother's proposal until he marries or leaves her."""
"2680","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of ghuluw (going to extremes) in religion, for those before you were destroyed only because of going to extremes in religion."""
"2681","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of wisal (continuous fasting without eating or drinking anything in between). Indeed, you are not like me in this; I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me to drink. So take upon yourselves only as much of deeds as you are able to bear."""
"2682","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, even if he is a disbeliever, for there is no veil between it (his cry) and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"2683","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of corrupted relations and mutual grudges, for indeed this is the trait that shaves off (religion), that is, destroys it."""
"2684","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of narrating many hadiths attributed to me. Whoever attributes something to me, let him say only what is true and truthful; and whoever fabricates against me something I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire of Hell."""
"2685","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of swearing many oaths in buying and selling, for it (the oath) sells the goods (for the moment) but then wipes out the blessing (of the business)."""
"2686","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of regarding sins as trivial, for the example of these small sins is like a people who halted in a valley; then one man brought a stick and another man brought a stick, until they had gathered enough wood with which they baked their bread. And indeed, the sins regarded as trivial, when they seize the one who committed them, will destroy him."""
"2687","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of regarding sins as minor and trivial, for they keep accumulating upon a man until they destroy him. Their example is like a man who was in a barren desert; then the time came for the people to cook their food, so one man began bringing a stick and another man began bringing a stick, until they gathered a heap from it and kindled a fire, then cooked whatever was in it."""
"2688","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of eating these two foul-smelling plants (that is, raw garlic and onion) and then entering our mosques. And if you must eat them, then cook them over fire to kill their smell."""
"2689","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Days of Tashriq (the 11th, 12th and 13th of Dhul-Hijjah) are days of eating, drinking and remembrance of Allah Almighty."""
"2690","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The days of Mina are days of eating and drinking."""
"2691","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of making the backs of your animals into pulpits (that is, delivering sermons or holding long conversations while sitting on them), for Allah Almighty subjected them to you only so that they may carry you to lands you could not have reached except with great hardship; and He has made the earth (a place of rest) for you, so attend to your needs upon it."""
"2692","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware of gaps (in the rows of prayer)."" (The narrator says that this refers to the gaps between people in the rows during prayer.)"
"2693","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever of you women intends to go to the mosque, let her not go near perfume at all."""
"2694","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you looks after the family and property of the one who goes out (for jihad) in a good way in his absence will have half the reward of the one who went out."""
"2695","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you has land or a date-palm grove (shared with someone), let him not sell it until he has offered it to his partner."""
"2696","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Which of you loves the wealth of his heir more than his own wealth? Indeed, his own wealth is what he has sent ahead (by spending it in the way of Allah), and the wealth of his heir is what he leaves behind (after death)."""
"2697","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Which of you would love to go out every morning to Buthan or to al-Aqiq (valleys of Madinah) and bring back from there two fat, beautiful she-camels, without any sin and without severing ties of kinship? Then for one of you to go out early in the morning to the mosque and learn or recite two verses from the Book of Allah is better for him than two she-camels, and three verses are better than three she-camels, and four verses are better than four she-camels, and likewise, however many verses there are, they are better than the same number of camels."""
"2698","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever calls his (Muslim) brother a disbeliever, then one of the two of them has returned with it (disbelief): if he (the one called a disbeliever) is as he said (then so be it); otherwise it (the verdict of disbelief) will return to the one who said it."""
"2699","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies while he has with him the very property of another person, whether he (the creditor) has received something from it or has not, then he (the owner) will be treated the same as the other creditors."""
"2700","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whichever Muslim man frees a Muslim man, that will be his release from the Fire of Hell; Allah Almighty will save one bone of his (the freer) from Hell in return for every bone of his (the slave). And whichever Muslim woman frees a Muslim woman, that will become a shield for her from the Fire of Hell; Allah Almighty will save one bone of hers (the woman who freed) from the Fire in return for every bone of hers (the slave woman). And whichever Muslim man frees two Muslim women, they will be the means of his release from the Fire; Allah Almighty will save one bone of his from the Fire in return for every two bones of theirs."""
"2701","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who puts on perfume and then goes out, and passes by people (non-mahram men) so that they may smell her fragrance, she is an adulteress, and every eye (that looks at her with lust) is adulterous."""
"2702","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who has been scented with incense (bakhur) should not attend the Isha prayer with us."""
"2703","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who puts on perfume and then goes out to the mosque, her prayer is not accepted until she takes a bath (to remove the effect of the perfume, like the ritual bath for major impurity)."""
"2704","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman whose husband dies and who marries (someone else) after him, she will belong (in Paradise) to her last husband."""
"2705","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who adds hair to her head that is not her (own), then indeed it is sheer falsehood that she is adding."""
"2706","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without any Shari'ah excuse or necessity, even the fragrance of Paradise is forbidden to her."""
"2707","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who has three of her children die, they will become a barrier (and a shield) for her from the Fire of Hell."""
"2708","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who takes off her clothes somewhere other than her own home (without any Shari'ah necessity), Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will remove His veil from her (that is, He will withdraw His protection and concealment of her)."""
"2709","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void, her marriage is void. If he (the man) consummates the marriage with her, then the dowry (mahr) is due to her in return for what he made lawful of her private part. Then if they (the guardians) dispute among themselves, the Muslim ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."""
"2710","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any woman who takes off her clothes somewhere other than her husband's home has indeed torn the veil that is between her and Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"2711","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any hide (of a dead animal) that is tanned becomes pure."""
"2712","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any caller who calls to misguidance and is followed, upon him will be sins equal to the sins of all those who followed him, and nothing will be reduced from their (the followers') sins. And any caller who calls to guidance and is followed, for him will be a reward equal to the rewards of all those who followed him, and nothing will be reduced from their (the followers') rewards."""
"2713","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any shepherd (or ruler) who deceives (and betrays) his subjects will go into the Fire of Hell."""
"2714","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man to whom Allah Almighty grants knowledge and he conceals it (from people), Allah Almighty will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire."""
"2715","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who gives another man something as an umra (a lifelong gift), saying that it is for you and your descendants, then that thing belongs to him and to his heirs from among his descendants, and will be divided among them as inheritance."""
"2716","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who gives another man something as an umra, saying that it is for you and your descendants, then indeed it becomes the property of the one to whom it was given; it will not return to the one who gave it."""
"2717","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who becomes bankrupt, and a (creditor) finds his very own goods with him, he has more right to it (to take back the goods) than other people (the other creditors)."""
"2718","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who leads people in prayer while they dislike him (because of some Shari'ah defect), his prayer does not rise above his ears (that is, it does not attain the honour of acceptance)."""
"2719","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who sells some goods, then finds his very own goods with the man (the buyer) who has become bankrupt, and he (the seller) had not received anything of its price, then the goods are his. And if he had received some part of its price, then he will be treated (with regard to the remaining goods) the same as the other creditors."""
"2720","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who sells some goods, then the buyer becomes bankrupt, and the seller had not received anything of its price, then he finds his very own goods present, he has the most right to it (to take it back). But if the buyer dies, then the owner of the goods will be treated the same as the other creditors."""
"2721","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who comes out and tries to create division among my Ummah (that is, to spread discord), strike his neck."""
"2722","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who wrongfully seizes even a hand-span of land, Allah Almighty will oblige him to dig it until he reaches the bottom of the seventh earth; then on the Day of Resurrection it will be made a collar around his neck until judgement is passed between the people."""
"2723","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who commits fornication with a free woman or a slave woman, the child born of it will be called a child of fornication (walad al-zina); he will neither inherit (from anyone) nor will anyone inherit from him."""
"2724","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who stands up to perform ablution intending to pray, then washes his hands, the sins of his hands fall away with the very first drop of water; then when he washes his face, the sins of his ears and eyes fall away with the very first drop; then when he washes his arms up to the elbows and his feet up to the ankles, he becomes free of every sin and error of his, just as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him. Then if he stands for prayer, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, raises him a degree by it (the prayer), and if he sits, he sits in safety."""
"2725","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who touches his private part should perform ablution, and any woman who touches her private part should (also) perform ablution."""
"2726","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, Allah Almighty will make one bone of the slave he freed a means of protection from the Fire of Hell for every bone of his (the freer). And any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, Allah Almighty will, on the Day of Resurrection, make one bone of the slave woman she freed a means of protection from the Fire of Hell for every bone of hers."""
"2727","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any Muslim man who calls a Muslim man a disbeliever: if he is truly a disbeliever (then so be it); otherwise, the one who said it will himself become the disbeliever."""
"2728","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man of my Ummah whom I have reviled or cursed in a state of anger, then I am also one of the children of Adam; I become angry just as you become angry. And Allah Almighty has sent me as a mercy to all the worlds, so on the Day of Resurrection I will make it (that harsh speech) a mercy and a supplication in their favour."""
"2729","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any child who performs Hajj and then reaches puberty must perform another Hajj; and any Bedouin who performs Hajj and then migrates must perform another Hajj; and any slave who performs Hajj and then is freed must (also) perform another Hajj."""
"2730","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any guest who stays with a people and wakes in the morning deprived (that is, he was not given hospitality), has the right to take from them the amount of his hospitality, and there is no sin upon him."""
"2731","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any slave who runs away from his masters has committed disbelief (ingratitude) until he returns to them."""
"2732","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any servant who commits something of what Allah has forbidden, and then the prescribed punishment (hadd) for it (the crime) is carried out upon him, Allah Almighty makes it an expiation for that sin of his."""
"2733","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any slave who marries without the permission of his masters is a fornicator."""
"2734","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any slave who marries without the permission of his masters is a fornicator."""
"2735","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any slave who makes a contract of manumission (mukatabah) for one hundred uqiyah (of silver) and pays all of it except ten uqiyah, he is (still) a slave; and any slave who makes a contract of manumission for one hundred dinars and pays the rest except ten dinars, he is (also still) a slave."""
"2736","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any slave who dies while in a state of running away will enter the Fire, even if he was killed in the path of Allah Almighty."""
"2737","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any town that you come to and stay in, you have your share in it; and any town that disobeys Allah and His Messenger, then indeed one fifth (khums) of it is for Allah and His Messenger, and then the rest is all for you."""
"2738","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any people who sit in a gathering, and after sitting for a long time they disperse before remembering Allah Almighty and sending blessings upon His Prophet, it will be a cause of regret and loss for them from Allah; if Allah wills He will punish them, and if He wills He will forgive them."""
"2739","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any Muslim who shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, whether it misses or hits the target, for him is a reward equal to freeing a slave from the descendants of Isma'il. And any man who grows old in the path of Allah, it (his old age) will be a light for him. And any man who frees a Muslim man, every limb of the freer becomes a ransom for him from the Fire of Hell in return for every limb of the freed one. And any man who stands intending to pray and washes the limbs of ablution properly, he becomes free of every sin and error of his; then if he stands for prayer, Allah Almighty will raise him a degree because of it, and if he sleeps, he will sleep in a state of safety."""
"2740","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any Muslim for whom four people bear witness to goodness, Allah Almighty will admit him into Paradise, and (likewise if) three or two (bear witness, he will enter Paradise)."""
"2741","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any two Muslims who meet, and one of them takes his companion's hand, and they shake hands and together praise Allah Almighty, they will part in such a state that no sin remains between them."""
"2742","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Fear Allah and be moderate in seeking provision, for no soul will die until it has received its provision in full, even if it is delayed. So fear Allah and be moderate in seeking provision: take what is lawful and leave what is unlawful."""
"2743","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! When this day (that is, Friday) comes, take a bath, and each of you should apply the best oil and perfume that he can find."""
"2744","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! Indeed Allah is pure and He accepts nothing but what is pure. And indeed Allah has commanded the believers with the same thing that He commanded the messengers, for He said: 'O messengers! Eat of the good things and do righteous deeds; indeed I am All-Knowing of what you do.' [Surah al-Mu'minun: 51] And He said: 'O you who believe! Eat of the good things that We have provided for you.' [Surah al-Baqarah: 172] Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned a man who travels a long journey, his hair dishevelled and his body covered in dust; he stretches out his hands towards the sky, saying: O my Lord! O my Lord! while his food is unlawful, his drink is unlawful, his clothing is unlawful, and he has been nourished with the unlawful. So how can the supplication of such a person be answered!"""
"2745","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people! I have indeed had many brothers and friends among you, and I declare before Allah that I am free of having any of you as my khalil (intimate friend). And if I were to take anyone from my Ummah as a khalil, I would certainly have taken Abu Bakr as a khalil. And indeed my Lord has taken me as His khalil just as He took Ibrahim (peace be upon him) as His khalil. Listen! Those before you used to take the graves of their prophets and righteous people as places of prostration (mosques). Beware! Do not take graves as places of prostration; I strictly forbid you from that."""
"2746","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people, nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the true dream, which a Muslim sees himself or which is seen for him. Listen! I have been forbidden to recite the Qur'an while bowing or prostrating. So in bowing (ruku'), proclaim the greatness of your Lord, and in prostration, strive hard in supplication, for it is worthy of being accepted for you."""
"2747","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people, hold fast to the middle way (moderation), hold fast to moderation, for Allah Almighty does not grow weary (of rewarding) until you grow weary (of doing deeds)."""
"2748","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people, I have left among you two things such that if you hold firmly to them you will never go astray: one is the Book of Allah, and the other is my family ('itrah), that is, the people of my household."""
"2749","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people, this practice of yours (that is, gathering behind me at night for voluntary prayer) continued until I began to fear that it might be made obligatory upon you. So make it your practice to pray in your homes, for the best prayer of a person is in his home, except the obligatory prayer."""
"2750","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O people, do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being. But when you do face them, stand firm, and know that Paradise lies beneath the shade of the swords."" (Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated:) 'Allahumma munzil al-kitab, wa mujri as-sahab, wa hazim al-ahzab, ihzimhum wansurna 'alayhim' (O Allah, Revealer of the Book, Mover of the clouds and Defeater of the confederates, defeat them and grant us victory over them)."""
"2751","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who takes usury (riba) and the one who gives it are equal (in sin)."""
"2752","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Now the oven has heated up (that is, now the battle has become truly fierce)."""
"2753","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Now his skin has become cool upon him (that is, now that the deceased's debt has been paid, he has found relief from punishment)."""
"2754","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Now we will attack them and they will not be able to attack us (he said this after the retreat of the disbelievers in the Battle of the Confederates)."""
"2755","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The signs (of the Hour) are like beads strung on a thread; when the thread breaks, they will fall one after another in quick succession."""
"2756","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The two verses at the end of Surah al-Baqarah are such that whoever recites them during a night, they will suffice him."""
"2757","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The leaders (that is, rulers) will be from Quraysh; their righteous will be rulers of the righteous, and their wicked will be rulers of the wicked. And if Quraysh appoint over you even an Abyssinian slave whose nose and ears have been cut off, then listen to him and obey, as long as none of you is given a choice between his Islam and having his neck struck. If he is given a choice between his Islam and having his neck struck, then let him offer his neck (but not abandon his religion)."""
"2758","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The leaders will be from Quraysh. They have a right over you, and you likewise have the same right over them: when they are asked for mercy, they should show mercy; when they are made to judge, they should be just; and when they make a covenant, they should fulfil it. Whoever of them does not do so, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all of mankind; neither his obligatory nor his voluntary worship will be accepted."""
"2759","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The farther one is from the mosque, the greater his reward will be."""
"2760","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Camels are a source of honour for their owners, sheep and goats are pure blessing, and goodness has been tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."""
"2761","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ithmid (antimony kohl) brightens the eyesight and makes the hair (of the eyelashes) grow."""
"2762","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ihsan is that you worship Allah as though you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then indeed He sees you."""
"2763","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The four sisters, namely Maymunah, Umm al-Fadl, Salma, and their maternal half-sister Asma' bint Umays, are believing women (of firm faith)."""
"2764","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The adhan consists of nineteen phrases and the iqamah of seventeen phrases."""
"2765","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The two ears are part of the head."""
"2766","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The land is Allah's land and the servants are (also) Allah's servants. Whoever brings barren (dead) land to life, it belongs to him."""
"2767","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Except for the graveyard and the bathhouse (hammam), the whole earth is a mosque (that is, a place of prostration and a place to pray)."""
"2768","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Souls are like assembled troops. Those that knew one another in the world of souls become close (in this world too), and those that were strangers to one another there are at odds (here too)."""
"2769","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The waist-wrapper (izar) should reach to the middle of the shin or to the ankles; there is no good in letting it hang below that."""
"2770","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Letting garments hang down applies to the waist-wrapper, the shirt and the turban. Whoever drags any of these (on the ground) out of pride and arrogance, Allah Almighty will not look at him (with mercy) on the Day of Resurrection."""
"2771","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Asking permission is (only) three times. Then if you are given permission to enter, (well and good); otherwise, go back."""
"2772","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cleaning oneself with stones is to be done in an odd number, stoning the Jamarat is odd, the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah is odd, and the Tawaf of the House of Allah is odd. So when any of you cleans himself with stones, let him use an odd number of stones."""
"2773","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Cleaning oneself after relieving oneself (istinja) should be done with (at least) three stones, provided there is no dung (or any impure thing) among them."""
"2774","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Islam is that: you establish the prayer, pay the zakah, perform Hajj to the House of Allah, fast the month of Ramadan, and take the ritual bath (ghusl) for major impurity (janabah)."""
"2775","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Islam is that you bear witness that there is no true god except Allah and that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, that you establish the prayer, pay the zakah, fast Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House of Allah if you are able to make your way there."""
"2776","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Islam is that you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, fast Ramadan, and perform Hajj to the House of Allah."""
"2777","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Islam wipes out all the (disbelieving) deeds and sins that came before it."""
"2778","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Islam always prevails and cannot be prevailed over."""
"2779","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(In blood money, that is, the compensation for injury,) all teeth are equal; the blood money for the front teeth and for the molars is the same."""
"2780","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(In matters of blood money,) teeth are equal; the blood money for each tooth is five (camels) each."""
"2781","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Exultant insolence (that is, arrogance and transgressing bounds) is an evil thing."""
"2782","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(In blood money, all) fingers are equal; for each one there are ten camels."""
"2783","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""All fingers are equal (in retribution and blood money); the blood money for each of them is ten camels."""
"2784","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The fingers are equal and the teeth are equal too; the front tooth and the molar are equal; this and this are equal."" (The narrator says that this refers to the thumb and the little finger.)"
"2785","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, those with the most wealth will be the lowest (in rank), except the one who spent his wealth like this and like this (that is, right and left, in front and behind, in good causes) and earned it from lawful and pure earnings."""
"2786","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam is a guarantor (that is, responsible). If he leads the prayer well, the reward is for him and for those following him; and if he makes a mistake, its burden is upon him and not upon those following him."""
"2787","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The imam is a guarantor and the muezzin is one entrusted. 'Allahumma arshid al-a'immah waghfir lil-mu'adhdhinin' (O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins)."""
"2788","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The rulers will be from Quraysh as long as they act among you upon three things: when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; when they distribute wealth, they do so fairly; and when they judge, they act with justice."""
"2789","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The matter (that is, the time of death) is coming far more swiftly than that (a person's hope)."""
"2790","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The prophets are alive in their graves, praying."""
"2791","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Ansar are like the inner garment worn next to the body (shi'ar), and the rest of the people are like the outer garment (dithar). If all the people were to take one valley or mountain pass, and the Ansar took another valley, I would take the path of the valley of the Ansar. And were it not for the (virtue of) Hijrah, I would have been one of the Ansar."""
"2792","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Ansar are my confidants and my close people. (In future) the people will increase in number while they decrease. So accept (the good deeds) of those among them who do good, and overlook those among them who err."""
"2793","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Ansar, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, Ghifar, Ashja', and those who are of Banu Abd al-Dar are all my allies to the exclusion of other people, and Allah and His Messenger are their Protector (and Helper)."""
"2794","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hands are of three kinds: the hand of Allah Almighty is the highest, the hand of the giver comes after it (in rank), and the hand of the one who asks is the lowest. So give away the surplus wealth (beyond your need), and do not make yourself helpless (that is, do not make yourself needy)."""
"2795","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is in essence patience and generosity (magnanimity)."""
"2796","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is that you believe in Allah, His angels, His Book, the meeting with Him and His messengers, and that you also believe in being raised again after death."""
"2797","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is that you believe in Allah, His angels, His Books, His messengers and the Last Day, and that you also believe in the divine decree, its good and its bad."""
"2798","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is that you believe in Allah, His angels, His Books and His messengers, and believe in Paradise, Hell and the Scale (the balance for weighing deeds), and believe in being brought back to life after death, and also believe in the divine decree, its good and its bad."""
"2799","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith has seventy-odd doors (branches). The lowest of them is removing something harmful from the road, and the highest is affirming 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah)."""
"2800","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith has seventy-odd branches. The most excellent of them is affirming 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no god but Allah), and the lowest branch is removing something harmful from the road; and modesty (haya) is also a branch of faith."""
"2801","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith has sixty-odd branches, and modesty (haya) is also an (important) branch of faith."""
"2802","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is a restraint against treacherous, sudden killing; no believer kills anyone treacherously."""
"2803","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is Yemeni (that is, the faith of the people of Yemen holds a very lofty station)."""
"2804","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is Yemeni. Listen! Harshness and hardness of hearts are among the loud-voiced herdsmen who follow behind the camels, where the two horns of Satan rise, (that is,) among the tribes of Rabi'ah and Mudar."""
"2805","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is Yemeni, but the trials are over there, and from that very place (towards the east) the horn of Satan will rise."""
"2806","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Faith is Yemeni, disbelief is towards the east, tranquillity and dignity belong to those who keep sheep and goats, while pride and showing off are among the loud-voiced owners of horses and camels. (Then he said:) The Messiah (the Dajjal) will come, and when he reaches behind Mount Uhud, the angels will turn his face towards Syria (al-Sham), and there he will perish."""
"2807","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one on the right has the first right, then (the one after him) on the right."""
"2808","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those on the right (have the first right), those on the right (have the first right), those on the right (have the first right)."""
"2809","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A previously married woman (a widow or divorcee) has more right over her own decision than her guardian, and a virgin girl too is to be asked for her permission regarding her marriage, and her permission is her silence."""
